window.SITE_INDEX=[["DMARC report reader", "dmarc-report-reader.html", "tool", "Read DMARC aggregate reports (XML, zip, gz): who sends as your domain, SPF and DKIM alignment, failing sources, ready for p=quarantine or p=reject"],["Beep code lookup", "beep-code-lookup.html", "tool", "BIOS beep codes and blink codes: AMI, Award, Phoenix, Dell, HP, Lenovo, Apple, debug LEDs, POST codes"],["UPS runtime calculator", "ups-runtime-calculator.html", "tool", "How long a UPS runs: load in watts, VA and power factor, battery Ah, aged batteries, shutdown timing"],["PoE budget calculator", "poe-budget-calculator.html", "tool", "Power over Ethernet budget: 802.3af, 802.3at PoE+, 802.3bt PoE++, classes, watts per port"],["New PC setup checklist", "new-pc-setup-checklist.html", "page", "Prepare a new PC or notebook for a user: firmware and updates, encryption, accounts, software, data, peripherals, the handover and the inventory entry."],["1 short beep: All is well", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=1%20short%20beep", "beep code", "One short beep at power-on is the self-test saying it passed. Most current boards ship without a speaker and stay silent."],["No beep: No beep and no picture", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=No%20beep", "beep code", "Most boards built after about 2015 have no speaker fitted, so silence means nothing by itself. Look for small lights on the board instead, or plug a speaker onto the SPEAKER pins of the front panel he"],["Continuous beep: Memory not found, or a power problem", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Continuous%20beep", "beep code", "A tone that does not stop, or short beeps without end, is the board saying it cannot find usable memory. On some boards the same pattern means a voltage is out of range."],["High-low siren: The processor is too hot", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=High-low%20siren", "beep code", "Two tones that alternate like a siren, at start or while the PC is running."],["AMI: 2 short: Memory error", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=AMI%3A%202%20short", "beep code", "The classic AMI codes for a parity error or a failure in the first block of memory."],["AMI: 4 short: System timer failure", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=AMI%3A%204%20short", "beep code", "A timer chip on the mainboard does not answer."],["AMI: 5 short: Processor error", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=AMI%3A%205%20short", "beep code", "The self-test could not get a sane answer from the processor."],["AMI: 6 short: Keyboard controller error", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=AMI%3A%206%20short", "beep code", "An old code for the controller that handles the keyboard and one memory address line."],["AMI: 8 short: Graphics error", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=AMI%3A%208%20short", "beep code", "The memory of the graphics card failed its test, or no graphics card answered."],["AMI: 9 short: BIOS chip or mainboard", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=AMI%3A%209%20short", "beep code", "The BIOS failed its own checksum, or a register or cache on the board failed."],["ASUS: 1 long, 2 short: No memory detected", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=ASUS%3A%201%20long%2C%202%20short", "beep code", "On ASUS boards with current firmware. On old Award BIOS versions the same pattern meant a graphics error."],["ASUS: 1 long, 3 short: No graphics card detected", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=ASUS%3A%201%20long%2C%203%20short", "beep code", "The board found no working display adapter."],["ASUS: 1 long, 4 short: Hardware component failure", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=ASUS%3A%201%20long%2C%204%20short", "beep code", "A general code for a part that failed, often the processor fan missing from the CPU_FAN header."],["Award: 1 long, 2 short: Graphics error", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Award%3A%201%20long%2C%202%20short", "beep code", "On boards with an Award BIOS, mostly older Gigabyte and similar."],["Award: repeating long beeps: Memory error", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Award%3A%20repeating%20long%20beeps", "beep code", "Long beeps that repeat without end."],["Phoenix: groups of beeps: Phoenix codes are read in groups", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Phoenix%3A%20groups%20of%20beeps", "beep code", "Phoenix BIOS versions beep in three or four groups with short pauses, written like 1-2-2-3. Count each group. Common ones: 1-2-2-3 is a BIOS checksum error, 1-3-1-1 and 1-3-4-1 to 1-4-1-1 are memory e"],["Dell: 1 beep: BIOS chip or mainboard", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Dell%3A%201%20beep", "beep code", "Dell desktops and notebooks repeat a number of beeps with a pause in between. One: the BIOS failed its checksum, or the board failed."],["Dell: 2 beeps: No memory detected", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Dell%3A%202%20beeps", "beep code", "Memory missing or not seated"],["Dell: 3 beeps: Mainboard chipset error", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Dell%3A%203%20beeps", "beep code", "Mainboard fault"],["Dell: 4 beeps: Memory read or write failure", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Dell%3A%204%20beeps", "beep code", "Memory was found and failed its test."],["Dell: 5 beeps: Real-time clock failure", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Dell%3A%205%20beeps", "beep code", "The clock that the coin cell keeps running failed."],["Dell: 6 beeps: Graphics error", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Dell%3A%206%20beeps", "beep code", "Graphics card or graphics chip"],["Dell: 7 beeps: Processor failure", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Dell%3A%207%20beeps", "beep code", "Processor or mainboard"],["Dell: 8 beeps: Display failure", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Dell%3A%208%20beeps", "beep code", "On notebooks: the built-in screen did not answer."],["Dell: power light blinks amber, then white: Dell blink codes: count amber, then white", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Dell%3A%20power%20light%20blinks%20amber%2C%20then%20white", "beep code", "Newer Dell machines blink the power button light instead of beeping: a number of amber blinks, then a number of white ones, then a pause. 2 then 1 is the processor, 2 then 2 the BIOS or board, 2 then "],["HP desktop: 2 blinks: Thermal protection", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=HP%20desktop%3A%202%20blinks", "beep code", "HP business desktops blink the power light red and beep the same number, once a second, then pause. Two: the PC switched itself off because it was too hot."],["HP desktop: 3 blinks: Processor not detected", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=HP%20desktop%3A%203%20blinks", "beep code", "Processor not seated"],["HP desktop: 4 blinks: Power failure", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=HP%20desktop%3A%204%20blinks", "beep code", "The power supply is overloaded or one of its outputs failed."],["HP desktop: 5 blinks: Memory error", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=HP%20desktop%3A%205%20blinks", "beep code", "Memory not seated, wrong type or defective"],["HP desktop: 6 blinks: Graphics error", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=HP%20desktop%3A%206%20blinks", "beep code", "Graphics card not seated or defective"],["HP desktop: 7 blinks: Mainboard failure, or a corrupt BIOS", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=HP%20desktop%3A%207%20blinks", "beep code", "Seven is the board itself, eight a BIOS that failed its checksum."],["HP notebook: Caps Lock blinks: HP notebooks blink the Caps Lock light", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=HP%20notebook%3A%20Caps%20Lock%20blinks", "beep code", "Count the blinks between pauses: 1 is the processor, 2 a corrupt BIOS, 3 the memory, 4 the graphics, 5 the mainboard, 6 a BIOS that failed authentication."],["Lenovo ThinkCentre: 3 short, 1 long: Memory not detected", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Lenovo%20ThinkCentre%3A%203%20short%2C%201%20long", "beep code", "Memory not seated or defective"],["Lenovo ThinkCentre: 2 long, 3 short: Graphics error", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Lenovo%20ThinkCentre%3A%202%20long%2C%203%20short", "beep code", "Graphics card not seated or defective"],["Lenovo ThinkPad: a short melody: ThinkPad tones are meant for an app", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Lenovo%20ThinkPad%3A%20a%20short%20melody", "beep code", "Current ThinkPads play a sequence of tones that encodes the error. Lenovo's diagnostics app for phones listens to it and shows the code. Older models use beep counts from the hardware maintenance manu"],["Apple: 1 tone every 5 seconds: No memory detected", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Apple%3A%201%20tone%20every%205%20seconds", "beep code", "Intel Macs with replaceable memory."],["Apple: 3 tones, pause, repeat: Memory failed its check", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Apple%3A%203%20tones%2C%20pause%2C%20repeat", "beep code", "A defective or incompatible module"],["Supermicro: 5 short, 1 long: No memory detected", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Supermicro%3A%205%20short%2C%201%20long", "beep code", "On Supermicro server boards."],["Server: continuous tone with a red or amber front light: Overheat or fan failure", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Server%3A%20continuous%20tone%20with%20a%20red%20or%20amber%20front%20light", "beep code", "A server that sounds a steady tone and lights its overheat or health light."],["Debug LEDs: CPU, DRAM, VGA, BOOT: The light that stays on names the stage", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Debug%20LEDs%3A%20CPU%2C%20DRAM%2C%20VGA%2C%20BOOT", "beep code", "Many boards have four small lights that come on one after the other during the start. The one that stays lit is where it stopped."],["Two-digit code display: A two-digit display on the board", "beep-code-lookup.html?q=Two-digit%20code%20display", "beep code", "Enthusiast and server boards show a hexadecimal code for each step of the start. The codes run past quickly: the one it stops on is the one that counts. On boards with an AMI BIOS, 55 means no memory "],["Alignment (DMARC)", "glossary.html#alignment-dmarc", "glossary", "The check that makes DMARC more than SPF plus DKIM: the domain that passed SPF or DKIM must match the domain in the From line the reader sees. A newsletter service that signs with its own domain authe"],["Aggregate report (DMARC)", "glossary.html#aggregate-report-dmarc", "glossary", "The XML file a mail receiver sends once a day to the address in your DMARC record's rua tag. It lists every server that sent mail with your domain in the From line, how many messages, and whether they"],["DKIM selector", "glossary.html#dkim-selector", "glossary", "The name that tells a receiver which of your DKIM keys signed a message. It is part of the DNS name where the public key lives: selector._domainkey.yourdomain. Each sending service gets its own."],["PoE budget", "glossary.html#poe-budget", "glossary", "The total power a switch can deliver to devices over the network cable. When phones, access points and cameras together need more, the switch leaves the last ports unpowered. PoE budget calculator"],["VA (volt-ampere)", "glossary.html#va-volt-ampere", "glossary", "The unit on a UPS box. It is not watts: multiply by the power factor of the UPS, between 0.6 and 1, to get the watts it can really deliver. UPS runtime calculator"],["OID", "glossary.html#oid", "glossary", "Object identifier. The numeric address of one value in SNMP, such as 1.3.6.1.2.1.1.3.0 for the uptime of a device. A MIB file translates the numbers into names. SNMP cheat sheet"],["Idempotent", "glossary.html#idempotent", "glossary", "An operation that leaves the same result whether it runs once or ten times. Configuration tools such as Ansible are built on it: a playbook describes a state, and running it again changes nothing. Ans"],["Inheritance (permissions)", "glossary.html#inheritance-permissions", "glossary", "Folders and files take over the permissions of the folder above them unless someone breaks the chain. Every broken chain is a place where access differs from what the top level suggests. NTFS and shar"],["Access-based enumeration", "glossary.html#access-based-enumeration", "glossary", "A file share setting that hides folders and files a user has no right to open, instead of showing them and answering \"access denied\"."],["Beep code", "glossary.html#beep-code", "glossary", "A pattern of beeps a computer gives when its self-test fails before the screen works. The pattern names the part. Beep code lookup"],["NTFS and share permissions cheat sheet", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "File server permissions on Windows: read and change them with icacls and PowerShell, find out who has access, inheritance and ownership, share permissions, copying with permissions intact, and the layout that stays manageable."],["Show the permissions of a folder", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Show%20the%20permissions%20of%20a%20folder", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "(OI)(CI) means it applies to files and subfolders, (I) means inherited from above. F is full control, M modify, RX read and execute. icacls \"D:\\Data\\Finance\""],["The same, readable, with PowerShell", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20same%2C%20readable%2C%20with%20PowerShell", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", " (Get-Acl \"D:\\Data\\Finance\").Access | Format-Table IdentityReference, FileSystemRights, AccessControlType, IsInherited, InheritanceFlags -AutoSize"],["Give a group modify rights", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Give%20a%20group%20modify%20rights", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "For this folder, its subfolders and files. Modify lets people change and delete, but not change permissions. icacls \"D:\\Data\\Finance\" /grant \"CORP\\GG-Finance-RW:(OI)(CI)M\""],["Give a group read rights", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Give%20a%20group%20read%20rights", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", " icacls \"D:\\Data\\Finance\" /grant \"CORP\\GG-Finance-RO:(OI)(CI)RX\""],["Remove a group or user from the list", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Remove%20a%20group%20or%20user%20from%20the%20list", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "/remove takes away the entries that were set on this folder. Inherited ones stay. icacls \"D:\\Data\\Finance\" /remove \"CORP\\j.smith\""],["Stop inheriting from the parent", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Stop%20inheriting%20from%20the%20parent", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "/inheritance:d keeps the inherited entries as a copy, so nobody loses access at that moment. /inheritance:r removes them, which can lock everyone out including you. icacls \"D:\\Data\\Finance\" /inheritance:d"],["Put subfolders back on inheritance", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Put%20subfolders%20back%20on%20inheritance", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "Removes every explicit entry below and lets the folder's permissions flow down again. Use it to clean up a folder tree that grew wild. icacls \"D:\\Data\\Finance\\*\" /reset /T /C /Q"],["Save permissions before you change them", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Save%20permissions%20before%20you%20change%20them", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "Writes every entry of the tree to a file. /restore puts them back, run against the parent folder. icacls \"D:\\Data\\Finance\" /save \"C:\\Temp\\finance-acl.txt\" /T /C icacls \"D:\\Data\" /restore \"C:\\Temp\\finance-acl.txt\""],["Who has access to what: a list of folders with explicit entries", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20has%20access%20to%20what%3A%20a%20list%20of%20folders%20with%20explicit%20entries", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "Two levels deep, only entries that are not inherited. This is the report an auditor asks for. Get-ChildItem \"D:\\Data\" -Directory -Depth 1 | ForEach-Object {   $p = $_.FullName   (Get-Acl $p).Access | Where-Object { -not $_.IsInherited } |  "],["Where does one user or group appear", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Where%20does%20one%20user%20or%20group%20appear", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "Finds every folder in the tree with an entry that names them directly. icacls \"D:\\Data\" /findsid \"CORP\\j.smith\" /T /C"],["What can this user really do here", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20can%20this%20user%20really%20do%20here", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "The Effective Access tab in the folder's Advanced security settings answers it, taking group memberships into account. From the command line, list the groups first. Get-ADPrincipalGroupMembership j.smith | Select-Object -ExpandProperty Name"],["Access denied to an admin: take ownership", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Access%20denied%20to%20an%20admin%3A%20take%20ownership", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "A folder whose owner removed everyone else. Take ownership for the Administrators group, then grant rights. takeown /F \"D:\\Data\\Old\" /A /R /D Y icacls \"D:\\Data\\Old\" /grant \"BUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)F\" /T /C"],["Entries that show only a long number", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Entries%20that%20show%20only%20a%20long%20number", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "An S-1-5-21-... entry belongs to an account that was deleted. Harmless, and worth removing during a clean-up. icacls \"D:\\Data\" /T /C | findstr /C:\"S-1-5-21\""],["List the shares of a server and their permissions", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20the%20shares%20of%20a%20server%20and%20their%20permissions", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", " Get-SmbShare | Where-Object Special -eq $false | Format-Table Name, Path, Description Get-SmbShareAccess -Name \"Data\""],["Create a share the usual way", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20share%20the%20usual%20way", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "Full access for authenticated users on the share, and NTFS decides the rest. Access-based enumeration hides folders a user cannot open. New-SmbShare -Name \"Data\" -Path \"D:\\Data\" -FullAccess \"NT AUTHORITY\\Authenticated Users\" -FolderEnumerat"],["Who has which files open", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20has%20which%20files%20open", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "Before a restart, or when a file is locked. Get-SmbOpenFile | Format-Table ClientUserName, ClientComputerName, Path Get-SmbOpenFile | Where-Object Path -like \"*budget.xlsx\" | Close-SmbOpenFile"],["Copy a folder tree with permissions, owner and timestamps", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Copy%20a%20folder%20tree%20with%20permissions%2C%20owner%20and%20timestamps", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "For a file server migration. /MIR deletes at the target what is not at the source: test with /L first, which only lists. robocopy \"D:\\Data\" \"\\\\NEWFS\\D$\\Data\" /MIR /COPYALL /DCOPY:DAT /R:1 /W:1 /MT:16 /XD \"$RECYCLE.BIN\" \"System Volume Inform"],["Copy only the permissions onto an existing copy", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Copy%20only%20the%20permissions%20onto%20an%20existing%20copy", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "When the data was copied without them. robocopy \"D:\\Data\" \"\\\\NEWFS\\D$\\Data\" /E /SECFIX /COPY:ATSO /XO /XN /XC /R:0 /W:0"],["Moving versus copying", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Moving%20versus%20copying", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "A classic surprise: a file moved within the same volume keeps its own permissions, a file copied or moved to another volume takes those of the new folder. # moved inside D:        -> permissions travel with the file # copied, or moved D: ->"],["Paths longer than 260 characters", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Paths%20longer%20than%20260%20characters", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "Old programs fail on them. robocopy and PowerShell cope, Explorer may not. Find them before a migration. Get-ChildItem \"D:\\Data\" -Recurse -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Where-Object { $_.FullName.Length -gt 250 } | Select-Object -ExpandPro"],["The layout that stays manageable", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20layout%20that%20stays%20manageable", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "Permissions go to groups, never to people. One read group and one write group per folder that needs its own access, and only on the top two levels. # User -> role group (GG-Finance) -> permission group (DL-Data-Finance-RW) -> folder # Break"],["Audit who deletes or changes files", "ntfs-share-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Audit%20who%20deletes%20or%20changes%20files", "snippet: NTFS and share permissions", "Switch on object access auditing by group policy, then set auditing on the folder. Events 4663 and 4660 appear in the security log. auditpol /set /subcategory:\"File System\" /success:enable Get-WinEvent -FilterHashtable @{LogName='Security';"],["Ansible cheat sheet", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Ansible for admins: inventory, ad-hoc commands, a playbook skeleton, check mode, variables, handlers, loops, vault for secrets, roles and the switches for running against part of the fleet."],["Install it, on the control machine only", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=Install%20it%2C%20on%20the%20control%20machine%20only", "snippet: Ansible", " python3 -m pip install --user ansible ansible --version"],["An inventory file", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=An%20inventory%20file", "snippet: Ansible", "Hosts in groups, with variables per group. # inventory.ini [web] web01.example.internal web02.example.internal  [db] db01.example.internal ansible_user=dbadmin  [all:vars] ansible_user=deploy ansible_python_interpreter=/usr/bin/python3"],["Can it reach everything?", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=Can%20it%20reach%20everything%3F", "snippet: Ansible", "ping here is an SSH login plus a Python check, not ICMP. ansible all -i inventory.ini -m ping"],["Run one command everywhere", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20one%20command%20everywhere", "snippet: Ansible", "Ad-hoc commands, for a quick look. -b becomes root with sudo. ansible web -i inventory.ini -a \"uptime\" ansible all -i inventory.ini -b -m apt -a \"name=curl state=present\" ansible all -i inventory.ini -m setup -a \"filter=ansible_distribution"],["A playbook skeleton", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20playbook%20skeleton", "snippet: Ansible", "Tasks run top to bottom. Each one names a module and the state you want. # site.yml - name: Web servers   hosts: web   become: true   tasks:     - name: Install nginx       ansible.builtin.apt:         name: nginx         state: present    "],["Run it", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20it", "snippet: Ansible", " ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini site.yml"],["See what would change, without changing it", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=See%20what%20would%20change%2C%20without%20changing%20it", "snippet: Ansible", "--check does a dry run, --diff shows the lines that would change in files. Do this before every run on production. ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini site.yml --check --diff"],["Run against part of the fleet", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20against%20part%20of%20the%20fleet", "snippet: Ansible", "--limit narrows the hosts, --tags the tasks. Start with one host. ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini site.yml --limit web01.example.internal ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini site.yml --limit 'web:!web02.example.internal' ansible-playbook -i"],["Roll out in batches", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=Roll%20out%20in%20batches", "snippet: Ansible", "serial updates a few hosts at a time and stops when one fails, so a bad change does not reach all of them. - hosts: web   serial: 1   max_fail_percentage: 0   tasks: []"],["Variables", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=Variables", "snippet: Ansible", "In the play, per group in group_vars/, per host in host_vars/. On the command line with -e, which wins over everything. # group_vars/web.yml nginx_worker_connections: 1024 site_name: intranet  # in a task or template \"{{ site_name }}.exampl"],["Loops and conditions", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=Loops%20and%20conditions", "snippet: Ansible", " - name: Install packages   ansible.builtin.apt:     name: \"{{ item }}\"     state: present   loop: [git, htop, unattended-upgrades]  - name: Only on Debian and Ubuntu   ansible.builtin.apt:     upgrade: dist   when: ansible_os_family == \"De"],["The modules you use every day", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20modules%20you%20use%20every%20day", "snippet: Ansible", "Prefer a module over shell: a module knows whether something changed. ansible.builtin.apt / dnf / package     # packages ansible.builtin.service / systemd      # start, stop, enable ansible.builtin.copy / template        # files, with varia"],["When you must use a command", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=When%20you%20must%20use%20a%20command", "snippet: Ansible", "Tell Ansible when it changed something, or it reports a change on every run. - name: Initialise the database once   ansible.builtin.command: /opt/app/bin/init-db   args:     creates: /var/lib/app/.initialised"],["Secrets: Ansible Vault", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=Secrets%3A%20Ansible%20Vault", "snippet: Ansible", "Encrypts a variables file so that it can live in Git. Never commit passwords in plain text. ansible-vault create group_vars/all/vault.yml ansible-vault edit group_vars/all/vault.yml ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini site.yml --ask-vault-pas"],["Roles", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=Roles", "snippet: Ansible", "A folder layout that makes tasks reusable. Roles written by others come from Ansible Galaxy: read them before you run them. ansible-galaxy init roles/nginx # roles/nginx/tasks/main.yml, handlers/main.yml, templates/, defaults/main.yml  - ho"],["Debug a failing task", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=Debug%20a%20failing%20task", "snippet: Ansible", " ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini site.yml -vvv ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini site.yml --start-at-task \"Deploy the site configuration\"  - name: Show a variable   ansible.builtin.debug:     var: ansible_default_ipv4.address"],["Check a playbook before running it", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20a%20playbook%20before%20running%20it", "snippet: Ansible", " ansible-playbook site.yml --syntax-check python3 -m pip install --user ansible-lint && ansible-lint site.yml"],["ansible.cfg next to the playbook", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=ansible.cfg%20next%20to%20the%20playbook", "snippet: Ansible", "Saves typing the inventory every time. [defaults] inventory = inventory.ini host_key_checking = True forks = 10 stdout_callback = yaml"],["Windows hosts", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20hosts", "snippet: Ansible", "Ansible manages Windows over WinRM or SSH with its own set of modules, all starting with win_. [windows:vars] ansible_connection=winrm ansible_winrm_transport=kerberos ansible_port=5986  - ansible.windows.win_feature:     name: Web-Server  "],["Habits that prevent accidents", "ansible-cheat-sheet.html?q=Habits%20that%20prevent%20accidents", "snippet: Ansible", " # 1. --check --diff first, always. # 2. --limit to one host, then a group, then all. # 3. Keep everything in Git: the diff is your change log. # 4. No task without a name: the name is what you read at three in the morning."],["SNMP and monitoring cheat sheet", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Query switches, printers, UPS units and servers with SNMP: snmpwalk and snmpget for v2c and v3, the OIDs worth knowing, turning counters into bandwidth, a minimal snmpd, and quick checks without a monitoring system."],["Install the tools", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=Install%20the%20tools", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", " sudo apt install snmp snmp-mibs-downloader      # Debian, Ubuntu sudo dnf install net-snmp-utils                 # Red Hat family"],["First contact", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=First%20contact", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "System description, uptime, name and location in one go. snmpwalk -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 system"],["The same with version 3", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20same%20with%20version%203", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "authPriv: signed with SHA and encrypted with AES. snmpwalk -v3 -l authPriv -u monitor -a SHA -A 'auth-passphrase' -x AES -X 'priv-passphrase' 10.87.99.2 system"],["One value", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=One%20value", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", " snmpget -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 sysUpTime.0 snmpget -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 1.3.6.1.2.1.1.5.0      # sysName by number"],["No answer: find out why", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=No%20answer%3A%20find%20out%20why", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "Timeout means nothing came back: wrong community, SNMP switched off, an access list on the device, or a firewall. SNMP uses UDP port 161. snmpget -v2c -c public -t 2 -r 1 10.87.99.2 sysDescr.0 sudo nmap -sU -p 161 10.87.99.2"],["All interfaces with name, state and speed", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=All%20interfaces%20with%20name%2C%20state%20and%20speed", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "ifOperStatus 1 is up, 2 is down. ifAlias holds the description someone typed on the switch. snmptable -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 ifTable snmpwalk -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 ifDescr snmpwalk -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 ifAlias snmpwalk -v2c -c p"],["Traffic counters", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=Traffic%20counters", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "Use the 64-bit counters (ifHC...). The old 32-bit ones wrap around within minutes on a gigabit link. snmpwalk -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 ifHCInOctets snmpwalk -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 ifHCOutOctets"],["From counters to bandwidth", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=From%20counters%20to%20bandwidth", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "Two readings some seconds apart. The difference in bytes times eight, divided by the seconds, is bits per second. a=$(snmpget -v2c -c public -Oqv 10.87.99.2 ifHCInOctets.3); sleep 10 b=$(snmpget -v2c -c public -Oqv 10.87.99.2 ifHCInOctets.3"],["Errors and discards on a port", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=Errors%20and%20discards%20on%20a%20port", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "Input errors that keep rising point at a cable, a transceiver or a duplex mismatch. Discards point at congestion. snmpwalk -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 ifInErrors snmpwalk -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 ifOutDiscards"],["Which MAC address is on which port", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20MAC%20address%20is%20on%20which%20port", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "The bridge table of a switch. snmpwalk -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 1.3.6.1.2.1.17.4.3.1.2"],["Servers: processor load, memory and disks", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=Servers%3A%20processor%20load%2C%20memory%20and%20disks", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "Needs an SNMP agent on the host. snmpwalk -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 hrProcessorLoad snmptable -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 hrStorageTable"],["Printers: toner and page count", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=Printers%3A%20toner%20and%20page%20count", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "Level and capacity per supply. A level of -3 means \"some left, amount unknown\". snmpwalk -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 1.3.6.1.2.1.43.11.1.1.6      # supply names snmpwalk -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 1.3.6.1.2.1.43.11.1.1.9      # current level s"],["UPS: on battery, charge, runtime", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=UPS%3A%20on%20battery%2C%20charge%2C%20runtime", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "The standard UPS MIB. Output source 3 is normal, 5 is on battery. Many vendors add their own tree with more detail. snmpget -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 1.3.6.1.2.1.33.1.4.1.0      # output source snmpget -v2c -c public 10.87.99.2 1.3.6.1.2.1."],["Find out what a device offers", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20out%20what%20a%20device%20offers", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "Walk everything into a file and search it. Vendor-specific values live under 1.3.6.1.4.1. snmpwalk -v2c -c public -On 10.87.99.2 .1 > walk.txt grep -i -E \"temp|fan|power\" walk.txt snmptranslate -On IF-MIB::ifHCInOctets"],["A minimal agent on a Linux server, version 3 only", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20minimal%20agent%20on%20a%20Linux%20server%2C%20version%203%20only", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "Read-only user, listening on the management address only. sudo apt install snmpd sudo systemctl stop snmpd sudo net-snmp-create-v3-user -ro -a SHA -A 'auth-passphrase' -x AES -X 'priv-passphrase' monitor # /etc/snmp/snmpd.conf agentaddress "],["On a switch: the same idea", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=On%20a%20switch%3A%20the%20same%20idea", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "Syntax differs by vendor. The three things to set are always: a v3 user, a read-only view, and an access list for the monitoring server. # Remove the default communities \"public\" and \"private\". # Version 3 with authentication and encryption"],["Quick checks without SNMP", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=Quick%20checks%20without%20SNMP", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "For the day the monitoring system is the thing that is down. ping -c 5 10.87.99.2 mtr -rwc 20 10.87.99.2 curl -o /dev/null -s -w \"%{http_code} %{time_total}s\\n\" https://intranet.example.org/ nc -zv 10.87.99.2 22 443 openssl s_client -connec"],["What to watch, and when to alert", "snmp-monitoring-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20to%20watch%2C%20and%20when%20to%20alert", "snippet: SNMP and monitoring", "Starting points. An alert nobody acts on is noise: every one needs an owner and a next step. # Disk space        warn at 80%, alert at 90%, or by days until full # Memory            alert when swap is in use for more than a few minutes # CP"],["Connector identifier", "connector-identifier.html", "tool", "Identify plugs, ports and slots by sight: USB, HDMI, DisplayPort, M.2, SATA, power connectors, IEC cords, fibre, SFP"],["The PC does not start", "diagnose.html#pc", "tool", "Wizard for a dead PC or notebook: no power, black screen, beeps, starts and switches off"],["Desktop PC hardware guide", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html", "guide", "Practical hardware tips for desktop PCs, with drawings: which memory slots to use, the front panel header, thermal paste, airflow and fan direction, power supplies, CMOS reset, BIOS updates and the classic build mistakes."],["Desktop PC: before you open it", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html#before", "hardware tip", "Shut down, switch the power supply off at the back, then press the power button once. That empties the capacitors: the board LED goes out."],["Desktop PC: it does not start: the short list", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html#no-start", "hardware tip", "Most PCs that \"died\" after a move, a cleaning or an upgrade have one of these. Go through them in order before you suspect a part."],["Desktop PC: memory: which slots", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html#memory", "hardware tip", "Two modules belong in the second and fourth slot counted from the processor, usually named A2 and B2. That gives dual channel, which matters most for integrated graphics."],["Desktop PC: the front panel header", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html#front-panel", "hardware tip", "The block of thin single plugs from the case: power button, reset button, two LEDs. The board prints tiny labels next to the pins, and the manual has the drawing."],["Desktop PC: resetting the BIOS settings", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html#cmos", "hardware tip", "With the power cord unplugged: move the jumper labelled CLR_CMOS or JBAT for ten seconds, or take the coin cell out for a minute. Some boards have a button for it at the back."],["Desktop PC: thermal paste and coolers", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html#paste", "hardware tip", "Clean both surfaces with isopropyl alcohol and a lint-free cloth until no old paste is left."],["Desktop PC: airflow", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html#airflow", "hardware tip", "Front and bottom fans blow in, rear and top fans blow out. A fan mounted the wrong way round works against all the others."],["Desktop PC: which way a fan blows", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html#fan-direction", "hardware tip", "Air leaves on the side where the motor is held by struts and where the label sits. The open side with the free view of the blades is the intake."],["Desktop PC: the power supply", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html#psu", "hardware tip", "Never use a modular cable from another power supply, even from the same brand. The plugs on the power supply side look alike and are wired differently. The result is 12 V on a 5 V line and dead drives"],["Desktop PC: adding or replacing a drive", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html#storage", "hardware tip", "A new empty drive does not show up in Explorer. It has to be initialised and given a volume first: diskmgmt.msc. This is the most common \"my new SSD is not detected\"."],["Desktop PC: updating the BIOS without regret", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html#bios-update", "hardware tip", "Only when it fixes something you have: a new processor that is not recognised, a security fix, a stability problem. It is not routine maintenance on a PC that works."],["Desktop PC: screws and standoffs", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html#screws", "hardware tip", "The brass standoffs under the mainboard belong only where the board has a hole. One extra standoff touching the back of the board is a short circuit, and the PC does not start."],["Desktop PC: getting into the BIOS", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html#keys", "hardware tip", ""],["Desktop PC: worth having in the drawer", "desktop-pc-hardware-guide.html#kit", "hardware tip", "A PH2 and a PH1 screwdriver with a long shaft, and a plastic pry tool."],["Notebook hardware guide", "notebook-hardware-guide.html", "guide", "Practical hardware tips for notebooks, with drawings: opening one without breaking clips, what can be replaced, the power drain trick, chargers and USB-C, battery health, ribbon cable latches, display faults and liquid spills."],["Notebook: before you open it", "notebook-hardware-guide.html#before", "hardware tip", "Get the service manual first. Dell, HP and Lenovo publish one for every business model: search for the model name plus \"service manual\" or \"hardware maintenance manual\". It shows every screw and every"],["Notebook: what is inside, and what can be replaced", "notebook-hardware-guide.html#inside", "hardware tip", "Business models usually let you replace the battery, the SSD, the Wi-Fi card and at least one memory module."],["Notebook: it is dead: do the power drain first", "notebook-hardware-guide.html#power-drain", "hardware tip", "A notebook that does nothing at all, or shows a light but no picture, is often not broken. The small controller that manages power has hung, and it never loses power as long as a battery is connected."],["Notebook: chargers and USB-C", "notebook-hardware-guide.html#charger", "hardware tip", "The charger must deliver at least the wattage printed on the original. A weaker one charges slowly, or not at all while the notebook is working, and many models then slow the processor down. \"Slow sin"],["Notebook: battery health", "notebook-hardware-guide.html#battery", "hardware tip", "Compare the full charge capacity with the design capacity. Below about two thirds, the battery is worn and worth replacing."],["Notebook: memory and SSD upgrades", "notebook-hardware-guide.html#upgrade", "hardware tip", "Check what the machine takes before you buy: the memory generation (DDR4 and DDR5 do not fit each other), the highest supported size, and the length of the SSD slot."],["Notebook: ribbon cables and their latches", "notebook-hardware-guide.html#ribbon", "hardware tip", "Keyboard, touchpad, display and fingerprint reader hang on flat ribbon cables in latched connectors. Pulling a cable out of a closed latch tears the connector off the board."],["Notebook: display faults: panel, cable or graphics", "notebook-hardware-guide.html#display", "hardware tip", "Connect an external monitor. A good picture there means the graphics chip is fine and the fault is in the panel or its cable."],["Notebook: liquid on the keyboard", "notebook-hardware-guide.html#spill", "hardware tip", "Switch it off at once: hold the power button until it is dark. Do not save, do not shut down nicely."],["Notebook: heat and fan noise", "notebook-hardware-guide.html#heat", "hardware tip", "The usual cause is a mat of lint between the fan and the cooling fins, like felt. Blowing into the vents from outside only moves it around. Open the cover, hold the fan still, and pull the mat out."],["Notebook: keyboard and touchpad", "notebook-hardware-guide.html#keyboard", "hardware tip", "To separate hardware from software, test in the BIOS setup or with a live Linux stick. A key that fails there is a hardware fault."],["Notebook: after the repair", "notebook-hardware-guide.html#wifi", "hardware tip", "Weak Wi-Fi after a repair: one of the two tiny antenna plugs on the Wi-Fi card came off or was pinched."],["Notebook: getting into the BIOS and the boot menu", "notebook-hardware-guide.html#keys", "hardware tip", ""],["Server hardware guide", "server-hardware-guide.html", "guide", "Practical hardware tips for servers, with drawings: remote management, reading the lights and the event log, replacing a disk safely, memory population, redundant power, rack units, airflow, firmware order and RAID controller pitfalls."],["Server: set up remote management first", "server-hardware-guide.html#bmc", "hardware tip", "Every server has a small computer of its own that runs as long as the power cords are in: iDRAC at Dell, iLO at HPE, XClarity Controller at Lenovo, IPMI or BMC on the rest. It shows the screen, mounts"],["Server: read the lights and the log before you touch anything", "server-hardware-guide.html#lights", "hardware tip", "A health light at the front, usually amber when something is wrong. Then one pair of lights per drive, per power supply, and often per memory slot on the board."],["Server: replacing a disk without making it worse", "server-hardware-guide.html#disk", "hardware tip", "Find the failed disk by two things that agree: the slot number from the controller, and the serial number printed on the carrier."],["Server: memory: fill by channel", "server-hardware-guide.html#memory", "hardware tip", "The lid usually has the population order printed on the inside. Follow it: a wrong order costs speed or keeps the server from starting."],["Server: power: two supplies, two feeds", "server-hardware-guide.html#power", "hardware tip", "Plug the two power supplies into two different power strips, on two different circuits if the room has them, one of them behind the UPS at least."],["Server: rack units and mounting", "server-hardware-guide.html#rack", "hardware tip", "Count the holes before you clip in the cage nuts. One hole off and the server sits crooked, or the next device does not fit."],["Server: airflow", "server-hardware-guide.html#airflow", "hardware tip", "Cold in at the front, hot out at the back, for every device in the rack. A switch mounted at the back that blows its hot air forwards heats the servers below it: many switches can be ordered or conver"],["Server: firmware: order and caution", "server-hardware-guide.html#firmware", "hardware tip", "Use the vendor's bundle for the model instead of single files: it contains versions that were tested together."],["Server: RAID controller pitfalls", "server-hardware-guide.html#raid", "hardware tip", "The controller's write cache is protected by a small battery or capacitor. When that fails, the controller switches the cache off to protect the data, and the server becomes several times slower from "],["Server: reseating is a real fix", "server-hardware-guide.html#reseat", "hardware tip", "After transport or after work inside, parts can sit a fraction of a millimetre out: memory, riser cards, power supplies, the cables to the drive backplane."],["Server: housekeeping", "server-hardware-guide.html#housekeeping", "hardware tip", "Keep one spare disk of each kind in use, and for servers out of warranty a spare power supply."],["USB-A", "connector-identifier.html#c-usb-a", "connector", "The flat rectangular plug on nearly every computer, charger and stick. Fits one way round only. Flat rectangle about 12 mm wide with a plastic tongue inside. A blue tongue usually means USB 3 (5 Gbit/"],["USB-B", "connector-identifier.html#c-usb-b", "connector", "The square plug on printers, scanners, audio interfaces and some monitors with a built-in hub. Nearly square, with two bevelled corners at the top. The USB 3 version is taller with a second block on t"],["Mini-USB (Mini-B)", "connector-identifier.html#c-mini-b", "connector", "Older cameras, GPS units, some external disks and many development boards. A small trapezoid about 7 mm wide, clearly thicker than Micro-USB, with sides that narrow towards the bottom."],["Micro-USB (Micro-B)", "connector-identifier.html#c-micro-b", "connector", "Phones before about 2017, power banks, headsets, e-readers, Raspberry Pi up to model 3. Flat, about 7 mm wide and under 2 mm tall, with two bevelled bottom corners. Fits one way round: the two small h"],["Micro-USB 3.0 (Micro-B SuperSpeed)", "connector-identifier.html#c-micro-b3", "connector", "External hard disks and disk enclosures from about 2010 to 2020. Looks like a Micro-USB plug with a second, rectangular plug attached to its side. About 12 mm wide."],["USB-C", "connector-identifier.html#c-usb-c", "connector", "The small oval plug on current notebooks, phones, docks and monitors. Fits both ways round. A flat oval, about 8 mm wide, with no up or down. The shape says nothing about what the port can do: look at"],["Thunderbolt 3, 4 and 5", "connector-identifier.html#c-thunderbolt", "connector", "The fastest kind of USB-C port: docks with several monitors, fast external storage, external graphics. A USB-C socket with a small lightning bolt printed next to it. Thunderbolt 1 and 2 used the Mini "],["HDMI", "connector-identifier.html#c-hdmi", "connector", "Monitors, televisions, projectors. Carries picture and sound. About 14 mm wide, flat, with the two bottom corners cut in a step. No screws and no latch."],["Mini and Micro HDMI", "connector-identifier.html#c-mini-hdmi", "connector", "Cameras, tablets, single-board computers. Raspberry Pi 4 and 5 use Micro HDMI. The HDMI shape, smaller: Mini is about 10 mm wide, Micro about 6 mm and easy to mistake for Micro-USB."],["DisplayPort", "connector-identifier.html#c-displayport", "connector", "Monitors on business PCs, docks and graphics cards. About 16 mm wide, rectangular, with exactly one corner cut off. Most plugs have a latch with a release button on top."],["Mini DisplayPort", "connector-identifier.html#c-mini-dp", "connector", "Older MacBooks, Microsoft Surface, some graphics cards and docks. About 7.5 mm wide, with two cut bottom corners. The same plug with a bolt symbol next to it is Thunderbolt 1 or 2."],["DVI", "connector-identifier.html#c-dvi", "connector", "Older monitors and graphics cards. Wide white plug with two thumbscrews, a block of square pins and a flat blade at one side. Four extra pins around the blade mean it also carries an analogue signal ("],["VGA", "connector-identifier.html#c-vga", "connector", "Old monitors and projectors, and still the console port of many servers. Blue, D-shaped, 15 pins in three rows, two thumbscrews."],["RJ45 (network)", "connector-identifier.html#c-rj45", "connector", "Ethernet: the cable between a computer, a wall socket and a switch. Also used for ISDN and for the console port of switches and routers. Clear plastic plug about 11.5 mm wide with eight gold contacts "],["RJ11 and RJ12 (telephone)", "connector-identifier.html#c-rj11", "connector", "Analogue phones, DSL modems, fax machines. Like a network plug but narrower, about 9.5 mm, with four or six contacts."],["SFP and SFP+ cage", "connector-identifier.html#c-sfp", "connector", "The slot in a switch, router or network card that takes a transceiver module: fibre, copper, or a direct-attach cable with fixed ends. A metal-edged rectangular slot about 14 mm wide, often with a dus"],["LC fibre connector", "connector-identifier.html#c-lc", "connector", "The standard fibre plug in data centres and on SFP modules. Usually two together: one fibre sends, one receives. Two small square plugs with a clip each, joined by a bracket, with a round white tip in"],["Coaxial F connector", "connector-identifier.html#c-coax-f", "connector", "Cable internet modems and satellite receivers. A round threaded sleeve with a single thin wire in the centre. Screws on."],["SATA data", "connector-identifier.html#c-sata-data", "connector", "The data cable from the mainboard to a hard disk, SSD or optical drive. A thin flat plug about 8 mm wide with an L-shaped opening. Seven contacts."],["SATA power", "connector-identifier.html#c-sata-power", "connector", "Power for hard disks and SSDs, coming from the power supply. The same L-shape as the data plug but twice as wide, about 15 mm, with 15 contacts. Sits right next to the data plug on the drive."],["SAS (SFF-8482)", "connector-identifier.html#c-sas", "connector", "Disks in servers and storage shelves. Looks like the SATA data and power plugs in one piece, with the gap between them filled in."],["M.2, M key (NVMe)", "connector-identifier.html#c-m2-m", "connector", "Current SSDs. The slot sits flat on the mainboard, and the SSD is held by one screw at the far end. One notch near the right end of the contact edge, seen with the label facing you and the contacts po"],["M.2, B and M key (SATA)", "connector-identifier.html#c-m2-bm", "connector", "Older and cheaper M.2 SSDs that use the SATA protocol. Two notches: one near the left and one near the right end of the contact edge."],["M.2, E key (Wi-Fi)", "connector-identifier.html#c-m2-e", "connector", "Wi-Fi and Bluetooth cards in notebooks and on mainboards. A short card, usually 22 by 30 mm, with one notch about a third in from one side and two tiny antenna sockets on top."],["M.2 lengths", "connector-identifier.html#c-m2-len", "connector", "M.2 cards come in several lengths. The number is width and length in millimetres: 2280 is 22 mm wide and 80 mm long. Measure from the contact edge to the screw notch. 2280 is the usual desktop and not"],["mSATA and Mini PCIe", "connector-identifier.html#c-mpcie", "connector", "Small cards in notebooks and mini PCs from about 2009 to 2015: SSDs, Wi-Fi and mobile data cards. A card about 30 mm wide with one notch off-centre in the contact edge and two screw holes at the far e"],["ATX 24-pin", "connector-identifier.html#c-atx24", "connector", "Main power from the power supply to the mainboard. The largest plug in the PC: two rows of twelve, with a clip in the middle of one long side. Often built as 20+4, with four pins that can be split off"],["CPU power, 8-pin EPS (4+4)", "connector-identifier.html#c-eps8", "connector", "Power for the processor, plugged in near the top left of the mainboard. Two rows of four. Usually built as two halves of four pins that slide together. The cable is labelled CPU."],["Graphics card power, PCIe 8-pin (6+2)", "connector-identifier.html#c-pcie8", "connector", "Extra power for a graphics card. Two rows of four, built as a block of six with a separate block of two that hangs next to it. The cable is labelled PCIe or VGA."],["12VHPWR and 12V-2x6", "connector-identifier.html#c-12vhpwr", "connector", "Power for current high-end graphics cards, up to 600 W through one plug. Two rows of six small pins, with four tiny sense pins in a row underneath."],["Molex, 4-pin peripheral", "connector-identifier.html#c-molex", "connector", "Old drives, case fans, pumps, and adapters to almost everything. A white or black plug about 21 mm wide with two bevelled corners and four round pins."],["Fan header, 3-pin and 4-pin", "connector-identifier.html#c-fan", "connector", "Case and CPU fans on the mainboard. A row of three or four pins with a plastic tab behind them. The plug has a groove that slides over the tab."],["IEC C13 and C14 (the PC power cord)", "connector-identifier.html#c-c13", "connector", "PCs, monitors, printers, most servers and switches. A plug with three flat pins in a row-of-one over row-of-two pattern and two bevelled corners."],["IEC C5 and C6 (cloverleaf)", "connector-identifier.html#c-c5", "connector", "Notebook power supplies, projectors, some monitors. Three round pins in a housing shaped like a three-leaf clover."],["IEC C7 and C8 (figure-8)", "connector-identifier.html#c-c7", "connector", "Small power supplies, radios, consoles, printers, Apple chargers. Two round pins in a flat housing with a waist, like the number 8 lying down. No earth."],["IEC C19 and C20", "connector-identifier.html#c-c19", "connector", "Large servers, blade chassis, big UPS units and the power strips (PDUs) in a rack. Bigger than the PC plug, rectangular, with three flat pins lying horizontally."],["Barrel plug (DC)", "connector-identifier.html#c-barrel", "connector", "The round plug of external power supplies: routers, switches, monitors, older notebooks. A metal sleeve with a hole in the middle, 3.5 to 7.4 mm across. Dozens of sizes exist."],["Memory modules: DIMM and SO-DIMM", "connector-identifier.html#c-dimm", "connector", "Main memory. DIMM in desktops and servers, the shorter SO-DIMM in notebooks and mini PCs. DIMM is 133 mm long, SO-DIMM 68 mm. The notch in the contact edge sits in a different place for each generatio"],["PCI Express slots", "connector-identifier.html#c-pcie-slot", "connector", "Expansion cards: graphics, network, storage controllers. Slots of four lengths, named after the number of lanes: x1 is about 25 mm long, x16 about 89 mm. A small ridge divides the short power section "],["3.5 mm audio jack", "connector-identifier.html#c-jack", "connector", "Headphones, headsets, speakers. A 3.5 mm pin. Two rings on the plug mean stereo sound, three rings mean stereo plus microphone (a headset plug)."],["Serial port, DB9 (RS-232)", "connector-identifier.html#c-db9", "connector", "Console access to switches, firewalls, UPS units, and machines on the factory floor. D-shaped, nine pins in two rows, two screws. Smaller than VGA and with fewer, thicker pins."],["PS/2", "connector-identifier.html#c-ps2", "connector", "Keyboards and mice before USB. Still on some mainboards and on KVM switches. Round, 6 pins, with a plastic block that only lets it in one way. Purple for the keyboard, green for the mouse."],["BMC", "glossary.html#bmc", "glossary", "Baseboard management controller. The small independent computer inside a server that stays on whenever the power cords are in: it shows the screen remotely, switches the server on and off and keeps th"],["CMOS battery", "glossary.html#cmos-battery", "glossary", "The coin cell on a mainboard, usually a CR2032, that keeps the clock running and on older boards the BIOS settings alive. When it is empty, the PC forgets the time and the boot order each time it is u"],["Dual channel", "glossary.html#dual-channel", "glossary", "Two memory modules working side by side so that the processor reads from both at once. Needs the modules in the right pair of slots, usually the second and fourth. Which slots"],["ECC memory", "glossary.html#ecc-memory", "glossary", "Memory with extra bits that let it correct a single flipped bit and detect two. Standard in servers. Corrected errors appear in the hardware log and are the early warning that a module is failing."],["Hot swap", "glossary.html#hot-swap", "glossary", "Replacing a part while the machine keeps running: disks in carriers, power supplies, fans. The part must be built for it, and for a disk the array must be told or must notice."],["M.2", "glossary.html#m-2", "glossary", "The small card format for SSDs and Wi-Fi cards that plugs flat onto the board. The notches (keys) say which slot a card fits, a four-digit number such as 2280 gives width and length in millimetres. Co"],["PDU", "glossary.html#pdu", "glossary", "Power distribution unit: the power strip of a rack. Managed ones measure the load per outlet and can switch outlets remotely."],["POST", "glossary.html#post", "glossary", "Power-on self-test. The checks a computer runs on its own hardware before it starts the operating system. A failure shows as beeps, a lit LED on the board or a code. Troubleshooting wizard"],["PWM (fan)", "glossary.html#pwm-fan", "glossary", "Pulse-width modulation. The fourth wire of a fan plug carries a signal with which the board sets the speed precisely. Three-wire fans can only be slowed by lowering the voltage."],["Rack unit", "glossary.html#rack-unit", "glossary", "The height unit of rack equipment, written U: 44.45 mm, or three holes of the rail. A 2U server is two of them high. How to count them"],["RDIMM", "glossary.html#rdimm", "glossary", "Registered memory module, the kind servers use: a buffer chip on the module lets a board drive many of them. Does not work in desktop boards, and desktop modules do not work in servers."],["SO-DIMM", "glossary.html#so-dimm", "glossary", "The short memory module used in notebooks and mini PCs, about half the length of a desktop module."],["Thermal throttling", "glossary.html#thermal-throttling", "glossary", "A processor that slows itself down because it has reached its temperature limit. The machine stays on and gets slow: the usual causes are dust, a dead fan or dried-out thermal paste."],["Thunderbolt", "glossary.html#thunderbolt", "glossary", "The fastest connection that uses the USB-C plug: 40 Gbit/s and more, several monitors and fast storage through one cable. Marked with a small bolt next to the port. Connector identifier"],["USB Power Delivery", "glossary.html#usb-power-delivery", "glossary", "The standard by which a USB-C charger and a device agree on voltage and current, up to 240 W. Charger, cable and device must all support the wattage, and the weakest of the three decides."],["ZIF connector", "glossary.html#zif-connector", "glossary", "Zero insertion force: the latched connector that holds a flat ribbon cable in notebooks and phones. The latch is opened first, then the cable slides out without force. The two kinds"],["Config reviewer", "config-reviewer.html", "tool", "Review sshd_config, nginx configuration and docker-compose.yml: root login, password authentication, weak ciphers, TLS versions, alias traversal, add_header, privileged containers, docker.sock, published ports, passwords in the file"],["sshd_config review", "config-reviewer.html", "tool", "Check an OpenSSH server configuration: PermitRootLogin, PasswordAuthentication, duplicate keywords, Match blocks"],["nginx config check", "config-reviewer.html", "tool", "Check an nginx configuration for TLS, headers, alias traversal, PHP, status pages and dot files"],["docker-compose security check", "config-reviewer.html", "tool", "Check a Compose file for privileged containers, the Docker socket, host mounts, exposed database ports and secrets"],["SQL playground", "sql-playground.html", "tool", "Learn SQL in the browser: 16 lessons with a practice database, queries are run and checked"],["The database is slow", "database-slow.html", "tool", "Walkthrough for slow PostgreSQL, MySQL, MariaDB, SQL Server: sessions, locks, slow query, execution plan, missing index, statistics, memory, storage"],["SQL lesson 1: Look at a table", "sql-playground.html#look", "lesson", "A table has columns with names and rows with values. SELECT says which columns you want, FROM says which table. The star means all columns."],["SQL lesson 2: Choose columns, filter rows", "sql-playground.html#where", "lesson", "Name the columns you want instead of the star, separated by commas. WHERE keeps only the rows for which the condition is true."],["SQL lesson 3: Combine conditions", "sql-playground.html#logic", "lesson", "AND needs both sides to be true, OR one of them. IN checks a value against a list, and LIKE compares text with a pattern where % stands for anything."],["SQL lesson 4: Missing values", "sql-playground.html#null", "lesson", "An empty field holds NULL, which means unknown. NULL is not zero and not an empty text."],["SQL lesson 5: Sort and cut", "sql-playground.html#order", "lesson", "Without ORDER BY the order of the rows is not defined, even if it looks stable. ORDER BY sorts by one or more columns, ascending unless you add DESC."],["SQL lesson 6: Count and add up", "sql-playground.html#count", "lesson", "COUNT(*) counts rows. SUM, AVG, MIN and MAX work on one column and skip the rows where it is NULL. The answer is a single row."],["SQL lesson 7: One line per group", "sql-playground.html#group", "lesson", "GROUP BY puts the rows with the same value into one group, and the functions then work per group: one line per category, per month, per user."],["SQL lesson 8: Filter the groups", "sql-playground.html#having", "lesson", "WHERE filters single rows before they are grouped. HAVING filters the groups afterwards, so it can use COUNT and SUM. A query may have both."],["SQL lesson 9: Join two tables", "sql-playground.html#join", "lesson", "The tickets table holds a user_id, not a name. The name is in the users table, in the row whose id is that number. JOIN puts the two rows side by side, and ON says which rows belong together."],["SQL lesson 10: Keep rows without a match", "sql-playground.html#left", "lesson", "A plain JOIN drops every row that has no partner: users without a department vanish from the example of the last lesson. LEFT JOIN keeps all rows of the left table and fills the columns of the right o"],["SQL lesson 11: Three tables, then group", "sql-playground.html#three", "lesson", "Joins chain: each JOIN adds one more table to the row. After that the wide row is filtered and grouped like any other."],["SQL lesson 12: Find duplicates", "sql-playground.html#dupes", "lesson", "A value that should be unique and is not: group by it and keep the groups with more than one row. It works with several columns too, for \"same category on the same day\"."],["SQL lesson 13: If, inside a query", "sql-playground.html#case", "lesson", "CASE gives a different value depending on a condition. It reads from the top and takes the first WHEN that is true."],["SQL lesson 14: Dates", "sql-playground.html#dates", "lesson", "Dates written as year-month-day sort correctly as text, so comparing with < and >= works. For a whole month, ask for \"from the first, and before the first of the next month\": that is right for every m"],["SQL lesson 15: A query on top of a query", "sql-playground.html#sub", "lesson", "The result of a query is a table again, so you can use it like one. WITH gives a query a name, and the main query reads from it. That keeps long questions readable: first the numbers per user, then th"],["SQL lesson 16: Change data without regret", "sql-playground.html#change", "lesson", "UPDATE and DELETE do exactly what the WHERE says, at once and without asking. Without WHERE they hit every row. Two habits prevent most accidents."],["Slow database: Is it the database, and since when?", "database-slow.html", "step", "\"The database is slow\" is what people say when an application is slow. Look at the machine first, and ask what changed."],["Slow database: What is running right now?", "database-slow.html", "step", "The list of sessions shows in ten seconds whether one statement is running for minutes, whether many wait, or whether there are simply too many."],["Slow database: Is something waiting for a lock?", "database-slow.html", "step", "A session that changed rows and has not committed keeps them locked. Everyone who wants the same rows waits, and from the outside it looks like a slow database."],["Slow database: Which statement costs the most time?", "database-slow.html", "step", "Guessing which query is slow rarely hits. The server keeps count: let it tell you which statements used the most time in total."],["Slow database: How does the database run that statement?", "database-slow.html", "step", "EXPLAIN shows the plan: which table is read how, and how many rows the database expects. Nearly every slow query shows its cause here."],["Slow database: Are statistics and housekeeping up to date?", "database-slow.html", "step", "The planner decides by statistics about the data. After a large import, a mass delete or an upgrade they are wrong until someone refreshes them, and queries that were fast yesterday crawl today."],["Slow database: Does the memory setting fit the machine?", "database-slow.html", "step", "A database is fast while the data it needs sits in memory. Out of the box, PostgreSQL and MySQL use about 128 MB for that, whatever the server has. SQL Server does the opposite and takes everything."],["Slow database: Is the storage the limit?", "database-slow.html", "step", "What does not fit in memory is read from disk, and every commit waits for the disk to confirm the write. Slow storage makes a well-tuned database slow."],["ACID", "glossary.html#acid", "glossary", "The four promises of a database transaction: atomic (all of it or none), consistent (the rules still hold afterwards), isolated (others do not see it half done) and durable (once committed, it survive"],["Connection pool", "glossary.html#connection-pool", "glossary", "A fixed set of open database connections that an application shares, instead of opening a new one for every request. Opening is slow, and every connection costs the server memory, so a pool is both fa"],["Deadlock (database)", "glossary.html#deadlock-database", "glossary", "Two transactions each hold a lock the other one needs. Neither can go on, so the database ends one of them with an error. The fix is in the application: touch tables in the same order and keep transac"],["Execution plan", "glossary.html#execution-plan", "glossary", "The way a database decided to run a query: which table it reads first, with which index, and how it joins. EXPLAIN shows it, and it is the first thing to look at for a slow query. The database is slow"],["Foreign key", "glossary.html#foreign-key", "glossary", "A column that holds the key of a row in another table, such as user_id in a tickets table. Declared as a constraint, the database refuses values that point at nothing."],["Index (database)", "glossary.html#index-database", "glossary", "A sorted side structure on one or more columns that lets the database find rows without reading the whole table, like the index of a book. Every index speeds up reads on those columns and slows down e"],["JOIN", "glossary.html#join", "glossary", "The SQL operation that puts rows from two tables side by side where a condition holds, usually key equals foreign key. LEFT JOIN also keeps the rows of the first table that have no partner. Try it"],["N+1 queries", "glossary.html#n-1-queries", "glossary", "An application loads a list with one query and then runs one more query per line for the details. Each is fast, but a page with 200 lines makes 201 round trips. Shows up in statistics as a small state"],["NULL", "glossary.html#null", "glossary", "The marker for a missing or unknown value in a database. It is not zero and not empty text, and nothing equals it, not even another NULL: ask with IS NULL. Try it"],["Point-in-time recovery", "glossary.html#point-in-time-recovery", "glossary", "Restoring a database to a chosen moment, such as one minute before a wrong DELETE, by replaying the logged changes on top of an older full backup. Needs the log (WAL, binary log, transaction log) to b"],["Primary key", "glossary.html#primary-key", "glossary", "The column, or columns, whose value identifies exactly one row of a table: unique and never empty. Usually a number called id."],["Recovery model", "glossary.html#recovery-model", "glossary", "The SQL Server setting that decides what happens to the transaction log. SIMPLE reuses it on its own and allows restores only to the last backup. FULL keeps everything until a log backup is taken, whi"],["Replication (database)", "glossary.html#replication-database", "glossary", "A second server that receives every change from the first and stays a copy of it. Used for failover and for moving read load. It is not a backup: a wrong DELETE is replicated within a second."],["SQL injection", "glossary.html#sql-injection", "glossary", "An attack where text typed by a user ends up inside an SQL statement and changes what it does. The cause is building statements by gluing strings together, and the cure is passing values as parameters"],["Transaction", "glossary.html#transaction", "glossary", "A group of changes that a database applies as a whole: after BEGIN nothing is final until COMMIT, and ROLLBACK undoes all of it. Try it"],["Vacuum", "glossary.html#vacuum", "glossary", "The PostgreSQL housekeeping that removes old row versions left behind by updates and deletes. Autovacuum does it in the background, and when it cannot keep up, tables grow and queries slow down. Postg"],["WAL", "glossary.html#wal", "glossary", "Write-ahead log. PostgreSQL writes every change to this log before it touches the data files, which is what makes a crash survivable. Archived WAL is also the raw material for replication and point-in"],["Database backup and restore cheat sheet", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Back up and restore PostgreSQL, MySQL, MariaDB, SQL Server and SQLite: nightly dumps with retention, point-in-time recovery, restore tests, and the mistakes that make a backup worthless."],["The three kinds, and what each is for", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20three%20kinds%2C%20and%20what%20each%20is%20for", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "Most setups need the first plus one of the others. # 1. Logical dump: the SQL to rebuild the database (pg_dump, mysqldump). #    Portable, restores single tables, slow for large databases. # 2. Physical backup: a copy of the data files take"],["Never copy the files of a running database", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=Never%20copy%20the%20files%20of%20a%20running%20database", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "A plain copy of the data directory catches the files at different moments and is usually unusable. That also goes for file-level backup agents and sync tools pointed at the data folder. # wrong: #   cp -r /var/lib/postgresql /backup/       "],["Virtual machine backups of a database server", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=Virtual%20machine%20backups%20of%20a%20database%20server", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "An image backup is fine if it is application-consistent: on Windows the backup software asks the database to flush through VSS. Without that it is crash-consistent, like pulling the plug. Keep a database-level backup next to it either way. "],["PostgreSQL: nightly dump with retention", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=PostgreSQL%3A%20nightly%20dump%20with%20retention", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "One file per database in custom format, the roles separately, older than 14 days removed. Run it as the postgres user. #!/usr/bin/env bash set -euo pipefail dir=/backup/postgres; day=$(date +%F); mkdir -p \"$dir\" pg_dumpall --globals-only > "],["PostgreSQL: schedule it", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=PostgreSQL%3A%20schedule%20it", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "In the crontab of the postgres user. The log shows whether it ran. sudo crontab -u postgres -e 30 1 * * * /usr/local/bin/pg-backup.sh >> /var/log/postgresql/backup.log 2>&1"],["PostgreSQL: restore", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=PostgreSQL%3A%20restore", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "Roles first, then each database into a fresh one. psql -f /backup/postgres/globals_2026-10-05.sql postgres createdb -O app mydb pg_restore -d mydb -j 4 /backup/postgres/mydb_2026-10-05.dump"],["PostgreSQL: point-in-time recovery, the setup", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=PostgreSQL%3A%20point-in-time%20recovery%2C%20the%20setup", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "Archive every WAL segment somewhere else, and take a base backup regularly. For production, pgBackRest or Barman do this with less room for error. # postgresql.conf, then restart wal_level = replica archive_mode = on archive_command = 'test"],["PostgreSQL: point-in-time recovery, the restore", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=PostgreSQL%3A%20point-in-time%20recovery%2C%20the%20restore", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "PostgreSQL 12 and newer. Unpack the base backup into an empty data directory, say where the WAL is and when to stop, and start. sudo systemctl stop postgresql # data directory empty, then unpack base.tar.gz into it and pg_wal.tar.gz into it"],["MySQL and MariaDB: nightly dump with retention", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=MySQL%20and%20MariaDB%3A%20nightly%20dump%20with%20retention", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "The password belongs in a file only root can read, not on the command line. # /root/.my.cnf   (chmod 600) [client] user=backup password=change-me  #!/usr/bin/env bash set -euo pipefail dir=/backup/mysql; day=$(date +%F); mkdir -p \"$dir\" mys"],["MySQL and MariaDB: a user for the backup", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=MySQL%20and%20MariaDB%3A%20a%20user%20for%20the%20backup", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "Only the rights a dump needs. CREATE USER 'backup'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'change-me'; GRANT SELECT, SHOW VIEW, TRIGGER, EVENT, LOCK TABLES, PROCESS, RELOAD ON *.* TO 'backup'@'localhost';"],["MySQL and MariaDB: restore one database from a full dump", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=MySQL%20and%20MariaDB%3A%20restore%20one%20database%20from%20a%20full%20dump", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "--one-database skips everything else in the file. It restores over the database of that name: to look at the old data first, restore on another server. gunzip < /backup/mysql/all_2026-10-05.sql.gz | mysql --one-database mydb"],["MySQL and MariaDB: point-in-time recovery", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=MySQL%20and%20MariaDB%3A%20point-in-time%20recovery", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "Needs the binary log switched on before the accident. Restore the dump, then replay the log up to the minute before. # my.cnf, [mysqld] section, then restart log_bin = /var/lib/mysql/binlog binlog_expire_logs_seconds = 1209600      # MariaD"],["SQL Server: a schedule to start from", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=SQL%20Server%3A%20a%20schedule%20to%20start%20from", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "Full on Sunday, differential every night, log every 15 minutes. As Agent jobs, or with the free scripts by Ola Hallengren. BACKUP DATABASE MyDb TO DISK = 'D:\\Backup\\MyDb_full.bak' WITH COMPRESSION, CHECKSUM, INIT; BACKUP DATABASE MyDb TO DI"],["SQL Server: restore the whole chain", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=SQL%20Server%3A%20restore%20the%20whole%20chain", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "Last full, last differential, then every log backup since, in order. Only the last step says RECOVERY. RESTORE DATABASE MyDb FROM DISK = 'D:\\Backup\\MyDb_full.bak' WITH NORECOVERY, REPLACE; RESTORE DATABASE MyDb FROM DISK = 'D:\\Backup\\MyDb_d"],["SQL Server: the database is damaged but the server still runs", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=SQL%20Server%3A%20the%20database%20is%20damaged%20but%20the%20server%20still%20runs", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "Back up the end of the log first. Without this tail-log backup, everything since the last log backup is lost. BACKUP LOG MyDb TO DISK = 'D:\\Backup\\MyDb_tail.trn' WITH NO_TRUNCATE, NORECOVERY;"],["SQL Server Express: no Agent, so use Task Scheduler", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=SQL%20Server%20Express%3A%20no%20Agent%2C%20so%20use%20Task%20Scheduler", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "A script file and one scheduled task. sqlcmd -S .\\SQLEXPRESS -E -C -Q \"BACKUP DATABASE MyDb TO DISK = 'D:\\Backup\\MyDb.bak' WITH CHECKSUM, INIT\"  schtasks /Create /TN \"SQL backup\" /SC DAILY /ST 01:30 /RU SYSTEM /TR \"sqlcmd -S .\\SQLEXPRESS -E"],["SQLite", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=SQLite", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "The .backup command copies a database that is in use safely. A plain file copy can catch it mid-write. sqlite3 /srv/app/data.db \".backup '/backup/data_$(date +%F).db'\" sqlite3 /backup/data_2026-10-05.db \"PRAGMA integrity_check;\""],["A database in a container", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20database%20in%20a%20container", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "Dump through the container, write the file on the host. Backing up the volume while the container runs is the file-copy mistake again. docker exec -t postgres pg_dump -U app -Fc mydb > /backup/mydb_$(date +%F).dump docker exec mariadb sh -c"],["Get the backup off the machine", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=Get%20the%20backup%20off%20the%20machine", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "A backup on the same disk, or the same server, protects against a typo and nothing else. restic encrypts and keeps versions. restic -r sftp:backup@nas.example.internal:/srv/restic/db backup /backup restic -r sftp:backup@nas.example.internal"],["The restore test", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20restore%20test", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "The only proof. Restore last night's backup under another name, count something, drop it. Put it on the calendar once a month, and time it: that number is your real recovery time. # PostgreSQL createdb restore_test && pg_restore -d restore_"],["Notice when the backup stops", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=Notice%20when%20the%20backup%20stops", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "A backup job that fails quietly is the common way to lose data. Check the age of the newest file from outside the job. # exit code 1 if there is no backup file younger than 26 hours find /backup/postgres -name '*.dump' -mmin -1560 | grep -q"],["Before a risky change", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=Before%20a%20risky%20change", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "A quick copy you can fall back on within minutes, next to the regular backup. # PostgreSQL: a copy of the whole database (nobody may be connected to the source) createdb -T mydb mydb_before_upgrade # MySQL, MariaDB mysqldump --single-transa"],["What to write down", "database-backup-restore-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20to%20write%20down", "snippet: Database backup and restore", "Decide these with the people who own the data, not during the outage. # How much data may be lost?   (decides how often: nightly, or logs every 15 minutes) # How long may it be down?     (decides the method: dump or physical backup, and the"],["SQL basics cheat sheet", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "SQL for admins in one sitting: select, filter, sort, join, group, change data safely with transactions, and the handful of patterns that answer most questions put to a database."],["Look at a table", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Look%20at%20a%20table", "snippet: SQL basics", "Never without a limit on a table you do not know. SQL Server writes it differently. SELECT * FROM users LIMIT 10; -- SQL Server: SELECT TOP 10 * FROM users;"],["Pick columns and filter rows", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Pick%20columns%20and%20filter%20rows", "snippet: SQL basics", "Text in single quotes. Double quotes are for names, not values. SELECT name, email FROM users WHERE active = 1 AND created_at >= '2026-01-01';"],["Filter by a list, a range, a pattern", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Filter%20by%20a%20list%2C%20a%20range%2C%20a%20pattern", "snippet: SQL basics", "LIKE with % matches any text. Whether it ignores case depends on the database: PostgreSQL has ILIKE for that. SELECT * FROM users WHERE department_id IN (3, 5, 8); SELECT * FROM users WHERE created_at BETWEEN '2026-01-01' AND '2026-03-31'; "],["Empty values", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Empty%20values", "snippet: SQL basics", "NULL means unknown and equals nothing, not even itself. = NULL is always false. SELECT * FROM users WHERE department_id IS NULL; SELECT name, COALESCE(email, 'no address') AS email FROM users;"],["Sort, and take the top few", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Sort%2C%20and%20take%20the%20top%20few", "snippet: SQL basics", "Newest first. SELECT name, created_at FROM users ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 5;"],["Count and summarise", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Count%20and%20summarise", "snippet: SQL basics", "One row of numbers for the whole table. SELECT COUNT(*) AS users, MIN(created_at) AS first, MAX(created_at) AS last FROM users;"],["Count per group", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Count%20per%20group", "snippet: SQL basics", "Every column in SELECT is either in GROUP BY or inside a function. SELECT department_id, COUNT(*) AS users FROM users GROUP BY department_id ORDER BY users DESC;"],["Filter groups", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Filter%20groups", "snippet: SQL basics", "WHERE filters rows before grouping, HAVING filters the groups afterwards. SELECT department_id, COUNT(*) AS users FROM users WHERE active = 1 GROUP BY department_id HAVING COUNT(*) >= 10;"],["Join two tables", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Join%20two%20tables", "snippet: SQL basics", "Only rows that have a match on both sides. SELECT u.name, d.name AS department FROM users u JOIN departments d ON d.id = u.department_id;"],["Join and keep rows without a match", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Join%20and%20keep%20rows%20without%20a%20match", "snippet: SQL basics", "LEFT JOIN keeps every user. The department columns are NULL where there is none. SELECT u.name, d.name AS department FROM users u LEFT JOIN departments d ON d.id = u.department_id;"],["Find what is missing on the other side", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20what%20is%20missing%20on%20the%20other%20side", "snippet: SQL basics", "Departments nobody belongs to. SELECT d.name FROM departments d LEFT JOIN users u ON u.department_id = d.id WHERE u.id IS NULL;"],["Find duplicates", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20duplicates", "snippet: SQL basics", "Values that occur more than once. SELECT email, COUNT(*) AS times FROM users GROUP BY email HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;"],["The newest row per group", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20newest%20row%20per%20group", "snippet: SQL basics", "A window function numbers the rows inside each group. Works on all current databases. SELECT * FROM (   SELECT u.*, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY department_id ORDER BY created_at DESC) AS rn   FROM users u ) t WHERE rn = 1;"],["Conditions inside a query", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Conditions%20inside%20a%20query", "snippet: SQL basics", "CASE is the if of SQL. SELECT name,        CASE WHEN active = 1 THEN 'active' ELSE 'disabled' END AS state FROM users;"],["Count with a condition", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Count%20with%20a%20condition", "snippet: SQL basics", "Several counts in one pass over the table. SELECT COUNT(*) AS all_users,        SUM(CASE WHEN active = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS active_users FROM users;"],["A query on top of a query", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20query%20on%20top%20of%20a%20query", "snippet: SQL basics", "A common table expression gives a subquery a name and keeps long queries readable. WITH per_dept AS (   SELECT department_id, COUNT(*) AS users FROM users GROUP BY department_id ) SELECT d.name, p.users FROM per_dept p JOIN departments d ON"],["Dates: the last 30 days, and per month", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Dates%3A%20the%20last%2030%20days%2C%20and%20per%20month", "snippet: SQL basics", "The one area where every database has its own words. -- PostgreSQL SELECT * FROM users WHERE created_at >= now() - interval '30 days'; SELECT date_trunc('month', created_at) AS month, COUNT(*) FROM users GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1; -- MySQL, Mar"],["Add a row", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Add%20a%20row", "snippet: SQL basics", "Name the columns. The order in the table may change. INSERT INTO users (name, email, department_id, active) VALUES ('Anna Example', 'anna@example.org', 3, 1);"],["Change rows, safely", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Change%20rows%2C%20safely", "snippet: SQL basics", "Run the SELECT first and check the count. Then the UPDATE with exactly the same WHERE. SELECT COUNT(*) FROM users WHERE department_id = 7;  UPDATE users SET department_id = 3 WHERE department_id = 7;"],["Delete rows, safely", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Delete%20rows%2C%20safely", "snippet: SQL basics", "An UPDATE or DELETE without WHERE hits every row. Inside a transaction you can still take it back. BEGIN; DELETE FROM users WHERE active = 0 AND created_at < '2020-01-01'; -- look at the reported row count, then one of: COMMIT; ROLLBACK;"],["Transactions", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Transactions", "snippet: SQL basics", "All or nothing. SQL Server says BEGIN TRANSACTION, MySQL also START TRANSACTION. BEGIN; UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance - 100 WHERE id = 1; UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance + 100 WHERE id = 2; COMMIT;"],["Create a table", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20table", "snippet: SQL basics", "A primary key, a required column, a default, and a reference to another table. CREATE TABLE users (   id            INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,   name          VARCHAR(200) NOT NULL,   email         VARCHAR(320) UNIQUE,   department_id INTEGER REF"],["Change a table", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Change%20a%20table", "snippet: SQL basics", "Add a column, and an index for a column you filter or join on. ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN last_login TIMESTAMP; CREATE INDEX idx_users_department ON users (department_id);"],["Why is this query slow", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Why%20is%20this%20query%20slow", "snippet: SQL basics", "Ask the database how it runs the query. A full scan of a big table for a few rows means an index is missing. EXPLAIN SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = 'anna@example.org'; -- PostgreSQL, with real timings: EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS) SELECT *"],["Copy query results into a new table", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Copy%20query%20results%20into%20a%20new%20table", "snippet: SQL basics", "A quick backup of the rows you are about to change. CREATE TABLE users_backup_20261005 AS SELECT * FROM users WHERE department_id = 7; -- SQL Server: SELECT * INTO users_backup_20261005 FROM users WHERE department_id = 7;"],["Never build SQL by gluing strings together", "sql-basics-cheat-sheet.html?q=Never%20build%20SQL%20by%20gluing%20strings%20together", "snippet: SQL basics", "A value typed by a user that ends up inside the statement can rewrite it: SQL injection. Pass values as parameters. -- wrong, in any language: --   \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = '\" + input + \"'\" -- right: a placeholder, and the value ha"],["PostgreSQL admin cheat sheet", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "PostgreSQL for the admin who inherits one: connect, look around, users and rights, what is running and what blocks it, sizes, vacuum, configuration, and backup and restore with pg_dump and base backups."],["Connect", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Locally as the database superuser, or over the network. sudo -u postgres psql psql -h db.example.internal -U app -d mydb"],["Look around in psql", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Look%20around%20in%20psql", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Databases, tables, one table in detail, users. \\x switches to one column per line for wide rows. \\l \\c mydb \\dt \\d+ users \\du \\x auto"],["Version, uptime, where the files are", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Version%2C%20uptime%2C%20where%20the%20files%20are", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Also shows which configuration file is in use. SELECT version(); SELECT now() - pg_postmaster_start_time() AS uptime; SHOW data_directory; SHOW config_file; SHOW hba_file;"],["Create a database with its own user", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20database%20with%20its%20own%20user", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "The user owns the database and nothing else. CREATE ROLE app LOGIN PASSWORD 'change-me'; CREATE DATABASE mydb OWNER app;"],["A read-only user", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20read-only%20user", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "For reporting tools. The last line covers tables created later. CREATE ROLE report LOGIN PASSWORD 'change-me'; GRANT CONNECT ON DATABASE mydb TO report; \\c mydb GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA public TO report; GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA pu"],["Change a password", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Change%20a%20password", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "\\password asks for it and does not write it into the history or the log. \\password app"],["Who may connect from where", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20may%20connect%20from%20where", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "pg_hba.conf decides: type, database, user, address, method. Reload after editing. # TYPE  DATABASE  USER  ADDRESS          METHOD host    mydb      app   10.87.20.0/24    scram-sha-256  SELECT pg_reload_conf();"],["Listen on the network", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Listen%20on%20the%20network", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Off by default: PostgreSQL only answers on localhost. Needs a restart. # postgresql.conf listen_addresses = '*'  sudo systemctl restart postgresql"],["What is running right now", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20is%20running%20right%20now", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Everything that is not idle, longest first. SELECT pid, usename, datname, state, now() - query_start AS running, wait_event_type, left(query, 80) AS query FROM pg_stat_activity WHERE state <> 'idle' ORDER BY running DESC;"],["Who is blocking whom", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20is%20blocking%20whom", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Each waiting session with the session that holds it up. SELECT a.pid AS waiting, a.usename, left(a.query, 60) AS waiting_query,        b.pid AS blocker, b.usename AS blocker_user, left(b.query, 60) AS blocker_query, b.state AS blocker_state"],["Stop a query, or end a session", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Stop%20a%20query%2C%20or%20end%20a%20session", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Cancel first. Terminate if that does not help. SELECT pg_cancel_backend(12345); SELECT pg_terminate_backend(12345);"],["Sessions that sit in an open transaction", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Sessions%20that%20sit%20in%20an%20open%20transaction", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "\"idle in transaction\" for minutes holds locks and stops vacuum. Usually an application that forgot to commit. SELECT pid, usename, now() - xact_start AS open_for, left(query, 80) AS last_query FROM pg_stat_activity WHERE state = 'idle in tr"],["Connections used and allowed", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connections%20used%20and%20allowed", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "\"too many connections\" means the limit was reached. A connection pooler helps more than a higher limit. SELECT count(*) AS used, current_setting('max_connections') AS allowed FROM pg_stat_activity; SELECT usename, count(*) FROM pg_stat_acti"],["Size of every database", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Size%20of%20every%20database", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Largest first. SELECT datname, pg_size_pretty(pg_database_size(datname)) AS size FROM pg_database ORDER BY pg_database_size(datname) DESC;"],["Largest tables, with their indexes", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Largest%20tables%2C%20with%20their%20indexes", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "In the current database. SELECT relname AS table, pg_size_pretty(pg_total_relation_size(relid)) AS total,        pg_size_pretty(pg_relation_size(relid)) AS data, n_live_tup AS rows FROM pg_stat_user_tables ORDER BY pg_total_relation_size(re"],["Tables that need vacuum", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Tables%20that%20need%20vacuum", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Dead rows are old versions that have not been cleaned up yet. Many of them, and an old last_autovacuum, mean autovacuum does not keep up. SELECT relname, n_live_tup, n_dead_tup, last_autovacuum, last_autoanalyze FROM pg_stat_user_tables ORD"],["Vacuum and analyse by hand", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Vacuum%20and%20analyse%20by%20hand", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Plain VACUUM runs alongside normal work. VACUUM FULL rewrites the table and locks it completely. VACUUM (VERBOSE, ANALYZE) users;"],["Indexes nobody uses", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Indexes%20nobody%20uses", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Scanned zero times since the statistics were last reset. They cost space and slow down every write. SELECT relname AS table, indexrelname AS index, pg_size_pretty(pg_relation_size(indexrelid)) AS size, idx_scan FROM pg_stat_user_indexes WHE"],["Tables read without an index", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Tables%20read%20without%20an%20index", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Many sequential scans on a large table point at a missing index. SELECT relname, seq_scan, seq_tup_read, idx_scan, n_live_tup FROM pg_stat_user_tables WHERE seq_scan > 0 ORDER BY seq_tup_read DESC LIMIT 15;"],["The slowest statements", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20slowest%20statements", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Needs the extension pg_stat_statements in shared_preload_libraries. Column names are those of PostgreSQL 13 and newer. CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pg_stat_statements; SELECT calls, round(total_exec_time) AS total_ms, round(mean_exec_time"],["Log every slow statement", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Log%20every%20slow%20statement", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Statements over half a second go to the server log. No restart needed. ALTER SYSTEM SET log_min_duration_statement = '500ms'; SELECT pg_reload_conf();"],["The settings that matter first", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20settings%20that%20matter%20first", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Rules of thumb for a dedicated server: shared_buffers a quarter of memory, effective_cache_size three quarters. SHOW shared_buffers; SHOW effective_cache_size; SHOW work_mem; SHOW maintenance_work_mem; SHOW max_connections;"],["Back up one database", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Back%20up%20one%20database", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Custom format: compressed, and restorable table by table. Consistent even while the database is in use. pg_dump -Fc -f /backup/mydb_$(date +%F).dump mydb"],["Back up users and everything else", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Back%20up%20users%20and%20everything%20else", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Roles and their passwords are not in a per-database dump. pg_dumpall --globals-only > /backup/globals_$(date +%F).sql pg_dumpall | gzip > /backup/all_$(date +%F).sql.gz"],["Restore a dump", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Restore%20a%20dump", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Into a fresh database. -j restores with several jobs at once. createdb -O app mydb_restored pg_restore -d mydb_restored -j 4 /backup/mydb_2026-10-05.dump pg_restore -l /backup/mydb_2026-10-05.dump | less      # what is in it"],["Restore one table", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Restore%20one%20table", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "Useful when one table was damaged and the rest is fine. pg_restore -d mydb -t users --data-only /backup/mydb_2026-10-05.dump"],["A physical backup of the whole server", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20physical%20backup%20of%20the%20whole%20server", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "The basis for point-in-time recovery together with archived WAL files. For real use, look at pgBackRest or Barman. pg_basebackup -D /backup/base_$(date +%F) -Ft -z -P -X stream"],["Is replication working", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20replication%20working", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "On the primary: one row per standby and how far behind it is. On a standby: the delay. SELECT client_addr, state, sync_state, replay_lag FROM pg_stat_replication; SELECT now() - pg_last_xact_replay_timestamp() AS delay;"],["Where is the log", "postgresql-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Where%20is%20the%20log", "snippet: PostgreSQL", "On Debian and Ubuntu in /var/log/postgresql, elsewhere in the data directory or the journal. SHOW logging_collector; SHOW log_directory; sudo journalctl -u postgresql -n 50"],["MySQL and MariaDB admin cheat sheet", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "MySQL and MariaDB for the admin who inherits one: connect, users and grants, the process list and locks, sizes, the slow query log, InnoDB settings, and backup and restore with mysqldump."],["Connect", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "On many Linux installs root logs in through the socket without a password, when you are root on the machine. sudo mysql mysql -h db.example.internal -u app -p mydb"],["Look around", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Look%20around", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "Databases, tables, the structure of one table, and how it was created. SHOW DATABASES; USE mydb; SHOW TABLES; DESCRIBE users; SHOW CREATE TABLE users\\G"],["Version, uptime, where the data is", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Version%2C%20uptime%2C%20where%20the%20data%20is", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "\\G at the end prints one column per line. SELECT VERSION(); SHOW GLOBAL STATUS LIKE 'Uptime'; SHOW VARIABLES LIKE 'datadir'; mysqld --verbose --help | grep -A1 \"Default options\"      # from the shell: which config files are read"],["Create a database with its own user", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20database%20with%20its%20own%20user", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "A user is always a name plus the host it may come from. % means anywhere. CREATE DATABASE mydb CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci; CREATE USER 'app'@'10.87.20.%' IDENTIFIED BY 'change-me'; GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON mydb.* TO 'ap"],["A read-only user", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20read-only%20user", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "For reporting tools. CREATE USER 'report'@'%' IDENTIFIED BY 'change-me'; GRANT SELECT ON mydb.* TO 'report'@'%';"],["All users, and what one of them may do", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=All%20users%2C%20and%20what%20one%20of%20them%20may%20do", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "An account with host % and broad rights deserves a second look. SELECT user, host, plugin FROM mysql.user ORDER BY user; SHOW GRANTS FOR 'app'@'10.87.20.%';"],["Change a password, remove a user", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Change%20a%20password%2C%20remove%20a%20user", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", " ALTER USER 'app'@'10.87.20.%' IDENTIFIED BY 'new-password'; DROP USER 'old'@'%';"],["Listen on the network", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Listen%20on%20the%20network", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "By default many packages bind to localhost only. Change it in the server section of the configuration and restart. # /etc/mysql/mysql.conf.d/mysqld.cnf  or  /etc/mysql/mariadb.conf.d/50-server.cnf [mysqld] bind-address = 0.0.0.0  sudo syste"],["What is running right now", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20is%20running%20right%20now", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "Everything that is not sleeping, longest first. SELECT id, user, host, db, command, time AS seconds, state, LEFT(info, 80) AS query FROM information_schema.processlist WHERE command <> 'Sleep' ORDER BY time DESC;"],["Stop a query, or end a connection", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Stop%20a%20query%2C%20or%20end%20a%20connection", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", " KILL QUERY 12345; KILL 12345;"],["Who is waiting for a lock", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20is%20waiting%20for%20a%20lock", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "MySQL 8 has a ready view. On MariaDB, look at the transaction section of the InnoDB status. -- MySQL 8 SELECT waiting_pid, LEFT(waiting_query, 60) AS waiting, blocking_pid, LEFT(blocking_query, 60) AS blocking, wait_age FROM sys.innodb_lock"],["Transactions that have been open for long", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Transactions%20that%20have%20been%20open%20for%20long", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "An open transaction holds locks and keeps old row versions alive. SELECT trx_mysql_thread_id AS id, trx_started, TIMESTAMPDIFF(SECOND, trx_started, NOW()) AS open_seconds, LEFT(trx_query, 80) AS query FROM information_schema.innodb_trx ORDE"],["Connections used and allowed", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connections%20used%20and%20allowed", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "\"Too many connections\": compare the peak with the limit. SHOW GLOBAL STATUS LIKE 'Threads_connected'; SHOW GLOBAL STATUS LIKE 'Max_used_connections'; SHOW VARIABLES LIKE 'max_connections';"],["Size of every database", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Size%20of%20every%20database", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "Data plus indexes, in MB. SELECT table_schema AS db, ROUND(SUM(data_length + index_length) / 1024 / 1024) AS mb FROM information_schema.tables GROUP BY table_schema ORDER BY mb DESC;"],["Largest tables", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Largest%20tables", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "With the storage engine. MyISAM tables in a database that should be InnoDB are a finding of their own. SELECT table_schema, table_name, engine, table_rows,        ROUND((data_length + index_length) / 1024 / 1024) AS mb FROM information_sche"],["Turn on the slow query log", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Turn%20on%20the%20slow%20query%20log", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "Without a restart. Everything slower than one second is written down. SET GLOBAL slow_query_log = 1; SET GLOBAL long_query_time = 1; SHOW VARIABLES LIKE 'slow_query_log_file';"],["Read the slow query log", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20the%20slow%20query%20log", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "Groups similar queries and sorts by total time. mysqldumpslow -s t -t 15 /var/log/mysql/mysql-slow.log"],["The statements that cost the most", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20statements%20that%20cost%20the%20most", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "MySQL 8 with the sys schema. Total time, calls and rows examined per kind of statement. SELECT LEFT(query, 80) AS query, exec_count, total_latency, rows_examined_avg FROM sys.statement_analysis ORDER BY total_latency DESC LIMIT 15;"],["How a query is executed", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=How%20a%20query%20is%20executed", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "type ALL with a large rows value is a full table scan. key shows the index that was used. EXPLAIN SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = 'anna@example.org'; SHOW INDEX FROM users;"],["The setting that matters first", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20setting%20that%20matters%20first", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "The InnoDB buffer pool should hold most of the data: 50 to 70% of memory on a dedicated server. Changing it in the configuration needs a restart on older versions. SHOW VARIABLES LIKE 'innodb_buffer_pool_size'; SHOW GLOBAL STATUS LIKE 'Inno"],["Back up one database", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Back%20up%20one%20database", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "--single-transaction gives a consistent copy of InnoDB tables without locking them. Routines and triggers are included with the extra switches. mysqldump --single-transaction --routines --triggers --events mydb | gzip > /backup/mydb_$(date "],["Back up everything", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Back%20up%20everything", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "All databases including the users in the mysql database. mysqldump --single-transaction --routines --triggers --events --all-databases | gzip > /backup/all_$(date +%F).sql.gz"],["Restore a dump", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Restore%20a%20dump", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "Into an existing, empty database. mysql -e \"CREATE DATABASE mydb_restored\" gunzip < /backup/mydb_2026-10-05.sql.gz | mysql mydb_restored"],["Large databases: a physical backup", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Large%20databases%3A%20a%20physical%20backup", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "Much faster to restore than a dump. Percona XtraBackup for MySQL, mariabackup for MariaDB. mariabackup --backup --target-dir=/backup/full --user=root mariabackup --prepare --target-dir=/backup/full"],["Point-in-time recovery needs the binary log", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Point-in-time%20recovery%20needs%20the%20binary%20log", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "A dump brings you back to last night. The binary log replays what happened since. SHOW VARIABLES LIKE 'log_bin'; SHOW BINARY LOGS; mysqlbinlog --start-datetime=\"2026-10-05 02:00:00\" --stop-datetime=\"2026-10-05 14:29:00\" /var/lib/mysql/binlo"],["Is replication working", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20replication%20working", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "Both threads must say Yes, and the delay should be near zero. Older versions say SLAVE instead of REPLICA. SHOW REPLICA STATUS\\G -- look at: Replica_IO_Running, Replica_SQL_Running, Seconds_Behind_Source, Last_Error"],["Check and repair tables", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20and%20repair%20tables", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "From the shell, for all databases. For InnoDB, \"repair\" usually means restore from backup. mysqlcheck --all-databases --check mysqlcheck --all-databases --analyze"],["Where is the error log", "mysql-mariadb-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Where%20is%20the%20error%20log", "snippet: MySQL and MariaDB", "The first place to look when the server does not start. SHOW VARIABLES LIKE 'log_error'; sudo journalctl -u mysql -n 50      # or mariadb"],["SQL Server admin cheat sheet", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "SQL Server for the accidental DBA: what is running and what blocks it, backups and restores that work, recovery models and the log file that fills the disk, sizes, missing indexes, integrity checks and the settings to look at first."],["Connect from the command line", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect%20from%20the%20command%20line", "snippet: SQL Server", "-E uses your Windows login, -C trusts the server certificate with the newer tools. sqlcmd -S SQL01 -E -C sqlcmd -S SQL01\\INSTANCE -U sa -P \"password\" -d MyDb"],["Version, edition, patch level, uptime", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Version%2C%20edition%2C%20patch%20level%2C%20uptime", "snippet: SQL Server", "The patch level tells you whether cumulative updates were ever installed. SELECT @@VERSION; SELECT SERVERPROPERTY('Edition') AS edition, SERVERPROPERTY('ProductLevel') AS level, SERVERPROPERTY('ProductUpdateLevel') AS cu; SELECT sqlserver_s"],["All databases with state and recovery model", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=All%20databases%20with%20state%20and%20recovery%20model", "snippet: SQL Server", "FULL without log backups is how log files fill disks. SELECT name, state_desc, recovery_model_desc, compatibility_level, create_date FROM sys.databases ORDER BY name;"],["What is running right now", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20is%20running%20right%20now", "snippet: SQL Server", "Every active request with its wait, its blocker and the statement. SELECT r.session_id, s.login_name, DB_NAME(r.database_id) AS db, r.status, r.wait_type,        r.blocking_session_id AS blocked_by, r.total_elapsed_time / 1000 AS seconds,  "],["Who is at the head of a blocking chain", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20is%20at%20the%20head%20of%20a%20blocking%20chain", "snippet: SQL Server", "Sessions that block others and are not blocked themselves. SELECT s.session_id, s.login_name, s.host_name, s.program_name, s.status, s.last_request_end_time FROM sys.dm_exec_sessions s WHERE s.session_id IN (SELECT blocking_session_id FROM "],["End a session", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=End%20a%20session", "snippet: SQL Server", "Its open transaction is rolled back, which can take as long as the work it had done. KILL 57;"],["When was each database last backed up", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=When%20was%20each%20database%20last%20backed%20up", "snippet: SQL Server", "D is a full backup, I a differential, L a log backup. NULL means never. SELECT d.name, d.recovery_model_desc,        MAX(CASE WHEN b.type = 'D' THEN b.backup_finish_date END) AS last_full,        MAX(CASE WHEN b.type = 'I' THEN b.backup_fin"],["Full backup", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Full%20backup", "snippet: SQL Server", "CHECKSUM verifies pages while reading. COPY_ONLY leaves the backup chain of your backup software alone. BACKUP DATABASE MyDb TO DISK = 'D:\\Backup\\MyDb_full.bak' WITH COMPRESSION, CHECKSUM, COPY_ONLY, STATS = 10;"],["Log backup", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Log%20backup", "snippet: SQL Server", "Only in the FULL or BULK_LOGGED recovery model. This is what lets the log file reuse its space. BACKUP LOG MyDb TO DISK = 'D:\\Backup\\MyDb_log.trn' WITH COMPRESSION, CHECKSUM;"],["Is the backup file readable", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20backup%20file%20readable", "snippet: SQL Server", "Checks the file without restoring it. Only a real restore proves the backup. RESTORE VERIFYONLY FROM DISK = 'D:\\Backup\\MyDb_full.bak' WITH CHECKSUM; RESTORE FILELISTONLY FROM DISK = 'D:\\Backup\\MyDb_full.bak';"],["Restore as a copy", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Restore%20as%20a%20copy", "snippet: SQL Server", "Under a new name with the files moved, next to the original. The logical names come from FILELISTONLY. RESTORE DATABASE MyDb_copy FROM DISK = 'D:\\Backup\\MyDb_full.bak' WITH MOVE 'MyDb' TO 'D:\\Data\\MyDb_copy.mdf',      MOVE 'MyDb_log' TO 'L:"],["Restore to a point in time", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Restore%20to%20a%20point%20in%20time", "snippet: SQL Server", "Full backup without recovery, then the log backups, stopping just before the mistake. RESTORE DATABASE MyDb FROM DISK = 'D:\\Backup\\MyDb_full.bak' WITH NORECOVERY, REPLACE; RESTORE LOG MyDb FROM DISK = 'D:\\Backup\\MyDb_log.trn' WITH STOPAT = "],["The log file fills the disk: why", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20log%20file%20fills%20the%20disk%3A%20why", "snippet: SQL Server", "log_reuse_wait_desc names what the log is waiting for. LOG_BACKUP means nobody takes log backups. SELECT name, recovery_model_desc, log_reuse_wait_desc FROM sys.databases; DBCC SQLPERF(LOGSPACE);"],["The log file fills the disk: the fix", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20log%20file%20fills%20the%20disk%3A%20the%20fix", "snippet: SQL Server", "Either take log backups regularly, or, if you do not need point-in-time recovery, switch to SIMPLE. Then shrink once. BACKUP LOG MyDb TO DISK = 'D:\\Backup\\MyDb_log.trn'; -- or, giving up point-in-time recovery: ALTER DATABASE MyDb SET RECOV"],["Size and free space of every file", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Size%20and%20free%20space%20of%20every%20file", "snippet: SQL Server", "In the current database. SELECT name, type_desc, physical_name, size / 128 AS size_mb,        size / 128 - CAST(FILEPROPERTY(name, 'SpaceUsed') AS int) / 128 AS free_mb, growth, is_percent_growth FROM sys.database_files;"],["Largest tables", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Largest%20tables", "snippet: SQL Server", "Rows and reserved space, in the current database. SELECT TOP 15 s.name + '.' + t.name AS table_name, SUM(p.rows) AS rows,        SUM(a.total_pages) * 8 / 1024 AS reserved_mb FROM sys.tables t JOIN sys.schemas s ON s.schema_id = t.schema_id "],["The statements that cost the most", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20statements%20that%20cost%20the%20most", "snippet: SQL Server", "From the plan cache, since the last restart. Total CPU time, calls and reads. SELECT TOP 15 qs.execution_count, qs.total_worker_time / 1000 AS cpu_ms, qs.total_logical_reads AS reads,        qs.total_elapsed_time / 1000 / qs.execution_count"],["Indexes the server wishes it had", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Indexes%20the%20server%20wishes%20it%20had", "snippet: SQL Server", "Suggestions from the optimiser. Treat them as hints: it never suggests fewer or combined indexes. SELECT TOP 15 DB_NAME(d.database_id) AS db, d.statement AS table_name, d.equality_columns, d.inequality_columns, d.included_columns,        s."],["Check a database for corruption", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20a%20database%20for%20corruption", "snippet: SQL Server", "Should run weekly. It reads everything, so not during peak hours. DBCC CHECKDB (MyDb) WITH NO_INFOMSGS, ALL_ERRORMSGS;"],["Update statistics", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Update%20statistics", "snippet: SQL Server", "Outdated statistics lead to bad plans. A cheap first step when queries got slower without a change. USE MyDb; EXEC sp_updatestats;"],["Memory: the setting to check first", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Memory%3A%20the%20setting%20to%20check%20first", "snippet: SQL Server", "By default SQL Server takes all memory it can get. Leave some for Windows: on a 32 GB server, about 26 GB. EXEC sp_configure 'show advanced options', 1; RECONFIGURE; EXEC sp_configure 'max server memory (MB)'; EXEC sp_configure 'max server "],["Logins, and who is sysadmin", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Logins%2C%20and%20who%20is%20sysadmin", "snippet: SQL Server", "Fewer sysadmins than you can count on one hand is the goal. SELECT name, type_desc, is_disabled, create_date FROM sys.server_principals WHERE type IN ('S', 'U', 'G') ORDER BY name; SELECT p.name FROM sys.server_role_members m JOIN sys.serve"],["Create a login with access to one database", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20login%20with%20access%20to%20one%20database", "snippet: SQL Server", "A SQL login as owner of nothing: reader and writer only. CREATE LOGIN app WITH PASSWORD = 'change-me-Long-1'; USE MyDb; CREATE USER app FOR LOGIN app; ALTER ROLE db_datareader ADD MEMBER app; ALTER ROLE db_datawriter ADD MEMBER app;"],["After a restore: the user exists but cannot log in", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=After%20a%20restore%3A%20the%20user%20exists%20but%20cannot%20log%20in", "snippet: SQL Server", "The database user points at a login ID from the old server. Reconnect it. USE MyDb; ALTER USER app WITH LOGIN = app;"],["Agent jobs that failed", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Agent%20jobs%20that%20failed", "snippet: SQL Server", "The last day of job history, failures only. SELECT j.name, h.step_name, h.run_date, h.run_time, LEFT(h.message, 200) AS message FROM msdb.dbo.sysjobhistory h JOIN msdb.dbo.sysjobs j ON j.job_id = h.job_id WHERE h.run_status = 0 AND h.run_da"],["Read the error log", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20the%20error%20log", "snippet: SQL Server", "The current log, filtered for a word. EXEC xp_readerrorlog 0, 1, N'error'; EXEC xp_readerrorlog 0, 1, N'Login failed';"],["Maintenance without writing it yourself", "sql-server-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Maintenance%20without%20writing%20it%20yourself", "snippet: SQL Server", "The free maintenance scripts by Ola Hallengren are the de facto standard for backups, integrity checks and index care. -- https://ola.hallengren.com EXEC dbo.DatabaseBackup @Databases = 'USER_DATABASES', @Directory = 'D:\\Backup', @BackupTyp"],["3-2-1 rule", "glossary.html#3-2-1-rule", "glossary", "Three copies of the data, on two different systems, one of them outside the building. The current form adds one copy that cannot be changed and zero errors when restoring. Check a plan against it"],["ACL (file)", "glossary.html#acl-file", "glossary", "An access control list on a file or folder: permissions for additional users and groups beyond the owner, the group and everyone else. On Linux set with setfacl, on Windows it is how NTFS permissions "],["AllowedIPs", "glossary.html#allowedips", "glossary", "The WireGuard setting that confuses everybody. For outgoing packets it is a routing table (send these addresses to this peer), for incoming ones a filter (accept only these source addresses from this "],["APIPA", "glossary.html#apipa", "glossary", "The 169.254.x.x address a device gives itself when it asked for an address by DHCP and nobody answered. It is a symptom, not a configuration: the problem sits between the device and the DHCP server."],["ARP", "glossary.html#arp", "glossary", "Address Resolution Protocol. How a device finds the hardware (MAC) address that belongs to an IP address in its own network. The ARP table on a router is where you look up which MAC has which address."],["Bug check", "glossary.html#bug-check", "glossary", "The proper name of a Windows blue screen: the kernel found a condition it cannot safely continue from and stopped. The stop code says which. Look up a stop code"],["Checkpoint", "glossary.html#checkpoint", "glossary", "Hyper-V's word for a snapshot of a virtual machine. Useful right before a change, a liability when forgotten. See Snapshot."],["Cron", "glossary.html#cron", "glossary", "The classic Unix scheduler. A line of five time fields and a command. Jobs run with almost no environment, which is why scripts that work by hand fail in cron."],["CSR", "glossary.html#csr", "glossary", "Certificate signing request. The file you send to a certificate authority: your public key and the names you want in the certificate, signed with your private key. The private key stays with you. Deco"],["DHCP relay", "glossary.html#dhcp-relay", "glossary", "A setting on the gateway of a network that forwards address requests to a DHCP server in another network. Without it, only devices in the same segment as the server get an address. On Cisco it is call"],["DMZ", "glossary.html#dmz", "glossary", "A network zone for systems that must be reachable from the internet, separated from the internal network by the firewall so that a break-in there does not lead straight inside."],["err-disabled", "glossary.html#err-disabled", "glossary", "A switch port the switch shut down by itself because a protection was triggered: a loop, too many MAC addresses, a rogue DHCP server. The port stays off until someone fixes the cause and re-enables it"],["Exit code", "glossary.html#exit-code", "glossary", "The number a program returns when it ends. Zero means success, anything else an error, by convention. Scripts and schedulers judge a job by this number alone. Robocopy is the famous exception: its cod"],["GFS (grandfather-father-son)", "glossary.html#gfs-grandfather-father-son", "glossary", "A retention scheme for backups: keep daily copies for a short time, weekly ones for longer, monthly ones for longer still. It reaches far back without keeping every day."],["Hot spare", "glossary.html#hot-spare", "glossary", "A disk that sits unused in an array and takes over automatically when another disk fails, so the rebuild starts at once instead of when someone arrives with a replacement."],["Hypervisor", "glossary.html#hypervisor", "glossary", "The software that runs virtual machines and shares the hardware between them: Hyper-V, VMware ESXi, Proxmox VE with KVM, and others."],["Inode", "glossary.html#inode", "glossary", "The record a Linux file system keeps for every file. A file system has a fixed number of them, so millions of tiny files can make a disk \"full\" while gigabytes are free. Check with df -i."],["Intermediate certificate", "glossary.html#intermediate-certificate", "glossary", "The certificate between a server's own certificate and the root that clients trust. The server has to send it along, otherwise clients that have never seen it reject the connection. Check a chain"],["iowait", "glossary.html#iowait", "glossary", "The share of time a processor sat idle because it was waiting for a disk. High iowait with low CPU use means the storage is the bottleneck. Walkthrough"],["Journal (systemd)", "glossary.html#journal-systemd", "glossary", "The log that systemd keeps for all services and the kernel, read with journalctl. It replaces or supplements the text files in /var/log on current Linux systems. Cheat sheet"],["Load average", "glossary.html#load-average", "glossary", "Three numbers from uptime: how many processes were running or waiting, averaged over 1, 5 and 15 minutes. It only means something compared with the number of processor cores."],["LVM", "glossary.html#lvm", "glossary", "Logical Volume Manager. A layer between disks and file systems on Linux that lets you grow volumes, add disks to a pool and take snapshots without repartitioning. Cheat sheet"],["MAC address", "glossary.html#mac-address", "glossary", "The hardware address of a network interface, six bytes written in hex. Switches forward by it. The first half identifies the manufacturer."],["MTU", "glossary.html#mtu", "glossary", "Maximum transmission unit: the largest packet a link carries, 1500 bytes on Ethernet. When a tunnel or a DSL line makes it smaller and something blocks the messages that would say so, small transfers "],["NAT", "glossary.html#nat", "glossary", "Network address translation. A router rewrites addresses so that many devices with private addresses share one public one, or so that a port on the public address leads to an internal machine (a port "],["OOM killer", "glossary.html#oom-killer", "glossary", "The part of the Linux kernel that ends a process when memory has run out completely. It picks what frees the most, which is not always what caused the problem. It leaves a line in the kernel log."],["Pending sector", "glossary.html#pending-sector", "glossary", "A sector a disk could not read and is waiting to retry or replace. Counted in SMART attribute 197. Above zero, files in those sectors may already be damaged. Read SMART output"],["PoE", "glossary.html#poe", "glossary", "Power over Ethernet. The switch powers a device through the network cable: access points, phones, cameras. Every switch has a total budget in watts that all ports share."],["Quorum", "glossary.html#quorum", "glossary", "The majority a cluster needs before it may act. It stops the two halves of a split cluster from both changing the same data. A two-node cluster needs a third vote from somewhere."],["RAID", "glossary.html#raid", "glossary", "Several disks combined so that one or more can fail without losing data or stopping the system. It protects against a dead disk and against nothing else. RAID calculator"],["Reallocated sector", "glossary.html#reallocated-sector", "glossary", "A damaged sector that a disk has replaced with a spare one. Counted in SMART attribute 5. A few that do not grow can be lived with, a rising number means the disk is failing."],["Resilver", "glossary.html#resilver", "glossary", "What ZFS calls rebuilding: copying data onto a new disk after a replacement so the pool is redundant again."],["Reverse proxy", "glossary.html#reverse-proxy", "glossary", "A web server that takes requests from the internet and passes them to an application behind it. It terminates HTTPS, can serve several applications under one address, and is why a 502 means \"the thing"],["SAN (certificate)", "glossary.html#san-certificate", "glossary", "Subject alternative name. The list of host names and addresses a certificate is valid for. Browsers look only here and ignore the older common name field."],["Scrub", "glossary.html#scrub", "glossary", "A background pass in which a storage system reads every block and compares it with its checksum, repairing from redundancy what does not match. How silent corruption gets found before it matters."],["setgid", "glossary.html#setgid", "glossary", "A permission bit. On a folder it makes new files inherit the folder's group, which is what makes shared folders work on Linux. On a program it runs the program with its group's rights."],["Shebang", "glossary.html#shebang", "glossary", "The first line of a script, starting with #!, that names the interpreter to run it with. #!/usr/bin/env bash finds Bash wherever it is installed."],["SMART", "glossary.html#smart", "glossary", "The health record every disk keeps about itself: counters for errors, wear, temperature and running time, and the results of its self-tests. Read with smartctl. SMART reader"],["Snapshot", "glossary.html#snapshot", "glossary", "A frozen view of a disk or virtual machine at one moment, made by keeping the old blocks when something changes. Instant and cheap, and stored in the same place as the original, which is why it is not"],["Spanning tree", "glossary.html#spanning-tree", "glossary", "The protocol that lets switches detect loops in the cabling and block the redundant link, so that one misplaced patch cable does not take the network down."],["Spooler", "glossary.html#spooler", "glossary", "The Windows service that takes print jobs from applications and feeds them to the printer. When printing hangs for everyone on a machine, restarting it is the first step."],["Steal time", "glossary.html#steal-time", "glossary", "Processor time a virtual machine wanted and the hypervisor gave to someone else. High values mean the host is overbooked, and nothing inside the VM can fix it."],["Stop code", "glossary.html#stop-code", "glossary", "The number on a Windows blue screen that says why the system stopped, such as 0x0000007E. Stop code lookup"],["Swap", "glossary.html#swap", "glossary", "Disk space used as overflow when memory runs out. A little is harmless. A server that actively swaps in and out is slow in every way at once."],["systemd unit", "glossary.html#systemd-unit", "glossary", "A file that tells systemd how to run something: a service, a timer, a mount. Changes belong in an override created with systemctl edit, which survives package updates."],["Thin provisioning", "glossary.html#thin-provisioning", "glossary", "Giving a virtual disk or a LUN more space on paper than physically exists, filling it only as data arrives. Saves space until the real storage runs full, at which point everything on it stops."],["Trunk port", "glossary.html#trunk-port", "glossary", "A switch port that carries several VLANs at once, each frame tagged with its VLAN number. Used between switches and towards access points and hypervisors."],["UPS", "glossary.html#ups", "glossary", "Uninterruptible power supply. A battery that carries equipment through short power cuts and gives servers time to shut down cleanly during long ones. The battery lasts three to four years."],["URE", "glossary.html#ure", "glossary", "Unrecoverable read error: a sector the disk cannot read back. During a RAID 5 rebuild there is no redundancy left to correct one, which is the argument for RAID 6 with large disks."],["Virtual host", "glossary.html#virtual-host", "glossary", "One web server answering for several sites, choosing by the host name in the request. Called a server block in nginx."],["VLAN", "glossary.html#vlan", "glossary", "A virtual LAN: one physical network split into separate logical ones on the switches. Devices in different VLANs can only talk through a router or firewall, which is where the rules go. Plan VLANs and"],["VLSM", "glossary.html#vlsm", "glossary", "Variable length subnet masking: cutting an address range into subnets of different sizes, each as large as its segment needs, instead of equal blocks."],["WireGuard", "glossary.html#wireguard", "glossary", "A modern VPN protocol with very little configuration: a key pair per device and a list of allowed addresses per peer. It is silent when something is wrong, which makes troubleshooting its own skill. C"],["ZFS", "glossary.html#zfs", "glossary", "A file system and volume manager in one, with checksums on all data, snapshots, built-in RAID and replication. The basis of TrueNAS and an option on Proxmox and Ubuntu. Cheat sheet"],["Small office blueprint", "small-office-blueprint.html", "tool", "What the IT of a small office should look like: enter the number of people and how you work, and get the network layout, a sized list of what to buy and a checklist of what has to be true before you call it done. SMB network design, VLANs, firewall, switch ports, PoE budget, access points, UPS, backup, IT checklist for a small business"],["Bash and PowerShell side by side", "bash-powershell-side-by-side.html", "tool", "The same 105 everyday tasks in Bash and in PowerShell, side by side: files, text, processes, services, network, users and scripting basics. Search by what you want to do or by the command you already know. grep, find, ps, systemctl, curl equivalents: Select-String, Get-ChildItem, Get-Process, Get-Service, Invoke-WebRequest"],["Bash scripting cheat sheet", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Bash scripts that survive real use: a safe skeleton, arguments, tests, loops over files with spaces, cleanup with trap, locking, logging, retries and the mistakes ShellCheck finds."],["A skeleton that fails loudly", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20skeleton%20that%20fails%20loudly", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Stop on errors, on unset variables and on failures inside pipes. IFS without the space stops word splitting surprises. #!/usr/bin/env bash set -euo pipefail IFS=$'\\n\\t'  main() {   echo \"work goes here\" }  main \"$@\""],["What set -euo pipefail really does", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20set%20-euo%20pipefail%20really%20does", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Three switches, three kinds of silent failure they end. # -e           stop when a command fails (exit status not 0) # -u           stop when a variable is used that was never set # -o pipefail  a pipe fails if any part fails, not only the "],["Clean up, whatever happens", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Clean%20up%2C%20whatever%20happens", "snippet: Bash scripting", "The trap runs on normal exit, on errors and on Ctrl+C. tmp=$(mktemp -d) cleanup() { rm -rf \"$tmp\"; } trap cleanup EXIT"],["Tell the user which line failed", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Tell%20the%20user%20which%20line%20failed", "snippet: Bash scripting", "With set -e the script just stops. This says where. trap 'echo \"error in line $LINENO: $BASH_COMMAND\" >&2' ERR"],["Arguments with a usage message", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Arguments%20with%20a%20usage%20message", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Positional arguments with a default, and a check that enough were given. usage() { echo \"usage: $0 SOURCE [TARGET]\" >&2; exit 2; } [[ $# -ge 1 ]] || usage src=$1 dst=${2:-/backup}"],["Options with getopts", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Options%20with%20getopts", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Short options, with and without a value. verbose=0; out=\"\" while getopts \":vo:h\" opt; do   case $opt in     v) verbose=1 ;;     o) out=$OPTARG ;;     h) echo \"usage: $0 [-v] [-o file] args\"; exit 0 ;;     *) echo \"unknown option -$OPTARG\" >"],["Tests you need every day", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Tests%20you%20need%20every%20day", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Double brackets are Bash's own and do not split words. [[ -f $file ]]        # is a regular file [[ -d $dir ]]         # is a directory [[ -s $file ]]        # exists and is not empty [[ -z $var ]]         # is empty [[ -n $var ]]         #"],["Is a program installed", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20a%20program%20installed", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Before the script depends on it. command -v rsync >/dev/null || { echo \"rsync is not installed\" >&2; exit 1; }"],["Must run as root, or must not", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Must%20run%20as%20root%2C%20or%20must%20not", "snippet: Bash scripting", "EUID is 0 for root. [[ $EUID -eq 0 ]] || { echo \"run this with sudo\" >&2; exit 1; }"],["Loop over files, even with spaces in the name", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Loop%20over%20files%2C%20even%20with%20spaces%20in%20the%20name", "snippet: Bash scripting", "The glob gives one word per file. nullglob makes the loop skip when nothing matches. shopt -s nullglob for f in /var/log/myapp/*.log; do   echo \"processing $f\" done"],["Loop over what find returns, safely", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Loop%20over%20what%20find%20returns%2C%20safely", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Names are separated by a zero byte, the only character a file name cannot contain. while IFS= read -r -d '' f; do   echo \"found $f\" done < <(find /srv/data -type f -name '*.csv' -print0)"],["Read a file line by line", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20a%20file%20line%20by%20line", "snippet: Bash scripting", "IFS= keeps leading spaces, -r keeps backslashes. The || part catches a last line without newline. while IFS= read -r line || [[ -n $line ]]; do   echo \"line: $line\" done < hosts.txt"],["Read a CSV line into variables", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20a%20CSV%20line%20into%20variables", "snippet: Bash scripting", "For simple files without quoted commas. For real CSV, use Python. while IFS=, read -r name ip role; do   echo \"$name has $ip and is a $role\" done < servers.csv"],["Arrays", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Arrays", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Always quote the expansion with [@], or elements with spaces fall apart. hosts=(web01 web02 \"db 01\") hosts+=(cache01) echo \"${#hosts[@]} hosts\" for h in \"${hosts[@]}\"; do echo \"$h\"; done"],["Key and value pairs", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Key%20and%20value%20pairs", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Associative arrays, Bash 4 and newer. declare -A port=([ssh]=22 [https]=443) port[rdp]=3389 for k in \"${!port[@]}\"; do echo \"$k uses ${port[$k]}\"; done"],["String surgery without sed", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=String%20surgery%20without%20sed", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Built-in expansions for the common cases. f=/var/log/app/error.log.gz echo \"${f##*/}\"      # error.log.gz   (strip the path) echo \"${f%/*}\"       # /var/log/app   (strip the file name) echo \"${f%.gz}\"      # strip a suffix echo \"${f/error/a"],["Functions that return something", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Functions%20that%20return%20something", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Print the result and capture it. return is only for the exit status. free_gb() {   df -BG --output=avail \"$1\" | tail -n 1 | tr -dc '0-9' } if (( $(free_gb /) < 10 )); then echo \"less than 10 GB free\"; fi"],["Arithmetic", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Arithmetic", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Double parentheses for integers. Bash has no floating point: use bc or awk. count=$((count + 1)) (( count > 5 )) && echo \"more than five\" pct=$(awk \"BEGIN { printf \\\"%.1f\\\", $used / $total * 100 }\")"],["Log with a timestamp, to screen and file", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Log%20with%20a%20timestamp%2C%20to%20screen%20and%20file", "snippet: Bash scripting", "A small function, and a line that sends everything the script prints into a log as well. log() { printf '%s %s\\n' \"$(date '+%F %T')\" \"$*\"; } exec > >(tee -a /var/log/myscript.log) 2>&1 log \"started\""],["Never run twice at the same time", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Never%20run%20twice%20at%20the%20same%20time", "snippet: Bash scripting", "A lock that the kernel releases when the script ends, even if it crashes. exec 9>/var/lock/myscript.lock flock -n 9 || { echo \"already running\" >&2; exit 1; }"],["Retry something that sometimes fails", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Retry%20something%20that%20sometimes%20fails", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Five attempts with a growing pause. for attempt in 1 2 3 4 5; do   curl -fsS https://example.org/health && break   echo \"attempt $attempt failed, waiting\" >&2   sleep $((attempt * 5)) done"],["Run things in parallel", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20things%20in%20parallel", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Four at a time. Each line of the input becomes one call. xargs -P 4 -I{} ssh {} uptime < hosts.txt"],["A block of text with variables in it", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20block%20of%20text%20with%20variables%20in%20it", "snippet: Bash scripting", "A here-document. Quote the word EOF to switch the variable expansion off. cat > /etc/myapp/config.ini <<EOF [server] host = $HOSTNAME port = ${port[https]} EOF"],["Ask before doing something drastic", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Ask%20before%20doing%20something%20drastic", "snippet: Bash scripting", "Reads one answer and only goes on for y or Y. read -r -p \"Delete everything in $dir? [y/N] \" answer [[ $answer == [yY] ]] || exit 0"],["Exit codes that mean something", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Exit%20codes%20that%20mean%20something", "snippet: Bash scripting", "0 is success. Scripts called by cron or monitoring are judged by this number alone. command_that_may_fail status=$? if (( status != 0 )); then echo \"failed with $status\" >&2; exit \"$status\"; fi exit 0"],["Scripts for cron", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Scripts%20for%20cron", "snippet: Bash scripting", "cron runs with almost no environment. Set the path, use full paths for files, and write output somewhere. #!/usr/bin/env bash PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin cd /opt/myapp || exit 1 ./job.sh >> /var/log/mya"],["Find the mistakes before production does", "bash-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20the%20mistakes%20before%20production%20does", "snippet: Bash scripting", "ShellCheck reads a script and explains every risky line. The second command prints each line as it runs. shellcheck myscript.sh bash -x myscript.sh"],["PowerShell scripting cheat sheet", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "PowerShell scripts that hold up: parameters, strict mode and real error handling, objects and the pipeline, CSV and JSON, REST calls, remoting, credentials without plain text, logging and scheduled tasks."],["A script skeleton", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20script%20skeleton", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "Parameters with types, strict mode, and errors that stop the script instead of scrolling past. [CmdletBinding()] param(     [Parameter(Mandatory)] [string] $Path,     [int] $Days = 30,     [switch] $WhatIf ) Set-StrictMode -Version Latest $"],["Catch errors properly", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Catch%20errors%20properly", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "try and catch only see terminating errors. -ErrorAction Stop turns the other kind into those. try {     Get-Item 'C:\\does\\not\\exist' -ErrorAction Stop } catch [System.Management.Automation.ItemNotFoundException] {     Write-Warning \"Not the"],["Did the program I called fail", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Did%20the%20program%20I%20called%20fail", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "Cmdlets throw errors. Programs such as robocopy or git set an exit code instead. robocopy C:\\Data D:\\Backup /E if ($LASTEXITCODE -ge 8) { throw \"robocopy failed with $LASTEXITCODE\" }"],["Filter, pick, sort", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Filter%2C%20pick%2C%20sort", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "The three verbs of the pipeline. Get-Process |     Where-Object { $_.WorkingSet64 -gt 500MB } |     Sort-Object WorkingSet64 -Descending |     Select-Object Name, Id, @{ n = 'MemMB'; e = { [math]::Round($_.WorkingSet64 / 1MB) } }"],["What can this object do", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20can%20this%20object%20do", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "Shows the properties and methods of whatever comes down the pipe. Get-Service | Get-Member Get-Service | Select-Object -First 1 -Property *"],["Build your own objects", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Build%20your%20own%20objects", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "One object per result, then the usual cmdlets can export, sort and filter them. $report = foreach ($s in 'web01', 'web02') {     [pscustomobject]@{         Server = $s         Online = Test-Connection $s -Count 1 -Quiet         Checked = Ge"],["Hashtables", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Hashtables", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "Key and value pairs. [ordered] keeps the order you wrote. $port = [ordered]@{ ssh = 22; https = 443 } $port['rdp'] = 3389 foreach ($k in $port.Keys) { \"$k uses $($port[$k])\" }"],["Long commands, readable: splatting", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Long%20commands%2C%20readable%3A%20splatting", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "Put the parameters into a hashtable and pass it with @. $params = @{     Path        = 'C:\\Reports\\users.csv'     Delimiter   = ';'     Encoding    = 'UTF8'     NoTypeInformation = $true } $report | Export-Csv @params"],["Read and write CSV", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20and%20write%20CSV", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "Every row becomes an object with the column names as properties. $users = Import-Csv .\\users.csv -Delimiter ';' $users | Where-Object Department -eq 'Sales' | Export-Csv .\\sales.csv -NoTypeInformation -Encoding UTF8"],["Read and write JSON", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20and%20write%20JSON", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "Raise -Depth when writing: the default cuts nested data off at two levels. $cfg = Get-Content .\\config.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json $cfg.server.port = 8443 $cfg | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 10 | Set-Content .\\config.json -Encoding UTF8"],["Call a REST API", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Call%20a%20REST%20API", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "The answer is already converted from JSON into objects. $headers = @{ Authorization = \"Bearer $token\" } $r = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri 'https://api.example.org/v1/items' -Headers $headers -Method Get $r.items | Select-Object id, name  $body = "],["Strings", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Strings", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "Double quotes expand variables, single quotes do not. $() for anything more than a plain variable. $name = 'web01' \"Server $name has $($disk.FreeGB) GB free\" 'Costs $5'                       # literal '{0:N2} GB on {1}' -f 12.3456, $name \"a"],["Regular expressions", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Regular%20expressions", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "-match fills $Matches. Named groups make the result readable. if ('Error 0x80070005 in line 42' -match '0x(?<code>[0-9A-F]+).*line (?<line>\\d+)') {     $Matches.code     $Matches.line } Select-String -Path .\\*.log -Pattern 'timeout' | Selec"],["Dates", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Dates", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "Arithmetic, formats, and files older than a number of days. (Get-Date).AddDays(-30) Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd_HHmm' Get-ChildItem C:\\Logs -File | Where-Object LastWriteTime -lt (Get-Date).AddDays(-30) New-TimeSpan -Start $start -End (Get"],["A function that takes pipeline input", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20function%20that%20takes%20pipeline%20input", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "process runs once per object that comes in. function Get-FolderSize {     [CmdletBinding()]     param([Parameter(Mandatory, ValueFromPipeline)] [string] $Path)     process {         $sum = (Get-ChildItem $Path -Recurse -File -ErrorAction Si"],["Run on many computers at once", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20on%20many%20computers%20at%20once", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "Remoting runs the block on up to 32 machines in parallel and labels every result with the computer name. $servers = 'web01', 'web02', 'db01' Invoke-Command -ComputerName $servers -ScriptBlock {     Get-Service Spooler | Select-Object Name, "],["Do things in parallel on one machine", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Do%20things%20in%20parallel%20on%20one%20machine", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "PowerShell 7 only. $servers | ForEach-Object -Parallel {     [pscustomobject]@{ Server = $_; Up = Test-Connection $_ -Count 1 -Quiet } } -ThrottleLimit 16"],["Credentials without typing them into the script", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Credentials%20without%20typing%20them%20into%20the%20script", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "Ask once, store encrypted for this user on this machine, load later. Other users and other machines cannot read the file. Get-Credential | Export-Clixml \"$env:USERPROFILE\\svc-cred.xml\" $cred = Import-Clixml \"$env:USERPROFILE\\svc-cred.xml\" I"],["A proper secret store", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20proper%20secret%20store", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "The SecretManagement module with a local vault. Works for unattended scripts too. Install-Module Microsoft.PowerShell.SecretManagement, Microsoft.PowerShell.SecretStore -Scope CurrentUser Register-SecretVault -Name Local -ModuleName Microso"],["Write a log of everything", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Write%20a%20log%20of%20everything", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "A transcript records all output of the session, with a time stamp in the name. Start-Transcript -Path \"C:\\Logs\\job_$(Get-Date -Format yyyyMMdd_HHmm).log\" # ... the work ... Stop-Transcript"],["Retry", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Retry", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "Three attempts with a pause, and the last error is thrown on. $tries = 0 do {     try { $r = Invoke-RestMethod 'https://api.example.org/health'; break }     catch { $tries++; if ($tries -ge 3) { throw }; Start-Sleep -Seconds (5 * $tries) } "],["Run a script every night", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20a%20script%20every%20night", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "A scheduled task that runs as SYSTEM whether or not someone is logged on. $action  = New-ScheduledTaskAction -Execute 'powershell.exe' -Argument '-NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File C:\\Scripts\\nightly.ps1' $trigger = New-ScheduledTaskT"],["\"Running scripts is disabled on this system\"", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=%22Running%20scripts%20is%20disabled%20on%20this%20system%22", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "The execution policy. RemoteSigned lets your own scripts run and still asks for a signature on downloaded ones. Get-ExecutionPolicy -List Set-ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope CurrentUser Unblock-File .\\downloaded-script.ps1"],["Test before it changes anything", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Test%20before%20it%20changes%20anything", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "Most cmdlets that change things understand -WhatIf. Your own functions get it with SupportsShouldProcess. Remove-Item C:\\Temp\\* -Recurse -WhatIf  function Remove-OldLogs {     [CmdletBinding(SupportsShouldProcess)]     param([string] $Path)"],["Which version am I in", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20version%20am%20I%20in", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "5.1 is Windows PowerShell, 7 is the cross-platform one. They have separate module folders. $PSVersionTable.PSVersion $PSVersionTable.PSEdition"],["Find the mistakes before production does", "powershell-scripting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20the%20mistakes%20before%20production%20does", "snippet: PowerShell scripting", "PSScriptAnalyzer is the linter. Set-PSDebug shows each line as it runs. Install-Module PSScriptAnalyzer -Scope CurrentUser Invoke-ScriptAnalyzer .\\myscript.ps1 Set-PSDebug -Trace 1"],["Python for admins cheat sheet", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Python for system administrators, standard library first: files and folders, CSV and JSON, running commands, HTTP calls, regular expressions, arguments, logging, checking ports and doing things on many hosts at once."],["A script skeleton", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20script%20skeleton", "snippet: Python for admins", "Arguments, logging and an exit code, in the shape most admin scripts end up with anyway. #!/usr/bin/env python3 import argparse, logging, sys  def main() -> int:     p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"What this script does\")     p.add"],["A clean environment per project", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20clean%20environment%20per%20project", "snippet: Python for admins", "A virtual environment keeps packages out of the system Python. python3 -m venv .venv source .venv/bin/activate          # Windows: .venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1 pip install requests pip freeze > requirements.txt"],["Paths and files", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Paths%20and%20files", "snippet: Python for admins", "pathlib replaces most of os.path and reads better. from pathlib import Path  p = Path(\"/var/log/myapp\") for f in p.glob(\"*.log\"):     print(f.name, f.stat().st_size) text = (p / \"error.log\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") (p "],["Walk a folder tree", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Walk%20a%20folder%20tree", "snippet: Python for admins", "Every file below a folder, here the twenty largest. from pathlib import Path  files = [f for f in Path(\"/srv/data\").rglob(\"*\") if f.is_file()] for f in sorted(files, key=lambda f: f.stat().st_size, reverse=True)[:20]:     print(f\"{f.stat()."],["Files older than 30 days", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Files%20older%20than%2030%20days", "snippet: Python for admins", "Compare the modification time with now. import time from pathlib import Path  cutoff = time.time() - 30 * 86400 for f in Path(\"/var/tmp\").iterdir():     if f.is_file() and f.stat().st_mtime < cutoff:         print(\"old:\", f)      # f.unlink"],["Read a large file line by line", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20a%20large%20file%20line%20by%20line", "snippet: Python for admins", "Does not load the file into memory. with open(\"/var/log/syslog\", encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") as fh:     for line in fh:         if \"error\" in line.lower():             print(line.rstrip())"],["Read CSV", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20CSV", "snippet: Python for admins", "DictReader gives one dictionary per row, keyed by the header. utf-8-sig copes with files from Excel. import csv  with open(\"users.csv\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8-sig\") as fh:     for row in csv.DictReader(fh, delimiter=\";\"):         print"],["Write CSV", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Write%20CSV", "snippet: Python for admins", "newline=\"\" stops the empty lines on Windows. import csv  rows = [{\"host\": \"web01\", \"up\": True}, {\"host\": \"web02\", \"up\": False}] with open(\"report.csv\", \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:     w = csv.DictWriter(fh, fieldnames=[\"host\","],["Read and write JSON", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20and%20write%20JSON", "snippet: Python for admins", "indent makes the file readable for people. import json  with open(\"config.json\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:     cfg = json.load(fh) cfg[\"server\"][\"port\"] = 8443 with open(\"config.json\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:     json.dump(cfg, fh, ind"],["Run a command and read its output", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20a%20command%20and%20read%20its%20output", "snippet: Python for admins", "A list of arguments, no shell: file names with spaces and odd characters are safe. check=True raises an error when the command fails. import subprocess  r = subprocess.run([\"df\", \"-h\", \"/\"], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True, timeo"],["Run a command that may fail", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20a%20command%20that%20may%20fail", "snippet: Python for admins", "Look at the return code yourself. import subprocess  r = subprocess.run([\"systemctl\", \"is-active\", \"nginx\"], capture_output=True, text=True) if r.returncode != 0:     print(\"nginx is not running:\", r.stdout.strip())"],["HTTP without extra packages", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=HTTP%20without%20extra%20packages", "snippet: Python for admins", "urllib from the standard library, for a simple GET with a timeout. import json, urllib.request  req = urllib.request.Request(\"https://api.example.org/v1/status\", headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer TOKEN\"}) with urllib.request.urlopen(req, ti"],["HTTP with requests", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=HTTP%20with%20requests", "snippet: Python for admins", "The third-party package everybody uses. Always set a timeout: the default is to wait for ever. import requests  r = requests.get(\"https://api.example.org/v1/items\", headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer TOKEN\"}, timeout=10) r.raise_for_status()"],["Regular expressions", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Regular%20expressions", "snippet: Python for admins", "Compile once, name the groups. import re  pat = re.compile(r\"Failed password for (?:invalid user )?(?P<user>\\S+) from (?P<ip>\\S+)\") m = pat.search(\"Failed password for root from 203.0.113.5 port 22 ssh2\") if m:     print(m[\"user\"], m[\"ip\"])"],["Count things", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Count%20things", "snippet: Python for admins", "Counter is the tool for \"top ten of anything\". from collections import Counter  ips = Counter() with open(\"access.log\", encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") as fh:     for line in fh:         ips[line.split(\" \", 1)[0]] += 1 for ip, n in ips."],["Dates and times", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Dates%20and%20times", "snippet: Python for admins", "Always work in UTC inside the script, and convert when printing. from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone  now = datetime.now(timezone.utc) print(now.isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\")) print((now - timedelta(days=30)).strftime(\"%Y-%m-"],["IP addresses and networks", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=IP%20addresses%20and%20networks", "snippet: Python for admins", "The ipaddress module knows subnets, so you do not have to. import ipaddress  net = ipaddress.ip_network(\"10.87.30.0/24\") print(net.num_addresses, net.netmask, net.broadcast_address) print(ipaddress.ip_address(\"10.87.30.77\") in net) print(ip"],["Is a port open", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20a%20port%20open", "snippet: Python for admins", "A TCP connection with a timeout. import socket  def port_open(host: str, port: int, timeout: float = 3.0) -> bool:     try:         with socket.create_connection((host, port), timeout=timeout):             return True     except OSError:   "],["Do it on many hosts at once", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Do%20it%20on%20many%20hosts%20at%20once", "snippet: Python for admins", "A thread pool for work that mostly waits on the network. from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor import socket  def check(host):     try:         with socket.create_connection((host, 22), timeout=3):             return host, True "],["Run a command over SSH", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20a%20command%20over%20SSH", "snippet: Python for admins", "With the ssh program that is already there, and keys. For more than this, look at the packages paramiko or fabric. import subprocess  def ssh(host, command):     r = subprocess.run([\"ssh\", \"-o\", \"BatchMode=yes\", \"-o\", \"ConnectTimeout=5\", ho"],["Secrets from the environment, not from the code", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Secrets%20from%20the%20environment%2C%20not%20from%20the%20code", "snippet: Python for admins", "Set the variable outside the script. Fail clearly when it is missing. import os, sys  token = os.environ.get(\"API_TOKEN\") if not token:     sys.exit(\"API_TOKEN is not set\")"],["Checksum of a file", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Checksum%20of%20a%20file", "snippet: Python for admins", "Read in pieces, so large files do not fill the memory. import hashlib  def sha256(path):     h = hashlib.sha256()     with open(path, \"rb\") as fh:         for chunk in iter(lambda: fh.read(1024 * 1024), b\"\"):             h.update(chunk)    "],["Pack and unpack archives", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Pack%20and%20unpack%20archives", "snippet: Python for admins", "shutil does zip and tar in one line each. import shutil  shutil.make_archive(\"/backup/site-2026-10-05\", \"gztar\", root_dir=\"/var/www/site\") shutil.unpack_archive(\"/backup/site-2026-10-05.tar.gz\", \"/tmp/restore\") total, used, free = shutil.di"],["Send a mail", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Send%20a%20mail", "snippet: Python for admins", "Through a server that accepts mail from this machine. With authentication, add server.login(). import smtplib from email.message import EmailMessage  msg = EmailMessage() msg[\"From\"] = \"scripts@example.org\" msg[\"To\"] = \"admin@example.org\" m"],["Retry with a growing pause", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Retry%20with%20a%20growing%20pause", "snippet: Python for admins", "A small helper for calls that sometimes fail. import time  def retry(fn, attempts=4, wait=2.0):     for n in range(1, attempts + 1):         try:             return fn()         except Exception as exc:             if n == attempts:        "],["A small database in one file", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20small%20database%20in%20one%20file", "snippet: Python for admins", "SQLite is built in. Good for inventories, state between runs and anything that outgrew a CSV file. import sqlite3  db = sqlite3.connect(\"inventory.db\") db.execute(\"create table if not exists host (name text primary key, ip text, seen text)\""],["Read YAML", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20YAML", "snippet: Python for admins", "Not in the standard library: pip install pyyaml. Always safe_load, never load. import yaml  with open(\"config.yaml\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:     cfg = yaml.safe_load(fh) print(cfg[\"server\"][\"port\"])"],["Useful one-liners from the shell", "python-for-admins-cheat-sheet.html?q=Useful%20one-liners%20from%20the%20shell", "snippet: Python for admins", "A web server for the current folder, pretty JSON, and a quick calculation. python3 -m http.server 8000 cat data.json | python3 -m json.tool python3 -c \"print(2**32 - 2)\""],["Log reader", "log-reader.html", "tool", "Drop a web server access log, an auth.log or a syslog and get the summary: password guessing and whether it worked, scanners and what they found, error bursts, out-of-memory kills and disk errors. nginx, Apache, sshd brute force, fail2ban, 404 scanners, 502 errors, OOM killer"],["SMART reader", "smart-reader.html", "tool", "Paste the output of smartctl -a and read it in plain words: is the disk failing, which attributes matter, what the numbers mean and whether it is the disk or the cable. Hard disks, SATA SSDs and NVMe. reallocated sectors, pending sectors, CRC errors, wear, NVMe percentage used"],["A snapshot is not a backup", "snapshot-is-not-a-backup.html", "explainer", "Why a snapshot, RAID or a replica does not replace a backup: eight things that go wrong, and which protection survives each of them, as a table you can click through."],["Proxmox VE cheat sheet", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Proxmox VE from the shell: virtual machines and containers, snapshots, backup and restore with vzdump, storage, cluster and quorum, migration, and what to check when the web interface is gone."],["Version of every component", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Version%20of%20every%20component", "snippet: Proxmox", "What support will ask for first. pveversion -v"],["List virtual machines and containers", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20virtual%20machines%20and%20containers", "snippet: Proxmox", "With ID, name, state and memory. qm list pct list"],["Start, shut down, stop", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Start%2C%20shut%20down%2C%20stop", "snippet: Proxmox", "shutdown asks the guest politely, stop pulls the plug. qm start 100 qm shutdown 100 qm stop 100"],["Show the configuration of a VM", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Show%20the%20configuration%20of%20a%20VM", "snippet: Proxmox", "Disks, network, CPU, memory, boot order. The file is /etc/pve/qemu-server/100.conf. qm config 100"],["\"VM is locked\"", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=%22VM%20is%20locked%22", "snippet: Proxmox", "A backup or snapshot that died left its lock behind. Make sure no such task is still running, then unlock. qm unlock 100 pct unlock 101"],["Get into a container without its password", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Get%20into%20a%20container%20without%20its%20password", "snippet: Proxmox", "Opens a root shell inside. pct enter 101"],["Snapshot before a change", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Snapshot%20before%20a%20change", "snippet: Proxmox", "With memory state if you add --vmstate 1. qm snapshot 100 before-upgrade --description \"before upgrade to 12.4\" qm listsnapshot 100"],["Roll back, or delete the snapshot", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Roll%20back%2C%20or%20delete%20the%20snapshot", "snippet: Proxmox", "Rollback throws away everything since the snapshot. Delete snapshots when the change has proven itself: they are not backups and they grow. qm rollback 100 before-upgrade qm delsnapshot 100 before-upgrade"],["Back up one guest now", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Back%20up%20one%20guest%20now", "snippet: Proxmox", "Snapshot mode backs up a running VM. zstd is fast and compresses well. vzdump 100 --storage backup --mode snapshot --compress zstd --notes-template '{{guestname}} manual'"],["Restore a VM or a container", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Restore%20a%20VM%20or%20a%20container", "snippet: Proxmox", "To a new ID if the old one still exists. The archive name is in the storage's dump folder. qmrestore /mnt/pve/backup/dump/vzdump-qemu-100-2026_10_05-02_00_01.vma.zst 120 --storage local-lvm pct restore 121 /mnt/pve/backup/dump/vzdump-lxc-10"],["Storage: state and free space", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Storage%3A%20state%20and%20free%20space", "snippet: Proxmox", "Every configured storage with type, total and used. pvesm status"],["What is on a storage", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20is%20on%20a%20storage", "snippet: Proxmox", "Disk images, ISO files, backups. pvesm list local-lvm pvesm list backup --content backup"],["Thin pool almost full", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Thin%20pool%20almost%20full", "snippet: Proxmox", "A full thin pool pauses every VM on it. Data% and Meta% are the columns to watch. lvs -a -o lv_name,vg_name,lv_size,data_percent,metadata_percent"],["Make a disk bigger", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Make%20a%20disk%20bigger", "snippet: Proxmox", "Grows the virtual disk. The partition and file system inside the guest have to be grown as well. qm resize 100 scsi0 +20G"],["Import a disk from another hypervisor", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Import%20a%20disk%20from%20another%20hypervisor", "snippet: Proxmox", "Converts a VMDK, VHDX or raw image and attaches it as an unused disk. qm disk import 100 /mnt/import/server-disk1.vmdk local-lvm"],["Clone a template", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Clone%20a%20template", "snippet: Proxmox", "A full clone is independent of the template. qm clone 9000 120 --name web01 --full"],["Cloud-init settings for a clone", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Cloud-init%20settings%20for%20a%20clone", "snippet: Proxmox", "Address, user and SSH key before the first boot. qm set 120 --ipconfig0 ip=10.87.20.31/24,gw=10.87.20.1 --ciuser admin --sshkeys ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub"],["Is the guest agent answering", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20guest%20agent%20answering", "snippet: Proxmox", "Needed for clean shutdowns, consistent snapshots and the IP addresses in the web interface. qm agent 100 ping qm guest cmd 100 network-get-interfaces"],["Move a running VM to another node", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Move%20a%20running%20VM%20to%20another%20node", "snippet: Proxmox", "Live migration. With local disks add --with-local-disks. qm migrate 100 node2 --online"],["Cluster and quorum", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Cluster%20and%20quorum", "snippet: Proxmox", "Quorate: Yes is what you need. Without quorum nothing can be changed and no VM can be started. pvecm status pvecm nodes"],["One node left and no quorum", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=One%20node%20left%20and%20no%20quorum", "snippet: Proxmox", "Tells the remaining node that one vote is enough. Only when you are sure the other nodes are really off, otherwise two halves change the same data. pvecm expected 1"],["High availability state", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=High%20availability%20state", "snippet: Proxmox", "Which guests are managed and where they run. ha-manager status"],["The web interface is not reachable", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20web%20interface%20is%20not%20reachable", "snippet: Proxmox", "The VMs keep running. Check the services, then restart the web part. systemctl status pve-cluster pvedaemon pveproxy pvestatd systemctl restart pveproxy pvedaemon"],["Grey question marks in the web interface", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Grey%20question%20marks%20in%20the%20web%20interface", "snippet: Proxmox", "The status service hangs, usually on a storage that does not answer, such as an NFS share that is gone. systemctl restart pvestatd pvesm status"],["Update a node", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Update%20a%20node", "snippet: Proxmox", "full-upgrade, never plain upgrade: Proxmox needs packages replaced. Migrate guests away first in a cluster. apt update apt full-upgrade"],["A container does not start", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20container%20does%20not%20start", "snippet: Proxmox", "Runs the start in the foreground with the real error message. pct start 101 --debug"],["Logs", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Logs", "snippet: Proxmox", "Tasks of the web interface, the cluster file system and one VM's start. journalctl -u pvedaemon -u pveproxy --since \"1 hour ago\" journalctl -u pve-cluster -u corosync --since \"1 hour ago\" tail -n 50 /var/log/pve/tasks/active"],["Apply a network change without rebooting", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=Apply%20a%20network%20change%20without%20rebooting", "snippet: Proxmox", "After editing /etc/network/interfaces. A typo here cuts you off: have the console at hand. ifreload -a"],["How fast is this node", "proxmox-cheat-sheet.html?q=How%20fast%20is%20this%20node", "snippet: Proxmox", "CPU, disk sync rate and DNS in one short benchmark. pveperf /var/lib/vz"],["Hyper-V cheat sheet", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Hyper-V with PowerShell: virtual machines, checkpoints and the files they leave behind, virtual disks, switches and VLANs, export and import, live migration, replication and a VM that hangs in Stopping."],["All VMs with state and load", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=All%20VMs%20with%20state%20and%20load", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Uptime resets on restart, Status shows problems such as a failed integration service. Get-VM | Sort-Object Name | Format-Table Name, State, CPUUsage, @{n='MemGB';e={[math]::Round($_.MemoryAssigned/1GB,1)}}, Uptime, Status"],["Start, shut down, turn off", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Start%2C%20shut%20down%2C%20turn%20off", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Stop-VM asks the guest to shut down. -TurnOff is the power button. Start-VM SRV01 Stop-VM SRV01 Stop-VM SRV01 -TurnOff"],["A VM hangs in Stopping or Starting", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20VM%20hangs%20in%20Stopping%20or%20Starting", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Every running VM has its own worker process. End the one that belongs to this VM. $id = (Get-VM SRV01).Id Get-CimInstance Win32_Process -Filter \"Name='vmwp.exe'\" | Where-Object CommandLine -match $id | ForEach-Object { Stop-Process -Id $_.P"],["Checkpoint before a change", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Checkpoint%20before%20a%20change", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Production checkpoints use the backup mechanism inside the guest and are the safe default for servers. Set-VM SRV01 -CheckpointType Production Checkpoint-VM -Name SRV01 -SnapshotName \"before update\""],["All checkpoints on the host, oldest first", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=All%20checkpoints%20on%20the%20host%2C%20oldest%20first", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Checkpoints are not backups. Anything older than a few days is forgotten and growing. Get-VM | Get-VMSnapshot | Sort-Object CreationTime | Format-Table VMName, Name, CreationTime, SnapshotType"],["Go back to a checkpoint", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Go%20back%20to%20a%20checkpoint", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Everything since then is lost. Restore-VMSnapshot -VMName SRV01 -Name \"before update\" -Confirm:$false"],["Delete a checkpoint", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Delete%20a%20checkpoint", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Starts a merge of the AVHDX file into its parent, which needs time and free disk space. Wait for it to finish. Remove-VMSnapshot -VMName SRV01 -Name \"before update\" Get-VM SRV01 | Select-Object Name, Status"],["Leftover AVHDX files", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Leftover%20AVHDX%20files", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Differencing disks that are still in use although no checkpoint is shown. Typical after a failed backup. Get-VM | Get-VMHardDiskDrive | Where-Object Path -like '*.avhdx' | Format-Table VMName, Path"],["Details of a virtual disk", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Details%20of%20a%20virtual%20disk", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Type, maximum size, real size on disk and the parent of a differencing disk. Get-VHD -Path 'D:\\VMs\\SRV01\\disk0.vhdx' | Format-List VhdType, @{n='SizeGB';e={$_.Size/1GB}}, @{n='FileGB';e={[math]::Round($_.FileSize/1GB,1)}}, ParentPath, Attac"],["Make a virtual disk bigger", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Make%20a%20virtual%20disk%20bigger", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Works while the VM runs if the disk hangs on a SCSI controller. Then extend the volume inside the guest. Resize-VHD -Path 'D:\\VMs\\SRV01\\disk0.vhdx' -SizeBytes 200GB"],["Shrink the file of a dynamic disk", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Shrink%20the%20file%20of%20a%20dynamic%20disk", "snippet: Hyper-V", "The VM must be off or the disk detached. Frees space that the guest deleted. Optimize-VHD -Path 'D:\\VMs\\SRV01\\disk0.vhdx' -Mode Full"],["Convert a disk", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Convert%20a%20disk", "snippet: Hyper-V", "From VHD to VHDX, or from dynamic to fixed. Writes a new file. Convert-VHD -Path 'D:\\Old\\disk0.vhd' -DestinationPath 'D:\\VMs\\SRV01\\disk0.vhdx' -VHDType Dynamic"],["Create a VM", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20VM", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Generation 2 with a new disk, connected to a switch. New-VM -Name SRV02 -Generation 2 -MemoryStartupBytes 4GB -NewVHDPath 'D:\\VMs\\SRV02\\disk0.vhdx' -NewVHDSizeBytes 80GB -SwitchName 'External' Set-VMProcessor SRV02 -Count 4 Add-VMDvdDrive S"],["A Linux VM does not boot from the ISO", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20Linux%20VM%20does%20not%20boot%20from%20the%20ISO", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Generation 2 uses Secure Boot with the Windows template by default. Set-VMFirmware SRV02 -SecureBootTemplate MicrosoftUEFICertificateAuthority"],["Memory: fixed or dynamic", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Memory%3A%20fixed%20or%20dynamic", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Databases and domain controllers are happier with fixed memory. Set-VMMemory SRV01 -DynamicMemoryEnabled $false -StartupBytes 8GB Set-VMMemory SRV02 -DynamicMemoryEnabled $true -MinimumBytes 2GB -StartupBytes 4GB -MaximumBytes 8GB"],["Virtual switches", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Virtual%20switches", "snippet: Hyper-V", "External reaches the network, Internal only host and VMs, Private only VMs. Get-VMSwitch | Format-Table Name, SwitchType, NetAdapterInterfaceDescription New-VMSwitch -Name 'External' -NetAdapterName 'Ethernet 2' -AllowManagementOS $true"],["Put a VM's network card into a VLAN", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Put%20a%20VM%27s%20network%20card%20into%20a%20VLAN", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Tags the traffic of that card. The physical switch port must be a trunk that carries the VLAN. Set-VMNetworkAdapterVlan -VMName SRV01 -Access -VlanId 30 Get-VMNetworkAdapterVlan -VMName SRV01"],["Run a command inside a VM without network", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20a%20command%20inside%20a%20VM%20without%20network", "snippet: Hyper-V", "PowerShell Direct, for Windows guests on the same host. Invoke-Command -VMName SRV01 -Credential (Get-Credential) -ScriptBlock { ipconfig /all } Enter-PSSession -VMName SRV01 -Credential (Get-Credential)"],["Copy a file into a VM", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Copy%20a%20file%20into%20a%20VM", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Needs the Guest Service Interface, which is off by default. Enable-VMIntegrationService -VMName SRV01 -Name 'Guest Service Interface' Copy-VMFile SRV01 -SourcePath 'C:\\Temp\\fix.msi' -DestinationPath 'C:\\Temp\\fix.msi' -FileSource Host -Creat"],["Export and import a VM", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Export%20and%20import%20a%20VM", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Export writes configuration and disks to a folder. Import with a new ID makes a copy next to the original. Export-VM -Name SRV01 -Path 'E:\\Export' Import-VM -Path 'E:\\Export\\SRV01\\Virtual Machines\\GUID.vmcx' -Copy -GenerateNewId -VirtualMac"],["Move a running VM", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Move%20a%20running%20VM", "snippet: Hyper-V", "To another host, or only its files to another disk. Move-VM SRV01 -DestinationHost HV02 -IncludeStorage -DestinationStoragePath 'D:\\VMs\\SRV01' Move-VMStorage SRV01 -DestinationStoragePath 'E:\\VMs\\SRV01'"],["Is replication healthy", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20replication%20healthy", "snippet: Hyper-V", "State and health of every replicated VM, and how far behind the replica is. Get-VMReplication | Format-Table VMName, State, Health, Mode, FrequencySec, PrimaryServer, ReplicaServer Measure-VMReplication | Format-Table VMName, Health, LReplT"],["Integration services of a VM", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Integration%20services%20of%20a%20VM", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Heartbeat, time sync, shutdown, backup. A service that is not OK explains failed backups and unclean shutdowns. Get-VMIntegrationService -VMName SRV01 | Format-Table Name, Enabled, PrimaryStatusDescription"],["Why did it fail: the Hyper-V logs", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Why%20did%20it%20fail%3A%20the%20Hyper-V%20logs", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Management service and worker, newest first. Get-WinEvent -LogName Microsoft-Windows-Hyper-V-VMMS-Admin -MaxEvents 30 | Format-Table TimeCreated, Id, LevelDisplayName, Message -Wrap Get-WinEvent -LogName Microsoft-Windows-Hyper-V-Worker-Adm"],["Is the host overcommitted", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20host%20overcommitted", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Logical processors and memory of the host against what the VMs were given. Get-VMHost | Format-List LogicalProcessorCount, @{n='HostMemGB';e={[math]::Round($_.MemoryCapacity/1GB)}} Get-VM | Measure-Object ProcessorCount -Sum | Select-Object"],["Hyper-V inside a VM", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Hyper-V%20inside%20a%20VM", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Nested virtualisation, for labs. The VM must be off. Set-VMProcessor SRV02 -ExposeVirtualizationExtensions $true"],["Failover cluster at a glance", "hyper-v-cheat-sheet.html?q=Failover%20cluster%20at%20a%20glance", "snippet: Hyper-V", "Nodes, cluster shared volumes and where each VM role runs. Get-ClusterNode Get-ClusterSharedVolume | Format-Table Name, State, OwnerNode Get-ClusterGroup | Where-Object GroupType -eq 'VirtualMachine' | Format-Table Name, OwnerNode, State"],["VMware ESXi cheat sheet", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "VMware ESXi from the host shell and with PowerCLI: list and control virtual machines, end a VM that hangs, find forgotten snapshots, datastores and storage paths, networking, esxtop, logs and maintenance mode."],["Version and build of the host", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Version%20and%20build%20of%20the%20host", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "The build number decides which patches apply. esxcli system version get"],["List the VMs on this host", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20the%20VMs%20on%20this%20host", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "With their ID, name and the path of the configuration file. vim-cmd vmsvc/getallvms"],["Power state, power on, shut down", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Power%20state%2C%20power%20on%2C%20shut%20down", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "shutdown needs VMware Tools in the guest, off is the power switch. vim-cmd vmsvc/power.getstate 12 vim-cmd vmsvc/power.on 12 vim-cmd vmsvc/power.shutdown 12 vim-cmd vmsvc/power.off 12"],["A VM hangs and will not power off", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20VM%20hangs%20and%20will%20not%20power%20off", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Find its world ID, then end it. Try soft first, then hard, force only as the last step. esxcli vm process list esxcli vm process kill --type=soft --world-id=1234567"],["Snapshots of a VM", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Snapshots%20of%20a%20VM", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Shows the tree with names and dates. vim-cmd vmsvc/snapshot.get 12"],["Create and remove snapshots", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20and%20remove%20snapshots", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "The two zeros mean no memory state and no quiescing. removeall merges everything back. vim-cmd vmsvc/snapshot.create 12 \"before upgrade\" \"by admin\" 0 0 vim-cmd vmsvc/snapshot.removeall 12"],["Snapshot files nobody remembers", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Snapshot%20files%20nobody%20remembers", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Delta files on the datastores. Large and old ones belong to snapshots that should have been removed long ago. find /vmfs/volumes/ -name \"*-delta.vmdk\" -o -name \"*-sesparse.vmdk\" | xargs ls -lh"],["Datastores and free space", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Datastores%20and%20free%20space", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "A full datastore stops every VM that has a thin disk or a snapshot on it. esxcli storage filesystem list df -h"],["Storage devices and paths", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Storage%20devices%20and%20paths", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Dead paths and devices in a state other than on point at cabling, zoning or the array. esxcli storage core device list | grep -E \"Display Name|Status:|Is SSD\" esxcli storage core path list | grep -E \"Runtime Name|State:\""],["Rescan storage", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Rescan%20storage", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "After new LUNs were presented or a path came back. esxcli storage core adapter rescan --all"],["Give back deleted space on a thin LUN", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Give%20back%20deleted%20space%20on%20a%20thin%20LUN", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Tells the array which blocks are free. esxcli storage vmfs unmap -l datastore1"],["Copy or convert a virtual disk", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Copy%20or%20convert%20a%20virtual%20disk", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Clones to a new file, here as thin. Also the way to repair a disk whose descriptor is fine. vmkfstools -i /vmfs/volumes/datastore1/vm/vm.vmdk /vmfs/volumes/datastore2/vm/vm.vmdk -d thin"],["Network cards and their link", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Network%20cards%20and%20their%20link", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Speed, duplex and whether the link is up. esxcli network nic list"],["Virtual switches, port groups, VMkernel addresses", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Virtual%20switches%2C%20port%20groups%2C%20VMkernel%20addresses", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "What is connected to which uplink, and the addresses of the host. esxcli network vswitch standard list esxcli network vswitch standard portgroup list esxcli network ip interface ipv4 get"],["Test the storage or vMotion network", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Test%20the%20storage%20or%20vMotion%20network", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "From a specific VMkernel port. 8972 with -d tests whether jumbo frames really pass end to end. vmkping -I vmk1 10.0.50.20 vmkping -I vmk1 -s 8972 -d 10.0.50.20"],["Maintenance mode", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Maintenance%20mode", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Enter before patching or hardware work, leave afterwards. esxcli system maintenanceMode set --enable true esxcli system maintenanceMode get esxcli system maintenanceMode set --enable false"],["Host shows as not responding in vCenter", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Host%20shows%20as%20not%20responding%20in%20vCenter", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "The VMs usually still run. Restart the management agents, not the host. /etc/init.d/hostd restart /etc/init.d/vpxa restart"],["The logs that matter", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20logs%20that%20matter", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Kernel and storage, the host agent, events, and the log of one VM in its own folder. tail -n 100 /var/log/vmkernel.log tail -n 100 /var/log/hostd.log tail -n 50 /var/log/vobd.log tail -n 100 /vmfs/volumes/datastore1/vm/vmware.log"],["esxtop: where is the bottleneck", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=esxtop%3A%20where%20is%20the%20bottleneck", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Start it, then press a key for the view. The comments name the columns worth reading. esxtop # c  CPU      %RDY above 10 per vCPU: the VM waits for a physical core. %CSTP high: too many vCPUs. # m  memory   MCTLSZ above 0: ballooning. SWCUR"],["Installed patches and drivers", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Installed%20patches%20and%20drivers", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "The list of VIBs with vendor and version. esxcli software vib list | less"],["Time and NTP", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=Time%20and%20NTP", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Wrong time on the host breaks logons and certificates in the guests that sync from it. esxcli system time get esxcli system ntp get"],["PowerCLI: connect", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=PowerCLI%3A%20connect", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Against vCenter, or a single host. Connect-VIServer vcenter.example.internal"],["PowerCLI: every snapshot with age and size", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=PowerCLI%3A%20every%20snapshot%20with%20age%20and%20size", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Snapshots older than a few days are forgotten ones. They slow the VM and fill the datastore. Get-VM | Get-Snapshot | Sort-Object Created | Format-Table VM, Name, Created, @{n='SizeGB';e={[math]::Round($_.SizeGB,1)}}"],["PowerCLI: VMs whose disks need consolidation", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=PowerCLI%3A%20VMs%20whose%20disks%20need%20consolidation", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "A snapshot was deleted but its files were not merged. Consolidate, at a quiet time. Get-VM | Where-Object { $_.ExtensionData.Runtime.ConsolidationNeeded } | Select-Object Name (Get-VM SRV01).ExtensionData.ConsolidateVMDisks()"],["PowerCLI: datastores by free space", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=PowerCLI%3A%20datastores%20by%20free%20space", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Fullest first. Get-Datastore | Sort-Object FreeSpaceGB | Format-Table Name, @{n='FreeGB';e={[math]::Round($_.FreeSpaceGB)}}, @{n='CapacityGB';e={[math]::Round($_.CapacityGB)}}"],["PowerCLI: hosts with version and state", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=PowerCLI%3A%20hosts%20with%20version%20and%20state", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Also shows hosts in maintenance mode or disconnected. Get-VMHost | Format-Table Name, ConnectionState, Version, Build, @{n='MemUsedPct';e={[math]::Round($_.MemoryUsageGB/$_.MemoryTotalGB*100)}}"],["PowerCLI: VMware Tools state", "vmware-esxi-cheat-sheet.html?q=PowerCLI%3A%20VMware%20Tools%20state", "snippet: VMware ESXi", "Guests without running tools cannot shut down cleanly or be backed up consistently. Get-VM | Select-Object Name, PowerState, @{n='Tools';e={$_.ExtensionData.Guest.ToolsStatus}} | Sort-Object Tools"],["ZFS and NAS cheat sheet", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "ZFS and NAS storage: pool health and scrubs, replacing a failed disk, datasets, snapshots and what they cost, replication with send and receive, SMART tests, and testing shares and throughput from a client."],["Is everything healthy", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20everything%20healthy", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "Prints one line when all pools are fine, details when not. zpool status -x"],["Pool layout, state and errors", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Pool%20layout%2C%20state%20and%20errors", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "READ, WRITE and CKSUM should all be 0. Checksum errors on one disk mean that disk or its cable returns wrong data. zpool status -v tank"],["Size, used, free and fragmentation", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Size%2C%20used%2C%20free%20and%20fragmentation", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "Keep pools below about 80%: beyond that, writes get slow. zpool list"],["Datasets with space", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Datasets%20with%20space", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "USED includes snapshots and children, REFER is what the dataset itself points to. zfs list -o name,used,avail,refer,mountpoint"],["Start a scrub and watch it", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Start%20a%20scrub%20and%20watch%20it", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "Reads every block and repairs from redundancy. Run monthly: it is how silent corruption gets found. zpool scrub tank zpool status tank | grep -A2 scan"],["Which physical disk is which", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20physical%20disk%20is%20which", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "Serial numbers are part of the by-id names, and on the label of the disk. ls -l /dev/disk/by-id/ | grep -v -- -part"],["Replace a failed disk", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Replace%20a%20failed%20disk", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "Take the old one offline, swap it, tell ZFS about the new one. The pool resilvers by itself. zpool offline tank ata-OLD-DISK-SERIAL zpool replace tank ata-OLD-DISK-SERIAL /dev/disk/by-id/ata-NEW-DISK-SERIAL zpool status tank"],["Create a pool", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20pool", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "A mirror of two disks, or RAID-Z2 over six. ashift=12 is right for every disk made in the last ten years and cannot be changed later. zpool create -o ashift=12 tank mirror /dev/disk/by-id/ata-DISK1 /dev/disk/by-id/ata-DISK2 zpool create -o "],["Grow a pool", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Grow%20a%20pool", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "By adding another mirror. Read the command twice: a single disk added by mistake cannot be taken out of a RAID-Z pool again. zpool add tank mirror /dev/disk/by-id/ata-DISK3 /dev/disk/by-id/ata-DISK4"],["Create a dataset with compression", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20dataset%20with%20compression", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "lz4 costs almost nothing and usually makes things faster. zfs create -o compression=lz4 -o atime=off tank/data"],["Limit and guarantee space", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Limit%20and%20guarantee%20space", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "A quota caps a dataset including its snapshots, a reservation guarantees it space. zfs set quota=500G tank/data zfs set reservation=50G tank/vm"],["Take a snapshot", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Take%20a%20snapshot", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "Instant, and free until data changes. -r includes all child datasets. zfs snapshot -r tank/data@2026-10-05-before-cleanup"],["List snapshots, oldest first", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20snapshots%2C%20oldest%20first", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "USED is what would be freed if only this snapshot were destroyed. zfs list -t snapshot -o name,used,refer,creation -s creation"],["Where did the space go", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Where%20did%20the%20space%20go", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "Splits the usage into data, snapshots, children and reservations. zfs list -o space"],["Get one file back from a snapshot", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Get%20one%20file%20back%20from%20a%20snapshot", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "Every dataset has a hidden folder with its snapshots, read-only. ls /tank/data/.zfs/snapshot/ cp /tank/data/.zfs/snapshot/2026-10-05-before-cleanup/report.xlsx /tank/data/"],["Roll a dataset back", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Roll%20a%20dataset%20back", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "Throws away everything since the snapshot. -r also destroys the newer snapshots in between. zfs rollback -r tank/data@2026-10-05-before-cleanup"],["Delete snapshots", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Delete%20snapshots", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "One, or a whole range with the percent sign. Add -n -v first to see what would go. zfs destroy tank/data@2026-09-01 zfs destroy -n -v tank/data@2026-08-01%2026-08-31"],["Replicate to another machine: first time", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Replicate%20to%20another%20machine%3A%20first%20time", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "Sends the dataset with all snapshots. This copy on another machine is what turns snapshots into a backup. zfs snapshot -r tank/data@repl-1 zfs send -R tank/data@repl-1 | ssh backup zfs receive -u backuppool/data"],["Replicate: every time after", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Replicate%3A%20every%20time%20after", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "Sends only what changed between the last common snapshot and the new one. zfs snapshot -r tank/data@repl-2 zfs send -R -i @repl-1 tank/data@repl-2 | ssh backup zfs receive -Fu backuppool/data"],["Move a pool to another machine", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Move%20a%20pool%20to%20another%20machine", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "Export cleanly, move the disks, import. Without a name, import lists what it finds. zpool export tank zpool import zpool import tank"],["What was done to this pool", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20was%20done%20to%20this%20pool", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "Every command since it was created, with date. zpool history tank | tail -n 30"],["Which disk is slow", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20disk%20is%20slow", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "Operations and throughput per disk, refreshed every two seconds. One disk far behind the others is suspicious. zpool iostat -v tank 2"],["How much memory ZFS uses", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=How%20much%20memory%20ZFS%20uses", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "The ARC cache takes free memory and gives it back. On a hypervisor, cap it so the VMs come first. arc_summary | head -n 30 echo \"options zfs zfs_arc_max=8589934592\" | sudo tee /etc/modprobe.d/zfs.conf     # 8 GB, after reboot"],["SMART: health and a long self-test", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=SMART%3A%20health%20and%20a%20long%20self-test", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "The test runs in the background for hours. Read the result with the second command. sudo smartctl -a /dev/sda sudo smartctl -t long /dev/sda sudo smartctl -l selftest /dev/sda"],["SMART health of every disk at once", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=SMART%20health%20of%20every%20disk%20at%20once", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "One line per disk. for d in /dev/sd?; do echo -n \"$d: \"; sudo smartctl -H \"$d\" | grep -E \"result|Status\"; done"],["Other NAS systems: software RAID and Btrfs", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Other%20NAS%20systems%3A%20software%20RAID%20and%20Btrfs", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "[UU] is healthy, [U_] is degraded. Btrfs has its own scrub. cat /proc/mdstat sudo btrfs scrub start /volume1 && sudo btrfs scrub status /volume1 sudo btrfs filesystem usage /volume1"],["What does the NAS offer", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20does%20the%20NAS%20offer", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "NFS exports and SMB shares, seen from a client. showmount -e nas.example.internal smbclient -L //nas.example.internal -U anna"],["Mount a share on Linux", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Mount%20a%20share%20on%20Linux", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "NFS and SMB. Put credentials for SMB into a file only root can read. sudo mount -t nfs nas.example.internal:/mnt/tank/data /mnt/data sudo mount -t cifs //nas.example.internal/data /mnt/data -o credentials=/root/.smbcred,vers=3.1.1,uid=1000"],["Is it the network or the disks", "zfs-nas-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20it%20the%20network%20or%20the%20disks", "snippet: ZFS and NAS", "iperf3 measures the network alone, fio the storage through the share. iperf3 -s                           # on the NAS iperf3 -c nas.example.internal      # on the client fio --name=seq --rw=write --bs=1M --size=2G --direct=1 --filename=/mn"],["Windows stop code lookup", "stop-code-lookup.html", "tool", "Blue screen BSOD bug check codes explained: causes and first steps"],["The 20 helpdesk tickets", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html", "page", "Password reset, cannot print, no internet, slow PC, Outlook, shared drive, MFA, VPN: what to ask, the usual fix, when to escalate"],["The Windows PC is slow", "windows-pc-slow.html", "tool", "Walkthrough: Task Manager, disk, startup programs, updates, thermal throttling, slow sign-in, system files"],["The printer does not print", "diagnose.html#printer", "tool", "Wizard: spooler, queue, wrong printer, driver errors, device, network, print server"],["0x0000000A IRQL_NOT_LESS_OR_EQUAL", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x0000000A", "stop code", "A driver or the kernel touched memory it was not allowed to touch at that moment. One of the most common stop codes."],["0x000000D1 DRIVER_IRQL_NOT_LESS_OR_EQUAL", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x000000D1", "stop code", "Like 0xA, but Windows is sure a driver did it and usually names the file."],["0x0000001E KMODE_EXCEPTION_NOT_HANDLED", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x0000001E", "stop code", "Code running in the kernel caused an error and nothing caught it."],["0x0000007E SYSTEM_THREAD_EXCEPTION_NOT_HANDLED", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x0000007E", "stop code", "A thread started by a driver crashed. The blue screen usually names the file."],["0x0000003B SYSTEM_SERVICE_EXCEPTION", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x0000003B", "stop code", "An error happened while a program was calling into the kernel."],["0x00000050 PAGE_FAULT_IN_NONPAGED_AREA", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x00000050", "stop code", "Windows looked for data in memory that should always be there, and it was not."],["0x0000001A MEMORY_MANAGEMENT", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x0000001A", "stop code", "The memory manager found its own data in a state that cannot be right."],["0x0000004E PFN_LIST_CORRUPT", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x0000004E", "stop code", "The list Windows keeps of physical memory pages is damaged."],["0x00000019 BAD_POOL_HEADER", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x00000019", "stop code", "A block of kernel memory was damaged, typically by a driver writing past the end of its own block."],["0x000000C2 BAD_POOL_CALLER", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x000000C2", "stop code", "A driver asked for kernel memory in a way that is not allowed, or freed something twice."],["0x00000139 KERNEL_SECURITY_CHECK_FAILURE", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x00000139", "stop code", "The kernel noticed that one of its data structures was damaged and stopped before more harm was done."],["0x0000013A KERNEL_MODE_HEAP_CORRUPTION", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x0000013A", "stop code", "A driver damaged the kernel's heap."],["0x00000109 CRITICAL_STRUCTURE_CORRUPTION", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x00000109", "stop code", "Protected kernel code or data was changed. Windows does not allow that, even by drivers."],["0x00000124 WHEA_UNCORRECTABLE_ERROR", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x00000124", "stop code", "The hardware itself reported a fatal error. This is almost never a Windows or driver problem."],["0x0000009C MACHINE_CHECK_EXCEPTION", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x0000009C", "stop code", "The processor detected a hardware error. The older sibling of 0x124."],["0x00000101 CLOCK_WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x00000101", "stop code", "One processor core stopped answering."],["0x0000007F UNEXPECTED_KERNEL_MODE_TRAP", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x0000007F", "stop code", "The processor raised an error the kernel could not handle."],["0x00000133 DPC_WATCHDOG_VIOLATION", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x00000133", "stop code", "A driver kept the processor busy for too long without letting go."],["0x0000009F DRIVER_POWER_STATE_FAILURE", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x0000009F", "stop code", "A driver did not answer when Windows went to sleep or woke up. Typical for laptops."],["0x000000A0 INTERNAL_POWER_ERROR", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x000000A0", "stop code", "The power manager ran into a fatal error, often around hibernation."],["0x00000116 VIDEO_TDR_FAILURE", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x00000116", "stop code", "The graphics driver stopped responding and could not be restarted."],["0x00000119 VIDEO_SCHEDULER_INTERNAL_ERROR", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x00000119", "stop code", "The graphics scheduler found a fatal problem."],["0x0000007B INACCESSIBLE_BOOT_DEVICE", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x0000007B", "stop code", "Windows started loading and then could not read its own disk any more."],["0x000000ED UNMOUNTABLE_BOOT_VOLUME", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x000000ED", "stop code", "The system volume could not be mounted."],["0x00000024 NTFS_FILE_SYSTEM", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x00000024", "stop code", "The NTFS driver hit a problem it could not recover from."],["0x0000007A KERNEL_DATA_INPAGE_ERROR", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x0000007A", "stop code", "Windows could not read data back from the disk that it had moved out of memory. KERNEL_STACK_INPAGE_ERROR (0x77) is the same family."],["0x00000154 UNEXPECTED_STORE_EXCEPTION", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x00000154", "stop code", "The component that compresses memory hit an error, which in practice points at the disk."],["0x000000EF CRITICAL_PROCESS_DIED", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x000000EF", "stop code", "A process Windows cannot live without ended unexpectedly."],["0x000000F4 CRITICAL_OBJECT_TERMINATION", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x000000F4", "stop code", "Like CRITICAL_PROCESS_DIED: an essential process or thread ended."],["0xC000021A WINLOGON_FATAL_ERROR", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0xC000021A", "stop code", "The part of Windows that handles logon and the session (winlogon or csrss) died. Also shown as STATUS_SYSTEM_PROCESS_TERMINATED."],["0x00000074 BAD_SYSTEM_CONFIG_INFO", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x00000074", "stop code", "The registry or the boot configuration is damaged or holds values Windows cannot use."],["0x00000051 REGISTRY_ERROR", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x00000051", "stop code", "Windows could not read part of the registry."],["0xC000000E Boot configuration data is missing or contains errors", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0xC000000E", "stop code", "Not a blue screen in the strict sense, but the same moment of panic: the boot manager cannot find what it needs to start Windows."],["0x000000C4 DRIVER_VERIFIER_DETECTED_VIOLATION", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x000000C4", "stop code", "Driver Verifier is switched on and caught a driver doing something wrong."],["0x000000C5 DRIVER_CORRUPTED_EXPOOL", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x000000C5", "stop code", "A driver damaged the kernel's memory pool."],["0x000000BE ATTEMPTED_WRITE_TO_READONLY_MEMORY", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x000000BE", "stop code", "A driver tried to write to memory that is read-only."],["0x000000FC ATTEMPTED_EXECUTE_OF_NOEXECUTE_MEMORY", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x000000FC", "stop code", "A driver tried to run code from memory that is marked as data."],["0x000000CA PNP_DETECTED_FATAL_ERROR", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x000000CA", "stop code", "Plug and Play ran into a fatal error while handling a device."],["0x00000044 MULTIPLE_IRP_COMPLETE_REQUESTS", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x00000044", "stop code", "A driver reported the same request as finished twice. REFERENCE_BY_POINTER (0x18) is a similar driver bookkeeping error."],["0x000000E2 MANUALLY_INITIATED_CRASH", "stop-code-lookup.html?q=0x000000E2", "stop code", "Someone caused the crash on purpose: by a keyboard shortcut configured for it, or by holding the power button (0x1C8 on newer devices)."],["I forgot my password / my account is locked", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#i-forgot-my-password-my-account-is-locked", "ticket", "The most frequent ticket of all, and the one attackers imitate. Verify who you are talking to before you reset anything."],["I cannot print", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#i-cannot-print", "ticket", "Half of these are the queue, a quarter the wrong printer, the rest the printer itself."],["The internet is not working", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#the-internet-is-not-working", "ticket", "Usually not the internet. Find out which layer: cable or Wi-Fi, address, DNS, or one website."],["My computer is slow", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#my-computer-is-slow", "ticket", "Vague on purpose. Narrow it down to since when and doing what before you touch anything."],["Outlook keeps asking for my password / does not send or receive", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#outlook-keeps-asking-for-my-password-does-not-send-or-receive", "ticket", "A changed password, an expired token, a full mailbox or a damaged profile."],["I cannot open the shared drive / folder", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#i-cannot-open-the-shared-drive-folder", "ticket", "Either the drive is not connected, or the permission is missing. They look the same to the user."],["I have a new phone and the authenticator does not work", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#i-have-a-new-phone-and-the-authenticator-does-not-work", "ticket", "Planned or after a loss, the fix is the same. The risk is the same too: this is how attackers get their own phone registered."],["The VPN does not connect", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#the-vpn-does-not-connect", "ticket", "Credentials, the network they are in, or the client."],["I need a program installed / I need admin rights", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#i-need-a-program-installed-i-need-admin-rights", "ticket", "A request, not a fault. The answer depends on your rules, so have rules."],["Nobody can hear me / my camera does not work in the meeting", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#nobody-can-hear-me-my-camera-does-not-work-in-the-meeting", "ticket", "Device selection, a mute switch, or permissions. Rarely a defect."],["My second screen / docking station does not work", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#my-second-screen-docking-station-does-not-work", "ticket", "Cable, input selection on the monitor, or the dock's firmware and power."],["I deleted a file / can you restore an old version", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#i-deleted-a-file-can-you-restore-an-old-version", "ticket", "The sooner they ask, the more options there are."],["My mailbox is full", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#my-mailbox-is-full", "ticket", "Or the archive, or the local data file."],["I got a strange email / I think I clicked on something", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#i-got-a-strange-email-i-think-i-clicked-on-something", "ticket", "Thank them for reporting. How this call goes decides whether people report next time."],["The Wi-Fi keeps dropping", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#the-wi-fi-keeps-dropping", "ticket", "One device, one place or everybody: that is the whole diagnosis."],["The program crashes / freezes", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#the-program-crashes-freezes", "ticket", "Find out whether it is the program, the file or the machine."],["A new colleague starts on Monday / someone is leaving", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#a-new-colleague-starts-on-monday-someone-is-leaving", "ticket", "Predictable work that arrives as an emergency. A form and a checklist turn it back into routine."],["Mail does not arrive on my phone", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#mail-does-not-arrive-on-my-phone", "ticket", "Account, password, or a policy that the phone no longer meets."],["My disk is full", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#my-disk-is-full", "ticket", "On a laptop, usually downloads, a mail file, or sync folders. On a server it is a different ticket."],["My laptop does not turn on / I got a blue screen", "helpdesk-top-tickets.html#my-laptop-does-not-turn-on-i-got-a-blue-screen", "ticket", "Dead, or looks dead, or crashed. Three different things."],["macOS admin cheat sheet", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "macOS from the terminal for admins who mostly run Windows: system and hardware info, updates, users, FileVault, Gatekeeper, MDM enrolment, network and DNS, logs, disks, Time Machine and launchd."],["Which macOS, which Mac", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20macOS%2C%20which%20Mac", "snippet: macOS", "Version and build, then model, chip, memory and serial number. sw_vers system_profiler SPHardwareDataType"],["Uptime and the reason for the last shutdown", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Uptime%20and%20the%20reason%20for%20the%20last%20shutdown", "snippet: macOS", "A negative cause code points to hardware or power, 5 is a normal shutdown, 3 a held power button. uptime log show --last 24h --predicate 'eventMessage contains \"Previous shutdown cause\"' --style compact"],["List and install updates", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20and%20install%20updates", "snippet: macOS", "-ia installs everything, -R restarts if needed. softwareupdate -l sudo softwareupdate -ia -R"],["Local user accounts", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Local%20user%20accounts", "snippet: macOS", "Without the system accounts, which start with an underscore. dscl . list /Users | grep -v '^_' dscl . -read /Groups/admin GroupMembership"],["Create an admin account", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20an%20admin%20account", "snippet: macOS", "Asks for the password of the new account. sudo sysadminctl -addUser itadmin -fullName \"IT Admin\" -password - -admin"],["Reset a user's password", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Reset%20a%20user%27s%20password", "snippet: macOS", "With an admin's credentials. The user's login keychain keeps the old password and has to be reset at next login. sudo sysadminctl -resetPasswordFor anna -newPassword - -adminUser itadmin -adminPassword -"],["Is the disk encrypted", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20disk%20encrypted", "snippet: macOS", "FileVault state, and who may unlock the disk at start. fdesetup status sudo fdesetup list"],["Is the Mac managed", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20Mac%20managed", "snippet: macOS", "Whether it is enrolled in MDM, by which server, and which profiles are installed. profiles status -type enrollment sudo profiles show"],["\"App is damaged\" or \"cannot be opened\"", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=%22App%20is%20damaged%22%20or%20%22cannot%20be%20opened%22", "snippet: macOS", "Gatekeeper blocks apps from the internet that are not notarised. Check why, and remove the quarantine flag only for software you trust. spctl --status spctl -a -vv /Applications/Example.app xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Examp"],["System Integrity Protection", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=System%20Integrity%20Protection", "snippet: macOS", "Should say enabled. Changing it needs the recovery system. csrutil status"],["Network interfaces and addresses", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Network%20interfaces%20and%20addresses", "snippet: macOS", "Names of the ports, then the address of one of them. networksetup -listallhardwareports ipconfig getifaddr en0 ipconfig getpacket en0"],["Which DNS servers are really used", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20DNS%20servers%20are%20really%20used", "snippet: macOS", "Shows the resolvers per interface and per domain, including those a VPN added. scutil --dns | grep -E \"resolver|nameserver|domain\""],["Flush the DNS cache", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Flush%20the%20DNS%20cache", "snippet: macOS", "After changing a record or a hosts file. sudo dscacheutil -flushcache; sudo killall -HUP mDNSResponder"],["Wi-Fi details", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Wi-Fi%20details", "snippet: macOS", "Signal, noise, channel and data rate. Hold Option and click the Wi-Fi icon for the same without a terminal. sudo wdutil info"],["Set DNS servers or go back to DHCP", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Set%20DNS%20servers%20or%20go%20back%20to%20DHCP", "snippet: macOS", "The service name is the one from System Settings, such as Wi-Fi. sudo networksetup -setdnsservers Wi-Fi 192.168.50.10 192.168.50.11 sudo networksetup -setdnsservers Wi-Fi empty"],["Read the system log", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20the%20system%20log", "snippet: macOS", "The unified log replaces the old text files. Filter, or it is far too much. log show --last 30m --predicate 'process == \"sharingd\"' --style compact log show --last 1h --predicate 'eventMessage contains[c] \"error\"' --style compact | tail -n "],["Follow the log live", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Follow%20the%20log%20live", "snippet: macOS", "Start it, reproduce the problem, stop with Ctrl+C. log stream --level info --predicate 'subsystem == \"com.apple.wifi\"'"],["What uses CPU and memory", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20uses%20CPU%20and%20memory", "snippet: macOS", "Sorted by CPU, refreshed every two seconds. top -o cpu -s 2 -n 15"],["Disks, volumes and free space", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Disks%2C%20volumes%20and%20free%20space", "snippet: macOS", "APFS shares free space between volumes of one container, so read the container. diskutil list diskutil apfs list df -h /"],["Check and repair a volume", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20and%20repair%20a%20volume", "snippet: macOS", "First Aid from the terminal. For the startup volume, repair from the recovery system. diskutil verifyVolume / sudo diskutil repairVolume /Volumes/Data"],["What takes the space", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20takes%20the%20space", "snippet: macOS", "Largest folders in the home directory. du -hd 1 ~ 2>/dev/null | sort -h | tail -n 12"],["Time Machine: state, backups, start one now", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Time%20Machine%3A%20state%2C%20backups%2C%20start%20one%20now", "snippet: macOS", "Also shows the destination. tmutil status tmutil destinationinfo tmutil listbackups tmutil startbackup"],["What starts automatically", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20starts%20automatically", "snippet: macOS", "The four places macOS loads background jobs from, besides Login Items in System Settings. ls /Library/LaunchDaemons /Library/LaunchAgents ~/Library/LaunchAgents sudo launchctl list | grep -v com.apple"],["Stop and unload a background job", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Stop%20and%20unload%20a%20background%20job", "snippet: macOS", "bootout stops it now. Remove or move the plist so it does not come back. sudo launchctl bootout system /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.example.agent.plist launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.example.helper.plist"],["System extensions and what they belong to", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=System%20extensions%20and%20what%20they%20belong%20to", "snippet: macOS", "Security agents, VPNs and virtualisation tools install these. systemextensionsctl list"],["Install a package without clicking", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Install%20a%20package%20without%20clicking", "snippet: macOS", "For .pkg installers. Apps in a .dmg are mounted and copied. sudo installer -pkg ~/Downloads/Example.pkg -target / hdiutil attach ~/Downloads/Example.dmg && cp -R /Volumes/Example/Example.app /Applications/ && hdiutil detach /Volumes/Example"],["Homebrew: update everything", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Homebrew%3A%20update%20everything", "snippet: macOS", "And list what was installed as an app. brew update && brew upgrade brew list --cask"],["Rename the Mac", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Rename%20the%20Mac", "snippet: macOS", "Three names: the friendly one, the network one and the Bonjour one. sudo scutil --set ComputerName \"MB-Anna\" sudo scutil --set HostName mb-anna sudo scutil --set LocalHostName mb-anna"],["Turn on remote login (SSH)", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Turn%20on%20remote%20login%20%28SSH%29", "snippet: macOS", "Needs Full Disk Access for the terminal on current versions. Otherwise: System Settings, General, Sharing. sudo systemsetup -setremotelogin on sudo systemsetup -getremotelogin"],["Battery health and why it woke up", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Battery%20health%20and%20why%20it%20woke%20up", "snippet: macOS", "Cycle count and condition, then the wake reasons of the last sleep periods. system_profiler SPPowerDataType | grep -E \"Cycle Count|Condition|Maximum Capacity\" pmset -g log | grep -i \"wake reason\" | tail -n 10"],["Keep the Mac awake for a job", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Keep%20the%20Mac%20awake%20for%20a%20job", "snippet: macOS", "Prevents sleep until the command ends. caffeinate -i rsync -a /Volumes/Source/ /Volumes/Target/"],["Spotlight finds nothing: rebuild the index", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Spotlight%20finds%20nothing%3A%20rebuild%20the%20index", "snippet: macOS", "Takes a while and uses the disk heavily. sudo mdutil -E /"],["Startup keys", "macos-admin-cheat-sheet.html?q=Startup%20keys", "snippet: macOS", "Intel: hold the keys at power on. Apple silicon: hold the power button until the options appear. # Recovery          Intel: Cmd+R             Apple silicon: hold power, then Options # Safe mode         Intel: Shift             Apple silicon"],["Printer troubleshooting cheat sheet", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Printers on Windows, Linux and macOS: clear a stuck queue, restart the spooler, add and remove printers and drivers with PowerShell, read the print log, and the error codes 0x0000011b, 0x00000709 and 0x0000007c."],["Which printers are installed, and how", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20printers%20are%20installed%2C%20and%20how", "snippet: Printers", "Name, driver, port and whether it is shared. WSD ports are the ones that go \"offline\" for no reason. Get-Printer | Format-Table Name, DriverName, PortName, Shared, PrinterStatus"],["What is in the queue", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20is%20in%20the%20queue", "snippet: Printers", "Jobs of one printer with owner, size and state. Get-PrintJob -PrinterName \"Office-2OG\" | Format-Table Id, UserName, DocumentName, JobStatus, Size"],["Delete all jobs of a printer", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Delete%20all%20jobs%20of%20a%20printer", "snippet: Printers", "When they go away, the queue was just stuck on one job. Get-PrintJob -PrinterName \"Office-2OG\" | Remove-PrintJob"],["The queue will not clear: restart the spooler and empty its folder", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20queue%20will%20not%20clear%3A%20restart%20the%20spooler%20and%20empty%20its%20folder", "snippet: Printers", "The classic fix. Jobs that refuse to be deleted are files in this folder. Stop-Service Spooler -Force Remove-Item \"$env:WINDIR\\System32\\spool\\PRINTERS\\*\" -Force Start-Service Spooler"],["Is the printer reachable", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20printer%20reachable", "snippet: Printers", "9100 is raw printing, 631 is IPP, 515 is LPR. No answer on any means network, not Windows. Test-NetConnection 192.168.50.20 -Port 9100 Test-NetConnection 192.168.50.20 -Port 631"],["Printer shows \"offline\" but works", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Printer%20shows%20%22offline%22%20but%20works", "snippet: Printers", "Windows asks the printer for its status over SNMP and believes it is gone when there is no answer. Turn the status check off on the port. Get-PrinterPort | Format-Table Name, PrinterHostAddress, SNMPEnabled Set-PrinterPort -Name \"IP_192.168"],["Add a network printer by address", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Add%20a%20network%20printer%20by%20address", "snippet: Printers", "Port, driver, printer. The driver must be in the driver store already (pnputil, or the vendor's package). Add-PrinterPort -Name \"IP_192.168.50.20\" -PrinterHostAddress 192.168.50.20 Add-PrinterDriver -Name \"HP Universal Printing PCL 6\" Add-P"],["Put a driver into the driver store", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Put%20a%20driver%20into%20the%20driver%20store", "snippet: Printers", "From the folder with the .inf file of the unpacked driver. pnputil /add-driver \"C:\\Drivers\\HP\\*.inf\" /install"],["Connect a printer from a print server", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect%20a%20printer%20from%20a%20print%20server", "snippet: Printers", "For the current user. The driver comes from the server. Add-Printer -ConnectionName \"\\\\printsrv\\Office-2OG\""],["Remove a printer and its driver", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Remove%20a%20printer%20and%20its%20driver", "snippet: Printers", "A broken driver stays behind when you only remove the printer. Remove both, restart the spooler in between if the driver is \"in use\". Remove-Printer -Name \"Office-2OG\" Get-PrinterDriver | Format-Table Name, MajorVersion, Manufacturer Remove"],["The dialog with all drivers and ports", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20dialog%20with%20all%20drivers%20and%20ports", "snippet: Printers", "Print Server Properties: the place to delete driver packages completely. printui /s /t2"],["Default printer", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Default%20printer", "snippet: Printers", "Read it, set it, and stop Windows from changing it to the last one used. (Get-CimInstance Win32_Printer -Filter \"Default=true\").Name (Get-CimInstance Win32_Printer -Filter \"Name='Office-2OG'\") | Invoke-CimMethod -MethodName SetDefaultPrinte"],["Print a test page", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Print%20a%20test%20page", "snippet: Printers", "Takes the application out of the picture. rundll32 printui.dll,PrintUIEntry /k /n \"Office-2OG\""],["Turn on and read the print log", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Turn%20on%20and%20read%20the%20print%20log", "snippet: Printers", "Off by default. It records every job and every error with a reason. wevtutil sl Microsoft-Windows-PrintService/Operational /e:true Get-WinEvent -LogName Microsoft-Windows-PrintService/Operational -MaxEvents 30 | Format-Table TimeCreated, Id"],["Error 0x0000011b when connecting to a shared printer", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Error%200x0000011b%20when%20connecting%20to%20a%20shared%20printer", "snippet: Printers", "Client and print server disagree about the security of the connection, since the PrintNightmare fixes. The real fix is current updates on both sides. # 1. Install the current cumulative updates on the print server AND the clients. # 2. Chec"],["Error 0x00000709 or 0x0000007c", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Error%200x00000709%20or%200x0000007c", "snippet: Printers", "Same family: the connection to the print server is refused, or the name does not resolve the way the server expects. # Update server and clients. Connect by the server's real name, not an alias or the IP address. # Check that the client res"],["Users are asked for an admin password to install a printer", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Users%20are%20asked%20for%20an%20admin%20password%20to%20install%20a%20printer", "snippet: Printers", "Since 2021 only administrators may install printer drivers. Deploy the driver in advance instead of loosening the rule. # Preferred: push the driver with Intune, a package or a startup script (pnputil /add-driver), then users can connect. #"],["Spooler crashes again and again", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Spooler%20crashes%20again%20and%20again", "snippet: Printers", "Almost always one bad driver. The Admin log names the module, then remove that driver. Get-WinEvent -FilterHashtable @{LogName='Application'; ProviderName='Application Error'} -MaxEvents 20 | Where-Object Message -like '*spoolsv*' | Format-"],["Scan to folder stopped working", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Scan%20to%20folder%20stopped%20working", "snippet: Printers", "Old multifunction devices speak only SMB1, which current Windows refuses. Do not switch SMB1 back on. # Options, best first: # 1. Firmware update for the device, then set SMB2 or SMB3 in its web interface. # 2. Scan to email, SFTP or a clou"],["Scan to email stopped working", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Scan%20to%20email%20stopped%20working", "snippet: Printers", "The mail provider no longer accepts a plain user name and password from devices. # Microsoft 365: use SMTP relay through a connector (fixed public IP, port 25 to the MX endpoint), # or direct send to internal recipients, or a mail relay ser"],["Linux (CUPS): status and queue", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Linux%20%28CUPS%29%3A%20status%20and%20queue", "snippet: Printers", "Everything about all printers, then cancel all jobs. lpstat -t cancel -a sudo cupsenable Office-2OG"],["Linux (CUPS): add a network printer without a driver", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Linux%20%28CUPS%29%3A%20add%20a%20network%20printer%20without%20a%20driver", "snippet: Printers", "Driverless printing (IPP Everywhere) works with most printers from the last ten years. sudo lpadmin -p Office-2OG -E -v ipp://192.168.50.20/ipp/print -m everywhere lp -d Office-2OG /usr/share/cups/data/testprint"],["Linux (CUPS): the log", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Linux%20%28CUPS%29%3A%20the%20log", "snippet: Printers", "Raise the level, reproduce, read, lower it again. sudo cupsctl --debug-logging sudo tail -f /var/log/cups/error_log sudo cupsctl --no-debug-logging"],["macOS: reset the printing system", "printer-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=macOS%3A%20reset%20the%20printing%20system", "snippet: Printers", "Removes all printers and queues. Right-click in the printer list in System Settings and choose Reset printing system, or from the terminal: lpstat -p cancel -a sudo launchctl kickstart -k system/org.cups.cupsd"],["IP plan builder", "ip-plan-builder.html", "tool", "Plan VLANs and subnets for a network: enter the address range and the segments with their host counts, get non-overlapping subnets with gateway, static and DHCP ranges, plus switch and DHCP configuration. VLSM, VLAN plan, DHCP scopes, Cisco, dnsmasq"],["Wi-Fi is slow or keeps dropping", "diagnose.html#wifi", "tool", "Wizard: coverage, interference, channel, capacity, roaming, access point uplink"],["No network on a wired port", "diagnose.html#wired", "tool", "Wizard: no link, 169.254 address, wrong VLAN, DHCP, gateway, DNS"],["WireGuard cheat sheet", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "WireGuard from key to tunnel: server and client configuration, road-warrior and site-to-site setups, routing and NAT, and how to find out why the handshake does not happen."],["Install", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Install", "snippet: WireGuard", "The kernel module is part of Linux since 5.6. The tools are a separate package. sudo apt install wireguard        # Debian, Ubuntu sudo dnf install wireguard-tools  # RHEL 9, Rocky, Alma, Fedora"],["Create a key pair", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20key%20pair", "snippet: WireGuard", "One pair per device. The private key stays on the device, the public key goes to the other side. umask 077 wg genkey | tee privatekey | wg pubkey > publickey"],["Optional: a preshared key per peer", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Optional%3A%20a%20preshared%20key%20per%20peer", "snippet: WireGuard", "A third secret on top of the key pairs, shared between exactly two peers. wg genpsk"],["Server configuration", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Server%20configuration", "snippet: WireGuard", "Save as /etc/wireguard/wg0.conf with mode 600. One [Peer] block per client. [Interface] Address = 10.99.0.1/24 ListenPort = 51820 PrivateKey = SERVER-PRIVATE-KEY  [Peer] # laptop anna PublicKey = CLIENT-PUBLIC-KEY AllowedIPs = 10.99.0.2/32"],["Client configuration: reach the office network", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Client%20configuration%3A%20reach%20the%20office%20network", "snippet: WireGuard", "Split tunnel: only the tunnel and the office network 192.168.50.0/24 go through the VPN. [Interface] Address = 10.99.0.2/32 PrivateKey = CLIENT-PRIVATE-KEY DNS = 192.168.50.10  [Peer] PublicKey = SERVER-PUBLIC-KEY Endpoint = vpn.example.org"],["Client configuration: send everything through the VPN", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Client%20configuration%3A%20send%20everything%20through%20the%20VPN", "snippet: WireGuard", "Full tunnel. All traffic including internet goes to the server. [Peer] PublicKey = SERVER-PUBLIC-KEY Endpoint = vpn.example.org:51820 AllowedIPs = 0.0.0.0/0, ::/0 PersistentKeepalive = 25"],["What AllowedIPs means", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20AllowedIPs%20means", "snippet: WireGuard", "The one setting that confuses everybody. It works in both directions. # Outgoing: packets to these addresses are sent to this peer (a routing table). # Incoming: packets from this peer are accepted only with these source addresses (a filter"],["Start, stop, enable at boot", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Start%2C%20stop%2C%20enable%20at%20boot", "snippet: WireGuard", "wg-quick reads /etc/wireguard/wg0.conf. sudo wg-quick up wg0 sudo wg-quick down wg0 sudo systemctl enable --now wg-quick@wg0"],["Is the tunnel up", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20tunnel%20up", "snippet: WireGuard", "\"latest handshake\" is the line that matters. No handshake line means the two sides have never talked. sudo wg show"],["Let clients reach the network behind the server", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Let%20clients%20reach%20the%20network%20behind%20the%20server", "snippet: WireGuard", "The server has to forward packets. Without this, clients reach the server and nothing else. echo 'net.ipv4.ip_forward=1' | sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/99-wireguard.conf sudo sysctl --system"],["NAT on the server", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=NAT%20on%20the%20server", "snippet: WireGuard", "The simple way: hosts in the office see the server's own address, no routes needed elsewhere. Add to [Interface], eth0 is the LAN interface. PostUp   = iptables -t nat -A POSTROUTING -s 10.99.0.0/24 -o eth0 -j MASQUERADE PostDown = iptables"],["Without NAT: a route on the office router", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Without%20NAT%3A%20a%20route%20on%20the%20office%20router", "snippet: WireGuard", "Cleaner: the office sees the real tunnel addresses. The router needs to know where the tunnel network lives. # on the office router or firewall, as a static route: # destination 10.99.0.0/24  via  192.168.50.5 (the LAN address of the WireGu"],["Open the port", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Open%20the%20port", "snippet: WireGuard", "UDP only. Forward the same port on the internet router to the server. sudo ufw allow 51820/udp sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-port=51820/udp && sudo firewall-cmd --reload"],["Site-to-site: office A", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Site-to-site%3A%20office%20A", "snippet: WireGuard", "Each side lists the other side's LAN in AllowedIPs. Both servers need forwarding switched on. [Interface] Address = 10.99.0.1/24 ListenPort = 51820 PrivateKey = A-PRIVATE-KEY  [Peer] PublicKey = B-PUBLIC-KEY Endpoint = b.example.org:51820 A"],["Site-to-site: office B", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Site-to-site%3A%20office%20B", "snippet: WireGuard", "The mirror image. The two LANs must not use the same range. [Interface] Address = 10.99.0.2/24 ListenPort = 51820 PrivateKey = B-PRIVATE-KEY  [Peer] PublicKey = A-PUBLIC-KEY Endpoint = a.example.org:51820 AllowedIPs = 10.99.0.1/32, 192.168."],["Add a client without stopping the tunnel", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Add%20a%20client%20without%20stopping%20the%20tunnel", "snippet: WireGuard", "Takes effect at once. Add it to the file too, or it is gone after a restart. sudo wg set wg0 peer CLIENT-PUBLIC-KEY allowed-ips 10.99.0.3/32 sudo wg-quick save wg0"],["Reload the configuration file without dropping connections", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Reload%20the%20configuration%20file%20without%20dropping%20connections", "snippet: WireGuard", "Applies changes made in the file. sudo bash -c 'wg syncconf wg0 <(wg-quick strip wg0)'"],["A QR code for the phone", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20QR%20code%20for%20the%20phone", "snippet: WireGuard", "The mobile apps import a configuration by scanning it. sudo apt install qrencode qrencode -t ansiutf8 < client-phone.conf"],["No handshake: is anything arriving", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=No%20handshake%3A%20is%20anything%20arriving", "snippet: WireGuard", "Run on the server while the client tries to connect. Nothing here means port forwarding, a firewall or the wrong endpoint. sudo tcpdump -ni any udp port 51820"],["No handshake: the checklist", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=No%20handshake%3A%20the%20checklist", "snippet: WireGuard", "WireGuard stays silent when keys do not match, so nothing shows up in a log. # 1. Packets arrive (tcpdump) but no handshake: a key is wrong. The server needs the CLIENT's public key and the other way round. # 2. Nothing arrives: port forwar"],["Handshake works, nothing else does", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Handshake%20works%2C%20nothing%20else%20does", "snippet: WireGuard", "Ping the tunnel address of the server first, then a host behind it. Where it stops tells you what is missing. ping 10.99.0.1         # fails: AllowedIPs on one side does not contain the tunnel addresses ping 192.168.50.10     # fails: no fo"],["Large transfers hang, small ones work", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Large%20transfers%20hang%2C%20small%20ones%20work", "snippet: WireGuard", "The classic MTU problem, common on DSL (PPPoE) and mobile lines. Set a lower MTU in [Interface] on both sides. MTU = 1380"],["The tunnel dies after a while behind NAT", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20tunnel%20dies%20after%20a%20while%20behind%20NAT", "snippet: WireGuard", "The router forgets the connection when it is quiet. The keepalive on the side behind NAT keeps it open. PersistentKeepalive = 25"],["Turn on debug messages", "wireguard-cheat-sheet.html?q=Turn%20on%20debug%20messages", "snippet: WireGuard", "WireGuard logs nothing by default. This writes to the kernel log. echo module wireguard +p | sudo tee /sys/kernel/debug/dynamic_debug/control sudo dmesg -wT | grep wireguard"],["OpenVPN cheat sheet", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "OpenVPN for admins who inherit one: read the log, the handful of errors that explain most outages, certificates and revocation, pushing routes and DNS, and testing a connection by hand."],["Is the server running", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20server%20running", "snippet: OpenVPN", "The unit name contains the name of the configuration file: server.conf gives openvpn-server@server. systemctl status openvpn-server@server sudo ss -ulnp | grep openvpn"],["Follow the server log", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Follow%20the%20server%20log", "snippet: OpenVPN", "Connect a client in parallel and watch. sudo journalctl -u openvpn-server@server -f"],["Who is connected", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20is%20connected", "snippet: OpenVPN", "The status file lists clients, their real address and their tunnel address. The path is the status line of the server configuration. sudo cat /run/openvpn-server/status-server.log"],["A minimal server configuration", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20minimal%20server%20configuration", "snippet: OpenVPN", "Routed tunnel on UDP 1194 with modern ciphers. Paths point at the files Easy-RSA created. port 1194 proto udp dev tun topology subnet server 10.8.0.0 255.255.255.0 ca ca.crt cert server.crt key server.key dh none tls-crypt tc.key data-ciphe"],["A minimal client configuration", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20minimal%20client%20configuration", "snippet: OpenVPN", "The .ovpn file. Certificates can be inlined between tags instead of separate files. client dev tun proto udp remote vpn.example.org 1194 resolv-retry infinite nobind persist-key persist-tun remote-cert-tls server data-ciphers AES-256-GCM:CH"],["Give clients the route to the office network", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Give%20clients%20the%20route%20to%20the%20office%20network", "snippet: OpenVPN", "In the server configuration. Clients then send only this network through the tunnel. push \"route 192.168.50.0 255.255.255.0\""],["Send all traffic through the VPN", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Send%20all%20traffic%20through%20the%20VPN", "snippet: OpenVPN", "In the server configuration. Needs NAT on the server. push \"redirect-gateway def1 bypass-dhcp\""],["Give clients the internal DNS server", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Give%20clients%20the%20internal%20DNS%20server", "snippet: OpenVPN", "Otherwise internal names do not resolve. Linux clients need the update-resolv-conf or update-systemd-resolved script to apply it. push \"dhcp-option DNS 192.168.50.10\" push \"dhcp-option DOMAIN example.internal\""],["Forwarding and NAT on the server", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Forwarding%20and%20NAT%20on%20the%20server", "snippet: OpenVPN", "Without them clients reach the server and nothing behind it. echo 'net.ipv4.ip_forward=1' | sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/99-openvpn.conf && sudo sysctl --system sudo iptables -t nat -A POSTROUTING -s 10.8.0.0/24 -o eth0 -j MASQUERADE"],["A fixed tunnel address for one client", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20fixed%20tunnel%20address%20for%20one%20client", "snippet: OpenVPN", "In the server configuration: client-config-dir ccd. Then one file per client, named like the certificate's common name. # /etc/openvpn/server/ccd/anna-laptop ifconfig-push 10.8.0.50 255.255.255.0"],["Create a client certificate", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20client%20certificate", "snippet: OpenVPN", "Easy-RSA 3. nopass leaves the key without a passphrase. cd /etc/openvpn/easy-rsa ./easyrsa build-client-full anna-laptop nopass"],["Revoke a client", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Revoke%20a%20client", "snippet: OpenVPN", "Revoke, rebuild the list, copy it where the server reads it. The server needs the line crl-verify crl.pem. ./easyrsa revoke anna-laptop ./easyrsa gen-crl sudo cp pki/crl.pem /etc/openvpn/server/crl.pem && sudo chmod 644 /etc/openvpn/server/"],["When do the certificates expire", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=When%20do%20the%20certificates%20expire", "snippet: OpenVPN", "The CA and the server certificate expiring is the classic \"VPN stopped for everyone this morning\". openssl x509 -enddate -noout -in /etc/openvpn/server/ca.crt openssl x509 -enddate -noout -in /etc/openvpn/server/server.crt openssl crl -next"],["Nobody can connect since today: the CRL expired", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Nobody%20can%20connect%20since%20today%3A%20the%20CRL%20expired", "snippet: OpenVPN", "The revocation list has its own expiry, 180 days by default. An expired list rejects every client. cd /etc/openvpn/easy-rsa && ./easyrsa gen-crl sudo cp pki/crl.pem /etc/openvpn/server/crl.pem sudo systemctl restart openvpn-server@server"],["TLS key negotiation failed to occur within 60 seconds", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=TLS%20key%20negotiation%20failed%20to%20occur%20within%2060%20seconds", "snippet: OpenVPN", "The client's packets get no answer. Almost always the network, not TLS: firewall, port forward, wrong protocol (UDP against TCP) or wrong address. sudo tcpdump -ni any udp port 1194     # on the server while the client connects"],["TLS Error: cannot locate HMAC / tls-crypt unwrap error", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=TLS%20Error%3A%20cannot%20locate%20HMAC%20/%20tls-crypt%20unwrap%20error", "snippet: OpenVPN", "Client and server use different tls-auth or tls-crypt keys, or one side has none. # compare the key in the client's <tls-crypt> block with tc.key on the server"],["AUTH_FAILED", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=AUTH_FAILED", "snippet: OpenVPN", "The user name or password plugin said no, or the certificate was revoked. The server log names the reason one line earlier. sudo journalctl -u openvpn-server@server --since \"10 min ago\" | grep -iE \"auth|verify|crl\""],["certificate verify failed", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=certificate%20verify%20failed", "snippet: OpenVPN", "Expired certificate, wrong CA, or a clock that is off. The log line says which certificate and why. openssl verify -CAfile ca.crt client.crt date"],["Connected, but nothing is reachable", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connected%2C%20but%20nothing%20is%20reachable", "snippet: OpenVPN", "Check on the client which routes arrived, then follow the packet. ip route | grep tun          # Linux route print | findstr 10.8   # Windows ping 10.8.0.1                # the server's tunnel address ping 192.168.50.10           # a host b"],["Connected, but no cipher in common", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connected%2C%20but%20no%20cipher%20in%20common", "snippet: OpenVPN", "Old clients offer BF-CBC or AES-256-CBC, OpenVPN 2.6 refuses them by default. Better to update the client than to allow the old cipher. # server log: \"No common cipher between server and client\" data-ciphers AES-256-GCM:CHACHA20-POLY1305:AE"],["Test a client configuration by hand", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Test%20a%20client%20configuration%20by%20hand", "snippet: OpenVPN", "In the foreground with full output. Ctrl+C ends it. sudo openvpn --config client.ovpn --verb 4"],["Windows client: where the log is", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20client%3A%20where%20the%20log%20is", "snippet: OpenVPN", "OpenVPN GUI: right-click the tray icon, View Log. The files are here. %USERPROFILE%\\OpenVPN\\log"],["Slow or hanging transfers over UDP", "openvpn-cheat-sheet.html?q=Slow%20or%20hanging%20transfers%20over%20UDP", "snippet: OpenVPN", "Fragmentation on the way. Lower the tunnel's packet size on both sides. tun-mtu 1400 mssfix 1360"],["Switching and VLAN cheat sheet", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Switch commands for daily work in Cisco IOS style: find a device by MAC address, VLANs, access and trunk ports, why a port is down or err-disabled, spanning tree, PoE, port security and LLDP."],["What is this switch", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20is%20this%20switch", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "Model, software version, uptime and the reason for the last reboot. show version"],["All ports at a glance", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=All%20ports%20at%20a%20glance", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "Connected or not, VLAN, speed and duplex. The first command on any switch. show interfaces status"],["Find which port a device is on", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20which%20port%20a%20device%20is%20on", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "By MAC address. If the port is an uplink, repeat on the next switch. show mac address-table address aabb.ccdd.eeff show mac address-table interface Gi1/0/12"],["From IP address to MAC to port", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=From%20IP%20address%20to%20MAC%20to%20port", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "On the device that routes: the ARP table gives the MAC, then look it up as above. show ip arp 192.168.30.57"],["What is connected to this port", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20is%20connected%20to%20this%20port", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "The neighbour tells its name, model and port. LLDP works across vendors, CDP is Cisco only. show lldp neighbors detail show cdp neighbors detail"],["List the VLANs", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20the%20VLANs", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "With the access ports in each. Trunk ports are not listed here. show vlan brief"],["Create a VLAN", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20VLAN", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "It also has to exist on every switch in between and be allowed on the trunks. configure terminal vlan 30  name Clients end"],["Put a port into a VLAN", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Put%20a%20port%20into%20a%20VLAN", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "An access port for one device. Portfast lets it forward at once instead of waiting 30 seconds for spanning tree. configure terminal interface Gi1/0/12  description Office 2.14 left socket  switchport mode access  switchport access vlan 30  "],["Phone and PC on one port", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Phone%20and%20PC%20on%20one%20port", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "The phone gets the voice VLAN, the PC behind it the access VLAN. interface Gi1/0/12  switchport mode access  switchport access vlan 30  switchport voice vlan 40  spanning-tree portfast"],["A trunk to another switch or an access point", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20trunk%20to%20another%20switch%20or%20an%20access%20point", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "Carries several VLANs with tags. Allow only the VLANs that are needed. interface Gi1/0/48  description Uplink to sw-floor2  switchport mode trunk  switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,30,40,60  switchport trunk native vlan 999"],["Add a VLAN to a trunk", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Add%20a%20VLAN%20to%20a%20trunk", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "The word add matters. Without it the list is replaced and every other VLAN drops off the link. interface Gi1/0/48  switchport trunk allowed vlan add 70"],["Which VLANs really pass a trunk", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20VLANs%20really%20pass%20a%20trunk", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "Allowed, active and forwarding are three different lists. A VLAN missing in the last one does not get through. show interfaces trunk"],["Why is this port down", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Why%20is%20this%20port%20down", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "Status, speed, duplex and the error counters in one view. show interfaces Gi1/0/12"],["Reading the error counters", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Reading%20the%20error%20counters", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "Which counter grows tells you where to look. # CRC, input errors      bad cable, bad connector, interference # late collisions, runts duplex mismatch: one side half, the other full # output drops           the port is too slow for what is s"],["Ports the switch shut down itself", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Ports%20the%20switch%20shut%20down%20itself", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "err-disabled means a protection kicked in. The second command says which one. show interfaces status err-disabled show errdisable recovery"],["Bring an err-disabled port back", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Bring%20an%20err-disabled%20port%20back", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "Fix the cause first: a loop, a small switch plugged into an access port, too many MAC addresses. configure terminal interface Gi1/0/12  shutdown  no shutdown end"],["Spanning tree: who is the root, what is blocked", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Spanning%20tree%3A%20who%20is%20the%20root%2C%20what%20is%20blocked", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "The root should be your core switch, not whichever switch has the lowest MAC address. show spanning-tree vlan 30 show spanning-tree summary"],["Make the core switch the root", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Make%20the%20core%20switch%20the%20root", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "On the core. Lower number wins. spanning-tree vlan 1-4094 priority 4096"],["PoE: who draws how much", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=PoE%3A%20who%20draws%20how%20much", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "Budget, used power and power per port. A phone or access point that stays dark is often a budget that ran out. show power inline"],["Restart a PoE device from the desk", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Restart%20a%20PoE%20device%20from%20the%20desk", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "Power-cycles an access point, camera or phone. configure terminal interface Gi1/0/12  power inline never  power inline auto end"],["Only known devices on a port", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Only%20known%20devices%20on%20a%20port", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "Port security: at most two MAC addresses, learned and remembered. A third one shuts the port. interface Gi1/0/12  switchport port-security  switchport port-security maximum 2  switchport port-security mac-address sticky  switchport port-sec"],["Stop a rogue DHCP server", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Stop%20a%20rogue%20DHCP%20server", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "DHCP snooping: answers from a DHCP server are accepted only on trusted ports, the uplinks. ip dhcp snooping ip dhcp snooping vlan 30,40,60 interface Gi1/0/48  ip dhcp snooping trust"],["Copy the traffic of a port to an analyser", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Copy%20the%20traffic%20of%20a%20port%20to%20an%20analyser", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "A mirror port for Wireshark. Port 24 receives a copy of everything on port 12. monitor session 1 source interface Gi1/0/12 both monitor session 1 destination interface Gi1/0/24"],["What happened recently", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20happened%20recently", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "Port up and down, spanning tree changes, err-disable events with time. show logging | include LINK|LINEPROTO|SPANTREE|ERR"],["Save the configuration", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=Save%20the%20configuration", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "Until you do, a reboot brings back the old state. That is also your undo. copy running-config startup-config"],["What changed since the last save", "switching-vlan-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20changed%20since%20the%20last%20save", "snippet: Switching and VLANs", "Before you save, see what you are about to make permanent. show archive config differences nvram:startup-config system:running-config"],["DNS and DHCP cheat sheet", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "DNS and DHCP for the small office: why a client gets no address or a 169.254 one, leases and reservations on Windows Server and dnsmasq, finding a rogue DHCP server, and checking name resolution step by step."],["What did the client get", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20did%20the%20client%20get", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "Address, mask, gateway, DNS servers, the DHCP server it came from and when the lease ends. ipconfig /all                       # Windows ip addr; ip route; resolvectl status   # Linux"],["169.254.x.x: what it means", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=169.254.x.x%3A%20what%20it%20means", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "The client asked for an address and nobody answered, so it made one up. The problem is between the client and the DHCP server, not on the client. # Check in this order: # 1. Cable, port, Wi-Fi association, the right VLAN on the switch port "],["Ask for a new lease", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Ask%20for%20a%20new%20lease", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "Gives the old one back first. ipconfig /release && ipconfig /renew        # Windows sudo dhclient -r eth0 && sudo dhclient -v eth0   # Linux with dhclient sudo networkctl renew eth0                  # Linux with systemd-networkd"],["Watch the DHCP conversation", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Watch%20the%20DHCP%20conversation", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "Discover, offer, request, acknowledge. A discover without an offer means nobody answers on this segment. sudo tcpdump -ni eth0 -vv port 67 or port 68"],["Find a rogue DHCP server", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20a%20rogue%20DHCP%20server", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "Sends a discover and lists every server that answers. More than one answer on a segment is the problem. sudo nmap --script broadcast-dhcp-discover -e eth0"],["Windows Server: scopes and how full they are", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20Server%3A%20scopes%20and%20how%20full%20they%20are", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "PercentageInUse near 100 means clients get nothing. Get-DhcpServerv4Scope Get-DhcpServerv4ScopeStatistics | Select-Object ScopeId, Free, InUse, PercentageInUse"],["Windows Server: who has which address", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20Server%3A%20who%20has%20which%20address", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "All leases of a scope, or the lease of one device. Get-DhcpServerv4Lease -ScopeId 192.168.30.0 | Sort-Object IPAddress | Format-Table IPAddress, HostName, ClientId, LeaseExpiryTime Get-DhcpServerv4Lease -ScopeId 192.168.30.0 | Where-Object "],["Windows Server: turn a lease into a reservation", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20Server%3A%20turn%20a%20lease%20into%20a%20reservation", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "The device keeps this address from now on. Get-DhcpServerv4Lease -IPAddress 192.168.30.57 | Add-DhcpServerv4Reservation"],["Windows Server: a reservation by MAC address", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20Server%3A%20a%20reservation%20by%20MAC%20address", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "For a device that has not asked yet. Add-DhcpServerv4Reservation -ScopeId 192.168.30.0 -IPAddress 192.168.30.20 -ClientId 'AA-BB-CC-DD-EE-FF' -Name 'printer-2og'"],["Windows Server: gateway and DNS of a scope", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20Server%3A%20gateway%20and%20DNS%20of%20a%20scope", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "The options every client of the scope receives. Get-DhcpServerv4OptionValue -ScopeId 192.168.30.0 Set-DhcpServerv4OptionValue -ScopeId 192.168.30.0 -Router 192.168.30.1 -DnsServer 192.168.50.10,192.168.50.11"],["Windows Server: the scope is full of stale leases", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20Server%3A%20the%20scope%20is%20full%20of%20stale%20leases", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "Shorten the lease time for networks with many passing devices, such as guest Wi-Fi. Set-DhcpServerv4Scope -ScopeId 192.168.70.0 -LeaseDuration 0.04:00:00 Get-DhcpServerv4Lease -ScopeId 192.168.70.0 | Where-Object AddressState -like '*Expire"],["Windows Server: is the DHCP server authorised", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20Server%3A%20is%20the%20DHCP%20server%20authorised", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "In a domain, an unauthorised Windows DHCP server stays silent. Get-DhcpServerInDC"],["Windows Server: two DHCP servers in failover", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20Server%3A%20two%20DHCP%20servers%20in%20failover", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "State of the relationship. NORMAL on both sides is what you want. Get-DhcpServerv4Failover | Format-List Name, PartnerServer, Mode, State"],["dnsmasq: a range, gateway and DNS", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=dnsmasq%3A%20a%20range%2C%20gateway%20and%20DNS", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "In /etc/dnsmasq.d/lan.conf. Restart dnsmasq afterwards. dhcp-range=192.168.30.50,192.168.30.200,255.255.255.0,12h dhcp-option=option:router,192.168.30.1 dhcp-option=option:dns-server,192.168.30.1 domain=example.internal"],["dnsmasq: a fixed address for a device", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=dnsmasq%3A%20a%20fixed%20address%20for%20a%20device", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "By MAC address. dhcp-host=aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff,printer-2og,192.168.30.20"],["dnsmasq: current leases", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=dnsmasq%3A%20current%20leases", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "One line per lease: expiry time, MAC, address, name. cat /var/lib/misc/dnsmasq.leases"],["Relay DHCP into another VLAN", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Relay%20DHCP%20into%20another%20VLAN", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "On the gateway of the client VLAN, pointing at the DHCP server. Cisco syntax. interface Vlan30  ip helper-address 192.168.50.10"],["Does the name resolve, and who answered", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Does%20the%20name%20resolve%2C%20and%20who%20answered", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "Start here for \"the internet is down\" and \"the server is not found\". nslookup intranet.example.internal                   # Windows, Linux Resolve-DnsName intranet.example.internal            # PowerShell dig intranet.example.internal +shor"],["Ask one particular DNS server", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Ask%20one%20particular%20DNS%20server", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "Compare the internal server with a public one. Different answers explain \"works for me\". nslookup example.org 192.168.50.10 dig @1.1.1.1 example.org +short Resolve-DnsName example.org -Server 192.168.50.10"],["Name works by IP but not by name", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Name%20works%20by%20IP%20but%20not%20by%20name", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "Then it is DNS and nothing else. Check which servers the client really uses. ping 192.168.50.10 Get-DnsClientServerAddress -AddressFamily IPv4     # Windows resolvectl status | grep -A2 \"DNS Servers\"         # Linux"],["Throw away cached answers", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Throw%20away%20cached%20answers", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "After changing a record, clients keep the old answer until its TTL ends. ipconfig /flushdns                    # Windows client sudo resolvectl flush-caches          # Linux with systemd-resolved Clear-DnsServerCache -Force           # Wind"],["The reverse entry", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20reverse%20entry", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "From address to name. Mail servers and some logins insist on it. nslookup 192.168.50.10 dig -x 192.168.50.10 +short"],["Follow the delegation from the root", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Follow%20the%20delegation%20from%20the%20root", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "Shows which server is authoritative and where the chain breaks. dig example.org +trace"],["Windows DNS server: records of a zone", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20DNS%20server%3A%20records%20of%20a%20zone", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "List, add and remove. Get-DnsServerResourceRecord -ZoneName example.internal | Sort-Object HostName Add-DnsServerResourceRecordA -ZoneName example.internal -Name intranet -IPv4Address 192.168.50.20 Remove-DnsServerResourceRecord -ZoneName e"],["Windows DNS server: where do unknown names go", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20DNS%20server%3A%20where%20do%20unknown%20names%20go", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "The forwarders. If they are dead, internal names work and the internet does not. Get-DnsServerForwarder Set-DnsServerForwarder -IPAddress 9.9.9.9,1.1.1.1"],["Domain clients: point DNS at the domain controller", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Domain%20clients%3A%20point%20DNS%20at%20the%20domain%20controller", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "A domain member that uses the router or a public server for DNS cannot find the domain: logons are slow, group policy fails. nslookup -type=SRV _ldap._tcp.dc._msdcs.example.internal ipconfig /registerdns"],["Two devices with the same address", "dns-dhcp-cheat-sheet.html?q=Two%20devices%20with%20the%20same%20address", "snippet: DNS and DHCP", "Windows logs it, Linux can probe for it. The reply shows the MAC address of the other device. sudo arping -D -I eth0 192.168.30.57 Get-WinEvent -FilterHashtable @{LogName='System'; Id=4199} -MaxEvents 5"],["The Linux server is slow", "linux-server-slow.html", "tool", "A walkthrough for a slow Linux server: eight steps from load average to CPU, memory, disk, network and the application, each with the commands, how to read the output and what to do. high load, iowait, steal time, swapping, OOM killer, disk full, inodes, slow DNS"],["systemd and journalctl cheat sheet", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "systemd and journalctl for daily server work: why a service failed, logs by unit and time, overrides, timers instead of cron, writing a unit file, keeping the journal small."],["Is the service running, and what did it say last", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20service%20running%2C%20and%20what%20did%20it%20say%20last", "snippet: systemd", "State, since when, main process and the last ten log lines in one view. systemctl status nginx"],["Start, stop, restart, reload", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Start%2C%20stop%2C%20restart%2C%20reload", "snippet: systemd", "Reload re-reads the configuration without dropping connections, where the service supports it. sudo systemctl restart nginx sudo systemctl reload nginx"],["Start now and at every boot", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Start%20now%20and%20at%20every%20boot", "snippet: systemd", "Enable alone only sets the boot behaviour. sudo systemctl enable --now nginx"],["Everything that failed", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Everything%20that%20failed", "snippet: systemd", "The first command after logging in to a server that misbehaves. systemctl --failed"],["Why did it fail", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Why%20did%20it%20fail", "snippet: systemd", "The last 50 lines of this service since boot. The reason is usually in the lines just before \"Failed with result\". journalctl -u nginx -b -n 50 --no-pager"],["Follow the log live", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Follow%20the%20log%20live", "snippet: systemd", "Like tail -f. Restart the service in a second terminal and watch. journalctl -u nginx -f"],["All errors since boot", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=All%20errors%20since%20boot", "snippet: systemd", "Priority err and worse, from every service and the kernel. journalctl -p err -b --no-pager"],["A time window", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20time%20window", "snippet: systemd", "When the user says \"around nine it stopped working\". journalctl --since \"2026-10-05 08:45\" --until \"2026-10-05 09:15\" journalctl -u nginx --since \"1 hour ago\""],["The boot before this one", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20boot%20before%20this%20one", "snippet: systemd", "After a crash or an unexpected reboot: what happened right before. journalctl --list-boots journalctl -b -1 -p warning --no-pager | tail -n 60"],["Kernel messages: out of memory, disk errors", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Kernel%20messages%3A%20out%20of%20memory%2C%20disk%20errors", "snippet: systemd", "The kernel says when it killed a process or a disk returned errors. journalctl -k -b | grep -iE \"out of memory|killed process|i/o error|ext4-fs error|xfs.*error\""],["Restart counter and exit status", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Restart%20counter%20and%20exit%20status", "snippet: systemd", "For a service that keeps coming back: how often, and with which result. systemctl show nginx -p NRestarts,Result,ExecMainStatus,ActiveEnterTimestamp"],["Clear the failed state", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Clear%20the%20failed%20state", "snippet: systemd", "After fixing the cause, or when the start limit was hit (\"start request repeated too quickly\"). sudo systemctl reset-failed nginx sudo systemctl start nginx"],["Show the unit file with all overrides", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Show%20the%20unit%20file%20with%20all%20overrides", "snippet: systemd", "What systemd really uses, including drop-ins. systemctl cat nginx"],["Change a unit without touching the original", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Change%20a%20unit%20without%20touching%20the%20original", "snippet: systemd", "Opens a drop-in file that survives package updates. Example content below. sudo systemctl edit nginx  # in the editor: [Service] Restart=on-failure RestartSec=5 LimitNOFILE=65535"],["Reload systemd after editing unit files by hand", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Reload%20systemd%20after%20editing%20unit%20files%20by%20hand", "snippet: systemd", "systemctl edit does this for you, a text editor does not. sudo systemctl daemon-reload"],["A service unit for your own program", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20service%20unit%20for%20your%20own%20program", "snippet: systemd", "Save as /etc/systemd/system/myapp.service, then daemon-reload and enable --now. [Unit] Description=My app After=network-online.target Wants=network-online.target  [Service] User=myapp WorkingDirectory=/opt/myapp ExecStart=/opt/myapp/bin/ser"],["A timer instead of a cron job", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20timer%20instead%20of%20a%20cron%20job", "snippet: systemd", "Two files: myjob.service does the work, myjob.timer says when. Persistent catches up after downtime. # /etc/systemd/system/myjob.service [Service] Type=oneshot ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/backup.sh  # /etc/systemd/system/myjob.timer [Timer] On"],["All timers and when they run next", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=All%20timers%20and%20when%20they%20run%20next", "snippet: systemd", "Also shows when each ran last. systemctl list-timers --all"],["Check a calendar expression", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20a%20calendar%20expression", "snippet: systemd", "Prints the next time it would fire, before you rely on it. systemd-analyze calendar \"Mon..Fri 02:30\" systemd-analyze calendar \"*-*-01 04:00\""],["Check a unit file for mistakes", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20a%20unit%20file%20for%20mistakes", "snippet: systemd", "Catches typos in directives and missing executables. systemd-analyze verify /etc/systemd/system/myapp.service"],["What slows down the boot", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20slows%20down%20the%20boot", "snippet: systemd", "Units by start time, and the chain that decided the total. systemd-analyze blame | head -n 15 systemd-analyze critical-chain"],["What a service waits for", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20a%20service%20waits%20for", "snippet: systemd", "The dependency tree. Useful when a service starts before the network or the database is ready. systemctl list-dependencies nginx"],["CPU and memory per service", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=CPU%20and%20memory%20per%20service", "snippet: systemd", "Like top, grouped by service. systemd-cgtop"],["How much disk the journal uses", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=How%20much%20disk%20the%20journal%20uses", "snippet: systemd", "Often gigabytes on a server that was never tuned. journalctl --disk-usage"],["Shrink the journal now", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Shrink%20the%20journal%20now", "snippet: systemd", "Keep two weeks, or cap the size. sudo journalctl --vacuum-time=14d sudo journalctl --vacuum-size=500M"],["Cap the journal for good", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Cap%20the%20journal%20for%20good", "snippet: systemd", "Set the limit, then restart the journal service. # /etc/systemd/journald.conf [Journal] SystemMaxUse=500M  sudo systemctl restart systemd-journald"],["Make sure a service can never start", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Make%20sure%20a%20service%20can%20never%20start", "snippet: systemd", "Stronger than disable: nothing can start it, not even as a dependency. sudo systemctl mask --now cups sudo systemctl unmask cups"],["How well is a service sandboxed", "systemd-journalctl-cheat-sheet.html?q=How%20well%20is%20a%20service%20sandboxed", "snippet: systemd", "A score from 0 (locked down) to 10 (exposed), with every missing hardening option listed. systemd-analyze security nginx"],["Linux users and permissions cheat sheet", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Linux users, groups and file permissions: create and lock accounts, sudo rules, chmod and chown, setgid folders, ACLs, and how to find out why access is denied."],["Create a user with a home directory", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20user%20with%20a%20home%20directory", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "Then set a password, or install an SSH key instead. sudo useradd -m -s /bin/bash anna sudo passwd anna"],["Create a service account that cannot log in", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20service%20account%20that%20cannot%20log%20in", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "System account, no shell, no home. For running a service or a job. sudo useradd -r -s /usr/sbin/nologin svc-backup"],["Add a user to a group", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Add%20a%20user%20to%20a%20group", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "The -a matters: without it the user is removed from every other group. Takes effect at the next login. sudo usermod -aG devs anna"],["Who is this user", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20is%20this%20user", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "User ID, primary group and all groups. id anna"],["Lock an account now", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Lock%20an%20account%20now", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "Locks the password and expires the account, which also stops SSH key logins. sudo usermod -L -e 1 anna"],["Unlock it again", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Unlock%20it%20again", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "Removes the lock and the expiry date. sudo usermod -U -e \"\" anna"],["Force a new password at the next login", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Force%20a%20new%20password%20at%20the%20next%20login", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "For a password you set for someone else. sudo chage -d 0 anna"],["Password age and expiry of an account", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Password%20age%20and%20expiry%20of%20an%20account", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "When it was changed, when it expires, when the account expires. sudo chage -l anna"],["Delete a user with home directory and mail spool", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Delete%20a%20user%20with%20home%20directory%20and%20mail%20spool", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "Check for running processes and cron jobs of the user first. sudo pkill -u anna sudo crontab -r -u anna sudo userdel -r anna"],["Who is logged in, and what are they doing", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20is%20logged%20in%2C%20and%20what%20are%20they%20doing", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "With source address and idle time. w"],["Recent logins and failed attempts", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Recent%20logins%20and%20failed%20attempts", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "last reads successful logins, lastb the failed ones. last -n 20 sudo lastb -n 20"],["What may this user run with sudo", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20may%20this%20user%20run%20with%20sudo", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "Reads all sudoers files the way sudo does. sudo -l -U anna"],["Allow one command with sudo", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Allow%20one%20command%20with%20sudo", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "Always edit through visudo: it checks the syntax and a broken sudoers file locks everyone out. sudo visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/anna  # line in the file: anna ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl restart nginx"],["Become another user with their environment", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Become%20another%20user%20with%20their%20environment", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "To test what that user can and cannot do. sudo -iu anna"],["Permissions in numbers", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Permissions%20in%20numbers", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "Read 4, write 2, execute 1, added up for owner, group, others. chmod 640 file      # owner read and write, group read, others nothing chmod 750 folder    # owner everything, group read and enter, others nothing"],["Fix a whole tree without making files executable", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Fix%20a%20whole%20tree%20without%20making%20files%20executable", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "The capital X sets execute only on folders and on files that already had it. chmod -R u=rwX,g=rX,o= /srv/data"],["Change owner and group", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Change%20owner%20and%20group", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "For a web root that the web server has to read. sudo chown -R www-data:www-data /var/www/site"],["A shared folder where new files belong to the group", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20shared%20folder%20where%20new%20files%20belong%20to%20the%20group", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "The setgid bit (the 2) makes new files inherit the group of the folder. sudo chgrp devs /srv/shared sudo chmod 2775 /srv/shared"],["Only the owner may delete in a shared folder", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Only%20the%20owner%20may%20delete%20in%20a%20shared%20folder", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "The sticky bit (the 1), as on /tmp. sudo chmod 1777 /srv/dropbox"],["Default permissions for new files", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Default%20permissions%20for%20new%20files", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "umask is what gets taken away: 027 means group cannot write, others get nothing. umask umask 027"],["Give one more user access with an ACL", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Give%20one%20more%20user%20access%20with%20an%20ACL", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "When owner and group are not enough. A plus sign in ls -l shows that an ACL exists. sudo setfacl -m u:anna:rwX /srv/project getfacl /srv/project"],["Make new files in a folder inherit an ACL", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Make%20new%20files%20in%20a%20folder%20inherit%20an%20ACL", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "The default ACL applies to everything created below from now on. sudo setfacl -R -m g:devs:rwX /srv/project sudo setfacl -R -d -m g:devs:rwX /srv/project"],["Why is access denied: check every folder on the way", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Why%20is%20access%20denied%3A%20check%20every%20folder%20on%20the%20way", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "Shows owner and permissions of each path component. One folder without x for the user is enough to block everything below. namei -l /var/www/site/index.html"],["Test access as the service user", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Test%20access%20as%20the%20service%20user", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "The quickest proof of whether the web server can read a file. sudo -u www-data cat /var/www/site/index.html > /dev/null && echo readable"],["Permissions that SSH insists on", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Permissions%20that%20SSH%20insists%20on", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "With looser permissions sshd silently ignores the key. chmod 700 ~/.ssh chmod 600 ~/.ssh/authorized_keys chmod go-w ~"],["Files without an owner", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Files%20without%20an%20owner", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "Left behind by deleted accounts. A new user who gets the same ID inherits them. sudo find / -xdev \\( -nouser -o -nogroup \\) -print"],["Permissions are right and it still fails: SELinux", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Permissions%20are%20right%20and%20it%20still%20fails%3A%20SELinux", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "On RHEL, Rocky, Alma and Fedora. Shows the mode and the latest denials. getenforce sudo ausearch -m avc -ts recent sudo restorecon -Rv /var/www/site"],["Permissions are right and it still fails: AppArmor", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=Permissions%20are%20right%20and%20it%20still%20fails%3A%20AppArmor", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "On Ubuntu, Debian and SUSE. sudo aa-status sudo journalctl -k | grep -i \"apparmor.*denied\" | tail"],["A file root cannot change", "linux-users-permissions-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20file%20root%20cannot%20change", "snippet: Linux users and permissions", "The immutable attribute. lsattr shows an i. lsattr file sudo chattr -i file"],["Linux disks and LVM cheat sheet", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Linux storage: find out what fills the disk, add and mount a disk, grow a volume with LVM after enlarging a virtual disk, snapshots, SMART health, swap and file system repair."],["What disks and partitions are there", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20disks%20and%20partitions%20are%20there", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "With file system, label, UUID and mount point. lsblk -f"],["How full are the file systems", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=How%20full%20are%20the%20file%20systems", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "With file system type. Above 90% it is time to act. df -hT"],["Disk full although df shows free space", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Disk%20full%20although%20df%20shows%20free%20space", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "Each file needs an inode. Millions of tiny files (sessions, cache, mail queue) use them up. df -i"],["What takes the space", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20takes%20the%20space", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "Top-level folders by size, staying on this file system. Repeat one level down. sudo du -xh --max-depth=1 / 2>/dev/null | sort -h | tail -n 15"],["Space that was deleted but is not free", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Space%20that%20was%20deleted%20but%20is%20not%20free", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "A deleted log file stays on disk while a process holds it open. Restart that process. sudo lsof +L1"],["Quick wins when the disk is full", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Quick%20wins%20when%20the%20disk%20is%20full", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "Package cache, old journal, old kernels. sudo journalctl --vacuum-time=7d sudo apt clean          # Debian, Ubuntu sudo dnf clean all      # RHEL, Rocky, Alma sudo apt autoremove --purge"],["Make the kernel see a new or enlarged virtual disk", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Make%20the%20kernel%20see%20a%20new%20or%20enlarged%20virtual%20disk", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "Without a reboot. The first line is for a new disk, the second for one that was enlarged. for h in /sys/class/scsi_host/host*; do echo \"- - -\" | sudo tee \"$h/scan\" > /dev/null; done echo 1 | sudo tee /sys/class/block/sda/device/rescan"],["Partition a new disk", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Partition%20a%20new%20disk", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "One partition over the whole disk. Destroys what is on it. sudo parted /dev/sdb --script mklabel gpt mkpart primary 0% 100%"],["Create a file system", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20file%20system", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "ext4 is the safe default, XFS the default on RHEL. Destroys what is on the partition. sudo mkfs.ext4 -L data /dev/sdb1 sudo mkfs.xfs -L data /dev/sdb1"],["Mount it for good", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Mount%20it%20for%20good", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "By UUID, never by device name: names change when disks are added. nofail lets the server boot if the disk is missing. sudo blkid /dev/sdb1 sudo mkdir -p /data  # line for /etc/fstab: UUID=PASTE-THE-UUID  /data  ext4  defaults,nofail  0  2  "],["LVM at a glance", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=LVM%20at%20a%20glance", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "Physical volumes, volume groups, logical volumes. VFree is the space you can still hand out. sudo pvs sudo vgs sudo lvs"],["Set up LVM on a new disk", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Set%20up%20LVM%20on%20a%20new%20disk", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "Disk into a volume group, one logical volume over all of it, then a file system. sudo pvcreate /dev/sdb sudo vgcreate vg_data /dev/sdb sudo lvcreate -n lv_data -l 100%FREE vg_data sudo mkfs.ext4 /dev/vg_data/lv_data"],["Grow a volume and its file system in one step", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Grow%20a%20volume%20and%20its%20file%20system%20in%20one%20step", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "The -r resizes the file system too. Works while mounted, for ext4 and XFS. sudo lvextend -r -L +20G /dev/vg_data/lv_data sudo lvextend -r -l +100%FREE /dev/vg_data/lv_data"],["Add another disk to a volume group", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Add%20another%20disk%20to%20a%20volume%20group", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "The new space shows up as VFree and can go to any volume in the group. sudo pvcreate /dev/sdc sudo vgextend vg_data /dev/sdc"],["The virtual disk was enlarged: use the new space", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20virtual%20disk%20was%20enlarged%3A%20use%20the%20new%20space", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "Grow the partition, tell LVM, grow the volume. Partition 3 of sda is an example, check with lsblk. sudo growpart /dev/sda 3 sudo pvresize /dev/sda3 sudo lvextend -r -l +100%FREE /dev/mapper/ubuntu--vg-ubuntu--lv"],["The same without LVM", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20same%20without%20LVM", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "Grow the partition, then the file system. growpart comes with cloud-guest-utils or cloud-utils-growpart. sudo growpart /dev/sda 1 sudo resize2fs /dev/sda1     # ext4 sudo xfs_growfs /            # XFS, takes the mount point"],["Snapshot before a risky change", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Snapshot%20before%20a%20risky%20change", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "Needs free space in the volume group. A snapshot that fills up becomes useless, so do not keep it for long. sudo lvcreate -s -n before_upgrade -L 5G /dev/vg_data/lv_data"],["Roll back to the snapshot, or drop it", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Roll%20back%20to%20the%20snapshot%2C%20or%20drop%20it", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "A merge of a mounted volume happens at the next activation, usually the next reboot. sudo lvconvert --merge /dev/vg_data/before_upgrade sudo lvremove /dev/vg_data/before_upgrade"],["Is the disk dying", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20disk%20dying", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "Watch Reallocated_Sector_Ct, Current_Pending_Sector and Offline_Uncorrectable: anything above zero and rising means replace it. sudo smartctl -H -A /dev/sda sudo nvme smart-log /dev/nvme0"],["Is the disk the bottleneck", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20disk%20the%20bottleneck", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "%util near 100 and a high await mean the disk cannot keep up. iostat -xz 2"],["Which process is writing", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20process%20is%20writing", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "Accumulated since start, only processes that do I/O. sudo iotop -oPa"],["Software RAID state", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Software%20RAID%20state", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "[UU] is healthy, [U_] means one disk is missing. cat /proc/mdstat sudo mdadm --detail /dev/md0"],["The file system went read-only", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20file%20system%20went%20read-only", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "The kernel does that after I/O errors to protect the data. Find the cause before you remount. sudo dmesg | grep -iE \"i/o error|remount|ext4-fs error|xfs\" | tail -n 20 sudo mount -o remount,rw /"],["Check and repair a file system", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20and%20repair%20a%20file%20system", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "Only on an unmounted file system. For the root file system, boot a rescue system. sudo umount /data sudo fsck -f /dev/sdb1          # ext4 sudo xfs_repair /dev/sdb1       # XFS"],["Add a swap file", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Add%20a%20swap%20file", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "For a server that has none and runs out of memory. Add the last line to /etc/fstab to keep it. sudo fallocate -l 2G /swapfile sudo chmod 600 /swapfile sudo mkswap /swapfile sudo swapon /swapfile # /swapfile none swap sw 0 0"],["Give back the space reserved for root", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Give%20back%20the%20space%20reserved%20for%20root", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "ext4 keeps 5% for root. On a large data volume that is a lot. sudo tune2fs -m 1 /dev/vg_data/lv_data"],["Tell an SSD or a thin disk what is free", "linux-disks-lvm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Tell%20an%20SSD%20or%20a%20thin%20disk%20what%20is%20free", "snippet: Linux disks and LVM", "Most distributions run this weekly by timer. sudo fstrim -av systemctl status fstrim.timer"],["nginx and Apache cheat sheet", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "nginx and Apache side by side: test and reload the configuration, virtual hosts, reverse proxy, HTTPS redirect, Let's Encrypt, reading access logs, and what 502, 504 and 413 mean."],["Test the configuration before you reload", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=Test%20the%20configuration%20before%20you%20reload", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "A reload with a broken configuration keeps the old one running, a restart takes the site down. sudo nginx -t sudo apachectl configtest"],["Apply changes without dropping connections", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=Apply%20changes%20without%20dropping%20connections", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "Reload, not restart. sudo systemctl reload nginx sudo systemctl reload apache2"],["Show what is really configured", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=Show%20what%20is%20really%20configured", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "nginx prints the complete merged configuration, Apache the list of virtual hosts and which one is the default. sudo nginx -T | less sudo apachectl -S"],["What is listening on 80 and 443", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20is%20listening%20on%2080%20and%20443", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "When the web server will not start because the port is taken. sudo ss -tlnp | grep -E ':(80|443)\\s'"],["nginx: a static site", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=nginx%3A%20a%20static%20site", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "Save in /etc/nginx/sites-available/example.org and link it into sites-enabled. server {     listen 80;     server_name example.org www.example.org;     root /var/www/example.org;     index index.html;      location / {         try_files $ur"],["nginx: enable a site", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=nginx%3A%20enable%20a%20site", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "The link is what switches it on. sudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/example.org /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/ sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx"],["nginx: reverse proxy to an app", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=nginx%3A%20reverse%20proxy%20to%20an%20app", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "The headers tell the app the real host, client address and protocol. The last three lines are for WebSockets. server {     listen 80;     server_name app.example.org;      location / {         proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;         proxy"],["nginx: send everything to HTTPS", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=nginx%3A%20send%20everything%20to%20HTTPS", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "A separate server block for port 80. server {     listen 80;     server_name example.org www.example.org;     return 301 https://$host$request_uri; }"],["nginx: sensible TLS settings", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=nginx%3A%20sensible%20TLS%20settings", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "Inside the server block for port 443. Add HSTS only when every subdomain works over HTTPS. listen 443 ssl http2; ssl_certificate     /etc/letsencrypt/live/example.org/fullchain.pem; ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/example.org/priv"],["Apache: a virtual host", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=Apache%3A%20a%20virtual%20host", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "Save in /etc/apache2/sites-available/example.org.conf. <VirtualHost *:80>     ServerName example.org     ServerAlias www.example.org     DocumentRoot /var/www/example.org     ErrorLog ${APACHE_LOG_DIR}/example.org-error.log     CustomLog ${"],["Apache: enable sites and modules", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=Apache%3A%20enable%20sites%20and%20modules", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "Debian and Ubuntu helpers. They create and remove the links for you. sudo a2ensite example.org sudo a2enmod rewrite ssl headers proxy proxy_http sudo apachectl configtest && sudo systemctl reload apache2"],["Apache: reverse proxy to an app", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=Apache%3A%20reverse%20proxy%20to%20an%20app", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "Needs the modules proxy and proxy_http. <VirtualHost *:80>     ServerName app.example.org     ProxyPreserveHost On     ProxyPass        / http://127.0.0.1:3000/     ProxyPassReverse / http://127.0.0.1:3000/     RequestHeader set X-Forwarded"],["Apache: send everything to HTTPS", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=Apache%3A%20send%20everything%20to%20HTTPS", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "Inside the virtual host for port 80. Redirect permanent / https://example.org/"],["A free certificate with Let's Encrypt", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=A%20free%20certificate%20with%20Let%27s%20Encrypt", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "certbot edits the configuration and sets up the renewal. Port 80 must be reachable from the internet. sudo certbot --nginx -d example.org -d www.example.org sudo certbot --apache -d example.org -d www.example.org"],["Will the renewal work", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=Will%20the%20renewal%20work", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "A rehearsal against the staging servers, and the timer that runs the real one. sudo certbot renew --dry-run systemctl list-timers | grep -i certbot"],["Test a site before DNS points to it", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=Test%20a%20site%20before%20DNS%20points%20to%20it", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "Sends the request to this server while asking for the real name. curl -sI --resolve example.org:443:127.0.0.1 https://example.org/ curl -sI -H \"Host: example.org\" http://127.0.0.1/"],["Follow the error log", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=Follow%20the%20error%20log", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "The reason for a 500 or 502 is here, not in the browser. sudo tail -f /var/log/nginx/error.log sudo tail -f /var/log/apache2/error.log"],["Who sends the most requests", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20sends%20the%20most%20requests", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "Top client addresses in the access log. sudo awk '{print $1}' /var/log/nginx/access.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -n 15"],["Status codes at a glance", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=Status%20codes%20at%20a%20glance", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "How many 200, 301, 404, 500 and so on. sudo awk '{print $9}' /var/log/nginx/access.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn"],["Which URLs fail", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20URLs%20fail", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "The most frequent paths that return a 5xx. sudo awk '$9 ~ /^5/ {print $9, $7}' /var/log/nginx/access.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -n 15"],["Requests per minute", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=Requests%20per%20minute", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "Shows when a spike started. sudo awk '{print substr($4, 2, 17)}' /var/log/nginx/access.log | uniq -c | tail -n 30"],["502 Bad Gateway", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=502%20Bad%20Gateway", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "The proxy works, the app behind it does not answer. Check that the app runs and listens where the proxy expects it. systemctl status myapp sudo ss -tlnp | grep 3000 curl -sI http://127.0.0.1:3000/"],["504 Gateway Timeout", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=504%20Gateway%20Timeout", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "The app answers too slowly. Raise the timeout only if slow answers are expected, otherwise fix the app. # nginx, inside the location block proxy_read_timeout 120s;  # Apache, inside the virtual host ProxyTimeout 120"],["413 Request Entity Too Large", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=413%20Request%20Entity%20Too%20Large", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "An upload is bigger than the server allows. The nginx default is 1 MB. # nginx, in http, server or location client_max_body_size 50m;  # Apache LimitRequestBody 52428800"],["403 or \"Permission denied\" in the error log", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=403%20or%20%22Permission%20denied%22%20in%20the%20error%20log", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "The web server user cannot read the file or enter a folder on the way. On RHEL-like systems it is often SELinux. namei -l /var/www/example.org/index.html sudo setsebool -P httpd_can_network_connect 1     # SELinux: allow proxying sudo resto"],["nginx: protect a path with a password", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=nginx%3A%20protect%20a%20path%20with%20a%20password", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "htpasswd comes with apache2-utils or httpd-tools. sudo htpasswd -c /etc/nginx/.htpasswd anna  # inside the location block auth_basic \"Restricted\"; auth_basic_user_file /etc/nginx/.htpasswd;"],["nginx: slow down a noisy client", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=nginx%3A%20slow%20down%20a%20noisy%20client", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "Ten requests per second per address, with a small burst. The first line goes into the http block. limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=perip:10m rate=10r/s;  # inside server or location limit_req zone=perip burst=20 nodelay;"],["nginx: block an address", "nginx-apache-cheat-sheet.html?q=nginx%3A%20block%20an%20address", "snippet: nginx and Apache", "Inside http, server or location. deny 203.0.113.7; deny 198.51.100.0/24;"],["Command builder", "command-builder.html", "tool", "Build robocopy, rsync, tar and find commands by ticking options: every switch explained in plain words, with warnings before a command deletes something. robocopy /MIR exit codes, rsync trailing slash --delete, tar extract create, find -mtime -delete -exec"],["robocopy command builder", "command-builder.html#t=robocopy", "tool", "Copy, mirror or move folders on Windows. /MIR /E /COPYALL /ZB /MT /XJ, exit codes"],["rsync command builder", "command-builder.html#t=rsync", "tool", "Synchronise folders over SSH. -a --delete --exclude --link-dest, trailing slash"],["tar command builder", "command-builder.html#t=tar", "tool", "Create, extract or list archives. gzip, xz, zstd, --strip-components"],["find command builder", "command-builder.html#t=find", "tool", "Find files by name, age, size, owner. -mtime -size -delete -exec xargs"],["Certificate decoder", "certificate-decoder.html", "tool", "Decode an X.509 certificate, chain or CSR from PEM: subject alternative names, expiry, key size, issuer, chain order, signature check, host name match, SSL TLS certificate errors explained"],["RAID calculator", "raid-calculator.html", "tool", "Usable capacity, fault tolerance and rebuild risk for RAID 0, 1, 5, 6, 10, 50, 60 and RAID-Z, with a comparison of every level for your disks."],["Backup planner", "backup-planner.html", "tool", "Plan a backup: retention with daily, weekly, monthly and yearly restore points, the storage it needs, how long backups and offsite uploads take, and a 3-2-1-1-0 check."],["Transfer time calculator", "transfer-time-calculator.html", "tool", "How long a copy, upload or migration takes: enter the amount of data and the speed of the line or disk, with Mbit/s and MB/s told apart and a comparison of common links."],["Firewall rule reviewer", "firewall-rule-reviewer.html", "tool", "Review firewall rules: Azure NSG JSON, iptables-save, Windows Firewall or CSV. Finds RDP, SSH and databases open to the internet, wide port ranges, shadowed and redundant rules, no outbound filtering"],["Conditional Access policy builder", "ca-policy-builder.html", "tool", "Build a Conditional Access baseline: MFA for admins and all users, block legacy authentication, device code flow, risk policies, managed devices, countries. PowerShell script and JSON, report-only, break-glass exclusion"],["Defender for Office 365 cheat sheet", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Defender for Office 365 with PowerShell and KQL: read the anti-phishing, Safe Links and Safe Attachments policies, find the allow entries that let mail through, manage quarantine and the Tenant Allow/Block List, purge a phish."],["Connect", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Exchange Online PowerShell covers almost every command on this page. Connect-ExchangeOnline -UserPrincipalName admin@contoso.com"],["Are the preset security policies switched on", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Are%20the%20preset%20security%20policies%20switched%20on", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Standard and Strict presets, and who they apply to. No output means nobody uses the presets. Get-EOPProtectionPolicyRule | Select-Object Name, State, Priority, SentTo, SentToMemberOf, RecipientDomainIs Get-ATPProtectionPolicyRule | Select-O"],["Compare your policies with Microsoft's recommendation", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Compare%20your%20policies%20with%20Microsoft%27s%20recommendation", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "The configuration analyzer as a list: every setting that is weaker than the Standard preset. Use Strict to compare against the strict one. Get-ConfigAnalyzerPolicyRecommendation -RecommendedPolicyType Standard |   Select-Object PolicyGroup,"],["Anti-phishing policies", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Anti-phishing%20policies", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Threshold 1 is the default, 2 to 4 are more aggressive. Impersonation protection is off until you list users and domains. Get-AntiPhishPolicy | Select-Object Name, Enabled, PhishThresholdLevel, EnableSpoofIntelligence,   EnableMailboxIntell"],["Who is protected against impersonation", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20is%20protected%20against%20impersonation", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "The people and domains an attacker would pretend to be: management, finance, your own domains, key partners. Get-AntiPhishPolicy | Select-Object Name, TargetedUsersToProtect, TargetedDomainsToProtect, ExcludedSenders, ExcludedDomains | Form"],["Safe Links policies", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Safe%20Links%20policies", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "AllowClickThrough should be False, otherwise users can click past the warning. Get-SafeLinksPolicy | Select-Object Name, EnableSafeLinksForEmail, EnableSafeLinksForTeams, EnableSafeLinksForOffice,   ScanUrls, DeliverMessageAfterScan, Enable"],["Safe Attachments policies", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Safe%20Attachments%20policies", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Action Block is the recommended setting. Allow means the feature only watches. Get-SafeAttachmentPolicy | Select-Object Name, Enable, Action, QuarantineTag, Redirect, RedirectAddress"],["Protection for SharePoint, OneDrive and Teams files", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Protection%20for%20SharePoint%2C%20OneDrive%20and%20Teams%20files", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "One switch for the whole tenant, and it is off by default. Get-AtpPolicyForO365 | Select-Object EnableATPForSPOTeamsODB, EnableSafeDocs, AllowSafeDocsOpen"],["Anti-spam policies: actions and thresholds", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Anti-spam%20policies%3A%20actions%20and%20thresholds", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "What happens to spam, phishing and bulk mail, and whether zero-hour auto purge is on. Get-HostedContentFilterPolicy | Select-Object Name, SpamAction, HighConfidenceSpamAction, PhishSpamAction,   HighConfidencePhishAction, BulkThreshold, Spa"],["Allowed senders and domains in anti-spam policies", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Allowed%20senders%20and%20domains%20in%20anti-spam%20policies", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Every entry here skips spam filtering and most phishing checks. Allowed domains are the classic hole: anyone can forge the domain. Get-HostedContentFilterPolicy | Where-Object { $_.AllowedSenderDomains -or $_.AllowedSenders } |   Select-Obj"],["Mail flow rules that bypass filtering", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Mail%20flow%20rules%20that%20bypass%20filtering", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Rules that set the spam confidence level to -1. Each one needs an owner and a reason. Get-TransportRule | Where-Object { $_.SetSCL -eq -1 } |   Select-Object Name, State, SenderDomainIs, SenderIpRanges, FromAddressContainsWords, Comments | "],["IP addresses on the connection filter allow list", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=IP%20addresses%20on%20the%20connection%20filter%20allow%20list", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Mail from these addresses skips spam filtering completely. Get-HostedConnectionFilterPolicy | Select-Object Name, IPAllowList, IPBlockList, EnableSafeList"],["Tenant Allow/Block List: what is in it", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Tenant%20Allow/Block%20List%3A%20what%20is%20in%20it", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "One list per type. Allow entries expire by design, block entries may be permanent. Get-TenantAllowBlockListItems -ListType Sender | Select-Object Value, Action, ExpirationDate, Notes Get-TenantAllowBlockListItems -ListType Url | Select-Obje"],["Block a sender or a domain", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Block%20a%20sender%20or%20a%20domain", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Blocked mail is treated as high confidence phishing and quarantined. New-TenantAllowBlockListItems -ListType Sender -Block -Entries 'bad@example.com','example.net' -NoExpiration -Notes 'Ticket 1234' "],["Block a URL", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Block%20a%20URL", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "The wildcard blocks every path below the host. New-TenantAllowBlockListItems -ListType Url -Block -Entries 'example.net/*' -ExpirationDate (Get-Date).AddDays(90) -Notes 'Ticket 1234' "],["Remove an entry again", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Remove%20an%20entry%20again", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "By value. Use the same list type you created it in. Remove-TenantAllowBlockListItems -ListType Sender -Entries 'bad@example.com' "],["Who sends mail in the name of your domains", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20sends%20mail%20in%20the%20name%20of%20your%20domains", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "The spoof intelligence insight: senders that forge a domain, with the verdict Microsoft chose. Get-SpoofIntelligenceInsight | Select-Object SpoofedUser, SendingInfrastructure, SpoofType, Action, MessageCount"],["Quarantined mail for one recipient", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Quarantined%20mail%20for%20one%20recipient", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "The last seven days. Type tells you why it was held. Get-QuarantineMessage -RecipientAddress user@contoso.com -StartReceivedDate (Get-Date).AddDays(-7) |   Select-Object ReceivedTime, SenderAddress, Subject, Type, PolicyName, ReleaseStatus,"],["Release a quarantined message", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Release%20a%20quarantined%20message", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "To everyone it was addressed to. Look at it first: Preview-QuarantineMessage shows the body. Preview-QuarantineMessage -Identity 'IDENTITY-FROM-THE-LIST' | Select-Object Subject, Body Release-QuarantineMessage -Identity 'IDENTITY-FROM-THE-L"],["Quarantine policies", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Quarantine%20policies", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "What users may do with their own quarantined mail, and whether they get notifications. Get-QuarantinePolicy | Select-Object Name, EndUserQuarantinePermissionsValue, ESNEnabled"],["DKIM signing state per domain", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=DKIM%20signing%20state%20per%20domain", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Enabled and Valid is the goal. CnameMissing means the two DNS records are not there yet. Get-DkimSigningConfig | Select-Object Domain, Enabled, Status, Selector1CNAME, Selector2CNAME"],["Purge a phish from every mailbox", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Purge%20a%20phish%20from%20every%20mailbox", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Security and Compliance PowerShell. Search, check the hit count, then soft delete. Removes at most ten items per mailbox per run. Connect-IPPSSession New-ComplianceSearch -Name 'Phish 1234' -ExchangeLocation All -ContentMatchQuery 'subject:"],["Phishing mail that was delivered (KQL)", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Phishing%20mail%20that%20was%20delivered%20%28KQL%29", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Advanced hunting. Mail the filter recognised as phishing and still delivered, usually because of an allow entry. EmailEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where ThreatTypes has \"Phish\" and DeliveryAction == \"Delivered\" | project Timestamp, "],["Which allow let bad mail through (KQL)", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20allow%20let%20bad%20mail%20through%20%28KQL%29", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Counts delivered mail with a threat by the override that allowed it. EmailEvents | where Timestamp > ago(30d) | where ThreatTypes != \"\" and DeliveryAction == \"Delivered\" | summarize Mails = count() by OrgLevelPolicy, OrgLevelAction, UserLev"],["Clicks on malicious links (KQL)", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Clicks%20on%20malicious%20links%20%28KQL%29", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Who clicked, and who clicked through the warning page. UrlClickEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where ThreatTypes != \"\" | project Timestamp, AccountUpn, Url, ActionType, IsClickedThrough, Workload, NetworkMessageId | order by Timestamp "],["What zero-hour auto purge removed (KQL)", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20zero-hour%20auto%20purge%20removed%20%28KQL%29", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Mail that was judged bad after delivery and pulled back out of the mailbox. EmailPostDeliveryEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where ActionType has \"ZAP\" | summarize Mails = count() by ActionType, ActionResult, ThreatTypes"],["Everyone who received the same mail (KQL)", "defender-office-365-cheat-sheet.html?q=Everyone%20who%20received%20the%20same%20mail%20%28KQL%29", "snippet: Defender for Office 365", "Start from one reported message and find the whole campaign by sender and subject. EmailEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where SenderFromAddress =~ \"bad@example.com\" or Subject has \"Invoice 4471\" | project Timestamp, RecipientEmailAddre"],["SharePoint sharing and guest access cheat sheet", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "External sharing in SharePoint and OneDrive and guest access in Entra with PowerShell: tenant and site sharing levels, Anyone links, guest expiry, domain limits, who may invite, audit queries."],["Connect", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "The admin URL is your tenant name followed by -admin. Connect-SPOService -Url https://contoso-admin.sharepoint.com"],["Sharing settings of the tenant", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Sharing%20settings%20of%20the%20tenant", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "The whole picture in one call. SharingCapability is the upper limit for every site. Get-SPOTenant | Select-Object SharingCapability, OneDriveSharingCapability, DefaultSharingLinkType, DefaultLinkPermission,   RequireAnonymousLinksExpireInDa"],["What the four sharing levels mean", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20the%20four%20sharing%20levels%20mean", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "From closed to open. The names in PowerShell do not match the labels in the admin center. # Disabled                          Only people in your organisation # ExistingExternalUserSharingOnly   Existing guests # ExternalUserSharingOnly    "],["Switch off Anyone links for the tenant", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Switch%20off%20Anyone%20links%20for%20the%20tenant", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "Guests still work, but every guest has to sign in. Set-SPOTenant -SharingCapability ExternalUserSharingOnly"],["Make the default link the careful one", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Make%20the%20default%20link%20the%20careful%20one", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "New links go to specific people with view permission unless the user chooses otherwise. Set-SPOTenant -DefaultSharingLinkType Direct -DefaultLinkPermission View"],["Let Anyone links expire and make them read-only", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Let%20Anyone%20links%20expire%20and%20make%20them%20read-only", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "If you keep Anyone links, limit how long they live and what they allow. Set-SPOTenant -RequireAnonymousLinksExpireInDays 14 -FileAnonymousLinkType View -FolderAnonymousLinkType View"],["Let guest access expire", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Let%20guest%20access%20expire", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "Guests lose access to a site after 90 days unless a site owner extends it. Set-SPOTenant -ExternalUserExpirationRequired $true -ExternalUserExpireInDays 90"],["Allow sharing only with certain domains", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Allow%20sharing%20only%20with%20certain%20domains", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "The list is one string with spaces between the domains. Set-SPOTenant -SharingDomainRestrictionMode AllowList -SharingAllowedDomainList 'partner.com supplier.de' "],["Stop guests from sharing onward", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Stop%20guests%20from%20sharing%20onward", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "Guests cannot share items they do not own. Set-SPOTenant -PreventExternalUsersFromResharing $true"],["Sharing level of every site", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Sharing%20level%20of%20every%20site", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "Sorted so the most open sites stand together. Get-SPOSite -Limit All | Select-Object Url, SharingCapability, Owner, LastContentModifiedDate |   Sort-Object SharingCapability, Url"],["Sites that allow Anyone links", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Sites%20that%20allow%20Anyone%20links", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "The short list worth reading line by line. Get-SPOSite -Limit All | Where-Object SharingCapability -eq 'ExternalUserAndGuestSharing' |   Select-Object Url, Owner, StorageUsageCurrent"],["Close one site to the outside", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Close%20one%20site%20to%20the%20outside", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "For sites with personnel, finance or customer data. Set-SPOSite -Identity https://contoso.sharepoint.com/sites/hr -SharingCapability Disabled"],["OneDrive sites and their sharing level", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=OneDrive%20sites%20and%20their%20sharing%20level", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "OneDrive has its own limit and is often more open than anyone remembers. Get-SPOSite -IncludePersonalSite $true -Limit All -Filter \"Url -like '-my.sharepoint.com/personal/'\" |   Select-Object Url, SharingCapability, Owner"],["External users known to SharePoint", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=External%20users%20known%20to%20SharePoint", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "Returns 50 per call. Raise Position by 50 until nothing comes back. Get-SPOExternalUser -Position 0 -PageSize 50 | Select-Object DisplayName, Email, AcceptedAs, WhenCreated"],["External users of one site", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=External%20users%20of%20one%20site", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "Who from outside can get into this site. Get-SPOExternalUser -SiteUrl https://contoso.sharepoint.com/sites/project-x -PageSize 50 |   Select-Object DisplayName, Email, AcceptedAs, WhenCreated"],["Read-only access from unmanaged devices", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read-only%20access%20from%20unmanaged%20devices", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "Browser only, no download, print or sync on devices that are not compliant or joined. Creates Conditional Access policies and needs Entra ID P1. Set-SPOTenant -ConditionalAccessPolicy AllowLimitedAccess"],["The same limit for one site only", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=The%20same%20limit%20for%20one%20site%20only", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "Leaves the rest of the tenant alone. You create the matching Conditional Access policy yourself. Set-SPOSite -Identity https://contoso.sharepoint.com/sites/finance -ConditionalAccessPolicy AllowLimitedAccess"],["Use Entra B2B for sharing", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Use%20Entra%20B2B%20for%20sharing", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "Guests who receive a file become real guest accounts, so Conditional Access and access reviews apply to them. Set-SPOTenant -EnableAzureADB2BIntegration $true"],["Who may invite guests", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20may%20invite%20guests", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "everyone includes guests themselves. adminsAndGuestInviters is the strict choice. Connect-MgGraph -Scopes 'Policy.Read.All' (Get-MgPolicyAuthorizationPolicy).AllowInvitesFrom # everyone | adminsGuestInvitersAndAllMembers | adminsAndGuestInv"],["Restrict who may invite guests", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Restrict%20who%20may%20invite%20guests", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "Needs Policy.ReadWrite.Authorization. Update-MgPolicyAuthorizationPolicy -AllowInvitesFrom 'adminsAndGuestInviters' "],["What guests can see in the directory", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20guests%20can%20see%20in%20the%20directory", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "The ID stands for one of three levels. (Get-MgPolicyAuthorizationPolicy).GuestUserRoleId # a0b1b346-4d3e-4e8b-98f8-753987be4970   same access as members # 10dae51f-b6af-4016-8d66-8c2a99b929b3   limited access (default) # 2af84b1e-32c8-42b7-"],["All guest accounts with their state", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=All%20guest%20accounts%20with%20their%20state", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "PendingAcceptance means the invitation was never redeemed. Get-MgUser -Filter \"userType eq 'Guest'\" -All -Property displayName, mail, createdDateTime, externalUserState |   Select-Object DisplayName, Mail, CreatedDateTime, ExternalUserState"],["Invitations nobody accepted", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Invitations%20nobody%20accepted", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "Older than 30 days and still pending: safe to remove. $cut = (Get-Date).AddDays(-30) Get-MgUser -Filter \"userType eq 'Guest' and externalUserState eq 'PendingAcceptance'\" -All -Property displayName, mail, createdDateTime |   Where-Object { "],["Teams and groups that contain guests", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Teams%20and%20groups%20that%20contain%20guests", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "Slow in a large tenant, since it reads the members of every Microsoft 365 group. Get-MgGroup -Filter \"groupTypes/any(c:c eq 'Unified')\" -All | ForEach-Object {   $g = $_   $n = @(Get-MgGroupMember -GroupId $g.Id -All | Where-Object { $_.Add"],["Sharing events from the audit log", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Sharing%20events%20from%20the%20audit%20log", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "Exchange Online PowerShell. Who created Anyone links and invitations in the last week. Search-UnifiedAuditLog -StartDate (Get-Date).AddDays(-7) -EndDate (Get-Date) -ResultSize 1000 `   -Operations AnonymousLinkCreated, SharingInvitationCrea"],["Who shares the most (KQL)", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20shares%20the%20most%20%28KQL%29", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "For a Sentinel workspace with the Microsoft 365 connector. OfficeActivity | where TimeGenerated > ago(30d) | where Operation in (\"AnonymousLinkCreated\", \"SharingInvitationCreated\", \"SecureLinkCreated\") | summarize Shares = count() by UserId"],["Anyone links that were opened (KQL)", "sharepoint-sharing-cheat-sheet.html?q=Anyone%20links%20that%20were%20opened%20%28KQL%29", "snippet: SharePoint sharing", "Each row is someone opening a link without signing in. The IP address is all you get. OfficeActivity | where TimeGenerated > ago(7d) | where Operation == \"AnonymousLinkUsed\" | project TimeGenerated, ClientIP, Site_Url, SourceFileName, Offic"],["Azure networking cheat sheet", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Azure networking with the Azure CLI: virtual networks and subnets, NSG rules open to the internet, effective rules and routes, Network Watcher checks, peering, private endpoints, private DNS and VPN."],["Virtual networks with their address space", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Virtual%20networks%20with%20their%20address%20space", "snippet: Azure networking", "Every network in the subscription. az network vnet list --query \"[].{name:name, rg:resourceGroup, location:location, space:join(', ', addressSpace.addressPrefixes)}\" -o table"],["Subnets with their NSG and route table", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Subnets%20with%20their%20NSG%20and%20route%20table", "snippet: Azure networking", "An empty nsg column means nothing filters that subnet. az network vnet subnet list -g RG --vnet-name VNET --query \"[].{name:name, prefix:addressPrefix, nsg:networkSecurityGroup.id, routes:routeTable.id}\" -o table"],["Subnets without an NSG", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Subnets%20without%20an%20NSG", "snippet: Azure networking", "Across the subscription. GatewaySubnet and AzureFirewallSubnet are meant to have none. az network vnet list --query \"[].subnets[] | [?networkSecurityGroup==null].id\" -o tsv"],["Is an address free, and which ones are", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20an%20address%20free%2C%20and%20which%20ones%20are", "snippet: Azure networking", "Before you give a VM or a private endpoint a static address. az network vnet check-ip-address -g RG -n VNET --ip-address 10.0.1.10 az network vnet subnet list-available-ips -g RG --vnet-name VNET -n SUBNET"],["Rules of an NSG including the defaults", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Rules%20of%20an%20NSG%20including%20the%20defaults", "snippet: Azure networking", "The default rules explain most \"why does this work\" questions. az network nsg rule list -g RG --nsg-name NSG --include-default -o table"],["Inbound rules open to the whole internet", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Inbound%20rules%20open%20to%20the%20whole%20internet", "snippet: Azure networking", "Resource Graph, all subscriptions you can read. RDP and SSH should never appear here. az graph query -q \"Resources | where type =~ 'microsoft.network/networksecuritygroups' | mv-expand rule = properties.securityRules | where rule.properties"],["Rules that really apply to a network card", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Rules%20that%20really%20apply%20to%20a%20network%20card", "snippet: Azure networking", "Subnet NSG and NIC NSG combined, with service tags resolved. The VM must be running. az network nic list-effective-nsg -g RG -n NIC"],["Routes that really apply to a network card", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Routes%20that%20really%20apply%20to%20a%20network%20card", "snippet: Azure networking", "System routes, your route table and BGP together. Shows where 0.0.0.0/0 goes. az network nic show-effective-route-table -g RG -n NIC -o table"],["Would this packet be allowed", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Would%20this%20packet%20be%20allowed", "snippet: Azure networking", "IP flow verify: names the rule that allows or denies. Local is the VM side. az network watcher test-ip-flow -g RG --vm VM --direction Inbound --protocol TCP --local 10.0.1.4:3389 --remote 203.0.113.10:50000"],["Where does traffic to this address go next", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Where%20does%20traffic%20to%20this%20address%20go%20next", "snippet: Azure networking", "Next hop: Internet, VirtualAppliance, VnetLocal, VirtualNetworkGateway or None, which means dropped. az network watcher show-next-hop -g RG --vm VM --source-ip 10.0.1.4 --dest-ip 10.20.0.5"],["Test a connection from a VM", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Test%20a%20connection%20from%20a%20VM", "snippet: Azure networking", "Connection troubleshoot. Reports each hop and where it stops. Needs the Network Watcher agent on the VM. az network watcher test-connectivity -g RG --source-resource VM --dest-address 10.20.0.5 --dest-port 443"],["Public IP addresses that nothing uses", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Public%20IP%20addresses%20that%20nothing%20uses", "snippet: Azure networking", "They cost money and tend to be forgotten. az network public-ip list --query \"[?ipConfiguration==null].{name:name, rg:resourceGroup, ip:ipAddress, sku:sku.name}\" -o table"],["VMs and their addresses", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=VMs%20and%20their%20addresses", "snippet: Azure networking", "Private and public side by side. Every public address here is attack surface. az vm list-ip-addresses -o table"],["Peerings of a network", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Peerings%20of%20a%20network", "snippet: Azure networking", "Connected is the only good state. Forwarded traffic and gateway transit matter in hub and spoke. az network vnet peering list -g RG --vnet-name VNET --query \"[].{name:name, state:peeringState, sync:peeringSyncLevel, forwarded:allowForwarded"],["Routes in a route table", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Routes%20in%20a%20route%20table", "snippet: Azure networking", "A 0.0.0.0/0 route to a virtual appliance sends all outbound traffic through the firewall. az network route-table route list -g RG --route-table-name RT -o table"],["DNS servers of a network", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=DNS%20servers%20of%20a%20network", "snippet: Azure networking", "Empty means Azure-provided DNS. Custom servers must be able to resolve the private zones. az network vnet show -g RG -n VNET --query dhcpOptions.dnsServers"],["Private endpoints and what they point at", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Private%20endpoints%20and%20what%20they%20point%20at", "snippet: Azure networking", "Approved is the state you want. Pending waits for the owner of the target. az network private-endpoint list --query \"[].{name:name, rg:resourceGroup, target:privateLinkServiceConnections[0].privateLinkServiceId, state:privateLinkServiceConn"],["Private DNS zones and the networks linked to them", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Private%20DNS%20zones%20and%20the%20networks%20linked%20to%20them", "snippet: Azure networking", "A private endpoint without a linked zone resolves to the public address. az network private-dns zone list --query \"[].{zone:name, rg:resourceGroup, records:numberOfRecordSets}\" -o table az network private-dns link vnet list -g RG -z private"],["Does the name resolve to the private address", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Does%20the%20name%20resolve%20to%20the%20private%20address", "snippet: Azure networking", "Run on a VM inside the network. A 10.x answer is right, a public address means the zone link or the DNS forwarder is missing. nslookup mystorage.blob.core.windows.net"],["Storage accounts open to every network", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Storage%20accounts%20open%20to%20every%20network", "snippet: Azure networking", "Default action Allow means the firewall of the account is off. az storage account list --query \"[?networkRuleSet.defaultAction=='Allow'].{name:name, rg:resourceGroup, publicAccess:publicNetworkAccess}\" -o table"],["State of a VPN connection", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=State%20of%20a%20VPN%20connection", "snippet: Azure networking", "Connected, Connecting or NotConnected, with the bytes in each direction. az network vpn-connection show -g RG -n CONNECTION --query \"{status:connectionStatus, bytesIn:ingressBytesTransferred, bytesOut:egressBytesTransferred, type:connection"],["BGP peers and learned routes of a gateway", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=BGP%20peers%20and%20learned%20routes%20of%20a%20gateway", "snippet: Azure networking", "For VPN with BGP and for ExpressRoute coexistence. az network vnet-gateway list-bgp-peer-status -g RG -n GATEWAY -o table az network vnet-gateway list-learned-routes -g RG -n GATEWAY -o table"],["Addresses behind a service tag", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Addresses%20behind%20a%20service%20tag", "snippet: Azure networking", "What a tag such as Storage.WestEurope stands for today. The list changes weekly. az network list-service-tags -l westeurope --query \"values[?name=='Storage.WestEurope'].properties.addressPrefixes | [0]\""],["Flow logs in a region", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Flow%20logs%20in%20a%20region", "snippet: Azure networking", "Which networks and NSGs are being logged, and where the logs go. az network watcher flow-log list -l westeurope --query \"[].{name:name, target:targetResourceId, enabled:enabled, storage:storageId}\" -o table"],["Denied flows by destination port (KQL)", "azure-networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Denied%20flows%20by%20destination%20port%20%28KQL%29", "snippet: Azure networking", "For a workspace with traffic analytics. Shows what the NSGs block most. NTANetAnalytics | where TimeGenerated > ago(1d) | where SubType == \"FlowLog\" and FlowStatus == \"Denied\" | summarize Flows = count() by DestPort, FlowDirection | top 20 "],["Device code phishing explained", "device-code-phishing-explained.html", "page", "Interactive diagram of a device code phishing attack: how an attacker gets tokens through the real Microsoft sign-in page, MFA included, and how to block it."],["Access token", "glossary.html#access-token", "glossary", "A short-lived proof, usually valid for about an hour, that an app presents to a service such as Exchange or Graph. It states who the user is and what …"],["Admin consent", "glossary.html#admin-consent", "glossary", "An administrator approves an app's permissions for the whole organisation, so individual users are no longer asked. Needed for application permissions…"],["App protection policy", "glossary.html#app-protection-policy", "glossary", "Intune rules that apply to a work app instead of the whole device: a PIN for Outlook, no copying into private apps, a selective wipe of company data. …"],["App registration", "glossary.html#app-registration", "glossary", "The definition of an application in Entra ID: its ID, its secrets and certificates, its redirect addresses and the permissions it asks for. It lives i…"],["Application permission", "glossary.html#application-permission", "glossary", "A permission an app uses on its own, without a signed-in user, for example reading every mailbox. It is not limited to one person and is not subject t…"],["Client secret", "glossary.html#client-secret", "glossary", "A password for an application. It ends up in config files and pipelines, cannot do MFA and is valid until it expires. A certificate or a managed ident…"],["Delegated permission", "glossary.html#delegated-permission", "glossary", "A permission an app uses on behalf of the signed-in user. The app can do at most what that user can do. Compare application permission."],["Device code flow", "glossary.html#device-code-flow", "glossary", "A sign-in method for devices without a browser or keyboard: the device shows a code and the user enters it on another device. Convenient for meeting r…"],["Enterprise application", "glossary.html#enterprise-application", "glossary", "The local copy of an app inside your tenant, technically its service principal. It carries what your tenant granted the app: consents, role assignment…"],["Group-based licensing", "glossary.html#group-based-licensing", "glossary", "Licences are assigned to a group and every member gets them. A leaver who is removed from the group loses the licence automatically. Licences assigned…"],["Litigation hold", "glossary.html#litigation-hold", "glossary", "A setting that keeps everything in a mailbox, including deleted items, for as long as it is on. Used to preserve evidence. A mailbox on hold needs a l…"],["PKCE", "glossary.html#pkce", "glossary", "An addition to the OAuth authorization code flow in which the app proves that it is the same app that started the sign-in. It stops an intercepted cod…"],["Redirect URI", "glossary.html#redirect-uri", "glossary", "The address Entra ID sends the result of a sign-in to. It must match one registered for the app exactly. A wildcard or an unencrypted address here let…"],["Refresh token", "glossary.html#refresh-token", "glossary", "A long-lived token an app uses to get new access tokens without asking the user again. It is what keeps an attacker in after a phish, and why revoking…"],["Safeguard hold", "glossary.html#safeguard-hold", "glossary", "Microsoft holds back a Windows feature update on devices with a known incompatibility, such as a driver or an application. The device simply is not of…"],["Shared mailbox", "glossary.html#shared-mailbox", "glossary", "A mailbox several people open with their own accounts, such as info@ or invoices@. It needs no licence while it stays under 50 GB and has no archive o…"],["Staging mode", "glossary.html#staging-mode", "glossary", "An Entra Connect server in staging mode imports and calculates everything but writes nothing to Entra ID or Active Directory. Used to prepare a replac…"],["Supervised device", "glossary.html#supervised-device", "glossary", "An iPhone or iPad enrolled in a way that gives the organisation deeper control: silent app installs, forced updates, more restrictions. Supervision is…"],["Update ring", "glossary.html#update-ring", "glossary", "An Intune or Group Policy setting that says how long a group of devices waits before installing Windows updates. A few rings with rising delays let a …"],["Verified publisher", "glossary.html#verified-publisher", "glossary", "A blue badge on an app's consent screen showing that the publisher has proven its identity to Microsoft. Its absence on an app that asks for mail acce…"],["Entra app audit", "app-audit.html", "tool", "Audit app registrations and enterprise apps: dangerous application permissions, consent phishing, credentials on service principals, expiring and long-lived secrets, unused apps, apps without owner"],["License optimizer", "license-optimizer.html", "tool", "Find wasted Microsoft 365 licences: blocked accounts, overlapping licences, inactive users, shared mailboxes, unassigned seats, with savings per month and an export script"],["Entra PIM and access reviews cheat sheet", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Privileged Identity Management and access reviews with Microsoft Graph PowerShell: eligible and permanent role assignments, activation, role settings, audit queries."],["Connect with the scopes for reading", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect%20with%20the%20scopes%20for%20reading", "snippet: PIM", "Enough for every read-only command on this page. Connect-MgGraph -Scopes 'RoleManagement.Read.Directory','RoleEligibilitySchedule.Read.Directory','RoleAssignmentSchedule.Read.Directory','AccessReview.Read.All'"],["Find the ID of a role", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20the%20ID%20of%20a%20role", "snippet: PIM", "Most PIM commands want the role definition ID, not the name. Get-MgRoleManagementDirectoryRoleDefinition -Filter \"displayName eq 'Exchange Administrator'\" | Select-Object DisplayName, Id"],["Who is Global Administrator right now", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20is%20Global%20Administrator%20right%20now", "snippet: PIM", "Active members at this moment, permanent or activated. Microsoft recommends fewer than five. $role = Get-MgDirectoryRole -Filter \"displayName eq 'Global Administrator'\" Get-MgDirectoryRoleMember -DirectoryRoleId $role.Id |   Select-Object I"],["All eligible assignments", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=All%20eligible%20assignments", "snippet: PIM", "Who may activate which role, and until when. Get-MgRoleManagementDirectoryRoleEligibilitySchedule -All -ExpandProperty principal,roleDefinition |   Select-Object @{n='Role';e={$_.RoleDefinition.DisplayName}},     @{n='Principal';e={$_.Princ"],["All active assignments, with how they came about", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=All%20active%20assignments%2C%20with%20how%20they%20came%20about", "snippet: PIM", "AssignmentType Assigned means given directly, Activated means through PIM. Get-MgRoleManagementDirectoryRoleAssignmentSchedule -All -ExpandProperty principal,roleDefinition |   Select-Object @{n='Role';e={$_.RoleDefinition.DisplayName}},   "],["Standing access: active and never expiring", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Standing%20access%3A%20active%20and%20never%20expiring", "snippet: PIM", "The list PIM exists to shrink. Break-glass accounts belong here, little else does. Get-MgRoleManagementDirectoryRoleAssignmentSchedule -All -ExpandProperty principal,roleDefinition |   Where-Object { $_.AssignmentType -eq 'Assigned' -and $_"],["Applications that hold directory roles", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Applications%20that%20hold%20directory%20roles", "snippet: PIM", "Service principals with admin roles are easy to forget and never do MFA. Get-MgRoleManagementDirectoryRoleAssignment -All -ExpandProperty principal |   Where-Object { $_.Principal.AdditionalProperties.'@odata.type' -eq '#microsoft.graph.ser"],["Groups that can be assigned to roles", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Groups%20that%20can%20be%20assigned%20to%20roles", "snippet: PIM", "Membership in one of these is the same as having the role. Get-MgGroup -Filter 'isAssignableToRole eq true' | Select-Object DisplayName, Id"],["Make someone eligible for a role", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Make%20someone%20eligible%20for%20a%20role", "snippet: PIM", "Eligible for six months. Needs RoleManagement.ReadWrite.Directory. $params = @{   action = 'adminAssign'   principalId = 'USER-OBJECT-ID'   roleDefinitionId = 'ROLE-DEFINITION-ID'   directoryScopeId = '/'   justification = 'Ticket 1234'   s"],["Remove an eligible assignment", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Remove%20an%20eligible%20assignment", "snippet: PIM", "Same request with a different action. $params = @{ action = 'adminRemove'; principalId = 'USER-OBJECT-ID'; roleDefinitionId = 'ROLE-DEFINITION-ID'; directoryScopeId = '/' } New-MgRoleManagementDirectoryRoleEligibilityScheduleRequest -BodyPa"],["Activate your own eligible role", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Activate%20your%20own%20eligible%20role", "snippet: PIM", "For two hours. Fails if the role settings ask for approval or MFA you have not done in this session. $me = (Get-MgContext).Account $params = @{   action = 'selfActivate'   principalId = (Get-MgUser -UserId $me).Id   roleDefinitionId = 'ROLE"],["Read the settings of a role", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20the%20settings%20of%20a%20role", "snippet: PIM", "Maximum activation time, whether MFA, justification or approval is required. Needs RoleManagementPolicy.Read.Directory. Get-MgPolicyRoleManagementPolicyAssignment -Filter \"scopeId eq '/' and scopeType eq 'DirectoryRole' and roleDefinitionId"],["Activations in the last 30 days (KQL)", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Activations%20in%20the%20last%2030%20days%20%28KQL%29", "snippet: PIM", "For a Log Analytics workspace that receives the Entra audit logs. AuditLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(30d) | where Category == \"RoleManagement\" and OperationName has \"PIM activation\" | where OperationName has \"completed\" | project TimeGen"],["Roles assigned outside PIM (KQL)", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Roles%20assigned%20outside%20PIM%20%28KQL%29", "snippet: PIM", "Someone added a role member directly. Either a mistake or an attacker making access permanent. AuditLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(30d) | where OperationName has \"outside of PIM\" | project TimeGenerated, By = tostring(InitiatedBy.user.use"],["List the access reviews", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20the%20access%20reviews", "snippet: PIM", "Every review definition with its state. Get-MgIdentityGovernanceAccessReviewDefinition -All | Select-Object DisplayName, Status, Id"],["Rounds of one review", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Rounds%20of%20one%20review", "snippet: PIM", "A recurring review has one instance per round. Get-MgIdentityGovernanceAccessReviewDefinitionInstance -AccessReviewScheduleDefinitionId 'REVIEW-ID' |   Select-Object Id, Status, StartDateTime, EndDateTime"],["Decisions of one round", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Decisions%20of%20one%20round", "snippet: PIM", "Who was approved, denied or not reviewed, and the reason given. Get-MgIdentityGovernanceAccessReviewDefinitionInstanceDecision -AccessReviewScheduleDefinitionId 'REVIEW-ID' -AccessReviewInstanceId 'INSTANCE-ID' -All |   Select-Object Decisi"],["Guests who have not signed in for 90 days", "entra-pim-cheat-sheet.html?q=Guests%20who%20have%20not%20signed%20in%20for%2090%20days", "snippet: PIM", "Candidates for the next guest review. Needs AuditLog.Read.All and Entra ID P1. $cut = (Get-Date).AddDays(-90) Get-MgUser -Filter \"userType eq 'Guest'\" -Property displayName, userPrincipalName, signInActivity -All |   Where-Object { $_.SignI"],["Windows Update troubleshooting cheat sheet", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Windows Update and Windows Update for Business: which policy applies, scan source, safeguard holds, logs, pending restarts and the classic repairs."],["Exact Windows version and build", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Exact%20Windows%20version%20and%20build", "snippet: Windows Update", "The number after the dot (UBR) tells you the installed monthly update. Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion' | Select-Object DisplayVersion, CurrentBuild, UBR, EditionID"],["Update policies set by Group Policy", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Update%20policies%20set%20by%20Group%20Policy", "snippet: Windows Update", "Deferrals, target version, WSUS server. Empty output means no GPO sets anything. Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WindowsUpdate' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Wi"],["Update policies set by Intune", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Update%20policies%20set%20by%20Intune", "snippet: Windows Update", "What the update ring delivered to this device. Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\PolicyManager\\current\\device\\Update' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue"],["Does the device still point at WSUS", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Does%20the%20device%20still%20point%20at%20WSUS", "snippet: Windows Update", "A leftover WUServer with UseWUServer = 1 is the usual reason an Intune-managed device finds no updates. $p = 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WindowsUpdate' (Get-ItemProperty $p -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).WUServer (Get-ItemPro"],["Is a target version pinned", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20a%20target%20version%20pinned", "snippet: Windows Update", "A forgotten TargetReleaseVersionInfo keeps a device on an old feature update for ever. Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WindowsUpdate' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |   Select-Object TargetReleaseVersion, TargetRe"],["Are updates paused", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Are%20updates%20paused", "snippet: Windows Update", "Set by the user in Settings or by policy. Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\WindowsUpdate\\UX\\Settings' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |   Select-Object PauseUpdatesExpiryTime, PauseFeatureUpdatesEndTime, PauseQualityUpdatesEndTime"],["Is a safeguard hold blocking the feature update", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20a%20safeguard%20hold%20blocking%20the%20feature%20update", "snippet: Windows Update", "Microsoft holds back a feature update on devices with a known incompatibility. A GatedBlockId here means this device is held. Get-ChildItem 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\AppCompatFlags\\TargetVersionUpgradeExperienceInd"],["Start an update scan now", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Start%20an%20update%20scan%20now", "snippet: Windows Update", "Same as pressing Check for updates. usoclient StartInteractiveScan"],["Recently installed updates", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Recently%20installed%20updates", "snippet: Windows Update", "Quick list of the latest hotfixes. Get-HotFix | Sort-Object InstalledOn -Descending | Select-Object -First 10 HotFixID, Description, InstalledOn"],["Update history including failures", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Update%20history%20including%20failures", "snippet: Windows Update", "ResultCode 2 is success, 4 is failed, 5 is aborted. The HResult is the error to search for. $s = (New-Object -ComObject Microsoft.Update.Session).CreateUpdateSearcher() $s.QueryHistory(0, 25) | Select-Object Date, ResultCode, @{n='HResult';"],["Is a restart pending", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20a%20restart%20pending", "snippet: Windows Update", "Either key present means Windows waits for a restart and will not install more. Test-Path 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\WindowsUpdate\\Auto Update\\RebootRequired' Test-Path 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\"],["Free space on the system drive", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Free%20space%20on%20the%20system%20drive", "snippet: Windows Update", "Feature updates need roughly 20 GB free. Low space fails silently more often than with an error. Get-PSDrive C | Select-Object @{n='FreeGB';e={[math]::Round($_.Free/1GB,1)}}, @{n='UsedGB';e={[math]::Round($_.Used/1GB,1)}}"],["Windows Update client events", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20Update%20client%20events", "snippet: Windows Update", "The operational log, newest first. Get-WinEvent -LogName 'Microsoft-Windows-WindowsUpdateClient/Operational' -MaxEvents 30 |   Select-Object TimeCreated, Id, LevelDisplayName, Message"],["Build the readable WindowsUpdate.log", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Build%20the%20readable%20WindowsUpdate.log", "snippet: Windows Update", "Converts the trace files into a text log on the desktop. Get-WindowsUpdateLog"],["Repair the component store", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Repair%20the%20component%20store", "snippet: Windows Update", "Run before resetting anything. Fixes most 0x800f08xx errors. DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth sfc /scannow"],["Reset the Windows Update components", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Reset%20the%20Windows%20Update%20components", "snippet: Windows Update", "The classic last resort: stop the services, set the caches aside, start again. The update history is lost. Stop-Service wuauserv, bits, cryptsvc -Force Rename-Item C:\\Windows\\SoftwareDistribution SoftwareDistribution.old Rename-Item C:\\Wind"],["Install an update package by hand", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Install%20an%20update%20package%20by%20hand", "snippet: Windows Update", "For a .msu downloaded from the Microsoft Update Catalog. wusa.exe C:\\Temp\\windows11.0-kb5000000-x64.msu /quiet /norestart"],["Remove an update", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Remove%20an%20update", "snippet: Windows Update", "List the packages first, then remove by its full package name. DISM /Online /Get-Packages /Format:Table | findstr /i \"Package_for\" DISM /Online /Remove-Package /PackageName:PACKAGE-NAME-FROM-THE-LIST /NoRestart"],["Delivery Optimization: where did the bytes come from", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Delivery%20Optimization%3A%20where%20did%20the%20bytes%20come%20from", "snippet: Windows Update", "Shows how much was fetched from peers and how much from Microsoft. Get-DeliveryOptimizationPerfSnapThisMonth Get-DeliveryOptimizationStatus | Select-Object FileId, Status, BytesFromPeers, BytesFromHttp"],["Update rings in the tenant", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Update%20rings%20in%20the%20tenant", "snippet: Windows Update", "Microsoft Graph PowerShell. The deferral days of every ring. Get-MgDeviceManagementDeviceConfiguration -Filter \"isof('microsoft.graph.windowsUpdateForBusinessConfiguration')\" |   Select-Object DisplayName, @{n='QualityDeferral';e={$_.Additi"],["Fleet update status (KQL)", "windows-update-cheat-sheet.html?q=Fleet%20update%20status%20%28KQL%29", "snippet: Windows Update", "For a workspace with Windows Update for Business reports enabled. UCClient | summarize arg_max(TimeGenerated, *) by DeviceName | summarize Devices = count() by OSVersion, OSSecurityUpdateStatus | order by Devices desc"],["Teams Phone cheat sheet", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Teams Phone administration with PowerShell: assign numbers, voice routing and dial plans, Direct Routing gateways, call forwarding, auto attendants and call queues."],["Connect", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect", "snippet: Teams Phone", "Signs in to Teams PowerShell. Connect-MicrosoftTeams"],["Voice settings of a user", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Voice%20settings%20of%20a%20user", "snippet: Teams Phone", "Number, whether Teams Phone is on, and the policies that decide how calls leave. Get-CsOnlineUser -Identity user@contoso.com |   Select-Object DisplayName, LineUri, EnterpriseVoiceEnabled, OnlineVoiceRoutingPolicy, TenantDialPlan, TeamsCall"],["Does the user have a Teams Phone licence", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Does%20the%20user%20have%20a%20Teams%20Phone%20licence", "snippet: Teams Phone", "MCOEV is Teams Phone Standard. E5 includes it. Calling Plans show up as MCOPSTN. Get-MgUserLicenseDetail -UserId user@contoso.com | Select-Object SkuPartNumber"],["Assign a phone number", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Assign%20a%20phone%20number", "snippet: Teams Phone", "The type must match where the number comes from: DirectRouting, CallingPlan or OperatorConnect. Set-CsPhoneNumberAssignment -Identity user@contoso.com -PhoneNumber +4930123456 -PhoneNumberType DirectRouting"],["Remove the number from a user", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Remove%20the%20number%20from%20a%20user", "snippet: Teams Phone", "Frees the number for someone else. Remove-CsPhoneNumberAssignment -Identity user@contoso.com -RemoveAll"],["Who has this number", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20has%20this%20number", "snippet: Teams Phone", "The fastest answer to \"this number is already assigned\". Get-CsPhoneNumberAssignment -TelephoneNumber +4930123456 |   Select-Object TelephoneNumber, NumberType, PstnAssignmentStatus, AssignedPstnTargetId"],["Numbers that are free", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Numbers%20that%20are%20free", "snippet: Teams Phone", "Unassigned numbers in the tenant. Get-CsPhoneNumberAssignment -PstnAssignmentStatus Unassigned -Top 200 |   Select-Object TelephoneNumber, NumberType, City"],["Give a user a voice routing policy", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Give%20a%20user%20a%20voice%20routing%20policy", "snippet: Teams Phone", "Direct Routing only. Without it the user can receive calls but not dial out. Grant-CsOnlineVoiceRoutingPolicy -Identity user@contoso.com -PolicyName 'DE-National'"],["Give a user a dial plan", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Give%20a%20user%20a%20dial%20plan", "snippet: Teams Phone", "Translates what people dial, such as a number without country code, into E.164. Grant-CsTenantDialPlan -Identity user@contoso.com -PolicyName 'DE-Berlin'"],["Test what a dialled number turns into", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Test%20what%20a%20dialled%20number%20turns%20into", "snippet: Teams Phone", "Runs the number through the user's effective dial plan. Get-CsEffectiveTenantDialPlan -Identity user@contoso.com | Test-CsEffectiveTenantDialPlan -DialedNumber 030123456"],["Session border controllers", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Session%20border%20controllers", "snippet: Teams Phone", "Direct Routing gateways known to the tenant. Get-CsOnlinePSTNGateway | Select-Object Fqdn, Enabled, SipSignalingPort, MaxConcurrentSessions, ForwardPai"],["Voice routes and usages", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Voice%20routes%20and%20usages", "snippet: Teams Phone", "Which number pattern goes out through which gateway, in priority order. Get-CsOnlineVoiceRoute | Sort-Object Priority | Select-Object Priority, Name, NumberPattern, OnlinePstnUsages, OnlinePstnGatewayList Get-CsOnlineVoiceRoutingPolicy | Se"],["Calling policies", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Calling%20policies", "snippet: Teams Phone", "What users may do: forwarding, voicemail, busy on busy. Get-CsTeamsCallingPolicy | Select-Object Identity, AllowPrivateCalling, AllowCallForwardingToPhone, AllowVoicemail, BusyOnBusyEnabledType"],["See a user's forwarding and delegation", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=See%20a%20user%27s%20forwarding%20and%20delegation", "snippet: Teams Phone", "What the user set in the Teams client. Get-CsUserCallingSettings -Identity user@contoso.com"],["Set call forwarding for a user", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Set%20call%20forwarding%20for%20a%20user", "snippet: Teams Phone", "For someone who is away and cannot set it themselves. Set-CsUserCallingSettings -Identity user@contoso.com -IsForwardingEnabled $true -ForwardingType Immediate -ForwardingTargetType SingleTarget -ForwardingTarget '+4930654321'"],["Create a resource account", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20resource%20account", "snippet: Teams Phone", "The account an auto attendant or call queue answers on. The first ID is for auto attendants, the second for call queues. New-CsOnlineApplicationInstance -UserPrincipalName aa-main@contoso.com -DisplayName 'Main line' -ApplicationId 'ce93338"],["List auto attendants and call queues", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20auto%20attendants%20and%20call%20queues", "snippet: Teams Phone", "With the settings people ask about most. Get-CsAutoAttendant | Select-Object Name, Identity, LanguageId, TimeZoneId Get-CsCallQueue | Select-Object Name, RoutingMethod, AgentAlertTime, OverflowThreshold, TimeoutThreshold"],["Emergency locations", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Emergency%20locations", "snippet: Teams Phone", "Addresses used for emergency calls. Every number needs one where the law requires it. Get-CsOnlineLisLocation | Select-Object Description, HouseNumber, StreetName, City, LocationId"],["Caller ID policies", "teams-phone-cheat-sheet.html?q=Caller%20ID%20policies", "snippet: Teams Phone", "Which number the other side sees. Get-CsCallingLineIdentity | Select-Object Identity, CallingIDSubstitute, EnableUserOverride"],["Entra Connect upgrade checklist", "entra-connect-upgrade-checklist.html", "page", "Upgrade or replace an Entra Connect Sync server without an outage: swing migration with a staging server, checks before cut-over and clean-up after."],["Tenant-to-tenant migration prep checklist", "tenant-migration-prep-checklist.html", "page", "What to clarify and prepare before moving users, mail, files and devices from one Microsoft 365 tenant to another, for example after a merger."],["New admin: the first 30 days checklist", "new-admin-first-30-days-checklist.html", "page", "What to find out, secure and write down in your first month as the administrator of an environment you did not build."],["Intune fleet analyzer", "intune-analyzer.html", "tool", "Analyze an Intune device export: non-compliant, unencrypted, stale and jailbroken devices, Windows versions out of support, duplicates, with fixes and Graph PowerShell"],["Mail flow debugger", "mailflow-debugger.html", "tool", "Paste a bounce message (NDR), SMTP error, message trace or spam headers and get the cause, who has to fix it, PowerShell commands and a reply for the user"],["Defender XDR hunting cheat sheet", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Advanced hunting queries for Microsoft Defender XDR: process, network, file, logon, email and vulnerability tables, ready to paste."],["What ran on a device", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20ran%20on%20a%20device", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Process timeline for one machine, newest first. DeviceProcessEvents | where Timestamp > ago(1d) | where DeviceName startswith \"pc01\" | project Timestamp, AccountName, FileName, ProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessFileName | order by Timest"],["Office app starting a shell or script host", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Office%20app%20starting%20a%20shell%20or%20script%20host", "snippet: Defender hunting", "A document that launches PowerShell or cmd is the classic first step after a malicious attachment. DeviceProcessEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where InitiatingProcessFileName in~ (\"winword.exe\",\"excel.exe\",\"powerpnt.exe\",\"outlook.exe\""],["Built-in Windows tools reaching the internet", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Built-in%20Windows%20tools%20reaching%20the%20internet", "snippet: Defender hunting", "certutil, bitsadmin and friends are used to download payloads without bringing any tool along. DeviceNetworkEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where InitiatingProcessFileName in~ (\"certutil.exe\",\"bitsadmin.exe\",\"mshta.exe\",\"regsvr32.exe\","],["Who received a phishing mail", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20received%20a%20phishing%20mail", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Start of every phishing clean-up. DeliveryLocation tells you whether it reached the inbox. EmailEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where SenderFromDomain == \"evil.example\" or Subject has \"Invoice 4471\" | project Timestamp, RecipientEmailA"],["Mails that contain a link to a domain", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Mails%20that%20contain%20a%20link%20to%20a%20domain", "snippet: Defender hunting", "When the sender changes but the link stays the same. EmailUrlInfo | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where UrlDomain == \"evil.example\" | join kind=inner (EmailEvents) on NetworkMessageId | project Timestamp, RecipientEmailAddress, SenderFromAddr"],["Who clicked the link", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20clicked%20the%20link", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Needs Safe Links. IsClickedThrough means the user went past the warning page. UrlClickEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where Url has \"evil.example\" | project Timestamp, AccountUpn, Url, ActionType, IsClickedThrough, IPAddress"],["Mails removed after delivery", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Mails%20removed%20after%20delivery", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Zero-hour auto purge. A failed result means the mail is still in the mailbox. EmailPostDeliveryEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where ActionType has \"ZAP\" | project Timestamp, RecipientEmailAddress, ActionType, ActionResult, NetworkMess"],["Where does a file hash exist", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Where%20does%20a%20file%20hash%20exist", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Which devices have seen this file, and under which names. DeviceFileEvents | where Timestamp > ago(30d) | where SHA256 == \"PASTE-SHA256-HERE\" | summarize FirstSeen = min(Timestamp), LastSeen = max(Timestamp), Names = make_set(FileName) by D"],["Which devices talked to a domain or IP", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20devices%20talked%20to%20a%20domain%20or%20IP", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Scope of a command-and-control or download address. DeviceNetworkEvents | where Timestamp > ago(30d) | where RemoteUrl has \"evil.example\" or RemoteIP == \"203.0.113.10\" | summarize Connections = count(), FirstSeen = min(Timestamp), LastSeen "],["Remote desktop logons from the internet", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Remote%20desktop%20logons%20from%20the%20internet", "snippet: Defender hunting", "A successful one means RDP is exposed. That should never return rows. DeviceLogonEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where LogonType == \"RemoteInteractive\" and ActionType == \"LogonSuccess\" | where RemoteIPType == \"Public\" | project Timesta"],["Account added to a local group", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Account%20added%20to%20a%20local%20group", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Catches a new local administrator. DeviceEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where ActionType == \"UserAccountAddedToLocalGroup\" | project Timestamp, DeviceName, InitiatingProcessAccountName, AccountSid, AdditionalFields"],["New autostart entries in the Run keys", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=New%20autostart%20entries%20in%20the%20Run%20keys", "snippet: Defender hunting", "A common way to survive a restart. DeviceRegistryEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where ActionType == \"RegistryValueSet\" | where RegistryKey has @\"\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run\" | project Timestamp, DeviceName, RegistryKey, Regi"],["Attempts to weaken Defender", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Attempts%20to%20weaken%20Defender", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Disabling real-time protection or adding exclusions from the command line. DeviceProcessEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where ProcessCommandLine has_any (\"Set-MpPreference\",\"Add-MpPreference\") | where ProcessCommandLine has_any (\"Disab"],["Shadow copies deleted or recovery disabled", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Shadow%20copies%20deleted%20or%20recovery%20disabled", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Ransomware does this minutes before it encrypts. Treat a hit as an incident. DeviceProcessEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where (FileName =~ \"vssadmin.exe\" and ProcessCommandLine has \"delete\" and ProcessCommandLine has \"shadows\")     o"],["Mass file renames", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Mass%20file%20renames", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Hundreds of renames by one process within five minutes looks like encryption in progress. Tune the threshold. DeviceFileEvents | where Timestamp > ago(1d) | where ActionType == \"FileRenamed\" | summarize Files = count() by DeviceName, Initia"],["Rare programs started from user-writable folders", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Rare%20programs%20started%20from%20user-writable%20folders", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Executables seen on only one or two devices, run from Temp, Public or ProgramData. DeviceProcessEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where FolderPath has_any (@\"\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\\", @\"\\Users\\Public\\\", @\"\\ProgramData\\\") | where FileName en"],["Remote access tools in use", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Remote%20access%20tools%20in%20use", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Tools you did not roll out yourself are a favourite of help-desk scammers and ransomware crews. DeviceProcessEvents | where Timestamp > ago(30d) | where FileName has_any (\"anydesk\",\"teamviewer\",\"screenconnect\",\"atera\",\"splashtop\",\"rustdesk\""],["Devices exposed to a CVE", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Devices%20exposed%20to%20a%20CVE", "snippet: Defender hunting", "From Defender Vulnerability Management. DeviceTvmSoftwareVulnerabilities | where CveId == \"CVE-2025-00000\" | project DeviceName, OSPlatform, SoftwareName, SoftwareVersion, VulnerabilitySeverityLevel"],["Where did an account sign in on-premises", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Where%20did%20an%20account%20sign%20in%20on-premises", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Needs Defender for Identity. Useful for a service account that should only ever be used from one server. IdentityLogonEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where AccountUpn == \"svc-backup@contoso.com\" | summarize Logons = count(), LastSeen ="],["Alerts that involve a device", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Alerts%20that%20involve%20a%20device", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Titles, severity and the ATT&CK techniques behind them. AlertEvidence | where Timestamp > ago(30d) | where DeviceName startswith \"pc01\" | join kind=inner (AlertInfo) on AlertId | distinct Timestamp, Title, Severity, Category, AttackTechniqu"],["Devices that stopped reporting", "defender-xdr-hunting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Devices%20that%20stopped%20reporting", "snippet: Defender hunting", "Onboarded machines with no data for a week. Either switched off or the sensor is broken. DeviceInfo | where Timestamp > ago(30d) | summarize LastSeen = max(Timestamp) by DeviceName, OSPlatform | where LastSeen < ago(7d) | order by LastSeen "],["Mail flow troubleshooting cheat sheet", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Exchange Online mail flow troubleshooting: message trace, quarantine, spam verdict headers, forwarding, connectors, DKIM and the DNS checks."],["Connect", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect", "snippet: Mail flow", "Needs the ExchangeOnlineManagement module. Connect-ExchangeOnline -UserPrincipalName admin@contoso.com"],["Trace mail to a recipient", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Trace%20mail%20to%20a%20recipient", "snippet: Mail flow", "The V2 cmdlets replace Get-MessageTrace. One query covers up to 10 days, within the last 90. Get-MessageTraceV2 -RecipientAddress user@contoso.com -StartDate (Get-Date).AddDays(-2) -EndDate (Get-Date) |   Select-Object Received, SenderAddre"],["Trace mail from a sender", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Trace%20mail%20from%20a%20sender", "snippet: Mail flow", "Works with external senders too. Get-MessageTraceV2 -SenderAddress someone@example.org -StartDate (Get-Date).AddDays(-2) -EndDate (Get-Date) |   Select-Object Received, RecipientAddress, Subject, Status"],["Only what failed or was quarantined", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Only%20what%20failed%20or%20was%20quarantined", "snippet: Mail flow", "Status can be Delivered, Failed, Pending, Quarantined, FilteredAsSpam, Expanded or GettingStatus. Get-MessageTraceV2 -RecipientAddress user@contoso.com -Status Failed, Quarantined -StartDate (Get-Date).AddDays(-7) -EndDate (Get-Date)"],["What happened to one message", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20happened%20to%20one%20message", "snippet: Mail flow", "Every hop and decision, including the mail flow rule or policy that acted on it. Get-MessageTraceDetailV2 -MessageTraceId 'TRACE-ID' -RecipientAddress user@contoso.com |   Select-Object Date, Event, Detail"],["Search further back or export a large trace", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Search%20further%20back%20or%20export%20a%20large%20trace", "snippet: Mail flow", "Runs in the background and mails you a CSV. Start-HistoricalSearch -ReportTitle 'Trace user' -ReportType MessageTrace -RecipientAddress user@contoso.com -StartDate (Get-Date).AddDays(-60) -EndDate (Get-Date) -NotifyAddress admin@contoso.com"],["What is in quarantine for a user", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=What%20is%20in%20quarantine%20for%20a%20user", "snippet: Mail flow", "Type and policy tell you why it was held. Get-QuarantineMessage -RecipientAddress user@contoso.com -StartReceivedDate (Get-Date).AddDays(-7) |   Select-Object ReceivedTime, SenderAddress, Subject, Type, PolicyName"],["Release a message from quarantine", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Release%20a%20message%20from%20quarantine", "snippet: Mail flow", "Look at it first. High-confidence phishing is in quarantine for a reason. Get-QuarantineMessage -MessageId '<MESSAGE-ID>' | Release-QuarantineMessage -ReleaseToAll"],["Read the spam verdict in the headers", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20the%20spam%20verdict%20in%20the%20headers", "snippet: Mail flow", "Fields of X-Forefront-Antispam-Report in the received message. SCL  -1 filtering skipped | 0-1 not spam | 5-6 spam | 9 high-confidence spam SFV  NSPM not spam | SPM spam | SKA allowed by the anti-spam policy | SKN made safe by a mail flow r"],["Block or allow a sender for the whole tenant", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Block%20or%20allow%20a%20sender%20for%20the%20whole%20tenant", "snippet: Mail flow", "Allow entries expire after 30 days by default, on purpose. Prefer reporting the false positive to Microsoft. Get-TenantAllowBlockListItems -ListType Sender New-TenantAllowBlockListItems -ListType Sender -Block -Entries 'evil.example' -NoExp"],["Is a user blocked from sending", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20a%20user%20blocked%20from%20sending", "snippet: Mail flow", "Accounts that hit the outbound spam limits get restricted. Find out why before you unblock: it is often a compromised account. Get-BlockedSenderAddress Remove-BlockedSenderAddress -SenderAddress user@contoso.com"],["Forwarding set on a mailbox", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Forwarding%20set%20on%20a%20mailbox", "snippet: Mail flow", "Forwarding configured by an admin or in Outlook on the web settings. Get-Mailbox user@contoso.com | Select-Object ForwardingAddress, ForwardingSmtpAddress, DeliverToMailboxAndForward"],["All mailboxes that forward", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=All%20mailboxes%20that%20forward", "snippet: Mail flow", "Check every external target. Attackers set this to keep reading mail after a password reset. Get-Mailbox -ResultSize Unlimited |   Where-Object { $_.ForwardingSmtpAddress -or $_.ForwardingAddress } |   Select-Object UserPrincipalName, Forwa"],["Inbox rules that forward, move or delete", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Inbox%20rules%20that%20forward%2C%20move%20or%20delete", "snippet: Mail flow", "The other hiding place. Rules that move mail to RSS Feeds or Conversation History are a red flag. Get-InboxRule -Mailbox user@contoso.com |   Select-Object Name, Enabled, ForwardTo, ForwardAsAttachmentTo, RedirectTo, DeleteMessage, MoveToFo"],["Is external auto-forwarding allowed", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20external%20auto-forwarding%20allowed", "snippet: Mail flow", "Automatic means the system decides, which today means off. The NDR for a blocked forward is 5.7.520. Get-HostedOutboundSpamFilterPolicy | Select-Object Name, AutoForwardingMode Get-RemoteDomain | Select-Object Name, AutoForwardEnabled"],["Connectors", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connectors", "snippet: Mail flow", "A partner connector with forced TLS or a wrong smart host explains mail that only fails for one domain. Get-InboundConnector | Select-Object Name, Enabled, ConnectorType, SenderDomains, RequireTls Get-OutboundConnector | Select-Object Name,"],["Does an address exist, and what is it", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Does%20an%20address%20exist%2C%20and%20what%20is%20it", "snippet: Mail flow", "Finds the object behind any address, including aliases. Get-Recipient -Filter \"EmailAddresses -eq 'smtp:info@contoso.com'\" |   Select-Object Name, RecipientTypeDetails, PrimarySmtpAddress"],["Mailbox size and quota", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Mailbox%20size%20and%20quota", "snippet: Mail flow", "A full mailbox bounces with 5.2.2. Get-MailboxStatistics user@contoso.com | Select-Object TotalItemSize, ItemCount Get-Mailbox user@contoso.com | Select-Object ProhibitSendQuota, ProhibitSendReceiveQuota"],["Message size limits", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Message%20size%20limits", "snippet: Mail flow", "The tenant default is 35 MB. Attachments grow by about a third in transit. Get-Mailbox user@contoso.com | Select-Object MaxSendSize, MaxReceiveSize"],["DKIM status and rotation", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=DKIM%20status%20and%20rotation", "snippet: Mail flow", "Status Valid and Enabled True is what you want for every sending domain. Get-DkimSigningConfig | Select-Object Domain, Enabled, Status, Selector1CNAME, Selector2CNAME Rotate-DkimSigningConfig -Identity contoso.com -KeySize 2048"],["DNS records that decide delivery", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=DNS%20records%20that%20decide%20delivery", "snippet: Mail flow", "MX, SPF, DMARC and the first DKIM selector. Resolve-DnsName contoso.com -Type MX Resolve-DnsName contoso.com -Type TXT | Where-Object Strings -like 'v=spf1*' Resolve-DnsName _dmarc.contoso.com -Type TXT Resolve-DnsName selector1._domainkey."],["Can this server reach Exchange Online on port 25", "mail-flow-cheat-sheet.html?q=Can%20this%20server%20reach%20Exchange%20Online%20on%20port%2025", "snippet: Mail flow", "For scanners and applications that relay. Many ISPs and Azure block outbound port 25. Test-NetConnection contoso-com.mail.protection.outlook.com -Port 25"],["Intune app deployment cheat sheet", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Intune Win32 app deployment: packaging, silent install commands, detection scripts, return codes, logs and how to force a retry."],["Package an installer as .intunewin", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Package%20an%20installer%20as%20.intunewin", "snippet: Intune apps", "Source folder, setup file, output folder. Everything in the source folder goes into the package, so keep it clean. IntuneWinAppUtil.exe -c C:\\Packages\\App\\Source -s setup.exe -o C:\\Packages\\App\\Output -q"],["Silent MSI install with a log", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Silent%20MSI%20install%20with%20a%20log", "snippet: Intune apps", "The log is what you will want when it fails on one device. msiexec /i \"app.msi\" /qn /norestart /l*v \"C:\\Windows\\Temp\\app-install.log\""],["Silent MSI uninstall", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Silent%20MSI%20uninstall", "snippet: Intune apps", "Uses the product code, so it works without the original file. msiexec /x \"{PRODUCT-CODE}\" /qn /norestart"],["Find the product code and uninstall command", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20the%20product%20code%20and%20uninstall%20command", "snippet: Intune apps", "Searches the 64-bit and 32-bit uninstall keys. Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Uninstall\\*', 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\WOW6432Node\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Uninstall\\*' |   Where-Object DisplayName -like '*Ap"],["Install command with a PowerShell wrapper", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Install%20command%20with%20a%20PowerShell%20wrapper", "snippet: Intune apps", "For installers that need more than one step. powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -NoProfile -File .\\install.ps1"],["Run the script in 64-bit PowerShell", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20the%20script%20in%2064-bit%20PowerShell", "snippet: Intune apps", "Add this to the top of install.ps1 if the wrapper starts as a 32-bit process and writes to the wrong registry view. if ($env:PROCESSOR_ARCHITEW6432 -eq 'AMD64') {   & \"$env:WINDIR\\SysNative\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe\" -ExecutionP"],["Test as SYSTEM", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Test%20as%20SYSTEM", "snippet: Intune apps", "Opens a PowerShell window as the account Intune installs with. Needs PsExec from Sysinternals. psexec.exe -s -i powershell.exe"],["Detection script", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Detection%20script", "snippet: Intune apps", "Detected means exit code 0 and some text on standard output. Anything else counts as not installed. $exe = 'C:\\Program Files\\App\\app.exe' if ((Test-Path $exe) -and ([version](Get-Item $exe).VersionInfo.FileVersion -ge [version]'2.4.0')) {  "],["Default return codes", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Default%20return%20codes", "snippet: Intune apps", "What Intune makes of the installer's exit code. Add your own in the app's Program settings. 0     success 1707  success 3010  soft reboot 1641  hard reboot 1618  retry (another installation is running)"],["Follow the app log live", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Follow%20the%20app%20log%20live", "snippet: Intune apps", "Win32 app processing is written to AppWorkload.log on current agent versions, older ones use IntuneManagementExtension.log. Get-Content 'C:\\ProgramData\\Microsoft\\IntuneManagementExtension\\Logs\\AppWorkload.log' -Tail 50 -Wait"],["Find the errors in the logs", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20the%20errors%20in%20the%20logs", "snippet: Intune apps", "Quick first pass over both logs. Select-String -Path 'C:\\ProgramData\\Microsoft\\IntuneManagementExtension\\Logs\\*.log' -Pattern 'error|failed|exit code' |   Select-Object -Last 40 | ForEach-Object { $_.Line }"],["Make the device check for apps now", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Make%20the%20device%20check%20for%20apps%20now", "snippet: Intune apps", "Restarting the agent triggers a new evaluation. Restart-Service IntuneManagementExtension"],["See what the agent recorded per app", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=See%20what%20the%20agent%20recorded%20per%20app", "snippet: Intune apps", "One key per user and app ID. Failed apps are retried only after 24 hours. Get-ChildItem 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\IntuneManagementExtension\\Win32Apps' -Recurse -Depth 1 | Select-Object Name"],["Force a retry of one failed app", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Force%20a%20retry%20of%20one%20failed%20app", "snippet: Intune apps", "Remove the app's key under the user's ID, then restart the agent. Use the app ID from the Intune URL. Get-ChildItem 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\IntuneManagementExtension\\Win32Apps' -Recurse |   Where-Object Name -like '*APP-ID*' | Remove-Item"],["Was the content downloaded", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Was%20the%20content%20downloaded", "snippet: Intune apps", "Packages are unpacked here before the install runs. An empty folder points to a download problem, not an installer problem. Get-ChildItem 'C:\\Windows\\IMECache' -Directory | Select-Object Name, LastWriteTime"],["MSI installer events", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=MSI%20installer%20events", "snippet: Intune apps", "What Windows Installer itself logged. Get-WinEvent -FilterHashtable @{LogName='Application'; ProviderName='MsiInstaller'} -MaxEvents 20 |   Select-Object TimeCreated, Id, Message"],["MDM event log", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=MDM%20event%20log", "snippet: Intune apps", "Policy and enrolment errors that stop apps before the agent even runs. Get-WinEvent -LogName 'Microsoft-Windows-DeviceManagement-Enterprise-Diagnostics-Provider/Admin' -MaxEvents 30 |   Select-Object TimeCreated, Id, LevelDisplayName, Messa"],["Silent install with winget", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Silent%20install%20with%20winget", "snippet: Intune apps", "Exact ID, machine scope, no prompts. Works well as the install command inside a wrapper. winget install --id 7zip.7zip --exact --silent --scope machine --accept-package-agreements --accept-source-agreements"],["Microsoft 365 Apps version and update channel", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Microsoft%20365%20Apps%20version%20and%20update%20channel", "snippet: Intune apps", "Read from the Click-to-Run configuration. Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Office\\ClickToRun\\Configuration' |   Select-Object VersionToReport, UpdateChannel, CDNBaseUrl"],["Update Microsoft 365 Apps now", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Update%20Microsoft%20365%20Apps%20now", "snippet: Intune apps", "Starts the Click-to-Run updater. & \"$env:CommonProgramFiles\\microsoft shared\\ClickToRun\\OfficeC2RClient.exe\" /update user"],["List the apps in the tenant", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20the%20apps%20in%20the%20tenant", "snippet: Intune apps", "Microsoft Graph PowerShell with DeviceManagementApps.Read.All. Get-MgDeviceAppManagementMobileApp -All |   Select-Object DisplayName, Id, @{n='Type';e={$_.AdditionalProperties.'@odata.type'}}"],["Who is an app assigned to", "intune-app-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20is%20an%20app%20assigned%20to", "snippet: Intune apps", "Intent is required, available or uninstall. Get-MgDeviceAppManagementMobileAppAssignment -MobileAppId 'APP-ID' |   Select-Object Intent, @{n='Target';e={$_.Target.AdditionalProperties | ConvertTo-Json -Compress}}"],["Find locked-out accounts", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20locked-out%20accounts", "snippet: Active Directory", "Every account that is locked right now. Search-ADAccount -LockedOut | Select-Object Name, SamAccountName, LastLogonDate"],["Unlock an account", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Unlock%20an%20account", "snippet: Active Directory", "Unlocks it. It will lock again if an old password is still stored on a phone or a mapped drive. Unlock-ADAccount -Identity jdoe"],["Find out where a lockout comes from", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20out%20where%20a%20lockout%20comes%20from", "snippet: Active Directory", "Event 4740 on the PDC emulator names the computer that sent the bad passwords. $pdc = (Get-ADDomain).PDCEmulator Get-WinEvent -ComputerName $pdc -FilterHashtable @{LogName='Security'; Id=4740} -MaxEvents 20 |   Select-Object TimeCreated, @{"],["Reset a password and force a change", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Reset%20a%20password%20and%20force%20a%20change", "snippet: Active Directory", "Prompts for the new password without showing it on screen. Set-ADAccountPassword -Identity jdoe -Reset -NewPassword (Read-Host -AsSecureString 'New password') Set-ADUser -Identity jdoe -ChangePasswordAtLogon $true"],["Enabled users who have not signed in for 90 days", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Enabled%20users%20who%20have%20not%20signed%20in%20for%2090%20days", "snippet: Active Directory", "Candidates for disabling. LastLogonDate can lag by up to 14 days. Search-ADAccount -AccountInactive -TimeSpan 90.00:00:00 -UsersOnly |   Where-Object Enabled | Select-Object Name, SamAccountName, LastLogonDate"],["Computers that have not signed in for 90 days", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Computers%20that%20have%20not%20signed%20in%20for%2090%20days", "snippet: Active Directory", "Stale computer accounts. Search-ADAccount -AccountInactive -TimeSpan 90.00:00:00 -ComputersOnly |   Select-Object Name, LastLogonDate"],["Accounts whose password never expires", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Accounts%20whose%20password%20never%20expires", "snippet: Active Directory", "Usually service accounts, and usually with old passwords. Get-ADUser -Filter 'PasswordNeverExpires -eq $true -and Enabled -eq $true' -Properties PasswordLastSet |   Select-Object Name, SamAccountName, PasswordLastSet"],["Members of a group, including nested groups", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Members%20of%20a%20group%2C%20including%20nested%20groups", "snippet: Active Directory", "Who is really a Domain Admin. Get-ADGroupMember -Identity 'Domain Admins' -Recursive |   Select-Object Name, SamAccountName, objectClass"],["All groups a user is in, including nested ones", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=All%20groups%20a%20user%20is%20in%2C%20including%20nested%20ones", "snippet: Active Directory", "Uses the in-chain matching rule, so indirect memberships show up too. $dn = (Get-ADUser jdoe).DistinguishedName Get-ADGroup -LDAPFilter \"(member:1.2.840.113556.1.4.1941:=$dn)\" | Select-Object Name"],["Password policy that applies to a user", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Password%20policy%20that%20applies%20to%20a%20user", "snippet: Active Directory", "The domain default, and the fine-grained policy if one wins for this user (empty output means the default applies). Get-ADDefaultDomainPasswordPolicy Get-ADUserResultantPasswordPolicy -Identity jdoe"],["Which DCs hold the FSMO roles", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20DCs%20hold%20the%20FSMO%20roles", "snippet: Active Directory", "All five operations master roles. netdom query fsmo"],["Replication summary", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Replication%20summary", "snippet: Active Directory", "One line per DC with the largest delta and the failure count. Start here. repadmin /replsummary"],["Replication errors only", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Replication%20errors%20only", "snippet: Active Directory", "Shows only the partners where the last attempt failed. repadmin /showrepl /errorsonly"],["Force replication across the forest", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Force%20replication%20across%20the%20forest", "snippet: Active Directory", "All partitions, across sites, push mode. repadmin /syncall /AdeP"],["Health check of all domain controllers", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Health%20check%20of%20all%20domain%20controllers", "snippet: Active Directory", "Quiet mode prints only the tests that fail. dcdiag /e /q"],["Which DC does this machine use", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20DC%20does%20this%20machine%20use", "snippet: Active Directory", "Locates a domain controller the way a client does. nltest /dsgetdc:contoso.com"],["Test and repair a computer's trust with the domain", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Test%20and%20repair%20a%20computer%27s%20trust%20with%20the%20domain", "snippet: Active Directory", "Fixes \"the trust relationship between this workstation and the primary domain failed\" without a rejoin. Test-ComputerSecureChannel -Verbose Test-ComputerSecureChannel -Repair -Credential (Get-Credential)"],["Accounts with a service principal name", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Accounts%20with%20a%20service%20principal%20name", "snippet: Active Directory", "These are what an attacker requests tickets for (Kerberoasting). Old password plus high privilege is the dangerous combination. Get-ADUser -Filter 'ServicePrincipalName -like \"*\"' -Properties ServicePrincipalName, PasswordLastSet, MemberOf "],["Accounts without Kerberos pre-authentication", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Accounts%20without%20Kerberos%20pre-authentication", "snippet: Active Directory", "Their password hash can be requested by anyone (AS-REP roasting). The list should be empty. Get-ADUser -Filter 'DoesNotRequirePreAuth -eq $true' | Select-Object Name, SamAccountName"],["Computers trusted for unconstrained delegation", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Computers%20trusted%20for%20unconstrained%20delegation", "snippet: Active Directory", "Domain controllers are expected here. Anything else is worth a close look. Get-ADComputer -Filter 'TrustedForDelegation -eq $true' | Select-Object Name, DNSHostName"],["Age of the krbtgt password", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Age%20of%20the%20krbtgt%20password", "snippet: Active Directory", "If it is years old, plan the double reset. It limits how long a stolen golden ticket works. Get-ADUser krbtgt -Properties PasswordLastSet | Select-Object PasswordLastSet"],["How many computers a normal user may join", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=How%20many%20computers%20a%20normal%20user%20may%20join", "snippet: Active Directory", "The default is 10. Set it to 0 and delegate joins instead. Get-ADObject (Get-ADDomain).DistinguishedName -Properties 'ms-DS-MachineAccountQuota' |   Select-Object 'ms-DS-MachineAccountQuota'"],["Is the AD Recycle Bin on", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20AD%20Recycle%20Bin%20on", "snippet: Active Directory", "Empty EnabledScopes means it is off. Enabling it cannot be undone. Get-ADOptionalFeature -Filter 'Name -like \"Recycle*\"' | Select-Object Name, EnabledScopes"],["Restore a deleted object", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Restore%20a%20deleted%20object", "snippet: Active Directory", "Needs the Recycle Bin. Check what the first command finds before you pipe it into the restore. Get-ADObject -Filter 'isDeleted -eq $true -and Name -like \"*jdoe*\"' -IncludeDeletedObjects Get-ADObject -Filter 'isDeleted -eq $true -and Name -l"],["Domain and forest functional level", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html?q=Domain%20and%20forest%20functional%20level", "snippet: Active Directory", "Decides which features are available. (Get-ADDomain).DomainMode (Get-ADForest).ForestMode"],["Show the sync scheduler", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Show%20the%20sync%20scheduler", "snippet: Entra Connect", "Interval, next run, whether the scheduler is on and whether the server is in staging mode. Get-ADSyncScheduler"],["Run a delta sync now", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20a%20delta%20sync%20now", "snippet: Entra Connect", "Syncs only what changed. This is what you want after editing a user. Start-ADSyncSyncCycle -PolicyType Delta"],["Run a full sync", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20a%20full%20sync", "snippet: Entra Connect", "Re-evaluates every object. Only needed after changing sync rules or filtering, and it takes a while. Start-ADSyncSyncCycle -PolicyType Initial"],["Pause and resume the scheduler", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Pause%20and%20resume%20the%20scheduler", "snippet: Entra Connect", "Pause before maintenance on sync rules. Do not forget to turn it back on. Set-ADSyncScheduler -SyncCycleEnabled $false Set-ADSyncScheduler -SyncCycleEnabled $true"],["Is this server in staging mode", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20this%20server%20in%20staging%20mode", "snippet: Entra Connect", "A staging server imports and syncs but exports nothing. True on the active server means nothing reaches Entra ID. (Get-ADSyncScheduler).StagingModeEnabled"],["Results of the last runs", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Results%20of%20the%20last%20runs", "snippet: Entra Connect", "Anything other than success is where to look next. Get-ADSyncRunProfileResult -NumberRequested 12 |   Select-Object ConnectorName, RunProfileName, Result, StartDate"],["List the connectors", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20the%20connectors", "snippet: Entra Connect", "One for each AD forest and one for Entra ID. Get-ADSyncConnector | Select-Object Name, Type"],["Is the sync service running", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20sync%20service%20running", "snippet: Entra Connect", "The service is called ADSync. Get-Service ADSync"],["Diagnose password hash sync", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Diagnose%20password%20hash%20sync", "snippet: Entra Connect", "Interactive check of the whole password sync pipeline. Invoke-ADSyncDiagnostics -PasswordSync"],["Look up one object in the connector space", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Look%20up%20one%20object%20in%20the%20connector%20space", "snippet: Entra Connect", "Shows what the server holds for this object. Use the name from Get-ADSyncConnector. Get-ADSyncCSObject -ConnectorName 'contoso.com' -DistinguishedName 'CN=John Doe,OU=Users,DC=contoso,DC=com'"],["Show the accidental-delete threshold", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Show%20the%20accidental-delete%20threshold", "snippet: Entra Connect", "By default an export that deletes more than 500 objects is stopped. Prompts for Entra credentials. Get-ADSyncExportDeletionThreshold"],["Export the server configuration", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Export%20the%20server%20configuration", "snippet: Entra Connect", "Writes the full configuration to a folder. Take one before every change. Get-ADSyncServerConfiguration -Path 'C:\\Temp\\EntraConnectConfig'"],["Calculate the ImmutableID of an AD user", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Calculate%20the%20ImmutableID%20of%20an%20AD%20user", "snippet: Entra Connect", "The Base64 form of objectGUID. This is the anchor that ties the AD account to the cloud account. [Convert]::ToBase64String((Get-ADUser jdoe).ObjectGUID.ToByteArray())"],["Turn an ImmutableID back into a GUID", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Turn%20an%20ImmutableID%20back%20into%20a%20GUID", "snippet: Entra Connect", "To find the AD object that belongs to a cloud account. [Guid][Convert]::FromBase64String('PASTE-IMMUTABLEID-HERE')"],["Hard match a cloud account to an AD account", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Hard%20match%20a%20cloud%20account%20to%20an%20AD%20account", "snippet: Entra Connect", "Sets the anchor on a cloud-only account so the next sync joins the two. Needs Microsoft Graph PowerShell. $id = [Convert]::ToBase64String((Get-ADUser jdoe).ObjectGUID.ToByteArray()) Update-MgUser -UserId 'jdoe@contoso.com' -OnPremisesImmuta"],["When did the tenant last sync", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=When%20did%20the%20tenant%20last%20sync", "snippet: Entra Connect", "From the cloud side, with Microsoft Graph PowerShell. Get-MgOrganization | Select-Object OnPremisesSyncEnabled, OnPremisesLastSyncDateTime"],["Roll over the Seamless SSO Kerberos key", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Roll%20over%20the%20Seamless%20SSO%20Kerberos%20key", "snippet: Entra Connect", "Microsoft recommends doing this at least every 30 days. Run per forest. Import-Module 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft Azure Active Directory Connect\\AzureADSSO.psd1' New-AzureADSSOAuthenticationContext Update-AzureADSSOForest -OnPremCredentials"],["Join state of a device", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Join%20state%20of%20a%20device", "snippet: Entra Connect", "Run on the client. AzureAdJoined plus DomainJoined both YES means hybrid joined. dsregcmd /status"],["Does the user have a Primary Refresh Token", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Does%20the%20user%20have%20a%20Primary%20Refresh%20Token", "snippet: Entra Connect", "Run as the user, not elevated. AzureAdPrt : NO explains most single sign-on and device-based Conditional Access failures. dsregcmd /status | findstr /i \"AzureAdPrt\""],["Trigger the hybrid join task", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Trigger%20the%20hybrid%20join%20task", "snippet: Entra Connect", "The task that registers a domain-joined device in Entra ID. The device object must have synced first. Start-ScheduledTask -TaskPath '\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Workplace Join\\' -TaskName 'Automatic-Device-Join'"],["Remove a device registration", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Remove%20a%20device%20registration", "snippet: Entra Connect", "Run elevated. The device re-registers at the next task run if it is still in scope. dsregcmd /leave"],["Device registration event log", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html?q=Device%20registration%20event%20log", "snippet: Entra Connect", "Errors from the join itself. Get-WinEvent -LogName 'Microsoft-Windows-User Device Registration/Admin' -MaxEvents 30 |   Select-Object TimeCreated, Id, LevelDisplayName, Message"],["Status of all drives", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Status%20of%20all%20drives", "snippet: BitLocker", "Encryption state, method, percentage and protectors. manage-bde -status"],["Status in PowerShell", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Status%20in%20PowerShell", "snippet: BitLocker", "Same information as objects. Get-BitLockerVolume | Select-Object MountPoint, VolumeStatus, EncryptionPercentage, ProtectionStatus, KeyProtector"],["Show the recovery password", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Show%20the%20recovery%20password", "snippet: BitLocker", "Prints the protector IDs and the 48-digit recovery password. manage-bde -protectors -get C:"],["Recovery password and its ID in PowerShell", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Recovery%20password%20and%20its%20ID%20in%20PowerShell", "snippet: BitLocker", "The first 8 characters of the ID are what the recovery screen shows. (Get-BitLockerVolume -MountPoint C:).KeyProtector |   Where-Object KeyProtectorType -eq 'RecoveryPassword' |   Select-Object KeyProtectorId, RecoveryPassword"],["Back up the key to Entra ID", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Back%20up%20the%20key%20to%20Entra%20ID", "snippet: BitLocker", "For Entra joined and hybrid joined devices. $id = ((Get-BitLockerVolume -MountPoint C:).KeyProtector | Where-Object KeyProtectorType -eq 'RecoveryPassword').KeyProtectorId BackupToAAD-BitLockerKeyProtector -MountPoint C: -KeyProtectorId $id"],["Back up the key to Active Directory", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Back%20up%20the%20key%20to%20Active%20Directory", "snippet: BitLocker", "Use the ID from the protectors list, with the braces. manage-bde -protectors -adbackup C: -id \"{PROTECTOR-ID}\""],["Read recovery keys from Active Directory", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20recovery%20keys%20from%20Active%20Directory", "snippet: BitLocker", "The keys are child objects of the computer account. Needs read access to them. $pc = (Get-ADComputer PC01).DistinguishedName Get-ADObject -SearchBase $pc -Filter 'objectClass -eq \"msFVE-RecoveryInformation\"' -Properties msFVE-RecoveryPasswo"],["Read a recovery key from Entra ID", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20a%20recovery%20key%20from%20Entra%20ID", "snippet: BitLocker", "Microsoft Graph PowerShell with BitLockerKey.Read.All. Reading the key is written to the audit log. Get-MgInformationProtectionBitlockerRecoveryKey -Filter \"deviceId eq 'DEVICE-ID'\" Get-MgInformationProtectionBitlockerRecoveryKey -Bitlocker"],["Turn BitLocker on", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Turn%20BitLocker%20on", "snippet: BitLocker", "Adds a recovery password first, then encrypts used space with the TPM as protector. Add-BitLockerKeyProtector -MountPoint C: -RecoveryPasswordProtector Enable-BitLocker -MountPoint C: -EncryptionMethod XtsAes256 -UsedSpaceOnly -TpmProtector"],["Suspend for a firmware or BIOS update", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Suspend%20for%20a%20firmware%20or%20BIOS%20update", "snippet: BitLocker", "Protection resumes by itself after one restart. Skipping this is the classic cause of a recovery prompt after an update. Suspend-BitLocker -MountPoint C: -RebootCount 1"],["Resume protection", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Resume%20protection", "snippet: BitLocker", "If it was suspended without a restart count. Resume-BitLocker -MountPoint C:"],["Unlock a data drive with the recovery password", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Unlock%20a%20data%20drive%20with%20the%20recovery%20password", "snippet: BitLocker", "For a drive moved from another machine. manage-bde -unlock D: -RecoveryPassword 111111-222222-333333-444444-555555-666666-777777-888888"],["Unlock a data drive automatically", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Unlock%20a%20data%20drive%20automatically", "snippet: BitLocker", "Unlocks with the system drive, which must be encrypted itself. Enable-BitLockerAutoUnlock -MountPoint D:"],["Replace the recovery password", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Replace%20the%20recovery%20password", "snippet: BitLocker", "After a key was read out to a user on the phone. Back up the new one afterwards. manage-bde -protectors -delete C: -type RecoveryPassword manage-bde -protectors -add C: -RecoveryPassword"],["TPM state", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=TPM%20state", "snippet: BitLocker", "Present, ready and enabled must all be true. Get-Tpm"],["Is the recovery environment enabled", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20recovery%20environment%20enabled", "snippet: BitLocker", "Silent encryption through Intune fails when Windows RE is disabled. reagentc /info"],["Why did the device ask for the recovery key", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Why%20did%20the%20device%20ask%20for%20the%20recovery%20key", "snippet: BitLocker", "The BitLocker management log, newest first. Get-WinEvent -LogName 'Microsoft-Windows-BitLocker/BitLocker Management' -MaxEvents 30 |   Select-Object TimeCreated, Id, Message"],["Force recovery at the next start", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Force%20recovery%20at%20the%20next%20start", "snippet: BitLocker", "To test that the stored key really works. Have the key ready before you run it. manage-bde -forcerecovery C:"],["Turn BitLocker off", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Turn%20BitLocker%20off", "snippet: BitLocker", "Decrypts the drive. This takes time and the device is unprotected afterwards. Disable-BitLocker -MountPoint C:"],["Read a password from Active Directory", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20a%20password%20from%20Active%20Directory", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Account name, password and expiry. Get-LapsADPassword -Identity PC01 -AsPlainText"],["Read older passwords too", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20older%20passwords%20too", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Useful after restoring a machine from a backup or snapshot. History must be enabled in the policy. Get-LapsADPassword -Identity PC01 -AsPlainText -IncludeHistory"],["Read a password from Entra ID", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Read%20a%20password%20from%20Entra%20ID", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Microsoft Graph PowerShell. Every read lands in the audit log. Connect-MgGraph -Scopes 'DeviceLocalCredential.Read.All','Device.Read.All' Get-LapsAADPassword -DeviceIds PC01 -IncludePasswords -AsPlainText"],["Rotate the password now, on the device", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Rotate%20the%20password%20now%2C%20on%20the%20device", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Run on the machine itself, elevated. Reset-LapsPassword"],["Rotate the password remotely through AD", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Rotate%20the%20password%20remotely%20through%20AD", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Expires it now. The device changes it at its next policy cycle. Set-LapsADPasswordExpirationTime -Identity PC01"],["Apply the policy now", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Apply%20the%20policy%20now", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Run on the device instead of waiting for the hourly cycle. Invoke-LapsPolicyProcessing"],["Extend the AD schema", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Extend%20the%20AD%20schema", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Once per forest, as Schema Admin. Update-LapsADSchema"],["Let computers write their own password", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Let%20computers%20write%20their%20own%20password", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Once per OU that contains managed computers. Set-LapsADComputerSelfPermission -Identity 'OU=Workstations,DC=contoso,DC=com'"],["Allow a group to read passwords", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Allow%20a%20group%20to%20read%20passwords", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Give this to the help desk group, not to individual users. Set-LapsADReadPasswordPermission -Identity 'OU=Workstations,DC=contoso,DC=com' -AllowedPrincipals 'CONTOSO\\HelpDesk'"],["Allow a group to trigger a rotation", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Allow%20a%20group%20to%20trigger%20a%20rotation", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Separate from the read permission. Set-LapsADResetPasswordPermission -Identity 'OU=Workstations,DC=contoso,DC=com' -AllowedPrincipals 'CONTOSO\\HelpDesk'"],["Who can read passwords in this OU", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20can%20read%20passwords%20in%20this%20OU", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Run it before go-live. Groups you did not expect usually come from inherited full control. Find-LapsADExtendedRights -Identity 'OU=Workstations,DC=contoso,DC=com'"],["Computers without a stored password", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Computers%20without%20a%20stored%20password", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Machines the policy has not reached yet. Get-ADComputer -Filter * -SearchBase 'OU=Workstations,DC=contoso,DC=com' -Properties 'msLAPS-PasswordExpirationTime' |   Where-Object { -not $_.'msLAPS-PasswordExpirationTime' } | Select-Object Name"],["Which policy is active on the device", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Which%20policy%20is%20active%20on%20the%20device", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "The first key is written by Intune, the second by Group Policy. If both exist, Intune wins. Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Policies\\LAPS' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVe"],["LAPS event log", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=LAPS%20event%20log", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Each policy cycle logs what it did and why it failed. Get-WinEvent -LogName 'Microsoft-Windows-LAPS/Operational' -MaxEvents 30 |   Select-Object TimeCreated, Id, LevelDisplayName, Message"],["Collect diagnostics", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Collect%20diagnostics", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Writes a zip with logs and policy state to the folder. Get-LapsDiagnostics -OutputFolder 'C:\\Temp\\LapsDiag'"],["Check the managed local account", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20the%20managed%20local%20account", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "Is it enabled and when was the password last set. Get-LocalUser | Select-Object Name, Enabled, PasswordLastSet"],["Is the old LAPS still in use", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Is%20the%20old%20LAPS%20still%20in%20use", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "A filled ms-Mcs-AdmPwd attribute means the legacy add-on wrote a password for this machine. Get-ADComputer PC01 -Properties 'ms-Mcs-AdmPwd', 'ms-Mcs-AdmPwdExpirationTime' |   Select-Object Name, 'ms-Mcs-AdmPwdExpirationTime'"],["Who read a password in Entra ID (KQL)", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20read%20a%20password%20in%20Entra%20ID%20%28KQL%29", "snippet: Windows LAPS", "For a Log Analytics workspace that receives the Entra audit logs. AuditLogs | where OperationName == \"Recover device local administrator password\" | project TimeGenerated, Actor = tostring(InitiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName), Device = tostr"],["AS-REP roasting", "glossary.html#as-rep-roasting", "glossary", "An attack on accounts that have Kerberos pre-authentication switched off. Anyone can request a ticket for such an account and crack its password offli…"],["Authentication strength", "glossary.html#authentication-strength", "glossary", "A Conditional Access setting that says which sign-in methods count, for example only phishing-resistant ones. It replaces the plain \"require MFA\" cont…"],["Business email compromise (BEC)", "glossary.html#business-email-compromise-bec", "glossary", "Fraud carried out from a real or imitated mailbox, usually to redirect a payment. Typical signs are a new inbox rule, a changed bank detail and pressu…"],["Command and control (C2)", "glossary.html#command-and-control-c2", "glossary", "The channel an attacker uses to steer malware inside your network, usually ordinary-looking HTTPS traffic to a server they own. Cutting it is a priori…"],["Compliance policy", "glossary.html#compliance-policy", "glossary", "Intune rules a device must meet, such as encryption on and a minimum OS version. Conditional Access can block devices that fail them."],["Consent phishing", "glossary.html#consent-phishing", "glossary", "A lure that asks the user to approve an app instead of typing a password. The app then reads mail and files with its own token, and a password reset d…"],["Continuous access evaluation (CAE)", "glossary.html#continuous-access-evaluation-cae", "glossary", "Lets Entra ID tell an app to drop a session within minutes when the user is disabled, the password changes or the location leaves the allowed range, i…"],["DCSync", "glossary.html#dcsync", "glossary", "An attack in which an account with replication rights asks a domain controller for password hashes, including krbtgt. Only domain controllers should h…"],["Device code phishing", "glossary.html#device-code-phishing", "glossary", "The attacker starts a device sign-in and gets the victim to enter the code on the real Microsoft page. The victim completes MFA and the attacker recei…"],["FSMO roles", "glossary.html#fsmo-roles", "glossary", "Five tasks in Active Directory that only one domain controller performs at a time, such as the PDC emulator and the RID master."],["Hybrid join", "glossary.html#hybrid-join", "glossary", "A Windows device that is joined to on-premises Active Directory and also registered in Entra ID. It lets Conditional Access trust domain machines."],["Immutable backup", "glossary.html#immutable-backup", "glossary", "A backup that cannot be changed or deleted for a set time, even by an administrator. It is what survives when ransomware reaches the backup server."],["ImmutableID", "glossary.html#immutableid", "glossary", "The value that ties an on-premises AD account to its cloud account, normally the Base64 form of objectGUID. A mismatch produces duplicate users after …"],["Indicator of compromise (IOC)", "glossary.html#indicator-of-compromise-ioc", "glossary", "A piece of evidence that points to an intrusion, such as a file hash, an IP address, a domain or a mail subject. You search your logs for it to find o…"],["MTA-STS", "glossary.html#mta-sts", "glossary", "A policy published over HTTPS that tells sending mail servers to deliver to your domain only over verified TLS. It stops downgrade attacks on mail in …"],["NDR (non-delivery report)", "glossary.html#ndr-non-delivery-report", "glossary", "The bounce message a sender gets when a mail cannot be delivered. The status code in it, such as 5.1.1 or 5.7.1, names the reason."],["RPO and RTO", "glossary.html#rpo-and-rto", "glossary", "Recovery point objective is how much data you can afford to lose, measured in time since the last backup. Recovery time objective is how long the rest…"],["Safe Links", "glossary.html#safe-links", "glossary", "A Defender for Office 365 feature that rewrites links in mail and checks them at the moment of the click. It is also what records who clicked."],["Temporary Access Pass", "glossary.html#temporary-access-pass", "glossary", "A time-limited passcode an admin issues so a user can sign in and register a passkey or other strong method without ever having a password."],["Token protection", "glossary.html#token-protection", "glossary", "A Conditional Access control that binds a sign-in token to the device it was issued to, so a stolen token is useless elsewhere. Coverage depends on th…"],["Active Directory cheat sheet", "active-directory-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Active Directory commands: lockouts, password resets, stale accounts, group membership, replication, DC health and the checks an attacker runs first."],["Entra Connect and hybrid join cheat sheet", "entra-connect-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Entra Connect Sync and hybrid join commands: sync cycles, scheduler, staging mode, ImmutableID matching, password hash sync diagnostics and dsregcmd."],["BitLocker cheat sheet", "bitlocker-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "BitLocker commands: status, recovery keys from the device, Active Directory and Entra ID, suspend for firmware updates, key rotation and recovery troubleshooting."],["Windows LAPS cheat sheet", "windows-laps-cheat-sheet.html", "page", "Windows LAPS commands: read and rotate local admin passwords from Active Directory and Entra ID, set permissions, check policy and troubleshoot."],["M365 license comparison","license-comparison.html","page","Compare Microsoft 365 and Entra ID license tiers: Business Basic, Standard, Premium, E3, E5 side by side"],["Subnet & CIDR calculator","subnet-calculator.html","page","Enter an IPv4 address and prefix, get network, broadcast, mask, host range and a visual address-space map"],["Incident runbook generator","incident-runbook.html","page","Build a tailored step-by-step incident response runbook for phishing clicks, compromised accounts, ransomware, lost devices, data leaks or malware"],["Password strength checker","password-strength.html","page","Check a password entropy and estimated crack time against online and offline attacks, computed locally in the browser"],["Status center","status-center.html","page","Official status page links for Microsoft 365, Azure, Entra ID, GitHub, Cloudflare and more, plus a live browser connectivity check"],["Product lifecycle lookup","product-lifecycle.html","page","Live end-of-support countdown for Windows Server, Windows, Exchange, SQL Server, Office and SharePoint, with status and official verify links"],["DNS lookup","dns-lookup.html","page","Look up A, AAAA, MX, TXT, NS, CNAME, SOA and CAA records for any domain via DNS-over-HTTPS, resolved live in your browser"],["Domain check","domain-check.html","page","Email security audit of a domain from live DNS: SPF lookup count, DMARC policy, DKIM selectors, MTA-STS, TLS-RPT, DNSSEC, CAA, spoofing risk and grade"],["Incident simulator","incident-sim.html","lab","Tabletop exercises: business email compromise and ransomware incident response with decisions, clock and debrief"],["Cockpit","cockpit.html","page","Personal dashboard stored only in your browser: domain grade, open attack routes, Conditional Access coverage, sign-in findings, end-of-support watchlist, Patch Tuesday, exploited vulnerabilities"],["Phish analyzer","phish-analyzer.html","page","Analyze a suspicious email (.eml): DMARC and SPF results, forged display names, look-alike domains, links that go elsewhere, risky attachments, phishing verdict"],["Attack map","attack-map.html","page","Interactive kill chain for Microsoft 365, Entra ID and Active Directory: phishing, AiTM, token theft, Kerberoasting, ransomware, mapped to MITRE ATT&CK and your controls"],["Conditional Access policy analyzer","ca-analyzer.html","page","Analyze a Conditional Access policy export for gaps: MFA, legacy authentication, report-only, exclusions, device code flow, plain-language policy summary"],["Sign-in log analyzer","signin-analyzer.html","page","Analyze an Entra ID sign-in log export for password spray, MFA fatigue, impossible travel, legacy authentication and scripted clients, in the browser"],["CVSS 3.1 calculator","cvss-calculator.html","page","Calculate or decode a CVSS 3.1 base score and vector string, with severity rating and an explanation of every metric"],["Patch Tuesday calendar","patch-tuesday.html","page","The next 8 Patch Tuesdays computed live, plus a common ring-based rollout cadence for planning deployment"],["Script generator","script-generator.html","page","Generate ready-to-run PowerShell/Graph scripts: offboarding, bulk user creation, mailbox permissions, Conditional Access policy"],["Offboarding script generator","script-generator.html#offboard-gen","tool","Generate a Graph PowerShell offboarding script: block sign-in, revoke sessions, remove licenses, convert mailbox"],["Bulk user creation script generator","script-generator.html#bulk-gen","tool","Generate a Graph PowerShell script to create multiple users at once from a pasted list"],["Mailbox permission script generator","script-generator.html#mailbox-gen","tool","Generate an Exchange Online PowerShell script granting Full Access, Send As or Send on Behalf"],["Conditional Access policy script generator","script-generator.html#ca-gen","tool","Generate Graph PowerShell to create a Conditional Access policy with MFA and compliant device grant controls"],["Troubleshooting wizard","diagnose.html","page","Interactive diagnostic wizards for sign-in, email delivery and network connectivity problems"],["Can't sign in to Microsoft 365 / Entra ID","diagnose.html#signin","lab","Diagnostic wizard for sign-in failures: AADSTS codes, lockouts, MFA, Conditional Access"],["Email isn't being delivered","diagnose.html#email","lab","Diagnostic wizard for email delivery: bounces, spam folder, quarantine, DNS"],["Can't reach a server or website","diagnose.html#network","lab","Diagnostic wizard for network connectivity: DNS, firewall, TLS, ports"],["Start here – find your track","start-here.html","page","Quick guide to admin_hub for new visitors: M365, Active Directory, Azure, security, Linux"],["Tools","tools.html","page","Free browser-based admin tools: CIDR calculator, JWT decoder, hash generator, password generator, time converter, Base64, GUID, email header analyzer…"],["Cheat sheets and references","cheat-sheets.html","page","Copy-and-paste cheat sheets for PowerShell, Microsoft Graph and KQL."],["Checklists","checklists.html","page","Security and admin checklists for Microsoft 365, Entra ID, incident response and user lifecycle."],["IT security glossary","glossary.html","page","Plain-language glossary of IT security and Microsoft admin terms: Kerberoasting, AiTM, DMARC, Conditional Access, PIM and more."],["Visual explainers","explainers.html","page","Interactive diagrams: Kerberos, OAuth, AiTM phishing, Conditional Access"],["aadsts-lookup: Entra sign-in error codes explained","aadsts-lookup.html","page","Look up Entra ID AADSTS sign-in error codes with their meaning and the usual fix."],["Windows event ID reference","event-id-reference.html","page","Common Windows event IDs for logons, accounts, services, scheduled tasks and Defender, with notes on what they mean."],["Email bounce error codes","email-error-codes.html","page","Exchange Online and Microsoft 365 NDR codes such as 5.1.10, 5.7.1, 5.7.509 and 4.4.7 explained with the usual fix."],["HTTP status codes","http-status-codes.html","page","HTTP status codes explained with common causes and what to check: 301, 302, 401, 403, 404, 429, 500, 502, 503, 504."],["Cryptography quick reference","crypto-quick-reference.html","page","Which hash, encryption, key and TLS choices are recommended, acceptable, legacy or broken: MD5, SHA-256, AES, RSA, Argon2, TLS 1.3."],["Azure CLI cheat sheet","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html","page","Azure CLI commands for subscriptions, resource groups, VMs, roles, networking and storage checks."],["Compromised account response checklist","compromised-account-response-checklist.html","page","Step-by-step checklist for responding to a compromised Microsoft 365 or Entra ID account."],["Docker cheat sheet","docker-cheat-sheet.html","page","Docker and Compose commands for containers, images, logs, cleanup and safer runs."],["Entra ID hardening checklist","entra-id-hardening-checklist.html","page","Checklist for hardening Microsoft Entra ID: Conditional Access, apps, guests, authentication and hybrid."],["Git cheat sheet","git-cheat-sheet.html","page","Everyday Git commands: status, history, undoing changes, branches, stash and searching."],["Microsoft Graph cheat sheet","graph-cheat-sheet.html","page","Microsoft Graph PowerShell commands for users, licenses, sign-in logs and Conditional Access."],["Intune and Defender cheat sheet","intune-defender-cheat-sheet.html","page","Intune and Microsoft Defender commands: device join state, MDM sync, Autopilot hash, scans, exclusions and Graph queries."],["KQL cheat sheet","kql-cheat-sheet.html","page","KQL queries for Entra ID sign-ins, Sentinel and Defender hunting."],["Linux cheat sheet","linux-cheat-sheet.html","page","Linux commands for admins and security checks: logins, ports, SUID files, services and updates."],["Microsoft 365 security checklist","m365-security-checklist.html","page","Checklist to secure a Microsoft 365 tenant: identity, email, apps, devices and monitoring."],["Networking cheat sheet","networking-cheat-sheet.html","page","Networking commands for admins: nmap, dig, curl, openssl, tcpdump and Wireshark filters."],["User onboarding and offboarding checklist","onboarding-offboarding-checklist.html","page","Checklists for onboarding and offboarding users in Microsoft 365 and Entra ID."],["PowerShell cheat sheet","powershell-cheat-sheet.html","page","PowerShell snippets for Exchange Online, Active Directory and Windows security checks."],["cidr-calculator","tools.html#cidr-calculator","tool","Enter an IPv4 address with prefix length and get network, broadcast, mask and host range."],["jwt-decoder","tools.html#jwt-decoder","tool","Paste a JSON Web Token to read its header and claims. Decoding happens in your browser; the signature is not verified."],["hash-generator","tools.html#hash-generator","tool","Type or paste text to get its SHA-1, SHA-256, SHA-384 and SHA-512 hashes, computed locally in your browser."],["password-generator","tools.html#password-generator","tool","Random passwords from your browser's secure random generator. Nothing is stored or sent."],["time-converter","tools.html#time-converter","tool","Convert Unix seconds, Unix milliseconds, Windows FILETIME (Active Directory values such as lastLogon and pwdLastSet) or a date string."],["base64-tool","tools.html#base64-tool","tool","Encode text as Base64, build a PowerShell -EncodedCommand string, or decode Base64 as UTF-8 and UTF-16LE to inspect encoded commands."],["guid-generator","tools.html#guid-generator","tool","Random version 4 GUIDs, generated in your browser."],["email-header-analyzer","tools.html#email-header-analyzer","tool","Paste the full raw headers of an email to see the sender fields, SPF, DKIM and DMARC results and the delivery path. Processed locally."],["port-reference","tools.html#port-reference","tool","Common TCP and UDP ports for admins. Search by number, service or keyword."],["regex-tester","tools.html#regex-tester","tool","Test a JavaScript regular expression against text and see matches and capture groups. Flags such as i, m and s are supported; g is always on."],["json-formatter","tools.html#json-formatter","tool","Validate JSON and get a formatted and a minified version."],["chmod-calculator","tools.html#chmod-calculator","tool","Set Linux file permissions with checkboxes or type an octal value such as 755."],["url-encoder","tools.html#url-encoder","tool","Percent-encode or decode text for use in URLs."],["cron-explainer","tools.html#cron-explainer","tool","Enter a standard five-field cron expression, or a shortcut such as @daily, and see what each field means."],["uac-decoder","tools.html#uac-decoder","tool","Decode an Active Directory userAccountControl value, in decimal or hex, into its flags."],["spf-explainer","tools.html#spf-explainer","tool","Paste an SPF record (the TXT value) and get each part explained, including a count of DNS lookups."],["dmarc-explainer","tools.html#dmarc-explainer","tool","Paste a DMARC record (the TXT value of _dmarc) and see the policy, alignment and reporting settings."],["Port 20-21 FTP","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Cleartext; prefer SFTP or FTPS"],["Port 22 SSH / SFTP","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Remote shell; use keys and restrict by IP"],["Port 23 Telnet","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Cleartext; avoid"],["Port 25 SMTP","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Server-to-server mail transfer"],["Port 53 DNS","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP/UDP. Zone transfers use TCP"],["Port 67-68 DHCP","tools.html#port-reference","port","UDP. Server 67, client 68"],["Port 69 TFTP","tools.html#port-reference","port","UDP. No authentication"],["Port 80 HTTP","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Unencrypted web"],["Port 88 Kerberos","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP/UDP. Active Directory authentication"],["Port 110 POP3","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Cleartext mail retrieval"],["Port 123 NTP","tools.html#port-reference","port","UDP. Time sync; Kerberos needs accurate time"],["Port 135 RPC Endpoint Mapper","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Windows RPC; do not expose to the internet"],["Port 137-139 NetBIOS","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP/UDP. Legacy name and session services"],["Port 143 IMAP","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Use STARTTLS or port 993"],["Port 161-162 SNMP","tools.html#port-reference","port","UDP. Use v3; v1 and v2c community strings are weak"],["Port 389 LDAP","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP/UDP. Cleartext unless signed or STARTTLS"],["Port 443 HTTPS","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Encrypted web"],["Port 445 SMB","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Windows file sharing; never expose to the internet"],["Port 464 Kerberos password change","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP/UDP. kpasswd"],["Port 465 SMTPS","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. SMTP over implicit TLS"],["Port 500 IKE","tools.html#port-reference","port","UDP. IPsec key exchange"],["Port 514 Syslog","tools.html#port-reference","port","UDP. Often unencrypted"],["Port 587 SMTP submission","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Client mail submission with STARTTLS"],["Port 636 LDAPS","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. LDAP over TLS"],["Port 853 DNS over TLS","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. "],["Port 873 rsync","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. "],["Port 993 IMAPS","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. IMAP over TLS"],["Port 995 POP3S","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. POP3 over TLS"],["Port 1194 OpenVPN","tools.html#port-reference","port","UDP. Default port"],["Port 1433 Microsoft SQL Server","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Default instance"],["Port 1521 Oracle Database","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Default listener"],["Port 1812-1813 RADIUS","tools.html#port-reference","port","UDP. Authentication and accounting"],["Port 2049 NFS","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP/UDP. "],["Port 3268-3269 Global Catalog","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. 3269 uses TLS"],["Port 3306 MySQL / MariaDB","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. "],["Port 3389 RDP","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP/UDP. Remote Desktop; do not expose directly to the internet"],["Port 4500 IPsec NAT-T","tools.html#port-reference","port","UDP. NAT traversal"],["Port 5060-5061 SIP","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP/UDP. 5061 uses TLS"],["Port 5432 PostgreSQL","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. "],["Port 5900 VNC","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Often weakly protected"],["Port 5985-5986 WinRM","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. 5985 HTTP, 5986 HTTPS; PowerShell remoting"],["Port 6379 Redis","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Do not expose to the internet"],["Port 8080 HTTP alternate","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Proxies and dev servers"],["Port 8443 HTTPS alternate","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. "],["Port 9200 Elasticsearch","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. HTTP API"],["Port 9389 AD Web Services","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. Used by the AD PowerShell module"],["Port 27017 MongoDB","tools.html#port-reference","port","TCP. "],["Port 51820 WireGuard","tools.html#port-reference","port","UDP. Default port"],["Sign in","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=Sign%20in","snippet: Azure CLI","Opens a browser for interactive sign-in. az login"],["Sign in with a device code","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=Sign%20in%20with%20a%20device%20code","snippet: Azure CLI","For machines without a browser. az login --use-device-code"],["Show the active account","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=Show%20the%20active%20account","snippet: Azure CLI","Current subscription and tenant. az account show"],["List subscriptions","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20subscriptions","snippet: Azure CLI","All subscriptions you can access. az account list --output table"],["Switch subscription","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=Switch%20subscription","snippet: Azure CLI","Set the subscription for later commands. az account set --subscription \"Subscription name or ID\""],["List resource groups","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20resource%20groups","snippet: Azure CLI","Overview as a table. az group list --output table"],["Create a resource group","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20resource%20group","snippet: Azure CLI","Example in West Europe. az group create --name myRG --location westeurope"],["List VMs with power state","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20VMs%20with%20power%20state","snippet: Azure CLI","Adds details such as the power state. az vm list --show-details --output table"],["Stop and deallocate a VM","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=Stop%20and%20deallocate%20a%20VM","snippet: Azure CLI","Only a deallocated VM stops compute billing. az vm deallocate --resource-group myRG --name myVM"],["Role assignments of a user","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=Role%20assignments%20of%20a%20user","snippet: Azure CLI","Everything a user can do across the subscription. az role assignment list --assignee user@contoso.com --all --output table"],["Assign a role","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=Assign%20a%20role","snippet: Azure CLI","Example: Reader on a subscription. az role assignment create --assignee user@contoso.com --role Reader --scope /subscriptions/SUBSCRIPTION_ID"],["List public IP addresses","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20public%20IP%20addresses","snippet: Azure CLI","Find what is exposed. az network public-ip list --output table"],["List NSG rules","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20NSG%20rules","snippet: Azure CLI","Rules of a network security group. az network nsg rule list --resource-group myRG --nsg-name myNSG --output table"],["Storage accounts with public blob access","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=Storage%20accounts%20with%20public%20blob%20access","snippet: Azure CLI","Security check with a JMESPath query. az storage account list --query \"[].{Name:name,PublicAccess:allowBlobPublicAccess}\" --output table"],["List Key Vault secrets","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20Key%20Vault%20secrets","snippet: Azure CLI","Names and metadata only, not the values. az keyvault secret list --vault-name myVault --output table"],["List Entra users","azure-cli-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20Entra%20users","snippet: Azure CLI","Names and user principal names. az ad user list --query \"[].{Name:displayName,UPN:userPrincipalName}\" --output table"],["List containers","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20containers","snippet: Docker","Running and stopped containers. docker ps -a"],["List images","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20images","snippet: Docker","Local images and their sizes. docker images"],["Run a container","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20a%20container","snippet: Docker","Detached, named, with a published port. docker run -d --name web -p 8080:80 nginx"],["Follow logs","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Follow%20logs","snippet: Docker","Last 100 lines, then live. docker logs -f --tail 100 web"],["Open a shell in a container","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Open%20a%20shell%20in%20a%20container","snippet: Docker","Interactive shell in a running container. docker exec -it web sh"],["Stop and remove a container","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Stop%20and%20remove%20a%20container","snippet: Docker","Stops it, then deletes it. docker stop web && docker rm web"],["Build an image","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Build%20an%20image","snippet: Docker","Builds from the Dockerfile in the current folder. docker build -t myapp:1.0 ."],["Start a Compose stack","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Start%20a%20Compose%20stack","snippet: Docker","Runs all services in the background. docker compose up -d"],["Follow Compose logs","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Follow%20Compose%20logs","snippet: Docker","Live logs of all services. docker compose logs -f"],["Stop a Compose stack","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Stop%20a%20Compose%20stack","snippet: Docker","Stops and removes containers and networks. docker compose down"],["Resource usage","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Resource%20usage","snippet: Docker","One snapshot of CPU and memory per container. docker stats --no-stream"],["Disk usage","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Disk%20usage","snippet: Docker","Space used by images, containers and volumes. docker system df"],["Clean up unused data","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Clean%20up%20unused%20data","snippet: Docker","Removes stopped containers, unused networks and dangling images after confirmation. docker system prune"],["Copy a file out of a container","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Copy%20a%20file%20out%20of%20a%20container","snippet: Docker","Container path first, then the local path. docker cp web:/etc/nginx/nginx.conf ./nginx.conf"],["Container IP address","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Container%20IP%20address","snippet: Docker","Read the address from the container metadata. docker inspect -f \"{{range .NetworkSettings.Networks}}{{.IPAddress}}{{end}}\" web"],["Run with fewer privileges","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20with%20fewer%20privileges","snippet: Docker","Read-only filesystem, no extra capabilities, no privilege gain. docker run --rm --read-only --cap-drop ALL --security-opt no-new-privileges alpine id"],["Scan an image for vulnerabilities","docker-cheat-sheet.html?q=Scan%20an%20image%20for%20vulnerabilities","snippet: Docker","Needs the Trivy scanner installed. trivy image nginx:latest"],["Status","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Status","snippet: Git","Changed, staged and untracked files. git status"],["Compact history","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Compact%20history","snippet: Git","Last 20 commits as a graph. git log --oneline --graph --decorate -n 20"],["Show staged changes","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Show%20staged%20changes","snippet: Git","What the next commit will contain. git diff --staged"],["Undo the last commit, keep the changes","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Undo%20the%20last%20commit%2C%20keep%20the%20changes","snippet: Git","Moves the commit back to the staging area. git reset --soft HEAD~1"],["Discard local changes in a file","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Discard%20local%20changes%20in%20a%20file","snippet: Git","The changes are lost. git restore filename"],["Unstage a file","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Unstage%20a%20file","snippet: Git","Keeps the changes in the working directory. git restore --staged filename"],["Amend the last commit","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Amend%20the%20last%20commit","snippet: Git","Change its message or add forgotten files. Avoid on pushed commits. git commit --amend"],["Create and switch to a branch","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20and%20switch%20to%20a%20branch","snippet: Git","New branch from the current one. git switch -c feature-name"],["Stash and restore work in progress","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Stash%20and%20restore%20work%20in%20progress","snippet: Git","Park changes and bring them back later. git stash push -m \"work in progress\" git stash pop"],["Revert a commit","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Revert%20a%20commit","snippet: Git","Creates a new commit that undoes an earlier one. git revert COMMIT_ID"],["Find who changed a line","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20who%20changed%20a%20line","snippet: Git","Author and commit for each line of a file. git blame filename"],["Search the history for a string","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Search%20the%20history%20for%20a%20string","snippet: Git","Commits that added or removed the text. git log -S \"search text\" --oneline"],["Stop tracking a file","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Stop%20tracking%20a%20file","snippet: Git","Keeps the file locally. A secret that was committed stays in the history, so rotate it. git rm --cached filename"],["Preview cleaning untracked files","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Preview%20cleaning%20untracked%20files","snippet: Git","Dry run; shows what would be deleted. git clean -n -d"],["Set your identity","git-cheat-sheet.html?q=Set%20your%20identity","snippet: Git","Name and email used for commits. git config --global user.name \"Your Name\" git config --global user.email \"you@example.com\""],["Install the Graph PowerShell SDK","graph-cheat-sheet.html?q=Install%20the%20Graph%20PowerShell%20SDK","snippet: Microsoft Graph","One-time setup. Install-Module Microsoft.Graph -Scope CurrentUser"],["Connect with specific scopes","graph-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect%20with%20specific%20scopes","snippet: Microsoft Graph","Request only the permissions you need. Connect-MgGraph -Scopes \"User.Read.All\",\"Group.Read.All\""],["Get one user","graph-cheat-sheet.html?q=Get%20one%20user","snippet: Microsoft Graph","Basic properties of a single user. Get-MgUser -UserId user@contoso.com -Property DisplayName,UserPrincipalName,AccountEnabled | Select-Object DisplayName,UserP…"],["Disabled users","graph-cheat-sheet.html?q=Disabled%20users","snippet: Microsoft Graph","All accounts that are disabled. Get-MgUser -All -Filter \"accountEnabled eq false\" -Property DisplayName,UserPrincipalName | Select-Object DisplayName,UserPrinc…"],["Guest users","graph-cheat-sheet.html?q=Guest%20users","snippet: Microsoft Graph","All guests with their creation date. Get-MgUser -All -Filter \"userType eq 'Guest'\" -Property DisplayName,UserPrincipalName,CreatedDateTime | Select-Object Disp…"],["License usage per SKU","graph-cheat-sheet.html?q=License%20usage%20per%20SKU","snippet: Microsoft Graph","Consumed and purchased units. Needs the Organization.Read.All scope. Get-MgSubscribedSku | Select-Object SkuPartNumber,ConsumedUnits,@{ n = \"Total\"; e = { $_.P…"],["Licenses assigned to a user","graph-cheat-sheet.html?q=Licenses%20assigned%20to%20a%20user","snippet: Microsoft Graph","Shows the SKU part numbers of a user. Get-MgUserLicenseDetail -UserId user@contoso.com | Select-Object SkuPartNumber"],["Recent sign-in logs","graph-cheat-sheet.html?q=Recent%20sign-in%20logs","snippet: Microsoft Graph","Needs the AuditLog.Read.All scope. Get-MgAuditLogSignIn -Top 20 | Select-Object CreatedDateTime,UserPrincipalName,AppDisplayName,@{ n = \"ErrorCode\"; e = { $_.S…"],["Conditional Access policies","graph-cheat-sheet.html?q=Conditional%20Access%20policies","snippet: Microsoft Graph","List policies and their state. Needs the Policy.Read.All scope. Get-MgIdentityConditionalAccessPolicy | Select-Object DisplayName,State"],["Revoke a user's sessions","graph-cheat-sheet.html?q=Revoke%20a%20user%27s%20sessions","snippet: Microsoft Graph","Signs the user out everywhere. Needs the User.RevokeSessions.All scope. Revoke-MgUserSignInSession -UserId user@contoso.com"],["Raw Graph request","graph-cheat-sheet.html?q=Raw%20Graph%20request","snippet: Microsoft Graph","Call any Graph endpoint with your current connection. Invoke-MgGraphRequest -Method GET -Uri \"https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/me\""],["Check join and registration state","intune-defender-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20join%20and%20registration%20state","snippet: Intune and Defender","Shows Entra join state, PRT status and MDM enrollment of a Windows device. dsregcmd /status"],["Trigger an MDM sync from the device","intune-defender-cheat-sheet.html?q=Trigger%20an%20MDM%20sync%20from%20the%20device","snippet: Intune and Defender","Widely used but not an officially documented method. Run in an elevated PowerShell. Get-ScheduledTask | Where-Object { $_.TaskName -eq \"PushLaunch\" } | Start-S…"],["Collect MDM diagnostics","intune-defender-cheat-sheet.html?q=Collect%20MDM%20diagnostics","snippet: Intune and Defender","Creates a ZIP with enrollment, provisioning and Autopilot logs. mdmdiagnosticstool.exe -area \"DeviceEnrollment;DeviceProvisioning;Autopilot\" -zip C:\\Temp\\MDMDi…"],["Export the Autopilot hardware hash","intune-defender-cheat-sheet.html?q=Export%20the%20Autopilot%20hardware%20hash","snippet: Intune and Defender","Installs the script and writes the hash to a CSV file. Install-Script -Name Get-WindowsAutopilotInfo -Force Get-WindowsAutopilotInfo -OutputFile C:\\Temp\\Autopi…"],["List managed devices in Intune","intune-defender-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20managed%20devices%20in%20Intune","snippet: Intune and Defender","Needs the DeviceManagementManagedDevices.Read.All scope. Connect-MgGraph -Scopes \"DeviceManagementManagedDevices.Read.All\" Get-MgDeviceManagementManagedDevice …"],["Non-compliant devices","intune-defender-cheat-sheet.html?q=Non-compliant%20devices","snippet: Intune and Defender","Devices Intune marks as non-compliant. Get-MgDeviceManagementManagedDevice -All -Filter \"complianceState eq 'noncompliant'\" | Select-Object DeviceName,UserPrin…"],["Sync a managed device from Graph","intune-defender-cheat-sheet.html?q=Sync%20a%20managed%20device%20from%20Graph","snippet: Intune and Defender","Needs the DeviceManagementManagedDevices.PrivilegedOperations.All scope. Sync-MgDeviceManagementManagedDevice -ManagedDeviceId $deviceId"],["Defender status","intune-defender-cheat-sheet.html?q=Defender%20status","snippet: Intune and Defender","Protection state and signature age on a Windows device. Get-MpComputerStatus | Select-Object AntivirusEnabled,RealTimeProtectionEnabled,IsTamperProtected,Antiv…"],["Update Defender signatures","intune-defender-cheat-sheet.html?q=Update%20Defender%20signatures","snippet: Intune and Defender","Downloads the latest definitions now. Update-MpSignature"],["Start a quick scan","intune-defender-cheat-sheet.html?q=Start%20a%20quick%20scan","snippet: Intune and Defender","Runs a Defender quick scan. Start-MpScan -ScanType QuickScan"],["Recent threat detections","intune-defender-cheat-sheet.html?q=Recent%20threat%20detections","snippet: Intune and Defender","Shows what Defender detected and when. Get-MpThreatDetection | Select-Object InitialDetectionTime,ThreatID,Resources"],["Review Defender exclusions","intune-defender-cheat-sheet.html?q=Review%20Defender%20exclusions","snippet: Intune and Defender","Exclusions weaken protection. Check them regularly. Get-MpPreference | Select-Object ExclusionPath,ExclusionExtension,ExclusionProcess"],["Attack surface reduction rules","intune-defender-cheat-sheet.html?q=Attack%20surface%20reduction%20rules","snippet: Intune and Defender","Configured rule IDs and their actions. Get-MpPreference | Select-Object AttackSurfaceReductionRules_Ids,AttackSurfaceReductionRules_Actions"],["Basics: time filter, count, chart","kql-cheat-sheet.html?q=Basics%3A%20time%20filter%2C%20count%2C%20chart","snippet: KQL","The pattern behind most queries. SigninLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(1h) | summarize count() by bin(TimeGenerated, 5m) | render timechart"],["Failed sign-ins by user","kql-cheat-sheet.html?q=Failed%20sign-ins%20by%20user","snippet: KQL","Failures in the last 24 hours, grouped by user and error code. SigninLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(24h) and ResultType != 0 | summarize Failures = count() b…"],["Password spray indicator","kql-cheat-sheet.html?q=Password%20spray%20indicator","snippet: KQL","One IP failing against many different users. SigninLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(1d) and ResultType in (50126, 50053) | summarize Users = dcount(UserPrincip…"],["MFA failures","kql-cheat-sheet.html?q=MFA%20failures","snippet: KQL","Sign-ins that failed the MFA step. SigninLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(7d) and ResultType == 500121 | summarize Failures = count() by UserPrincipalName | or…"],["Blocked by Conditional Access","kql-cheat-sheet.html?q=Blocked%20by%20Conditional%20Access","snippet: KQL","Sign-ins stopped by a Conditional Access policy (53003). SigninLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(7d) and ResultType == 53003 | summarize Blocks = count() by App…"],["Legacy authentication sign-ins","kql-cheat-sheet.html?q=Legacy%20authentication%20sign-ins","snippet: KQL","Successful sign-ins that do not use modern clients. SigninLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(30d) and ResultType == 0 | where ClientAppUsed !in (\"Browser\", \"Mobi…"],["Users signing in from several countries","kql-cheat-sheet.html?q=Users%20signing%20in%20from%20several%20countries","snippet: KQL","Successful sign-ins from more than one country in 7 days. SigninLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(7d) and ResultType == 0 | summarize Countries = make_set(tostr…"],["Role assignment changes","kql-cheat-sheet.html?q=Role%20assignment%20changes","snippet: KQL","Who was added to a directory role. AuditLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(30d) and OperationName has \"member to role\" | project TimeGenerated, OperationName, In…"],["Windows failed logons","kql-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20failed%20logons","snippet: KQL","Event 4625 by account and source IP, per hour. SecurityEvent | where TimeGenerated > ago(1d) and EventID == 4625 | summarize Failures = count() by Account, IpA…"],["Encoded PowerShell commands","kql-cheat-sheet.html?q=Encoded%20PowerShell%20commands","snippet: KQL","Defender XDR advanced hunting, which uses Timestamp instead of TimeGenerated. DeviceProcessEvents | where Timestamp > ago(7d) | where FileName =~ \"powershell.e…"],["New or changed inbox rules","kql-cheat-sheet.html?q=New%20or%20changed%20inbox%20rules","snippet: KQL","Microsoft 365 audit data in Sentinel. OfficeActivity | where TimeGenerated > ago(7d) and Operation in (\"New-InboxRule\", \"Set-InboxRule\") | project TimeGenerate…"],["Failed SSH logins","linux-cheat-sheet.html?q=Failed%20SSH%20logins","snippet: Linux","Debian and Ubuntu log file. On RHEL-based systems use /var/log/secure. sudo grep \"Failed password\" /var/log/auth.log | tail -n 50"],["SSH service log","linux-cheat-sheet.html?q=SSH%20service%20log","snippet: Linux","The unit is called sshd on RHEL-based systems. sudo journalctl -u ssh --since \"1 hour ago\""],["Listening ports and their processes","linux-cheat-sheet.html?q=Listening%20ports%20and%20their%20processes","snippet: Linux","TCP and UDP sockets in listening state. sudo ss -tulpn"],["Accounts with UID 0","linux-cheat-sheet.html?q=Accounts%20with%20UID%200","snippet: Linux","Only root should normally appear here. awk -F: '$3 == 0 { print $1 }' /etc/passwd"],["Members of the sudo group","linux-cheat-sheet.html?q=Members%20of%20the%20sudo%20group","snippet: Linux","The group is called wheel on RHEL-based systems. getent group sudo"],["Recent logins","linux-cheat-sheet.html?q=Recent%20logins","snippet: Linux","Last 20 logins from the wtmp log. last -n 20"],["SUID files","linux-cheat-sheet.html?q=SUID%20files","snippet: Linux","Files that run with the owner's privileges. Review unexpected entries. sudo find / -xdev -perm -4000 -type f 2>/dev/null"],["World-writable files","linux-cheat-sheet.html?q=World-writable%20files","snippet: Linux","Files any user can modify. sudo find / -xdev -type f -perm -0002 2>/dev/null"],["Largest directories","linux-cheat-sheet.html?q=Largest%20directories","snippet: Linux","Find what fills the disk. sudo du -xh / 2>/dev/null | sort -rh | head -n 20"],["Pending package updates","linux-cheat-sheet.html?q=Pending%20package%20updates","snippet: Linux","Debian and Ubuntu. apt list --upgradable"],["Firewall status (UFW)","linux-cheat-sheet.html?q=Firewall%20status%20%28UFW%29","snippet: Linux","Rules and default policy. sudo ufw status verbose"],["Running services","linux-cheat-sheet.html?q=Running%20services","snippet: Linux","All active systemd services. systemctl list-units --type=service --state=running"],["Cron jobs","linux-cheat-sheet.html?q=Cron%20jobs","snippet: Linux","Current user's crontab and the system cron folders. crontab -l; ls -l /etc/cron.*"],["SHA-256 checksum of a file","linux-cheat-sheet.html?q=SHA-256%20checksum%20of%20a%20file","snippet: Linux","Compare with the checksum published by the vendor. sha256sum filename"],["Host discovery","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Host%20discovery","snippet: Networking","Ping sweep of a subnet without port scanning. nmap -sn 192.168.1.0/24"],["Service versions on common ports","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Service%20versions%20on%20common%20ports","snippet: Networking","Detects services on the 100 most common ports. nmap -sV --top-ports 100 192.168.1.10"],["Web page titles on specific ports","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Web%20page%20titles%20on%20specific%20ports","snippet: Networking","Uses an nmap script against ports 80 and 443. nmap -p 80,443 --script http-title 192.168.1.10"],["DNS A record","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=DNS%20A%20record","snippet: Networking","Short answer for the IPv4 address. dig +short A example.com"],["MX records","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=MX%20records","snippet: Networking","Mail servers of a domain. dig +short MX example.com"],["SPF record","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=SPF%20record","snippet: Networking","Look for the TXT record starting with v=spf1. dig +short TXT example.com"],["DMARC record","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=DMARC%20record","snippet: Networking","The policy sits in a TXT record on the _dmarc name. dig +short TXT _dmarc.example.com"],["TXT record on Windows","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=TXT%20record%20on%20Windows","snippet: Networking","Same lookup with nslookup. nslookup -type=TXT example.com"],["HTTP response headers","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=HTTP%20response%20headers","snippet: Networking","Check status, redirects and security headers. curl -I https://example.com"],["TLS certificate dates and issuer","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=TLS%20certificate%20dates%20and%20issuer","snippet: Networking","Reads the certificate a server presents. openssl s_client -connect example.com:443 -servername example.com </dev/null 2>/dev/null | openssl x509 -noout -dates …"],["Test a TCP port on Windows","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Test%20a%20TCP%20port%20on%20Windows","snippet: Networking","PowerShell replacement for telnet. Test-NetConnection example.com -Port 443"],["Listening ports on Windows","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Listening%20ports%20on%20Windows","snippet: Networking","With the owning process ID. netstat -ano | findstr LISTENING"],["Capture DNS traffic","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Capture%20DNS%20traffic","snippet: Networking","Replace eth0 with your interface. sudo tcpdump -i eth0 -n port 53"],["Flush the DNS cache on Windows","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Flush%20the%20DNS%20cache%20on%20Windows","snippet: Networking","Clears the local resolver cache. ipconfig /flushdns"],["Wireshark filter: new connection attempts","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Wireshark%20filter%3A%20new%20connection%20attempts","snippet: Networking","SYN without ACK. Many in a row can indicate scanning. tcp.flags.syn == 1 && tcp.flags.ack == 0"],["Wireshark filter: DNS errors","networking-cheat-sheet.html?q=Wireshark%20filter%3A%20DNS%20errors","snippet: Networking","Responses with a non-zero return code. dns.flags.rcode != 0"],["Install the Exchange Online module","powershell-cheat-sheet.html?q=Install%20the%20Exchange%20Online%20module","snippet: PowerShell","One-time setup for Exchange Online administration. Install-Module ExchangeOnlineManagement -Scope CurrentUser"],["Connect to Exchange Online","powershell-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect%20to%20Exchange%20Online","snippet: PowerShell","Sign in interactively with an admin account. Connect-ExchangeOnline -UserPrincipalName admin@contoso.com"],["Largest mailboxes","powershell-cheat-sheet.html?q=Largest%20mailboxes","snippet: PowerShell","Top 20 mailboxes by size. Get-Mailbox -ResultSize Unlimited | Get-MailboxStatistics | Sort-Object TotalItemSize -Descending | Select-Object DisplayName,TotalIt…"],["Mailbox permissions","powershell-cheat-sheet.html?q=Mailbox%20permissions","snippet: PowerShell","Who has access to a mailbox, without the owner's own entry. Get-MailboxPermission -Identity user@contoso.com | Where-Object { $_.User -ne \"NT AUTHORITY\\SELF\" }"],["Inbox rules that forward or delete","powershell-cheat-sheet.html?q=Inbox%20rules%20that%20forward%20or%20delete","snippet: PowerShell","Quick check on a possibly compromised mailbox. Get-InboxRule -Mailbox user@contoso.com | Select-Object Name,ForwardTo,ForwardAsAttachmentTo,RedirectTo,DeleteMe…"],["Mailboxes with forwarding configured","powershell-cheat-sheet.html?q=Mailboxes%20with%20forwarding%20configured","snippet: PowerShell","Find mailboxes that forward mail to another address. Get-Mailbox -ResultSize Unlimited | Where-Object { $_.ForwardingSmtpAddress -or $_.ForwardingAddress } | S…"],["Locked-out AD accounts","powershell-cheat-sheet.html?q=Locked-out%20AD%20accounts","snippet: PowerShell","Requires the ActiveDirectory module (RSAT). Search-ADAccount -LockedOut | Select-Object Name,SamAccountName,LockedOut"],["Inactive AD users (90 days)","powershell-cheat-sheet.html?q=Inactive%20AD%20users%20%2890%20days%29","snippet: PowerShell","Enabled or disabled users without a logon for 90 days. Search-ADAccount -AccountInactive -TimeSpan 90.00:00:00 -UsersOnly | Select-Object Name,SamAccountName,L…"],["Users whose password never expires","powershell-cheat-sheet.html?q=Users%20whose%20password%20never%20expires","snippet: PowerShell","Review these accounts for service accounts and exceptions. Get-ADUser -Filter 'PasswordNeverExpires -eq $true' -Properties PasswordNeverExpires | Select-Object…"],["Domain Admins members","powershell-cheat-sheet.html?q=Domain%20Admins%20members","snippet: PowerShell","List members including nested groups. Get-ADGroupMember -Identity \"Domain Admins\" -Recursive | Select-Object Name,SamAccountName"],["Recent failed logons (event 4625)","powershell-cheat-sheet.html?q=Recent%20failed%20logons%20%28event%204625%29","snippet: PowerShell","Run on the machine or domain controller, as administrator. Get-WinEvent -FilterHashtable @{ LogName = \"Security\"; Id = 4625 } -MaxEvents 50 | Select-Object Tim…"],["Listening TCP ports","powershell-cheat-sheet.html?q=Listening%20TCP%20ports","snippet: PowerShell","See which ports a Windows machine is listening on. Get-NetTCPConnection -State Listen | Select-Object LocalAddress,LocalPort,OwningProcess | Sort-Object LocalP…"],["Local administrators","powershell-cheat-sheet.html?q=Local%20administrators","snippet: PowerShell","Members of the local Administrators group. Get-LocalGroupMember -Group \"Administrators\""],["BitLocker status","powershell-cheat-sheet.html?q=BitLocker%20status","snippet: PowerShell","Encryption and protection state per volume. Get-BitLockerVolume | Select-Object MountPoint,VolumeStatus,ProtectionStatus"],["AADSTS","glossary.html#aadsts","glossary","Prefix of error codes returned by Microsoft Entra ID when a sign-in or token request fails. It stands for Azure Active Directory Security Token Servi…"],["Active Directory","glossary.html#active-directory","glossary","Microsoft's directory service for Windows domains. It stores users, computers and groups and handles authentication and policies in on-premises netwo…"],["Adversary-in-the-middle (AiTM)","glossary.html#adversary-in-the-middle-aitm","glossary","A phishing technique where a proxy sits between the victim and the real sign-in page and captures the password and the session cookie. It can bypass …"],["Attack surface","glossary.html#attack-surface","glossary","All the points where an attacker could try to get in, such as exposed services, accounts, apps and people."],["Azure AD","glossary.html#azure-ad","glossary","Former name of Microsoft Entra ID. Older tools, commands and documents still use it."],["Break-glass account","glossary.html#break-glass-account","glossary","An emergency admin account for cases where normal admin access fails, for example after a Conditional Access mistake. It is excluded from most polici…"],["Brute force attack","glossary.html#brute-force-attack","glossary","Trying many passwords or keys against one account or target until one works."],["CIDR","glossary.html#cidr","glossary","Classless Inter-Domain Routing. Notation such as 192.168.1.0/24 that describes an IP range by network address and prefix length. CIDR calculator"],["Conditional Access","glossary.html#conditional-access","glossary","Entra ID feature that decides at sign-in whether to allow, block or require extra steps such as MFA, based on user, device, location and risk. Entra …"],["Credential stuffing","glossary.html#credential-stuffing","glossary","Logging in with username and password pairs leaked in other breaches, hoping people reused them."],["CVE","glossary.html#cve","glossary","Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures. A public identifier such as CVE-2024-12345 for a specific known vulnerability."],["CVSS","glossary.html#cvss","glossary","Common Vulnerability Scoring System. A score from 0 to 10 that rates the technical severity of a vulnerability."],["DKIM","glossary.html#dkim","glossary","DomainKeys Identified Mail. A cryptographic signature on outgoing email that lets receivers check the message came from the domain and was not altere…"],["DLP","glossary.html#dlp","glossary","Data loss prevention. Rules and tools that detect and block sensitive data, such as card numbers, from leaving the organization."],["DMARC","glossary.html#dmarc","glossary","Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting and Conformance. A DNS policy that tells receivers what to do with mail that fails SPF and DKIM alignm…"],["EDR","glossary.html#edr","glossary","Endpoint detection and response. Software on devices that records activity, detects suspicious behavior and helps respond, for example by isolating a…"],["Entra ID","glossary.html#entra-id","glossary","Microsoft's cloud identity and access service, previously called Azure AD. It handles sign-in, MFA, Conditional Access and app access for Microsoft 3…"],["Exploit","glossary.html#exploit","glossary","Code or a technique that takes advantage of a vulnerability."],["FIDO2","glossary.html#fido2","glossary","An open standard for passwordless and phishing-resistant sign-in with security keys or passkeys."],["FILETIME","glossary.html#filetime","glossary","Windows timestamp counting 100-nanosecond intervals since 1 January 1601 UTC. Active Directory uses it for attributes such as lastLogon. Time convert…"],["Golden ticket","glossary.html#golden-ticket","glossary","A Kerberos attack where the attacker forges ticket-granting tickets with the password hash of the krbtgt account, gaining long-lasting domain access."],["Group Policy","glossary.html#group-policy","glossary","Windows feature for centrally managing settings and security configuration of computers and users in an Active Directory domain."],["Hash","glossary.html#hash","glossary","A fixed-length value calculated from data by a one-way function. Used for integrity checks and for storing passwords. Hash generator"],["Intune","glossary.html#intune","glossary","Microsoft's cloud service for managing devices and apps, including compliance and configuration policies."],["JWT","glossary.html#jwt","glossary","JSON Web Token. A signed token made of a header, claims and a signature, widely used in OAuth and OpenID Connect. JWT decoder"],["Kerberoasting","glossary.html#kerberoasting","glossary","An attack where an authenticated user requests service tickets for accounts with service principal names and cracks them offline to recover the servi…"],["Kerberos","glossary.html#kerberos","glossary","Ticket-based authentication protocol used in Active Directory domains."],["KQL","glossary.html#kql","glossary","Kusto Query Language. The query language of Microsoft Sentinel, Log Analytics and Defender advanced hunting. KQL cheat sheet"],["LAPS","glossary.html#laps","glossary","Local Administrator Password Solution. Manages a unique, regularly changed local administrator password for each device. Windows LAPS is built into s…"],["Lateral movement","glossary.html#lateral-movement","glossary","Moving from one compromised system or account to others inside a network."],["Legacy authentication","glossary.html#legacy-authentication","glossary","Older protocols such as IMAP, POP and basic SMTP AUTH that do not support MFA. Blocking them closes a common attack path."],["Managed identity","glossary.html#managed-identity","glossary","Azure feature that gives a resource an identity managed by the platform, so apps can access other services without stored secrets."],["MFA","glossary.html#mfa","glossary","Multi-factor authentication. Signing in with more than one kind of proof, such as a password plus an app approval or a security key."],["MITRE ATT&CK","glossary.html#mitre-att-ck","glossary","A public knowledge base of attacker tactics and techniques, used to describe attacks and plan detections."],["NTLM","glossary.html#ntlm","glossary","Older Windows challenge-response authentication protocol, still present for compatibility and often targeted by attacks such as pass-the-hash."],["OAuth 2.0","glossary.html#oauth-2-0","glossary","Authorization framework that lets an app access resources on a user's behalf using tokens instead of passwords."],["OpenID Connect","glossary.html#openid-connect","glossary","Identity layer on top of OAuth 2.0 that lets apps verify who signed in."],["Pass-the-hash","glossary.html#pass-the-hash","glossary","Using a captured password hash to authenticate without knowing the password itself."],["Passkey","glossary.html#passkey","glossary","A passwordless credential based on public-key cryptography, bound to a device or synced by a platform, and resistant to phishing."],["Password spraying","glossary.html#password-spraying","glossary","Trying a few common passwords against many accounts to avoid lockouts. KQL query for spray detection"],["Penetration test","glossary.html#penetration-test","glossary","An authorized simulated attack used to find weaknesses before real attackers do."],["Phishing","glossary.html#phishing","glossary","Fraudulent messages that trick people into giving up credentials, running malware or approving requests. Email header analyzer"],["PIM","glossary.html#pim","glossary","Privileged Identity Management. Entra feature for just-in-time, time-limited and approved admin roles."],["Primary Refresh Token (PRT)","glossary.html#primary-refresh-token-prt","glossary","A token issued to Entra-joined or registered devices that enables single sign-on across apps. Stealing it is a known attacker goal."],["Principle of least privilege","glossary.html#principle-of-least-privilege","glossary","Give users, apps and systems only the access they need for their task and no more."],["Privilege escalation","glossary.html#privilege-escalation","glossary","Gaining higher permissions than originally granted, for example from a normal user to an administrator."],["Ransomware","glossary.html#ransomware","glossary","Malware that encrypts data and demands payment for its release, often combined with data theft."],["Red team and blue team","glossary.html#red-team-and-blue-team","glossary","The red team simulates attackers, the blue team defends and detects. Working together is sometimes called purple teaming."],["SAML","glossary.html#saml","glossary","Security Assertion Markup Language. XML-based standard for single sign-on between an identity provider and an app."],["Secure Score","glossary.html#secure-score","glossary","Microsoft's numeric rating of a tenant's security posture, with recommended improvement actions."],["Service principal","glossary.html#service-principal","glossary","The identity of an application in an Entra tenant, used to grant it permissions."],["SIEM","glossary.html#siem","glossary","Security information and event management. Collects and analyzes logs from many sources to detect threats. Microsoft Sentinel is an example."],["Smart lockout","glossary.html#smart-lockout","glossary","Entra ID feature that blocks sign-in attempts after repeated failures while trying to keep the real user able to sign in."],["Social engineering","glossary.html#social-engineering","glossary","Manipulating people, rather than systems, to gain access or information."],["SPF","glossary.html#spf","glossary","Sender Policy Framework. A DNS record listing the servers allowed to send mail for a domain."],["SSO","glossary.html#sso","glossary","Single sign-on. Signing in once to access multiple applications."],["Tenant","glossary.html#tenant","glossary","A dedicated instance of Entra ID and Microsoft 365 that belongs to one organization."],["Tier 0","glossary.html#tier-0","glossary","The most sensitive assets in the enterprise access model, such as domain controllers and identity systems. Compromising tier 0 means compromising eve…"],["Token theft","glossary.html#token-theft","glossary","Stealing an access, refresh or session token to impersonate a user without needing their password or MFA."],["TPM","glossary.html#tpm","glossary","Trusted Platform Module. A hardware chip that stores keys securely and supports features such as BitLocker."],["UPN","glossary.html#upn","glossary","User principal name. The sign-in name of a user in email-like form, such as name@contoso.com."],["Vulnerability","glossary.html#vulnerability","glossary","A weakness in software, configuration or process that can be abused."],["XDR","glossary.html#xdr","glossary","Extended detection and response. Correlates signals across endpoints, identities, email and cloud."],["Zero Trust","glossary.html#zero-trust","glossary","A security model built on never trusting by default: verify each request explicitly, use least privilege and assume breach."],["Zero-day","glossary.html#zero-day","glossary","A vulnerability that is exploited or public before a fix exists."],["AADSTS50011","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50011","error code","The redirect URI in the request does not match the ones registered for the app."],["AADSTS50013","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50013","error code","The assertion is invalid, for example because of a bad signature, wrong issuer or audience, or an expired token."],["AADSTS50020","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50020","error code","The signed-in account comes from an identity provider that has no matching user in this tenant."],["AADSTS50034","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50034","error code","The user account does not exist in the directory."],["AADSTS50053","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50053","error code","The account is locked after too many failed sign-in attempts (smart lockout) or the sign-in came from a blocked source."],["AADSTS50055","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50055","error code","The user's password has expired."],["AADSTS50057","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50057","error code","The user account is disabled."],["AADSTS50058","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50058","error code","A silent sign-in request found no signed-in user or not enough session information."],["AADSTS50072","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50072","error code","The user must enroll in multi-factor authentication before signing in."],["AADSTS50074","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50074","error code","Strong authentication (MFA) is required to continue."],["AADSTS50076","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50076","error code","MFA is required because of a policy or Conditional Access rule for this sign-in."],["AADSTS50079","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50079","error code","The user must register for MFA before signing in (security info registration required)."],["AADSTS50089","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50089","error code","The flow token expired, so authentication failed."],["AADSTS50097","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50097","error code","Device authentication is required for this sign-in."],["AADSTS50105","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50105","error code","The signed-in user is not assigned to a role for the application."],["AADSTS50126","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50126","error code","The username or password is invalid."],["AADSTS50132","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50132","error code","The session is no longer valid, for example after a password change or expiry."],["AADSTS50133","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50133","error code","The session is invalid because of expiration or a recent password change."],["AADSTS50140","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50140","error code","The user hit the Keep me signed in prompt during sign-in."],["AADSTS50144","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50144","error code","The user's on-premises Active Directory password has expired."],["AADSTS50158","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50158","error code","An external security challenge was not satisfied, for example from a federated or external MFA provider."],["AADSTS50173","aadsts-lookup.html?q=50173","error code","The provided grant is no longer valid, for example after a password change or a revoked session."],["AADSTS53000","aadsts-lookup.html?q=53000","error code","Access is blocked because the device is not in the required state, for example not compliant."],["AADSTS53001","aadsts-lookup.html?q=53001","error code","Access is blocked because the device is not domain joined as the policy requires."],["AADSTS53002","aadsts-lookup.html?q=53002","error code","The application is not an approved app for a policy that requires one."],["AADSTS53003","aadsts-lookup.html?q=53003","error code","Access was blocked by a Conditional Access policy."],["AADSTS65001","aadsts-lookup.html?q=65001","error code","The user or an admin has not consented to the app's requested permissions."],["AADSTS65004","aadsts-lookup.html?q=65004","error code","The user declined to consent to the requested permissions."],["AADSTS65005","aadsts-lookup.html?q=65005","error code","The app's required resource access list is invalid, for example it lists permissions of an app that does not exist or is not consented."],["AADSTS70008","aadsts-lookup.html?q=70008","error code","The authorization code or refresh token has expired due to inactivity."],["AADSTS70011","aadsts-lookup.html?q=70011","error code","The requested scope is invalid or not allowed."],["AADSTS70016","aadsts-lookup.html?q=70016","error code","Device code flow: authorization is still pending."],["AADSTS70019","aadsts-lookup.html?q=70019","error code","Device code flow: the verification code has expired."],["AADSTS70043","aadsts-lookup.html?q=70043","error code","The refresh token has expired or is invalid due to a sign-in frequency rule."],["AADSTS80012","aadsts-lookup.html?q=80012","error code","The user is signing in outside the allowed logon hours."],["AADSTS90002","aadsts-lookup.html?q=90002","error code","The tenant was not found. The tenant ID or domain in the authority URL is wrong."],["AADSTS90014","aadsts-lookup.html?q=90014","error code","A required field is missing from the request."],["AADSTS90094","aadsts-lookup.html?q=90094","error code","Admin consent is required for the requested permissions."],["AADSTS500011","aadsts-lookup.html?q=500011","error code","The resource the app asked for was not found in the tenant."],["AADSTS700003","aadsts-lookup.html?q=700003","error code","The device object is disabled or was deleted."],["AADSTS700016","aadsts-lookup.html?q=700016","error code","No application with this client ID was found in the directory."],["AADSTS700082","aadsts-lookup.html?q=700082","error code","The refresh token expired because it was not used for a long time."],["AADSTS7000215","aadsts-lookup.html?q=7000215","error code","The client secret is invalid. A common cause is using the secret ID instead of the secret value."],["AADSTS7000218","aadsts-lookup.html?q=7000218","error code","The request has no client secret or assertion, often because a public client calls a flow that needs a confidential client."],["AADSTS7000222","aadsts-lookup.html?q=7000222","error code","The client secret has expired."],["Event 4624 Successful logon","event-id-reference.html?q=4624","event id","Security. Check the logon type: 2 interactive, 3 network, 10 remote interactive"],["Event 4625 Failed logon","event-id-reference.html?q=4625","event id","Security. Many in a row can mean brute force or password spray"],["Event 4634 Account logged off","event-id-reference.html?q=4634","event id","Security. "],["Event 4647 User-initiated logoff","event-id-reference.html?q=4647","event id","Security. "],["Event 4648 Logon with explicit credentials","event-id-reference.html?q=4648","event id","Security. Seen with runas and in some lateral movement"],["Event 4672 Special privileges assigned to new logon","event-id-reference.html?q=4672","event id","Security. Admin-level logon"],["Event 4688 New process created","event-id-reference.html?q=4688","event id","Security. Command line is only logged if that audit setting is enabled"],["Event 4697 Service installed on the system","event-id-reference.html?q=4697","event id","Security. Security log version of 7045"],["Event 4698 Scheduled task created","event-id-reference.html?q=4698","event id","Security. Common persistence method"],["Event 4699 Scheduled task deleted","event-id-reference.html?q=4699","event id","Security. "],["Event 4702 Scheduled task updated","event-id-reference.html?q=4702","event id","Security. "],["Event 4719 System audit policy changed","event-id-reference.html?q=4719","event id","Security. Attackers may weaken auditing"],["Event 4720 User account created","event-id-reference.html?q=4720","event id","Security. "],["Event 4722 User account enabled","event-id-reference.html?q=4722","event id","Security. "],["Event 4723 Attempt to change an account password","event-id-reference.html?q=4723","event id","Security. User changing their own password"],["Event 4724 Attempt to reset an account password","event-id-reference.html?q=4724","event id","Security. Done by an administrator"],["Event 4725 User account disabled","event-id-reference.html?q=4725","event id","Security. "],["Event 4726 User account deleted","event-id-reference.html?q=4726","event id","Security. "],["Event 4728 Member added to a security-enabled global group","event-id-reference.html?q=4728","event id","Security. Watch privileged groups"],["Event 4732 Member added to a security-enabled local group","event-id-reference.html?q=4732","event id","Security. Watch the local Administrators group"],["Event 4738 User account changed","event-id-reference.html?q=4738","event id","Security. "],["Event 4740 User account locked out","event-id-reference.html?q=4740","event id","Security. Find the source in the caller computer name"],["Event 4756 Member added to a security-enabled universal group","event-id-reference.html?q=4756","event id","Security. "],["Event 4768 Kerberos TGT requested","event-id-reference.html?q=4768","event id","Security. Logged on domain controllers"],["Event 4769 Kerberos service ticket requested","event-id-reference.html?q=4769","event id","Security. Unusual encryption types can hint at Kerberoasting"],["Event 4771 Kerberos pre-authentication failed","event-id-reference.html?q=4771","event id","Security. Wrong password for a domain account"],["Event 4776 NTLM credential validation","event-id-reference.html?q=4776","event id","Security. Logged on domain controllers"],["Event 5140 Network share accessed","event-id-reference.html?q=5140","event id","Security. "],["Event 1102 Audit log cleared","event-id-reference.html?q=1102","event id","Security. Often suspicious; find out who did it"],["Event 4104 Script block logged","event-id-reference.html?q=4104","event id","PowerShell/Operational. Needs script block logging enabled"],["Event 7045 New service installed","event-id-reference.html?q=7045","event id","System. Look for unknown service paths"],["Event 1116 Malware detected","event-id-reference.html?q=1116","event id","Defender/Operational. "],["Event 1117 Action taken on malware","event-id-reference.html?q=1117","event id","Defender/Operational. "],["Event 41 Kernel-Power: unexpected restart","event-id-reference.html?q=41","event id","System. Crash or power loss"],["Event 6005 Event log service started","event-id-reference.html?q=6005","event id","System. Roughly marks system boot"],["Event 6006 Event log service stopped","event-id-reference.html?q=6006","event id","System. Roughly marks a clean shutdown"],["Event 1074 Shutdown or restart initiated","event-id-reference.html?q=1074","event id","System. Shows the process and the reason"],["Bounce 5.1.1","email-error-codes.html?q=5.1.1","bounce code","Recipient address does not exist or is invalid."],["Bounce 5.1.10","email-error-codes.html?q=5.1.10","bounce code","Recipient not found by SMTP address lookup (RESOLVER.ADR.RecipientNotFound)."],["Bounce 5.4.1","email-error-codes.html?q=5.4.1","bounce code","Recipient address rejected: access denied. Often directory-based edge blocking for a recipient that does not exist."],["Bounce 5.7.1","email-error-codes.html?q=5.7.1","bounce code","Delivery not authorized. The sender may not send to this recipient or group."],["Bounce 5.7.57","email-error-codes.html?q=5.7.57","bounce code","The client was not authenticated to send anonymous mail."],["Bounce 5.7.60","email-error-codes.html?q=5.7.60","bounce code","The client does not have permission to send as this sender."],["Bounce 5.7.64","email-error-codes.html?q=5.7.64","bounce code","Tenant attribution failed and relay access was denied."],["Bounce 5.7.139","email-error-codes.html?q=5.7.139","bounce code","Authentication unsuccessful, often because SMTP AUTH or basic authentication is disabled."],["Bounce 5.7.509","email-error-codes.html?q=5.7.509","bounce code","Access denied. The sending domain fails DMARC and its policy is reject."],["Bounce 5.7.708","email-error-codes.html?q=5.7.708","bounce code","Access denied. Traffic from this IP address is not accepted."],["Bounce 5.2.2","email-error-codes.html?q=5.2.2","bounce code","The recipient mailbox is full."],["Bounce 5.2.3","email-error-codes.html?q=5.2.3","bounce code","The message size exceeds the recipient's limit."],["Bounce 5.3.4","email-error-codes.html?q=5.3.4","bounce code","The message is too large for the system."],["Bounce 4.4.7","email-error-codes.html?q=4.4.7","bounce code","Message expired. Delivery kept failing with a temporary error until the retry time ran out."],["HTTP 100 Continue","http-status-codes.html?q=100","http status","The server received the request headers; the client can send the body."],["HTTP 101 Switching Protocols","http-status-codes.html?q=101","http status","The server agrees to switch protocols, for example to WebSocket."],["HTTP 200 OK","http-status-codes.html?q=200","http status","The request succeeded."],["HTTP 201 Created","http-status-codes.html?q=201","http status","A new resource was created."],["HTTP 202 Accepted","http-status-codes.html?q=202","http status","The request was accepted but is not finished yet."],["HTTP 204 No Content","http-status-codes.html?q=204","http status","Success with no response body."],["HTTP 206 Partial Content","http-status-codes.html?q=206","http status","Only the requested byte range is returned."],["HTTP 301 Moved Permanently","http-status-codes.html?q=301","http status","The resource has a new permanent URL. Search engines follow it."],["HTTP 302 Found","http-status-codes.html?q=302","http status","Temporary redirect. The method may change to GET."],["HTTP 303 See Other","http-status-codes.html?q=303","http status","Redirect to another URL with GET, often after a POST."],["HTTP 304 Not Modified","http-status-codes.html?q=304","http status","The cached copy is still valid."],["HTTP 307 Temporary Redirect","http-status-codes.html?q=307","http status","Temporary redirect that keeps the request method."],["HTTP 308 Permanent Redirect","http-status-codes.html?q=308","http status","Permanent redirect that keeps the request method."],["HTTP 400 Bad Request","http-status-codes.html?q=400","http status","The server cannot understand the request, for example malformed syntax."],["HTTP 401 Unauthorized","http-status-codes.html?q=401","http status","Authentication is missing or invalid. Check credentials or the token."],["HTTP 403 Forbidden","http-status-codes.html?q=403","http status","The server understood the request but refuses it. The user lacks permission, or an IP or policy rule blocks it."],["HTTP 404 Not Found","http-status-codes.html?q=404","http status","The resource does not exist at this URL, or the server hides it."],["HTTP 405 Method Not Allowed","http-status-codes.html?q=405","http status","The HTTP method is not allowed for this resource. Check the Allow header."],["HTTP 406 Not Acceptable","http-status-codes.html?q=406","http status","The server cannot produce a response matching the Accept headers."],["HTTP 408 Request Timeout","http-status-codes.html?q=408","http status","The server timed out waiting for the request."],["HTTP 409 Conflict","http-status-codes.html?q=409","http status","The request conflicts with the current state of the resource, for example an edit conflict."],["HTTP 410 Gone","http-status-codes.html?q=410","http status","The resource was removed on purpose and will not return."],["HTTP 413 Content Too Large","http-status-codes.html?q=413","http status","The request body exceeds the server limit. Check upload size limits on the server and proxy."],["HTTP 414 URI Too Long","http-status-codes.html?q=414","http status","The URL is longer than the server accepts."],["HTTP 415 Unsupported Media Type","http-status-codes.html?q=415","http status","The server does not accept the content type of the request."],["HTTP 421 Misdirected Request","http-status-codes.html?q=421","http status","The request was sent to a server that cannot answer for this host, common with TLS and virtual hosts."],["HTTP 422 Unprocessable Content","http-status-codes.html?q=422","http status","The syntax is valid but the content fails validation."],["HTTP 429 Too Many Requests","http-status-codes.html?q=429","http status","Rate limit reached. Check the Retry-After header and slow down."],["HTTP 431 Request Header Fields Too Large","http-status-codes.html?q=431","http status","Headers or cookies are too big."],["HTTP 451 Unavailable For Legal Reasons","http-status-codes.html?q=451","http status","Access is blocked for legal reasons."],["HTTP 500 Internal Server Error","http-status-codes.html?q=500","http status","An unexpected error on the server. Check the application and server logs."],["HTTP 501 Not Implemented","http-status-codes.html?q=501","http status","The server does not support the requested method or feature."],["HTTP 502 Bad Gateway","http-status-codes.html?q=502","http status","A proxy or gateway got an invalid response from the upstream server. Check the backend service and the proxy configuration."],["HTTP 503 Service Unavailable","http-status-codes.html?q=503","http status","The server is overloaded or down for maintenance. It may include a Retry-After header."],["HTTP 504 Gateway Timeout","http-status-codes.html?q=504","http status","A proxy or gateway did not get a response from the upstream server in time."],["HTTP 505 HTTP Version Not Supported","http-status-codes.html?q=505","http status","The server does not support the HTTP version of the request."],["HTTP 511 Network Authentication Required","http-status-codes.html?q=511","http status","The client must authenticate to get network access, typical for captive portals."],["MD5","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=MD5","crypto","broken. Collisions are practical. Not for security use; acceptable only for non-security checksums."],["SHA-1","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=SHA-1","crypto","legacy. Collisions have been demonstrated. Avoid for signatures and new designs."],["SHA-256, SHA-384, SHA-512","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=SHA-256","crypto","recommended. General purpose hashing and integrity checks."],["SHA-3","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=SHA-3","crypto","recommended. Different construction than SHA-2. A good alternative."],["Argon2id","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=Argon2id","crypto","recommended. Modern choice for storing passwords. Memory-hard."],["scrypt","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=scrypt","crypto","acceptable. Memory-hard, widely available."],["bcrypt","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=bcrypt","crypto","acceptable. Adaptive and proven. Only the first 72 bytes of input count."],["PBKDF2","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=PBKDF2","crypto","acceptable. Use with a high iteration count. Widely supported."],["AES-256-GCM, AES-128-GCM","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=AES-256-GCM","crypto","recommended. Authenticated encryption. Never reuse a nonce with the same key."],["ChaCha20-Poly1305","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=ChaCha20-Poly1305","crypto","recommended. Authenticated and fast on devices without AES hardware."],["AES-CBC","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=AES-CBC","crypto","legacy. Needs a separate MAC and is prone to padding oracle mistakes."],["AES-ECB","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=AES-ECB","crypto","broken. Leaks patterns in the data. Never use."],["3DES","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=3DES","crypto","legacy. Small block size. Being phased out."],["DES","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=DES","crypto","broken. 56-bit key can be brute forced."],["RC4","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=RC4","crypto","broken. Biased output. Prohibited in TLS."],["RSA 2048","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=RSA%202048","crypto","acceptable. Common minimum today. Use 3072 bits or more for longer protection."],["RSA 1024","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=RSA%201024","crypto","broken. Too short."],["ECDSA, ECDH (P-256)","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=ECDSA","crypto","recommended. Widely used in TLS and certificates."],["Ed25519, X25519","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=Ed25519","crypto","recommended. Modern curves, fast and simple to use safely."],["Diffie-Hellman 1024-bit","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=Diffie-Hellman%201024-bit","crypto","broken. Too weak. Use larger groups or elliptic curves."],["TLS 1.3","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=TLS%201.3","crypto","recommended. Current version with a simpler and safer design."],["TLS 1.2","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=TLS%201.2","crypto","acceptable. Fine with strong cipher suites: AEAD and forward secrecy."],["TLS 1.1, TLS 1.0","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=TLS%201.1","crypto","legacy. Deprecated. Disable where possible."],["SSL 3.0","crypto-quick-reference.html?q=SSL%203.0","crypto","broken. Vulnerable to POODLE. Must be disabled."],["Kerberos and Kerberoasting explained","kerberos-explained.html","page","Interactive step-by-step diagrams of how Kerberos authentication works and how the Kerberoasting attack abuses it, with defenses."],["OAuth 2.0 authorization code flow explained","oauth-flow-explained.html","page","Interactive diagram of the OAuth 2.0 authorization code flow with PKCE and OpenID Connect in Microsoft Entra ID."],["AiTM phishing explained","aitm-phishing-explained.html","page","Interactive diagram of an adversary-in-the-middle phishing attack that steals session cookies and bypasses MFA, and how to defend."],["How Conditional Access works","conditional-access-explained.html","page","Interactive diagram of the Conditional Access decision process in Microsoft Entra ID with risk, device compliance and policy evaluation."],["Conditional Access simulator","conditional-access-simulator.html","page","What-if simulator: choose user, device, location and risk and toggle policies"],["Security self-check","security-self-check.html","page","21-question Microsoft 365 and Entra ID security self-assessment with score"],["OpenSSL cheat sheet","openssl-cheat-sheet.html","page","OpenSSL commands for certificates: inspect, CSR, self-signed, PFX and PEM conversion, chain checks and TLS tests."],["SSH cheat sheet","ssh-cheat-sheet.html","page","SSH commands and config: keys, port forwarding, jump hosts, scp and rsync, debugging and sshd hardening."],["Windows troubleshooting cheat sheet","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html","page","Windows admin commands: sfc, DISM, gpresult, services, processes, network checks, robocopy and event log export."],["Phish or legit?","phish-or-legit.html","page","Interactive game: ten messages, phishing or legit, with the red flags explained"],["Show certificate details","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Show%20certificate%20details","snippet: OpenSSL","Subject, issuer, validity, extensions. openssl x509 -in cert.pem -text -noout"],["Check expiry dates","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20expiry%20dates","snippet: OpenSSL","Start and end date of a certificate file. openssl x509 -in cert.pem -noout -dates"],["SHA-256 fingerprint","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=SHA-256%20fingerprint","snippet: OpenSSL","Compare with the fingerprint shown in a browser or by the CA. openssl x509 -in cert.pem -noout -fingerprint -sha256"],["Certificate of a remote server","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Certificate%20of%20a%20remote%20server","snippet: OpenSSL","Subject, issuer, dates and alternative names of what a server presents. openssl s_client -connect example.com:443 -servername example.com </dev/null 2>/dev/null"],["Show the full certificate chain","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Show%20the%20full%20certificate%20chain","snippet: OpenSSL","Prints every certificate the server sends. openssl s_client -connect example.com:443 -servername example.com -showcerts </dev/null"],["Test a specific TLS version","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Test%20a%20specific%20TLS%20version","snippet: OpenSSL","Use -tls1_3 to test TLS 1.3. A handshake failure means the version is not offered. openssl s_client -connect example.com:443 -tls1_2 </dev/null"],["Create a private key and CSR","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20private%20key%20and%20CSR","snippet: OpenSSL","RSA 2048 key without a passphrase, plus a certificate signing request. openssl req -new -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes -keyout server.key -out server.csr"],["CSR with alternative names","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=CSR%20with%20alternative%20names","snippet: OpenSSL","Modern browsers need the names in subjectAltName. Needs OpenSSL 1.1.1 or newer. openssl req -new -key server.key -out server.csr -subj \"/CN=example.com\" -addext"],["Inspect a CSR","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Inspect%20a%20CSR","snippet: OpenSSL","Check the subject and names before sending it to a CA. openssl req -in server.csr -noout -text"],["Self-signed certificate for testing","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Self-signed%20certificate%20for%20testing","snippet: OpenSSL","Valid for one year. Not for production use. openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes -keyout key.pem -out cert.pem -days 365 -subj \"/CN=localhost\""],["Check that key and certificate match","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20that%20key%20and%20certificate%20match","snippet: OpenSSL","For RSA. Both commands must print the same hash. openssl x509 -noout -modulus -in cert.pem | openssl sha256 openssl rsa -noout -modulus -in key.pem | openssl sh"],["Verify a certificate against a chain","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Verify%20a%20certificate%20against%20a%20chain","snippet: OpenSSL","Checks the certificate against a CA bundle. openssl verify -CAfile chain.pem cert.pem"],["PEM to PFX","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=PEM%20to%20PFX","snippet: OpenSSL","Bundle key, certificate and chain for Windows or IIS. openssl pkcs12 -export -out cert.pfx -inkey key.pem -in cert.pem -certfile chain.pem"],["PFX to PEM","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=PFX%20to%20PEM","snippet: OpenSSL","Extracts everything. The private key ends up unencrypted, so protect the file. openssl pkcs12 -in cert.pfx -nodes -out all.pem"],["DER to PEM","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=DER%20to%20PEM","snippet: OpenSSL","Convert a .cer or .der file to PEM text. openssl x509 -inform der -in cert.cer -out cert.pem"],["Random secret","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Random%20secret","snippet: OpenSSL","Base64 or hex random bytes, for example for a token or a key. openssl rand -base64 32 openssl rand -hex 32"],["Hash a file","openssl-cheat-sheet.html?q=Hash%20a%20file","snippet: OpenSSL","Compute a SHA-256 digest of a file. openssl dgst -sha256 file"],["Create an Ed25519 key","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20an%20Ed25519%20key","snippet: SSH","Modern default key type. ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C \"you@example.com\""],["Copy your key to a server","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Copy%20your%20key%20to%20a%20server","snippet: SSH","Adds the public key to authorized_keys. ssh-copy-id user@host"],["Connect with a key and a port","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect%20with%20a%20key%20and%20a%20port","snippet: SSH","Use a specific identity file and a non-standard port. ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 -p 2222 user@host"],["Local port forward","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Local%20port%20forward","snippet: SSH","Opens local port 8080 that reaches port 80 on the remote side. ssh -L 8080:localhost:80 user@host"],["Remote port forward","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Remote%20port%20forward","snippet: SSH","Makes local port 3000 reachable on the server as port 9000. ssh -R 9000:localhost:3000 user@host"],["SOCKS proxy","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=SOCKS%20proxy","snippet: SSH","Routes browser traffic through the server via a local SOCKS proxy on port 1080. ssh -D 1080 user@host"],["Jump through a bastion host","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Jump%20through%20a%20bastion%20host","snippet: SSH","Reach an internal machine via a jump host. ssh -J jumpuser@jumphost user@internal"],["Client config entry","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Client%20config%20entry","snippet: SSH","Goes into ~/.ssh/config. Afterwards, ssh web is enough. Host web   HostName 203.0.113.10   User admin   IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519   Port 2222"],["Copy files with scp","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Copy%20files%20with%20scp","snippet: SSH","Copy a local file to a server. scp file.txt user@host:/tmp/"],["Sync a folder with rsync","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Sync%20a%20folder%20with%20rsync","snippet: SSH","Archive mode with compression and progress. rsync -avz --progress ./dir/ user@host:/backup/dir/"],["Run one remote command","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20one%20remote%20command","snippet: SSH","Runs the command and returns. ssh user@host \"uptime\""],["Show a key fingerprint","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Show%20a%20key%20fingerprint","snippet: SSH","Fingerprint of a public key file. ssh-keygen -lf ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub"],["Remove an old host key","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Remove%20an%20old%20host%20key","snippet: SSH","After a server was rebuilt and the host key changed. ssh-keygen -R hostname"],["Load a key into the agent","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Load%20a%20key%20into%20the%20agent","snippet: SSH","Enter the passphrase once per session. eval \"$(ssh-agent -s)\" ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519"],["Debug a connection","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Debug%20a%20connection","snippet: SSH","Verbose output. Repeat -v for more detail. ssh -vvv user@host"],["Hardening lines for sshd_config","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Hardening%20lines%20for%20sshd_config","snippet: SSH","Key-only login and no root login. Test the config, then reload the service. PasswordAuthentication no PermitRootLogin no PubkeyAuthentication yes"],["Test the sshd configuration","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Test%20the%20sshd%20configuration","snippet: SSH","Checks the syntax before you reload. sudo sshd -t"],["Fetch a server's host key","ssh-cheat-sheet.html?q=Fetch%20a%20server%27s%20host%20key","snippet: SSH","Useful for known_hosts or to compare fingerprints. ssh-keyscan -t ed25519 host"],["Check and repair system files","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20and%20repair%20system%20files","snippet: Windows","Run in an elevated prompt. sfc /scannow"],["Repair the component store","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Repair%20the%20component%20store","snippet: Windows","Use when sfc reports problems it cannot fix. DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth"],["Refresh Group Policy","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Refresh%20Group%20Policy","snippet: Windows","Re-applies computer and user policies. gpupdate /force"],["Applied policies report","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Applied%20policies%20report","snippet: Windows","HTML report of the policies that apply to this computer and user. gpresult /h C:\\Temp\\gpresult.html /f"],["Groups and privileges of the current user","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Groups%20and%20privileges%20of%20the%20current%20user","snippet: Windows","Check what a token really contains. whoami /groups whoami /priv"],["Who is logged on","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Who%20is%20logged%20on","snippet: Windows","Sessions on the local machine or a terminal server. query user"],["Local users","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Local%20users","snippet: Windows","Enabled state and last logon. Get-LocalUser | Select-Object Name,Enabled,LastLogon"],["Windows version and build","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20version%20and%20build","snippet: Windows","Product name, version and build number. Get-ComputerInfo | Select-Object WindowsProductName,WindowsVersion,OsBuildNumber"],["Latest installed updates","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Latest%20installed%20updates","snippet: Windows","The ten most recent hotfixes. Get-HotFix | Sort-Object InstalledOn -Descending | Select-Object -First 10"],["Uptime","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Uptime","snippet: Windows","Time since the last boot. (Get-Date) - (Get-CimInstance Win32_OperatingSystem).LastBootUpTime"],["Automatic services that are not running","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Automatic%20services%20that%20are%20not%20running","snippet: Windows","Often the first hint when something is broken after a reboot. Get-Service | Where-Object { $_.StartType -eq \"Automatic\" -and $_.Status -ne \"Running\" }"],["Top CPU processes","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Top%20CPU%20processes","snippet: Windows","Ten processes with the most CPU time. Get-Process | Sort-Object CPU -Descending | Select-Object -First 10 Name,Id,CPU"],["Free disk space","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Free%20disk%20space","snippet: Windows","Used and free bytes per drive. Get-PSDrive -PSProvider FileSystem | Select-Object Name,Used,Free"],["Network configuration","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Network%20configuration","snippet: Windows","IP addresses, gateway and DNS per adapter. Get-NetIPConfiguration"],["Resolve a DNS record","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Resolve%20a%20DNS%20record","snippet: Windows","Query a specific record type. Resolve-DnsName example.com -Type MX"],["Enabled scheduled tasks","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Enabled%20scheduled%20tasks","snippet: Windows","Everything that is not disabled. Get-ScheduledTask | Where-Object { $_.State -ne \"Disabled\" } | Select-Object TaskName,TaskPath,State"],["Mirror a folder with robocopy","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Mirror%20a%20folder%20with%20robocopy","snippet: Windows","Careful: /MIR deletes files in the destination that are not in the source. robocopy C:\\Source D:\\Backup /MIR /R:2 /W:5 /LOG:C:\\Temp\\robocopy.log"],["Reset the network stack","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Reset%20the%20network%20stack","snippet: Windows","Needs a restart afterwards. netsh winsock reset netsh int ip reset"],["Export an event log","windows-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet.html?q=Export%20an%20event%20log","snippet: Windows","Saves the Security log to an .evtx file. wevtutil epl Security C:\\Temp\\security.evtx"],["Security news","news.html","page","Latest security headlines from public feeds, updated automatically"],["Known exploited vulnerabilities","cve.html","page","Recent CISA KEV entries: CVEs that attackers exploit now"],["Admin links","admin-links.html","page","Portals, diagnostics, CVE sources, TLS and DNS checkers"],["Microsoft 365 admin center","https://admin.microsoft.com","link","Users, licenses, domains and service health."],["Microsoft Entra admin center","https://entra.microsoft.com","link","Identity, Conditional Access, sign-in logs and app registrations."],["Intune admin center","https://intune.microsoft.com","link","Device management, compliance and app deployment."],["Microsoft Defender portal","https://security.microsoft.com","link","Incidents, advanced hunting, Defender for Endpoint and Office 365."],["Microsoft Purview portal","https://purview.microsoft.com","link","Audit log, data loss prevention, retention and eDiscovery."],["Exchange admin center","https://admin.exchange.microsoft.com","link","Mailboxes, mail flow and message trace."],["Teams admin center","https://admin.teams.microsoft.com","link","Teams policies, voice and meeting settings."],["Azure portal","https://portal.azure.com","link","Azure resources, subscriptions and role assignments."],["Power Platform admin center","https://admin.powerplatform.microsoft.com","link","Environments and data policies for Power Apps and Power Automate."],["My Sign-Ins","https://mysignins.microsoft.com","link","Where users manage security info and review sign-in activity."],["My Apps","https://myapps.microsoft.com","link","Apps assigned to a user."],["Microsoft Graph Explorer","https://developer.microsoft.com/graph/graph-explorer","link","Try Microsoft Graph API calls in the browser."],["Remote Connectivity Analyzer","https://testconnectivity.microsoft.com","link","Test Exchange, Outlook and Microsoft 365 connectivity and mail flow."],["Message Header Analyzer","https://mha.azurewebsites.net","link","Microsoft's tool for reading email headers."],["MSRC Update Guide","https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide","link","Security updates and CVEs for Microsoft products."],["License and service plan reference","https://learn.microsoft.com/entra/identity/users/licensing-service-plan-reference","link","Official list of SKU names, GUIDs and service plans."],["Microsoft Learn","https://learn.microsoft.com","link","Official documentation and training."],["Microsoft 365 roadmap","https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap","link","Upcoming and rolling-out features."],["Sysinternals","https://learn.microsoft.com/sysinternals/","link","Process Explorer, Autoruns and other troubleshooting tools."],["CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities","https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog","link","Vulnerabilities that are exploited in the wild."],["National Vulnerability Database","https://nvd.nist.gov","link","Details and scores for CVEs."],["CVE program","https://www.cve.org","link","The CVE identifier system."],["MITRE ATT&CK","https://attack.mitre.org","link","Attacker tactics and techniques."],["Have I Been Pwned","https://haveibeenpwned.com","link","Check accounts and domains against known breaches."],["VirusTotal","https://www.virustotal.com","link","Scan files, URLs and hashes."],["CIS Benchmarks","https://www.cisecurity.org/cis-benchmarks","link","Hardening guides for operating systems and services."],["OWASP Top 10","https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/","link","The most common web application risks."],["SSL Labs Server Test","https://www.ssllabs.com/ssltest/","link","Grades the TLS configuration of a public server."],["Security Headers","https://securityheaders.com","link","Checks HTTP security headers of a site."],["MXToolbox","https://mxtoolbox.com","link","DNS, mail and blocklist lookups."],["crt.sh","https://crt.sh","link","Search certificate transparency logs."],["CyberChef","https://gchq.github.io/CyberChef/","link","Encode, decode and analyze data in the browser."],["regex101","https://regex101.com","link","Build and test regular expressions."],["crontab guru","https://crontab.guru","link","Explains cron expressions."],["ExplainShell","https://explainshell.com","link","Explains what a shell command does."],["Wireshark","https://www.wireshark.org","link","Network protocol analyzer."],["Entra ID roles reference","entra-id-roles-reference.html","page","What common Entra ID directory roles can do"],["Exchange Online PowerShell deep dive","exchange-online-deep-dive.html","page","Mailbox delegation, mail flow rules, tracing, audit"],["Server hardening checklist","server-hardening-checklist.html","page","Windows/Linux server hardening: OS, accounts, logging, network, backup"],["New site onboarding checklist","site-onboarding-checklist.html","page","Bringing a new office online: network, devices, identity, users"],["Global Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Global+Administrator","entra role","Full access to all administrative features in Entra ID and services that federate to it. Break-glass and a small number of named admins only. Assign t"],["Privileged Role Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Privileged+Role+Administrator","entra role","Manages role assignments in Entra ID and within Privileged Identity Management. As powerful as Global Administrator in practice, since it can grant it"],["User Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=User+Administrator","entra role","Creates and manages users and groups, resets non-admin passwords. Cannot reset passwords for administrators."],["Helpdesk Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Helpdesk+Administrator","entra role","Resets passwords for non-administrators and limited admin roles. A safer choice than User Administrator for a support desk."],["Password Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Password+Administrator","entra role","Resets passwords for non-administrator users only. Narrower than Helpdesk Administrator."],["Authentication Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Authentication+Administrator","entra role","Sets or resets authentication methods for non-privileged users, can require re-registration of MFA. Privileged Authentication Administrator is needed "],["Privileged Authentication Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Privileged+Authentication+Administrator","entra role","Sets or resets authentication methods for any user, including other administrators. High impact: can effectively take over any account's sign-in metho"],["Conditional Access Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Conditional+Access+Administrator","entra role","Creates and manages Conditional Access policies. Can lock out the whole tenant with a bad policy; test with report-only first."],["Security Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Security+Administrator","entra role","Reads security information and manages security features across Microsoft 365 and Entra ID. Broad read and configure access to security tooling, not t"],["Security Reader","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Security+Reader","entra role","Read-only access to security information and reports. Good default for SOC analysts who should not change configuration."],["Application Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Application+Administrator","entra role","Creates and manages all aspects of app registrations and enterprise apps. Can add credentials to any app, which can be a path to broad access."],["Cloud Application Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Cloud+Application+Administrator","entra role","Same as Application Administrator except it cannot manage app proxy. Slightly narrower than Application Administrator."],["Exchange Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Exchange+Administrator","entra role","Manages Exchange Online, including mail flow and mailbox settings. Scope is Exchange Online only."],["SharePoint Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=SharePoint+Administrator","entra role","Manages SharePoint Online and OneDrive settings. Scope is SharePoint and OneDrive only."],["Teams Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Teams+Administrator","entra role","Manages the Microsoft Teams service, policies and configuration. Scope is Teams only."],["Intune Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Intune+Administrator","entra role","Manages devices, compliance and configuration policies in Intune. Broad control over managed devices."],["Compliance Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Compliance+Administrator","entra role","Manages compliance features: retention, DLP, insider risk and eDiscovery configuration. Compliance Data Administrator has narrower, data-focused acces"],["Reports Reader","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Reports+Reader","entra role","Reads sign-in and usage reports across Microsoft 365. Read-only, no configuration access."],["Global Reader","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Global+Reader","entra role","Read-only access to the same information a Global Administrator can see. Useful for auditors without granting any change rights."],["Groups Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Groups+Administrator","entra role","Creates and manages groups and group settings, including dynamic membership rules. Can affect access indirectly through group-based licensing and role"],["Billing Administrator","entra-id-roles-reference.html?q=Billing+Administrator","entra role","Manages subscriptions, licenses and support tickets. No access to security or identity settings."],["Connect with a specific certificate","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Connect+with+a+specific+certificate","snippet: Exchange deep dive","For unattended/app-only automation instead of interactive sign-in. Connect-ExchangeOnline -CertificateThumbprint $thumbprint -AppId $appId -Organization contoso"],["Create a shared mailbox","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Create+a+shared+mailbox","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Also used when converting a former employee's mailbox. New-Mailbox -Shared -Name \"Helpdesk\" -DisplayName \"Helpdesk\" -Alias helpdesk"],["Convert a user mailbox to shared","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Convert+a+user+mailbox+to+shared","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Do this before removing the license, so mail is not lost. Set-Mailbox -Identity user@contoso.com -Type Shared"],["Grant full access and auto-mapping","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Grant+full+access+and+auto-mapping","snippet: Exchange deep dive","The delegate sees the mailbox appear automatically in Outlook. Add-MailboxPermission -Identity shared@contoso.com -User user@contoso.com -AccessRights FullAcces"],["Grant Send As","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Grant+Send+As","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Lets the delegate send mail that appears to come from the mailbox. Add-RecipientPermission -Identity shared@contoso.com -Trustee user@contoso.com -AccessRights "],["Grant Send on Behalf","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Grant+Send+on+Behalf","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Recipients see 'on behalf of' in the From field. Set-Mailbox -Identity shared@contoso.com -GrantSendOnBehalfTo user@contoso.com"],["Set an out-of-office message","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Set+an+out-of-office+message","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Enable automatic replies for internal and external senders. Set-MailboxAutoReplyConfiguration -Identity user@contoso.com -AutoReplyState Enabled -InternalMessag"],["Set mailbox storage quotas","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Set+mailbox+storage+quotas","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Values are in the format like 49GB or 50GB. Set-Mailbox -Identity user@contoso.com -IssueWarningQuota 45GB -ProhibitSendQuota 49GB -ProhibitSendReceiveQuota 50G"],["Create a mail flow rule (transport rule)","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Create+a+mail+flow+rule+(transport+rule)","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Example: add a disclaimer footer to outbound mail. New-TransportRule -Name \"External footer\" -FromScope InOrganization -SentToScope NotInOrganization -ApplyHtml"],["Block auto-forwarding to external domains","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Block+auto-forwarding+to+external+domains","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Common step after a compromised mailbox investigation. New-TransportRule -Name \"Block external auto-forward\" -FromScope InOrganization -SentToScope NotInOrganiz"],["List all mail flow rules","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=List+all+mail+flow+rules","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Overview sorted by priority. Get-TransportRule | Sort-Object Priority | Select-Object Name,State,Priority"],["Trace a message","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Trace+a+message","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Find out where a message went and why. Get-MessageTrace -SenderAddress user@contoso.com -StartDate (Get-Date).AddDays(-2) -EndDate (Get-Date)"],["Detailed trace for one message","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Detailed+trace+for+one+message","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Needs a message ID from Get-MessageTrace. Get-MessageTraceDetail -MessageTraceId $traceId -RecipientAddress recipient@contoso.com"],["Search and delete a phishing mail tenant-wide","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Search+and+delete+a+phishing+mail+tenant-wide","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Search first without -DeleteContent to confirm scope, then rerun with it. New-ComplianceSearch -Name \"Phish cleanup\" -ExchangeLocation All -ContentMatchQuery 's"],["Mailbox audit log search","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Mailbox+audit+log+search","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Find mailbox actions like access, sends and deletes. Search-MailboxAuditLog -Identity user@contoso.com -LogonTypes Delegate,Admin -StartDate (Get-Date).AddDays("],["List accepted domains","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=List+accepted+domains","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Domains this tenant can receive mail for. Get-AcceptedDomain | Select-Object DomainName,DomainType,Default"],["List connectors","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=List+connectors","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Inbound and outbound connectors, often used for on-premises relay or third-party filtering. Get-InboundConnector | Select-Object Name,Enabled,SenderIPAddresses "],["Distribution group membership","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Distribution+group+membership","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Members of a distribution or mail-enabled security group. Get-DistributionGroupMember -Identity \"All Staff\" | Select-Object DisplayName,PrimarySmtpAddress"],["Check the anti-spam policy","exchange-online-deep-dive.html?q=Check+the+anti-spam+policy","snippet: Exchange deep dive","Confirms which spam filter policy applies and its action for high-confidence spam. Get-HostedContentFilterPolicy | Select-Object Name,HighConfidenceSpamAction,B"],["SharePoint and Teams PowerShell cheat sheet","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html","page","PnP PowerShell and Teams PowerShell commands"],["Group Policy cheat sheet","group-policy-cheat-sheet.html","page","List, report, back up GPOs, find links, force replication"],["Wi-Fi and network troubleshooting cheat sheet","wifi-network-cheat-sheet.html","page","Windows Wi-Fi status, profiles, connectivity tests"],["Connect to SharePoint Online","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect%20to%20SharePoint%20Online","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Uses the PnP PowerShell module. Install-Module PnP.PowerShell -Scope CurrentUser Connect-PnPOnline -Url https://contoso.sharepoint.com -Interactive"],["List all site collections","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20all%20site%20collections","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Overview of every site in the tenant. Get-PnPTenantSite | Select-Object Url,Owner,StorageUsageCurrent,Template"],["Site storage usage, largest first","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=Site%20storage%20usage%2C%20largest%20first","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Find sites approaching their quota. Get-PnPTenantSite | Sort-Object StorageUsageCurrent -Descending | Select-Object -First 20 Url,StorageUsageCurrent,StorageQuo"],["List external (guest) users on a site","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20external%20%28guest%29%20users%20on%20a%20site","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Find who outside the tenant has access. Get-PnPUser -Web https://contoso.sharepoint.com/sites/finance | Where-Object { $_.LoginName -like \"*#ext#*\" }"],["Site sharing settings","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=Site%20sharing%20settings","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Whether a site allows external sharing. Get-PnPTenantSite -Identity https://contoso.sharepoint.com/sites/finance | Select-Object Url,SharingCapability"],["List document libraries on a site","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20document%20libraries%20on%20a%20site","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Lists and their item counts. Get-PnPList | Where-Object { $_.BaseTemplate -eq 101 } | Select-Object Title,ItemCount"],["Check versioning settings on a library","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20versioning%20settings%20on%20a%20library","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Whether version history is on and how many versions are kept. Get-PnPList -Identity \"Documents\" | Select-Object Title,EnableVersioning,MajorVersionLimit"],["Restore a deleted site from the recycle bin","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=Restore%20a%20deleted%20site%20from%20the%20recycle%20bin","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Within the retention window, usually 93 days. Restore-PnPTenantRecycleBinItem -Identity https://contoso.sharepoint.com/sites/finance"],["Connect to Teams PowerShell","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect%20to%20Teams%20PowerShell","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Separate module from SharePoint and Exchange. Install-Module MicrosoftTeams -Scope CurrentUser Connect-MicrosoftTeams"],["List all teams","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20all%20teams","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Display name, visibility and archived state. Get-Team | Select-Object DisplayName,Visibility,Archived"],["List members and owners of a team","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20members%20and%20owners%20of%20a%20team","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Needs the team's group ID from Get-Team. Get-TeamUser -GroupId $groupId | Select-Object User,Role"],["Create a team from an existing group","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20team%20from%20an%20existing%20group","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Turns a Microsoft 365 group into a team. New-Team -GroupId $groupId"],["Archive a team","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=Archive%20a%20team","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Makes it read-only. Content stays available. Set-TeamArchivedState -GroupId $groupId -Archived $true"],["List Teams meeting policies","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20Teams%20meeting%20policies","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","See what each policy allows, for example recording or transcription. Get-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy | Select-Object Identity,AllowCloudRecording,AllowTranscription"],["Assign a policy to a user","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=Assign%20a%20policy%20to%20a%20user","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Apply a specific meeting or messaging policy. Grant-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy -Identity user@contoso.com -PolicyName \"Restricted\""],["List external access settings","sharepoint-teams-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20external%20access%20settings","snippet: SharePoint/Teams","Whether users can chat with people in other Microsoft 365 tenants. Get-CsTenantFederationConfiguration | Select-Object AllowFederatedUsers,AllowedDomains"],["List all GPOs in the domain","group-policy-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20all%20GPOs%20in%20the%20domain","snippet: Group Policy","Names and links, requires the GroupPolicy module (RSAT). Get-GPO -All | Select-Object DisplayName,GpoStatus,ModificationTime"],["Generate an HTML report for one GPO","group-policy-cheat-sheet.html?q=Generate%20an%20HTML%20report%20for%20one%20GPO","snippet: Group Policy","Full settings report for a single policy. Get-GPOReport -Name \"Default Domain Policy\" -ReportType Html -Path C:\\Temp\\gpo-report.html"],["Find which OU a GPO is linked to","group-policy-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20which%20OU%20a%20GPO%20is%20linked%20to","snippet: Group Policy","Search all OUs for links to a specific policy. Get-ADOrganizationalUnit -Filter * | Get-GPInheritance | Where-Object { $_.GpoLinks.DisplayName -contains \"Passwo"],["Backup all GPOs","group-policy-cheat-sheet.html?q=Backup%20all%20GPOs","snippet: Group Policy","Creates a backup folder you can restore from later. Backup-GPO -All -Path C:\\Temp\\GPO-Backup"],["Find GPOs with no links (orphaned)","group-policy-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20GPOs%20with%20no%20links%20%28orphaned%29","snippet: Group Policy","Candidates for cleanup after a review. Get-GPO -All | Where-Object { (Get-GPOReport -Guid $_.Id -ReportType Xml) -notmatch \"<LinksTo>\" }"],["Set a registry-based preference","group-policy-cheat-sheet.html?q=Set%20a%20registry-based%20preference","snippet: Group Policy","Example: disable a setting via Group Policy Preferences registry item, run from the GPMC PowerShell context. Set-GPRegistryValue -Name \"Default Domain Policy\" -"],["Force replication between domain controllers","group-policy-cheat-sheet.html?q=Force%20replication%20between%20domain%20controllers","snippet: Group Policy","Pushes changes to a specific target DC now. repadmin /syncall /AdeP"],["Windows Wi-Fi status","wifi-network-cheat-sheet.html?q=Windows%20Wi-Fi%20status","snippet: Wi-Fi/network","Signal quality, radio type and channel of the current connection. netsh wlan show interfaces"],["List saved Wi-Fi profiles","wifi-network-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20saved%20Wi-Fi%20profiles","snippet: Wi-Fi/network","All networks Windows remembers. netsh wlan show profiles"],["Show a saved Wi-Fi password","wifi-network-cheat-sheet.html?q=Show%20a%20saved%20Wi-Fi%20password","snippet: Wi-Fi/network","Reveals the stored key in clear text. netsh wlan show profile name=\"SSID\" key=clear"],["Wi-Fi report with history","wifi-network-cheat-sheet.html?q=Wi-Fi%20report%20with%20history","snippet: Wi-Fi/network","Generates an HTML report of Wi-Fi sessions and disconnect reasons. netsh wlan show wlanreport"],["Test connectivity to a specific port","wifi-network-cheat-sheet.html?q=Test%20connectivity%20to%20a%20specific%20port","snippet: Wi-Fi/network","PowerShell replacement for telnet with route info. Test-NetConnection -ComputerName host -Port 443 -InformationLevel Detailed"],["Release and renew a DHCP lease","wifi-network-cheat-sheet.html?q=Release%20and%20renew%20a%20DHCP%20lease","snippet: Wi-Fi/network","Common fix for IP or connectivity issues. ipconfig /release ipconfig /renew"],["Azure subscription limits reference","azure-limits-reference.html","page","Default Azure subscription and service limits"],["Bicep and ARM cheat sheet","bicep-arm-cheat-sheet.html","page","Deployments, what-if, modules, loops, Key Vault references"],["Microsoft Graph permissions reference","graph-permissions-reference.html","page","Delegated vs application permissions, admin consent, what each allows"],["Backup and disaster recovery checklist","backup-disaster-recovery-checklist.html","page","Backup coverage, ransomware protection, restore testing, DR planning"],["Subscriptions per Azure AD tenant","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Subscriptions%20per%20Azure%20AD%20tenant","azure limit","No hard limit Governance limit in practice, not a platform cap"],["Resource groups per subscription","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Resource%20groups%20per%20subscription","azure limit","980 Soft, can be raised by request"],["Resources per resource group","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Resources%20per%20resource%20group","azure limit","800 per resource type Varies; some types are lower"],["Tags per resource, resource group or subscription","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Tags%20per%20resource%2C%20resource%20group%20or%20subscription","azure limit","50 "],["Virtual networks per region per subscription","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Virtual%20networks%20per%20region%20per%20subscription","azure limit","1,000 "],["Subnets per virtual network","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Subnets%20per%20virtual%20network","azure limit","3,000 "],["Network security groups per subscription per region","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Network%20security%20groups%20per%20subscription%20per%20region","azure limit","5,000 "],["Route tables per subscription per region","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Route%20tables%20per%20subscription%20per%20region","azure limit","200 "],["Public IP addresses per subscription (Basic)","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Public%20IP%20addresses%20per%20subscription%20%28Basic%29","azure limit","Varies by offer Check quota in the portal under Usage + quotas"],["VM cores per subscription per region","azure-limits-reference.html?q=VM%20cores%20per%20subscription%20per%20region","azure limit","Varies by series and offer Common default is 20 to 350 vCPUs; request an increase"],["Storage accounts per region per subscription","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Storage%20accounts%20per%20region%20per%20subscription","azure limit","250 Can be raised by request"],["Max storage account capacity","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Max%20storage%20account%20capacity","azure limit","5 PiB default Higher available on request"],["Max blob size (block blob)","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Max%20blob%20size%20%28block%20blob%29","azure limit","About 190.7 TiB "],["Max file share size (Azure Files, standard)","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Max%20file%20share%20size%20%28Azure%20Files%2C%20standard%29","azure limit","100 TiB "],["Key Vaults per subscription per region","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Key%20Vaults%20per%20subscription%20per%20region","azure limit","1,000 "],["Secrets, keys and certificates per Key Vault","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Secrets%2C%20keys%20and%20certificates%20per%20Key%20Vault","azure limit","No fixed count, sized by transaction throughput "],["App Service Plans per resource group","azure-limits-reference.html?q=App%20Service%20Plans%20per%20resource%20group","azure limit","100 per region per plan tier "],["Azure SQL Database max size","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Azure%20SQL%20Database%20max%20size","azure limit","Up to 4 TB in most tiers, higher in Hyperscale "],["Azure Functions max execution time (Consumption plan)","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Azure%20Functions%20max%20execution%20time%20%28Consumption%20plan%29","azure limit","10 minutes 230 seconds for HTTP triggers; Premium/Dedicated plans allow longer"],["Resource name length (varies by type)","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Resource%20name%20length%20%28varies%20by%20type%29","azure limit","Typically 1 to 64 characters Check the specific resource type"],["ARM template resources per deployment","azure-limits-reference.html?q=ARM%20template%20resources%20per%20deployment","azure limit","800 "],["Role assignments per subscription","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Role%20assignments%20per%20subscription","azure limit","4,000 "],["Management groups per tenant","azure-limits-reference.html?q=Management%20groups%20per%20tenant","azure limit","10,000 "],["User.Read","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=User.Read","graph permission","Delegated, admin consent: No. Sign in and read the signed-in user's own profile."],["User.Read.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=User.Read.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Read all users' full profiles."],["User.ReadWrite.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=User.ReadWrite.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Read and write all users' full profiles."],["Group.Read.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=Group.Read.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Read all groups and their properties and memberships."],["Group.ReadWrite.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=Group.ReadWrite.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Read and write all groups, including creating and deleting them."],["Directory.Read.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=Directory.Read.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Read directory data: users, groups, apps and organizational information."],["Directory.ReadWrite.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=Directory.ReadWrite.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Read and write most directory data. Broad and sensitive."],["Mail.Read","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=Mail.Read","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Read mail in all mailboxes."],["Mail.ReadWrite","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=Mail.ReadWrite","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Read and write mail in all mailboxes, including deleting messages."],["Mail.Send","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=Mail.Send","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Send mail as any user, without a signed-in context."],["Files.Read.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=Files.Read.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Read files in all site collections and users' OneDrive."],["Files.ReadWrite.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=Files.ReadWrite.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Read and write files in all site collections and OneDrive."],["Sites.Read.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=Sites.Read.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Read items in all SharePoint site collections."],["Sites.FullControl.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=Sites.FullControl.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Full control of all SharePoint site collections."],["AuditLog.Read.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=AuditLog.Read.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Read the tenant's audit log and sign-in log data."],["Policy.Read.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=Policy.Read.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Read Conditional Access and other directory policies."],["Policy.ReadWrite.ConditionalAccess","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=Policy.ReadWrite.ConditionalAccess","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Create and modify Conditional Access policies. High impact."],["RoleManagement.ReadWrite.Directory","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=RoleManagement.ReadWrite.Directory","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Manage directory role assignments, including granting admin roles."],["DeviceManagementManagedDevices.Read.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=DeviceManagementManagedDevices.Read.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Read Intune-managed device data."],["DeviceManagementManagedDevices.PrivilegedOperations.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=DeviceManagementManagedDevices.PrivilegedOperations.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Perform privileged actions on managed devices, such as wipe."],["Application.ReadWrite.All","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=Application.ReadWrite.All","graph permission","Application, admin consent: Yes. Manage all app registrations, including adding credentials to any app."],["offline_access","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=offline_access","graph permission","Delegated, admin consent: No. Lets the app get refresh tokens to stay signed in without the user present."],["openid, profile, email","graph-permissions-reference.html?q=openid%2C%20profile%2C%20email","graph permission","Delegated, admin consent: No. Basic identity claims used with OpenID Connect sign-in."],["Minimal resource group deployment","bicep-arm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Minimal%20resource%20group%20deployment","snippet: Bicep/ARM","Deploy a Bicep file to a resource group. az deployment group create --resource-group myRG --template-file main.bicep --parameters storageName=mystorageacct"],["Preview changes (what-if)","bicep-arm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Preview%20changes%20%28what-if%29","snippet: Bicep/ARM","Shows what a deployment would change without applying it. az deployment group what-if --resource-group myRG --template-file main.bicep"],["Subscription-level deployment","bicep-arm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Subscription-level%20deployment","snippet: Bicep/ARM","For resources like resource groups or policies defined at subscription scope. az deployment sub create --location westeurope --template-file main.bicep"],["Convert an ARM template to Bicep","bicep-arm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Convert%20an%20ARM%20template%20to%20Bicep","snippet: Bicep/ARM","Decompiles an existing JSON template. az bicep decompile --file azuredeploy.json"],["Build Bicep to ARM JSON","bicep-arm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Build%20Bicep%20to%20ARM%20JSON","snippet: Bicep/ARM","Useful to inspect the generated template. az bicep build --file main.bicep"],["Basic storage account resource","bicep-arm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Basic%20storage%20account%20resource","snippet: Bicep/ARM","A minimal Bicep resource block with a parameter. param storageName string param location string = resourceGroup().location  resource sa 'Microsoft.Storage/stora"],["Reference an existing resource","bicep-arm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Reference%20an%20existing%20resource","snippet: Bicep/ARM","Read properties of a resource that already exists, without redeploying it. resource existingVnet 'Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks@2023-05-01' existing = {   n"],["Module reference","bicep-arm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Module%20reference","snippet: Bicep/ARM","Call a reusable Bicep module with parameters. module storage 'modules/storage.bicep' = {   name: 'storageDeployment'   params: {     storageName: 'mystorageacct"],["Output a value from a deployment","bicep-arm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Output%20a%20value%20from%20a%20deployment","snippet: Bicep/ARM","Return the storage account's endpoint for use elsewhere. output blobEndpoint string = sa.properties.primaryEndpoints.blob"],["Loop to create multiple resources","bicep-arm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Loop%20to%20create%20multiple%20resources","snippet: Bicep/ARM","Creates one storage account per name in the array. param storageNames array resource sa 'Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts@2023-01-01' = [for name in storageNam"],["Conditional resource deployment","bicep-arm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Conditional%20resource%20deployment","snippet: Bicep/ARM","Only creates the resource when the condition is true. resource sa 'Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts@2023-01-01' = if (deployStorage) {   name: storageName   lo"],["Reference a Key Vault secret as a parameter","bicep-arm-cheat-sheet.html?q=Reference%20a%20Key%20Vault%20secret%20as%20a%20parameter","snippet: Bicep/ARM","Pulls a secret value in at deployment time without exposing it in the template. param adminPassword string = '' // In the parameters file: // \"adminPassword\": {"],["DNS record types reference","dns-record-types-reference.html","page","A, AAAA, MX, TXT, SPF, DKIM, DMARC, CAA, SRV, DNSSEC explained"],["Docker Compose cheat sheet","docker-compose-cheat-sheet.html","page","Volumes, networks, health checks, overrides, resource limits"],["A","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=A","dns record","Maps a hostname to an IPv4 address."],["AAAA","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=AAAA","dns record","Maps a hostname to an IPv6 address."],["CNAME","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=CNAME","dns record","An alias that points one name to another name. Cannot coexist with other records on the same name."],["MX","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=MX","dns record","Mail server for the domain, with a priority; lower number is tried first."],["TXT","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=TXT","dns record","Free-text data, used for domain verification and policies such as SPF and DMARC."],["NS","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=NS","dns record","Delegates a zone or subdomain to a set of name servers."],["SOA","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=SOA","dns record","Start of authority: the zone's primary name server, admin contact and refresh/retry/expire timers."],["PTR","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=PTR","dns record","Reverse DNS: maps an IP address back to a hostname. Lives in the in-addr.arpa or ip6.arpa zone."],["SRV","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=SRV","dns record","Points to a host and port for a specific service, used by protocols like SIP and some Microsoft services."],["CAA","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=CAA","dns record","States which certificate authorities are allowed to issue certificates for the domain."],["DKIM (TXT)","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=DKIM%20%28TXT%29","dns record","Public key for verifying DKIM-signed mail, published at a selector name."],["DMARC (TXT)","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=DMARC%20%28TXT%29","dns record","Policy for handling mail that fails SPF/DKIM alignment, published at _dmarc."],["NAPTR","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=NAPTR","dns record","Used in some VoIP and ENUM setups to rewrite a name into another form before further lookups."],["DS / DNSKEY","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=DS%20/%20DNSKEY","dns record","Records used for DNSSEC: DS is published in the parent zone, DNSKEY holds the zone's public signing key."],["TLSA","dns-record-types-reference.html?q=TLSA","dns record","Associates a TLS certificate with a hostname and port for DNS-based authentication (DANE)."],["Minimal web app service","docker-compose-cheat-sheet.html?q=Minimal%20web%20app%20service","snippet: Docker Compose","A service definition with a build context, port mapping and a restart policy. services:   web:     build: .     ports:       - \"8080:80\"     restart: unless-sto"],["Environment variables from a file","docker-compose-cheat-sheet.html?q=Environment%20variables%20from%20a%20file","snippet: Docker Compose","Keeps secrets and config out of the compose file itself. services:   api:     image: myapi:latest     env_file:       - .env"],["Named volume for persistent data","docker-compose-cheat-sheet.html?q=Named%20volume%20for%20persistent%20data","snippet: Docker Compose","The volume survives container recreation. services:   db:     image: postgres:16     volumes:       - db-data:/var/lib/postgresql/data volumes:   db-data:"],["Bind mount for local development","docker-compose-cheat-sheet.html?q=Bind%20mount%20for%20local%20development","snippet: Docker Compose","Maps a local folder into the container for live editing. services:   app:     build: .     volumes:       - ./src:/app/src"],["Service dependency with a health check","docker-compose-cheat-sheet.html?q=Service%20dependency%20with%20a%20health%20check","snippet: Docker Compose","Waits for the database to be healthy before starting the app. services:   db:     image: postgres:16     healthcheck:       test: [\"CMD-SHELL\", \"pg_isready -U p"],["Custom network between services","docker-compose-cheat-sheet.html?q=Custom%20network%20between%20services","snippet: Docker Compose","Services on the same network can reach each other by service name. services:   app:     build: .     networks: [backend]   db:     image: postgres:16     networ"],["Resource limits","docker-compose-cheat-sheet.html?q=Resource%20limits","snippet: Docker Compose","Caps CPU and memory for a service. services:   app:     image: myapp:latest     deploy:       resources:         limits:           cpus: \"1.0\"           memory:"],["Override file for local development","docker-compose-cheat-sheet.html?q=Override%20file%20for%20local%20development","snippet: Docker Compose","docker compose automatically merges docker-compose.override.yml on top of the base file. # docker-compose.override.yml services:   app:     ports:       - \"9229"],["Run a one-off command in a service","docker-compose-cheat-sheet.html?q=Run%20a%20one-off%20command%20in%20a%20service","snippet: Docker Compose","Runs a command in a new container using the service's image and config. docker compose run --rm app npm test"],["Scale a service to multiple instances","docker-compose-cheat-sheet.html?q=Scale%20a%20service%20to%20multiple%20instances","snippet: Docker Compose","Runs three instances of the worker service, useful with a load balancer in front. docker compose up -d --scale worker=3"],["markdown-previewer","tools.html#markdown-previewer","tool","Live-render Markdown: headings, bold, italics, links, lists, code, tables"],["text-diff","tools.html#text-diff","tool","Compare two blocks of text line by line"],["case-converter","tools.html#case-converter","tool","Convert text to camelCase, PascalCase, snake_case, kebab-case"],["ipv6-tool","tools.html#ipv6-tool","tool","Expand or compress an IPv6 address"],["Terraform cheat sheet (Azure)","terraform-cheat-sheet.html","page","azurerm resources, variables, remote state, count, for_each"],["Regex patterns library","regex-patterns-library.html","page","Copy-paste patterns: email, IPv4, UUID, passwords, MAC, semver"],["Email address","regex-patterns-library.html?q=Email%20address","regex pattern","Good enough for form validation. Real email syntax is far more permissive; do not use this to reject valid addresses outright."],["IPv4 address","regex-patterns-library.html?q=IPv4%20address","regex pattern","Matches the shape but not the range; add logic to check each octet is 0 to 255."],["URL (http/https)","regex-patterns-library.html?q=URL%20%28http/https%29","regex pattern","Covers common cases. For strict validation use a URL parser instead of regex."],["UUID / GUID","regex-patterns-library.html?q=UUID%20/%20GUID","regex pattern","Matches the standard 8-4-4-4-12 hyphenated format."],["Hex color","regex-patterns-library.html?q=Hex%20color","regex pattern","Matches #fff and #ffffff style values."],["Windows file path","regex-patterns-library.html?q=Windows%20file%20path","regex pattern","Matches a drive letter followed by backslash-separated segments."],["Strong password","regex-patterns-library.html?q=Strong%20password","regex pattern","Requires lowercase, uppercase, a digit, a symbol and at least 12 characters using lookaheads."],["Log line timestamp (ISO 8601)","regex-patterns-library.html?q=Log%20line%20timestamp%20%28ISO%208601%29","regex pattern","Extracts an ISO timestamp from a log line; use it with a capture or as a search anchor."],["MAC address","regex-patterns-library.html?q=MAC%20address","regex pattern","Matches colon- or hyphen-separated MAC addresses."],["Semantic version","regex-patterns-library.html?q=Semantic%20version","regex pattern","Matches versions like 1.4.2, 2.0.0-beta.1 or 1.0.0+build.5."],["CIDR notation","regex-patterns-library.html?q=CIDR%20notation","regex pattern","Matches shape only, for example 10.0.0.0/24; validate ranges separately."],["Whitespace-only line","regex-patterns-library.html?q=Whitespace-only%20line","regex pattern","Useful to find or strip blank lines in a file."],["HTML tag","regex-patterns-library.html?q=HTML%20tag","regex pattern","Matches a single opening or closing tag. Regex is not reliable for parsing full HTML documents; use a real parser for that."],["Credit card number (loose)","regex-patterns-library.html?q=Credit%20card%20number%20%28loose%29","regex pattern","Matches only digit count and says nothing about validity. Use the Luhn algorithm to actually validate a card number, and avoid storing card numbers at"],["Trailing whitespace","regex-patterns-library.html?q=Trailing%20whitespace","regex pattern","Matches spaces or tabs at the end of a line, handy for cleanup scripts."],["Provider block for Azure","terraform-cheat-sheet.html?q=Provider%20block%20for%20Azure","snippet: Terraform","Pins the azurerm provider version. Run terraform init after adding this. terraform {   required_providers {     azurerm = {       source  = \"hashicorp/azurerm\" "],["Resource group","terraform-cheat-sheet.html?q=Resource%20group","snippet: Terraform","The most basic Azure resource. resource \"azurerm_resource_group\" \"main\" {   name     = \"rg-example\"   location = \"westeurope\" }"],["Reference another resource's attribute","terraform-cheat-sheet.html?q=Reference%20another%20resource%27s%20attribute","snippet: Terraform","Terraform infers the dependency automatically from the reference. resource \"azurerm_storage_account\" \"main\" {   name                     = \"examplestorageacct\" "],["Variables and a default value","terraform-cheat-sheet.html?q=Variables%20and%20a%20default%20value","snippet: Terraform","Declare an input variable with a type and default. variable \"location\" {   type    = string   default = \"westeurope\" }"],["Output a value","terraform-cheat-sheet.html?q=Output%20a%20value","snippet: Terraform","Prints a value after apply, or lets other configurations reference it with terraform_remote_state. output \"storage_account_id\" {   value = azurerm_storage_accou"],["Remote state in Azure Storage","terraform-cheat-sheet.html?q=Remote%20state%20in%20Azure%20Storage","snippet: Terraform","Keeps state off your laptop and lets a team share it. terraform {   backend \"azurerm\" {     resource_group_name = \"rg-terraform-state\"     storage_account_name "],["Data source: look up an existing resource","terraform-cheat-sheet.html?q=Data%20source%3A%20look%20up%20an%20existing%20resource","snippet: Terraform","Reads an existing resource group without managing it. data \"azurerm_resource_group\" \"existing\" {   name = \"rg-shared\" }"],["Count to create multiple resources","terraform-cheat-sheet.html?q=Count%20to%20create%20multiple%20resources","snippet: Terraform","Creates three storage accounts named example-storage-0, -1, -2. resource \"azurerm_storage_account\" \"main\" {   count                    = 3   name               "],["for_each over a map","terraform-cheat-sheet.html?q=for_each%20over%20a%20map","snippet: Terraform","Creates one resource per entry, named by key instead of index. variable \"storage_accounts\" {   type = map(string)   default = {     logs   = \"examplelogs\"     b"],["Core CLI workflow","terraform-cheat-sheet.html?q=Core%20CLI%20workflow","snippet: Terraform","The commands you run in order, every time. terraform init terraform plan -out=tfplan terraform apply tfplan"],["Format and validate","terraform-cheat-sheet.html?q=Format%20and%20validate","snippet: Terraform","Run before committing. fmt rewrites files in place. terraform fmt -recursive terraform validate"],["Import an existing resource","terraform-cheat-sheet.html?q=Import%20an%20existing%20resource","snippet: Terraform","Brings a resource created outside Terraform under its management, matched to this resource block. terraform import azurerm_resource_group.main /subscriptions/SU"],["Target a single resource","terraform-cheat-sheet.html?q=Target%20a%20single%20resource","snippet: Terraform","Applies changes to just one resource, useful for troubleshooting. terraform apply -target=azurerm_storage_account.main"],["Destroy everything","terraform-cheat-sheet.html?q=Destroy%20everything","snippet: Terraform","Removes every resource this configuration manages. There is no undo. terraform destroy"],["Windows Server roles reference","windows-server-roles-reference.html","page","AD DS, AD CS, DNS, DHCP, IIS, Hyper-V, WSUS, NPS, RDS explained"],["How certificate chain validation works","pki-chain-explained.html","page","Interactive diagram: leaf, intermediate, root store, revocation, common TLS failures"],["Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS)","windows-server-roles-reference.html?q=Active","server role","Provides the domain directory: authentication, Kerberos, Group Policy and the object store for users, computers and groups. One of the most sensitive "],["DNS Server","windows-server-roles-reference.html?q=DNS","server role","Resolves hostnames to IP addresses. Usually installed alongside AD DS and integrated with the Active Directory database. Active Directory depends enti"],["DHCP Server","windows-server-roles-reference.html?q=DHCP","server role","Automatically assigns IP addresses, gateways and DNS servers to devices on the network. Only one DHCP server should normally serve a given scope, or u"],["File and Storage Services","windows-server-roles-reference.html?q=File","server role","Serves shared folders (SMB) and manages storage, including quotas and deduplication. SMBv1 should be disabled; use SMB signing and encryption where po"],["Remote Desktop Services (RDS)","windows-server-roles-reference.html?q=Remote","server role","Provides remote access to full desktops or individual published applications for multiple users. Not the same as enabling RDP for administration; RDS "],["Web Server (IIS)","windows-server-roles-reference.html?q=Web","server role","Hosts websites and web applications on Windows. Keep it patched and remove default sample sites and unused modules."],["Hyper-V","windows-server-roles-reference.html?q=Hyper-V","server role","Windows' built-in hypervisor role for running virtual machines. Host patching and backup strategy matter as much as the guest VMs."],["Windows Server Update Services (WSUS)","windows-server-roles-reference.html?q=Windows","server role","Centrally manages and distributes Windows updates to devices on the network instead of each device downloading them separately. Approve and test updat"],["Network Policy and Access Services (NPS)","windows-server-roles-reference.html?q=Network","server role","Provides RADIUS authentication, commonly used for Wi-Fi, VPN and 802.1X network access control. Often the RADIUS server behind on-premises network aut"],["Print and Document Services","windows-server-roles-reference.html?q=Print","server role","Centralizes print queue management and driver deployment. The Print Spooler service has had multiple serious vulnerabilities; disable it on servers th"],["Failover Clustering","windows-server-roles-reference.html?q=Failover","server role","A feature (not a role) that lets multiple servers work together to keep a service available if one node fails. Used under many roles, such as file ser"],["Common log file locations reference","log-file-locations-reference.html","page","Where to find logs on Windows, Linux, Microsoft 365"],["Microsoft Purview compliance cheat sheet","purview-compliance-cheat-sheet.html","page","Unified audit log, retention, DLP, sensitivity labels, eDiscovery"],["Windows Security log","log-file-locations-reference.html?q=Windows","log location","Logons, logoffs, privilege use, account changes. Events 4624, 4625, 4720 and more."],["PowerShell Operational log","log-file-locations-reference.html?q=PowerShell","log location","Script block logging (event 4104) when enabled; useful for detecting obfuscated commands."],["IIS logs","log-file-locations-reference.html?q=IIS","log location","Per-site HTTP request logs: client IP, URL, status code, user agent."],["DNS Server debug log","log-file-locations-reference.html?q=DNS","log location","Query and response detail when enabled; heavy performance cost, enable only when troubleshooting."],["DHCP Server audit log","log-file-locations-reference.html?q=DHCP","log location","Lease assignments, renewals, conflicts, one file per day of the week."],["Linux system log (systemd)","log-file-locations-reference.html?q=Linux","log location","Central log for systemd-based distributions; replaces most of /var/log for many services."],["Nginx access/error logs","log-file-locations-reference.html?q=Nginx","log location","Per-request HTTP logs and server-side errors."],["Apache access/error logs","log-file-locations-reference.html?q=Apache","log location","Per-request HTTP logs and server-side errors."],["Docker container logs","log-file-locations-reference.html?q=Docker","log location","stdout and stderr of the container's main process."],["Exchange Online message trace","log-file-locations-reference.html?q=Exchange","log location","Mail flow: sender, recipient, subject, status, for the last 10 days by default (90 with extended reporting)."],["Microsoft 365 Unified Audit Log","log-file-locations-reference.html?q=Microsoft","log location","User and admin activity across Exchange, SharePoint, Teams and Entra ID."],["Entra ID sign-in logs","log-file-locations-reference.html?q=Entra","log location","Every sign-in attempt with result, location, device and Conditional Access outcome."],["Connect to Security & Compliance PowerShell","purview-compliance-cheat-sheet.html?q=Connect%20to%20Security%20%26%20Compliance%20PowerShell","snippet: Purview/Compliance","Uses the same ExchangeOnlineManagement module, a different connection function. Connect-IPPSSession -UserPrincipalName admin@contoso.com"],["Search the unified audit log","purview-compliance-cheat-sheet.html?q=Search%20the%20unified%20audit%20log","snippet: Purview/Compliance","Basic search across a date range for a specific user. Search-UnifiedAuditLog -StartDate (Get-Date).AddDays(-7) -EndDate (Get-Date) -UserIds user@contoso.com -Re"],["Search for a specific operation","purview-compliance-cheat-sheet.html?q=Search%20for%20a%20specific%20operation","snippet: Purview/Compliance","Filter to one type of action, for example file downloads. Search-UnifiedAuditLog -StartDate (Get-Date).AddDays(-7) -EndDate (Get-Date) -Operations FileDownloade"],["Create a retention policy","purview-compliance-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20retention%20policy","snippet: Purview/Compliance","Applies a retention period to Exchange and SharePoint locations. New-RetentionCompliancePolicy -Name \"7-year-retention\" -ExchangeLocation All -SharePointLocatio"],["List DLP policies","purview-compliance-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20DLP%20policies","snippet: Purview/Compliance","Overview of configured data loss prevention policies. Get-DlpCompliancePolicy | Select-Object Name,Mode,Enabled"],["Create a basic DLP policy","purview-compliance-cheat-sheet.html?q=Create%20a%20basic%20DLP%20policy","snippet: Purview/Compliance","Detects a built-in sensitive information type across Exchange and SharePoint. New-DlpCompliancePolicy -Name \"Credit Card Protection\" -ExchangeLocation All -Shar"],["List sensitivity labels","purview-compliance-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20sensitivity%20labels","snippet: Purview/Compliance","Labels available to apply to content. Get-Label | Select-Object Name,DisplayName,Priority"],["List label policies","purview-compliance-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20label%20policies","snippet: Purview/Compliance","Which labels are published to which users. Get-LabelPolicy | Select-Object Name,Labels,ExchangeLocation"],["Start a Content Search (eDiscovery)","purview-compliance-cheat-sheet.html?q=Start%20a%20Content%20Search%20%28eDiscovery%29","snippet: Purview/Compliance","Basic keyword search across mailboxes. New-ComplianceSearch -Name \"Investigation01\" -ExchangeLocation All -ContentMatchQuery 'subject:\"contract termination\"' St"],["Check Content Search status","purview-compliance-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20Content%20Search%20status","snippet: Purview/Compliance","Searches can take time on large tenants. Get-ComplianceSearch -Identity \"Investigation01\" | Select-Object Name,Status,Items"],["List insider risk policies","purview-compliance-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20insider%20risk%20policies","snippet: Purview/Compliance","Overview of configured insider risk management policies. Get-InsiderRiskPolicy | Select-Object Name,Type,Status"],["Check mailbox litigation hold status","purview-compliance-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20mailbox%20litigation%20hold%20status","snippet: Purview/Compliance","Whether a mailbox is under legal hold. Get-Mailbox -Identity user@contoso.com | Select-Object LitigationHoldEnabled,LitigationHoldDuration"],["Windows Autopilot deployment cheat sheet","autopilot-deployment-cheat-sheet.html","page","Hardware hash, device registration, group tags, ESP diagnostics"],["Certificate authentication and smart card cheat sheet","certificate-authentication-cheat-sheet.html","page","Certificate stores, PFX export/import, smart cards, Windows Hello"],["Export the hardware hash for Autopilot","autopilot-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Export%20the%20hardware%20hash%20for%20Autopilot","snippet: autopilot deployment","Installs the community script and writes the hash to CSV, ready to upload to Intune. Install-Script -Name Get-WindowsAutopilotInfo -Force Get-WindowsAutopilotIn"],["List Autopilot devices","autopilot-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20Autopilot%20devices","snippet: autopilot deployment","Serial number, group tag and enrollment state, via Microsoft Graph. Connect-MgGraph -Scopes \"DeviceManagementServiceConfig.Read.All\" Get-MgDeviceManagementWindo"],["Assign a group tag to an Autopilot device","autopilot-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Assign%20a%20group%20tag%20to%20an%20Autopilot%20device","snippet: autopilot deployment","Group tags drive dynamic group membership and profile assignment. Update-MgDeviceManagementWindowAutopilotDeviceIdentity -WindowsAutopilotDeviceIdentityId $devi"],["Delete an Autopilot device registration","autopilot-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Delete%20an%20Autopilot%20device%20registration","snippet: autopilot deployment","Needed before re-registering a device that was wiped or reused. Remove-MgDeviceManagementWindowAutopilotDeviceIdentity -WindowsAutopilotDeviceIdentityId $device"],["Trigger ESP troubleshooting log collection","autopilot-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Trigger%20ESP%20troubleshooting%20log%20collection","snippet: autopilot deployment","Collects Autopilot and Enrollment Status Page logs from the device for troubleshooting. Get-AutopilotDiagnostics -Online"],["Check the current Autopilot profile on a device","autopilot-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20the%20current%20Autopilot%20profile%20on%20a%20device","snippet: autopilot deployment","Shows whether a device recognizes its Autopilot profile and deployment mode. Get-ItemProperty -Path \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Provisioning\\Diagnostics\\Autopilot"],["List Intune configuration profiles","autopilot-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20Intune%20configuration%20profiles","snippet: autopilot deployment","Overview of configuration profiles and their assignment. Get-MgDeviceManagementDeviceConfiguration | Select-Object DisplayName,Id"],["List Win32 app deployments","autopilot-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20Win32%20app%20deployments","snippet: autopilot deployment","Apps packaged as .intunewin and their install status summary. Get-MgDeviceAppManagementMobileApp -Filter \"isof('microsoft.graph.win32LobApp')\" | Select-Object D"],["Force a device to check in with Intune","autopilot-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Force%20a%20device%20to%20check%20in%20with%20Intune","snippet: autopilot deployment","Same as clicking Sync in Company Portal, but scriptable. Sync-MgDeviceManagementManagedDevice -ManagedDeviceId $deviceId"],["Retire vs wipe a device","autopilot-deployment-cheat-sheet.html?q=Retire%20vs%20wipe%20a%20device","snippet: autopilot deployment","Retire removes company data and management but leaves personal data and the OS; wipe resets the device to factory settings. Invoke-MgRetireDeviceManagementManag"],["Request a certificate from a template","certificate-authentication-cheat-sheet.html?q=Request%20a%20certificate%20from%20a%20template","snippet: certificate authentication","Uses the certreq workflow against an internal CA; commonly done via MMC or auto-enrollment instead. certreq -new request.inf request.req certreq -submit -config"],["List certificates in the personal store","certificate-authentication-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20certificates%20in%20the%20personal%20store","snippet: certificate authentication","Shows subject, thumbprint and expiry for the current user. Get-ChildItem -Path Cert:\\CurrentUser\\My | Select-Object Subject,Thumbprint,NotAfter"],["List certificates in the machine store","certificate-authentication-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20certificates%20in%20the%20machine%20store","snippet: certificate authentication","Same as above for the local machine account, needs an elevated prompt. Get-ChildItem -Path Cert:\\LocalMachine\\My | Select-Object Subject,Thumbprint,NotAfter"],["Find certificates expiring soon","certificate-authentication-cheat-sheet.html?q=Find%20certificates%20expiring%20soon","snippet: certificate authentication","Certificates in the machine store expiring within 30 days. Get-ChildItem -Path Cert:\\LocalMachine\\My | Where-Object { $_.NotAfter -lt (Get-Date).AddDays(30) } |"],["Export a certificate with its private key","certificate-authentication-cheat-sheet.html?q=Export%20a%20certificate%20with%20its%20private%20key","snippet: certificate authentication","Creates a password-protected PFX file. Keep the password and file secure. $pwd = ConvertTo-SecureString -String \"P@ssw0rd!\" -Force -AsPlainText Get-ChildItem -P"],["Import a PFX certificate","certificate-authentication-cheat-sheet.html?q=Import%20a%20PFX%20certificate","snippet: certificate authentication","Imports into the current user's personal store. $pwd = ConvertTo-SecureString -String \"P@ssw0rd!\" -Force -AsPlainText Import-PfxCertificate -FilePath C:\\Temp\\ce"],["Check a smart card reader's status on Windows","certificate-authentication-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20a%20smart%20card%20reader%27s%20status%20on%20Windows","snippet: certificate authentication","Lists Plug and Play devices related to smart card readers. Get-PnpDevice -Class SmartCardReader | Select-Object FriendlyName,Status"],["Enable the Smart Card service","certificate-authentication-cheat-sheet.html?q=Enable%20the%20Smart%20Card%20service","snippet: certificate authentication","The service must be running for smart card sign-in to work. Set-Service -Name SCardSvr -StartupType Automatic Start-Service -Name SCardSvr"],["Check the Windows Hello for Business enrollment status","certificate-authentication-cheat-sheet.html?q=Check%20the%20Windows%20Hello%20for%20Business%20enrollment%20status","snippet: certificate authentication","Registry key that reflects whether the device completed Hello for Business provisioning. Get-ItemProperty -Path \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Cryptography\\Ngc\" -Err"],["List issued client authentication certificates on an AD CS server","certificate-authentication-cheat-sheet.html?q=List%20issued%20client%20authentication%20certificates%20on%20an%20AD%20CS%20server","snippet: certificate authentication","Requires the certificate authority PowerShell module. Get-CATemplate | Select-Object Name,SchemaVersion certutil -view -restrict \"Disposition=20\" -out \"Requeste"],["Incident war stories","war-stories.html","page","Composite incident scenarios: AiTM phishing, Kerberoasting, ransomware backup failure"],["The help desk that answered too fast","aitm-help-desk.html","story","A finance employee approved an MFA prompt for a sign-in that wasn't theirs. Forty minutes later, an invoice went out with different bank details."],["The service account nobody remembered","kerberoast-service-account.html","story","A five-year-old service account with a never-expiring password became the quiet path from a regular user account to Domain Admin."],["The backup that had never been tested","ransomware-backup-gap.html","story","Backups were running every night for three years. Nobody had actually tried to restore from one until the night it mattered."]];
